aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc2VjcmV0Y2hpbmEuY29tL25ld3MvZ2IvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC8xMTA2OTQ2Lmh0bWw=,PICKUP,中国CDCが集団感染（甲類感染症であるペスト8例・死亡1例）を公表したこと、かつロシアでも原因不明肺炎による研究者の死亡が報告されており、肺ペストの可能性やヒト-ヒト感染リスクが懸念されるため、フルリスク評価への移行が適切と判断した。,COVID-19; Pneumonic Plague; Plague,Moscow; Hubei Sheng; Shanghai Shi; Henan Sheng; Irkutskaya Oblast’; Irkutsk; Shanghai; Chongqing; Wuhan; Chengdu; Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region; Chongqing Shi; Sichuan Sheng; Moskva; United States; Russian Federation; People's Republic of China,Signals of a plague resurgence? CPC reports first death case (Photo) - Op-Ed - Chen Jing,瘟疫再起的信号？中共通报首例死亡病例(图) - 时评 - 陈静,2026-11-04T00:41:58+00:00,https://www.secretchina.com/news/gb/2026/11/04/1106946.html,CHINESE,humans; animals; environment,"As of 2026-11-04, China’s CDC quietly disclosed in September 2026 an overview listing eight Class A plague cases with one death, but provided no location, patient details, or transmission information. In early October, Russia’s Irkutsk Anti-Plague Research Institute reported a female laboratory technician died from pneumonia of unknown origin; Moscow denied any “anti-plague measures” and offered to assist the United States with infectious diseases. Chinese-language social media circulated claims that pneumonic plague had entered China, with unreported “plague alerts” reportedly circulating in Henan, Inner Mongolia, Shanghai, and Chongqing. In Chengdu, a fever clinic doctor privately warned that a patient who had recently returned from Russia deteriorated rapidly, echoing Li Wenliang’s warnings from the COVID-19 era. The piece links to a broader call for transparency and preparedness, drawing parallels to the 2019–2020 Wuhan outbreak and criticizing information suppression.",Yes,Yes,不明,No,2,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,不明,3,Yes,不明,不明,記事は政治色の強いオピニオン記事であり、具体的な発生地点・症例詳細・感染経路は公式に未公表。ロシア（イルクーツク）の事例は対象国リストに含まれないため除外。情報の信頼性・一次情報源の確認が必要であり、続報の収集とWHO/中国CDC公式発表の確認を優先すべき。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc2VjcmV0Y2hpbmEuY29tL25ld3MvYjUvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC8xMTA2OTQ2Lmh0bWw=,WATCH,中国CDCがペスト8例・死亡1例を報告したが詳細不明であり、ロシアでの関連死やペスト性肺炎流入の噂は未確認の論評記事であるため、続報を注視する必要がある。,COVID-19; Pneumonic Plague; Plague,Hubei Sheng; Irkutskaya Oblast’; Irkutsk; Wuhan; Chengdu; Sichuan Sheng; Shuangliu Xian; United States; Russian Federation; People's Republic of China,Signals of a Plague Resurgence? The CCP Reports Its First Death Case (Photo) - Op-Ed - Chen Jing,瘟疫再起的信號？中共通報首例死亡病例(圖) - 時評 - 陳靜,2026-11-04T00:46:28+00:00,https://www.secretchina.com/news/b5/2026/11/04/1106946.html,CHINESE,humans; environment,"China’s CDC quietly released a September 2026 summary showing eight Class A plague cases with one death, but without details on location, age, or transmission, raising concerns of underreporting. The article links this death to broader alarm: on Oct 6, Irkutsk, Russia, an Anti-Plague Research Institute technician reportedly died from plague-related illness; Russia denied “anti-plague measures” and offered to assist the US on infectious diseases. Following online rumors that pneumonic plague had entered China, authorities issued debunking and censored posts. In Chengdu, a Shuangliu District fever clinic patient with high fever reportedly prompted a private warning from a clinician about a recent Russian returnee whose condition deteriorated rapidly—an echo of Li Wenliang’s early whistleblowing. The piece argues this reflects opaque public health reporting, referencing the 2019 Wuhan COVID-19 events, and urges vigilance and preparedness; it is an opinion piece from Look China.",不明,不明,不明,No,0,不明,不明,不明,不明,不明,0,Yes,Yes,不明,本記事は反体制系メディアによる評論記事であり、ロシアでの死亡例や肺ペスト流入の噂は未確認・政府により否定されている。中国CDCの公式集計（ペストはクラスA感染症として常時報告対象）自体は事実と見られるが、詳細情報（地域・年齢・感染経路）が欠如しており、情報の信頼性評価には追加確認が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubnl0aW1lcy5jb20vMjAyNi8xMS8wMy93b3JsZC9hZnJpY2EvY29uZ28tYW50aHJheC1oaXBwb3MtdmlydW5nYS1wYXJrLmh0bWw=,PICKUP,DRCのヴィルンガ国立公園で炭疽により多数のカバが死亡しており、食料不安・貧困層による感染肉の摂取リスクやエボラ流行で逼迫する公衆衛生体制との重なりがあり、ヒトへの波及リスクと社会的関心（NYT報道）が確認されるためフルリスク評価へ進める。,Anthrax; Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,,Anthrax Outbreak in Africa's Oldest National Park Is Killing Hippos,2026-11-04T00:48:08+00:00,https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/03/world/africa/congo-anthrax-hippos-virunga-park.html,ENGLISH,animals; humans,"Anthrax outbreak in Virunga National Park, the Democratic Republic of Congo, has killed 30 hippopotamuses since September, with the outbreak confirmed by laboratory analyses. This marks the park's second anthrax outbreak since last year. Congo is also contending with an Ebola epidemic that has killed more than 4,800 people since May, straining resources and public health capacity. Health officials note that anthrax outbreaks in the region intersect with food insecurity, conflict, poverty, and disproportionately affect rural populations with limited access to care. Park authorities are raising awareness to prevent contact with or consumption of meat from affected carcasses and to report any finds. Virunga's response focuses on surveillance, safe carcass management, and reducing risks to wildlife and people through documentation of mortalities and coordinated disposal of carcasses.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,Yes,3,Yes,Yes,不明,本記事の主題は野生動物（カバ）における炭疽流行であり、ヒト感染例は明記されていない。ただし感染肉摂取を介したヒトへの波及リスク、及び同国で進行中のエボラ流行による医療資源逼迫との関連が指摘されており、続報での人的被害確認が重要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9maW5hbmNlLmpyai5jb20uY24vMjAyNi8xMS8wNDA5MDY1OTAwMzY0MS5zaHRtbA==,DISMISS,企業の財務業績とワクチン開発に関する業界ニュースであり、実際の疾病発生や公衆衛生上の緊急事態を報じるものではない。,African Swine Fever,Gansu Sheng; Lanzhou,"PulaiKe's net profit attributable to the parent in the first three quarters fell 49.38%, and its African swine fever subunit vaccine received a clinical trial approval in October.",普莱柯前三季度归母净利降49.38%，其非洲猪瘟亚单位疫苗10月获临床试验批件,2026-11-04T01:06:14+00:00,https://finance.jrj.com.cn/2026/11/04090659003641.shtml,CHINESE,animals,"PulaiKe Biotech reported 2026 year-to-date revenue of 7.38 billion yuan, down 10.32% year over year, with net profit attributable to shareholders of 79.545 million yuan, down 49.38%. In Q3, revenue was 2.47 billion yuan, down 6.38%, and net profit 2.2207 million yuan, with non-recurring net loss of 5.6515 million yuan, pressured by lower pig-vaccine orders and bioscience VAT changes. In October 2026, in collaboration with the Lanzhou Veterinary Research Institute of the Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences, the African swine fever subunit vaccine obtained clinical-trial approval from the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs. The company plans to advance high-barrier technologies, expand pet vaccines and other veterinary products, and optimize sales channels across breeders, veterinary clinics, and online platforms to weather the downturn and position for future recovery in the pig sector.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,本記事は企業の財務報告とワクチン開発の進捗に関するもので、具体的なアフリカ豚熱の発生事例を報じていないため、対象国の発生地域としては計上しない。,
