aHR0cHM6Ly9mci5xei5jb20vdW5lLXBpZG1pZS1kZS1jaGFyYm9uLXR1ZS0zMC1oaXBwb3BvdGFtZXMtYXUtcGFyYy1uYXRpb25hbC1kZXMtdmlydW5nYS0xMTA0MjY=,WATCH,動物（カバ）の炭疽感染事例であり、現時点でヒトへの感染報告はないが、地元住民への注意喚起がなされており人獣共通感染症としての拡大リスクを注視する必要がある。,Anthrax,Democratic Republic of the Congo,"Anthrax kills 30 hippopotamuses in Virunga National Park, Congo.","Le charbon tue 30 hippopotames dans le parc national des Virunga, Congo.",2026-11-04T01:07:55+00:00,https://fr.qz.com/une-pidmie-de-charbon-tue-30-hippopotames-au-parc-national-des-virunga-110426,FRENCH,animals,"Anthrax has killed 30 hippopotamuses in Virunga National Park, Democratic Republic of the Congo, with deaths dating back to September. Laboratory analyses confirmed anthrax as the cause of the outbreak, according to reporting by the New York Times. Laura Parker, who heads conservation programs at Virunga, said observers noticed suspect carcasses in September. Local communities have been urged to avoid touching or eating meat from carcasses and to report any findings to authorities. Virunga’s response prioritizes surveillance, safe carcass management, and reducing risks to both wildlife and people. Teams are monitoring the affected area, documenting new mortalities, and coordinating safe disposal of carcasses. The aim is to limit transmission while the outbreak is investigated and managed.",No,Yes,No,No,1,Yes,不明,Yes,不明,不明,2,不明,不明,不明,現時点ではヒト感染例の報告はなく、動物（カバ）における炭疽の集団死事例。人への感染リスク低減のため肉の接触・摂取を避けるよう地元住民に注意喚起されている。続報でヒト感染の有無を確認する必要がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmF0aW9udGhhaWxhbmQuY29tL2hlYWx0aC13ZWxsbmVzcy80MDA3MzA4Mg==,DISMISS,タイ国内で既に確立された監視体制下での定期報告であり、新規性・異常性は認められず、社会的関心の急激な高まりも記事からは読み取れない。,Mpox,Kingdom of Thailand,,Thailand reports 470 mpox cases and three deaths as health officials urge early testing,2026-11-04T02:13:00+00:00,https://www.nationthailand.com/health-wellness/40073082,ENGLISH,humans,"Thailand reports 470 mpox cases and three deaths from January 1 to October 31, 2026, prompting the Department of Disease Control (DDC) to urge early testing for suspicious symptoms. Dr Montien Kanasawadse notes mpox remains under surveillance under the 2015 Communicable Diseases Act and the 2022 Ministry notification. Early symptoms include fever, headaches, back and muscle pains, swollen lymph nodes, followed by rashes or lesions on the face, body, genitals or around the anus; some patients have few lesions or anal-area pain. PCR testing of skin-lesion material is required to confirm infection; blood tests are not definitive. Most patients recover with supportive care; higher risk for immunocompromised individuals, pregnancy, and young children. Prevent transmission by avoiding close contact with lesions, not sharing linens, and maintaining hygiene. Globally, 68,096 confirmed infections and 272 deaths reported across 107 countries from Jan 2025 to Aug 31, 2026 per WHO, a separate reporting period.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,不明,No,No,2026年1月〜10月の累計症例報告であり、既存の感染症法・監視制度下での定期的な公衆衛生広報記事。新規アウトブレイクや異常な増加を示す記述はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9uZXdzLmNoaW5hLmNvbS9zb2NpYWxnZC8xMDAwMDE2OS8yMDI2MTEwNC80OTgzODQ4Mi5odG1s,WATCH,季節性インフルエンザの早期流行と複数株の共同流行を報告しているが、通常の季節性疾患の注意喚起であり、国際的拡大や渡航制限等の懸念は見られないため、経過観察とする。,Human Infection with Swine Influenza A H3N2; Influenza; Human Infection with Swine Influenza A H1N1; Influenza A; Unknown Encephalitis,People's Republic of China,China CDC Warns: This Year's Influenza Season Is Starting Early! Multiple Strains Are Co-Circulating.,中疾控提醒：今年流感季提前！多毒株共同活跃,2026-11-04T02:53:56+00:00,https://news.china.com/socialgd/10000169/20261104/49838482.html,CHINESE,humans,"China's CDC reports the autumn-winter influenza season has begun in China, with multiple strains co-circulating. Influenza A H3N2 accounts for about 70% of positive samples, and A(H1N1) about 30%. The season features multi-strain activity and an earlier peak. Distinguishing influenza from the common cold is crucial: influenza onset is abrupt with high fever and systemic symptoms, whereas the cold has gradual onset with nasal symptoms; flu typically lasts 7–10 days and is more severe. High-risk groups include children, adults aged 65 and older, pregnant and postpartum women, people with chronic diseases, and the immunocompromised. Possible complications include pneumonia; severe cough, chest tightness, and dyspnea; children may develop encephalitis; young adults may experience myocarditis after fatigue or lack of sleep; elderly may show appetite loss and confusion. Cross-protection between strains is weak; infection with one strain does not preclude others. Sequential infections (H3N2 followed by H1N1) are possible; maintain protective measures through fall and winter.",No,No,No,No,0,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,No,4,Yes,Yes,No,季節性インフルエンザの通常の流行パターンの一環と考えられるが、流行開始の早期化と複数株共存、小児脳炎等の合併症言及があるため、重症化動向を注視する必要がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9jb25nbHkudm4vZGEtbmFuZy10YW5nLWN1b25nLXBob25nLWNob25nLXNvdC14dWF0LWh1eWV0LTU0NjA5MC5odG1s,WATCH,ベトナム・ダナン市で季節性デング熱が前年比2.5倍に増加し地域的な対策強化が行われているが、重症度や国際的拡大の情報はなく、現時点では地方自治体が通常の対応を実施している段階。,Dengue,Da Nang; Thành Phố Đà Nẵng; Socialist Republic of Vietnam,Da Nang strengthens dengue fever prevention and control,"Đà Nẵng tăng cường phòng, chống sốt xuất huyết",2026-11-04T01:25:01+00:00,https://congly.vn/da-nang-tang-cuong-phong-chong-sot-xuat-huyet-546090.html,VIETNAMESE,humans; vectors; environment,"Dengue fever in Da Nang, Vietnam, is rising. In the week 19–25 October 2026, 720 cases were reported (23.5 per 100,000). From January 1 to 25 October, total cases reached 6,338 (206.7 per 100,000), up 2.5 times versus 2025, with 464 outbreaks, up 4.3 times. In the last four weeks, 2,377 cases were concentrated in wards Ngũ Hành Sơn (224), An Khê (167), Sơn Trà (119), Điện Bàn Bắc (112), and Điện Bàn Đông (106), showing spatial heterogeneity. On 2 November 2026, Da Nang issued Directive 11383/UBND-SYT mandating local authorities to assume responsibility and implement dengue measures. Focus is on eliminating larval breeding sites lăng quăng and bọ gậy, supported by the Fatherland Front, youth, women, and health workers. Frequency depends on risk: high-risk areas weekly; high indices twice weekly; others monthly. Inspections of homes, yards, and water-holding items (tires, boxes, buckets, basins) are emphasized, with strengthened surveillance and treatment capacity.",不明,No,No,No,0,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,No,3,不明,Yes,No,ダナン市当局が指令（Directive 11383/UBND-SYT）を発出し、ボウフラ駆除など地域主体の対策を実施中。死亡者数や重症例の報告はなく、国際的拡大の兆候もないため現時点ではフルRRAの必要性は低いが、感染者数の急増傾向は継続監視が望ましい。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYWluZG9uZXNpYS5jb20vbnVzYW50YXJhLzk1MjA5MS9jZWdhaC1wZW51bGFyYW4tdHViZXJrdWxvc2lzLXBhZGFuZy1zaWFwa2FuLTI0Mi1sb2thc2ktcGVtZXJpa3NhYW4tZGktMTA0LWtlbHVyYWhhbg==,DISMISS,既知の風土病である結核に対する通常の公衆衛生対応（接触者追跡・検診強化）であり、異常性や国際的拡大リスクは認められない。,Tuberculosis,Padang; Provinsi Sumatera Barat; Republic of Indonesia,"Prevent TB Transmission, Padang Prepares 242 TB Screening Locations in 104 Urban Villages.","Cegah Penularan Tuberkulosis, Padang Siapkan 242 Lokasi Pemeriksaan di 104 Kelurahan",2026-11-04T03:08:52+00:00,https://mediaindonesia.com/nusantara/952091/cegah-penularan-tuberkulosis-padang-siapkan-242-lokasi-pemeriksaan-di-104-kelurahan,INDONESIAN,humans,"Padang City Health Office intensifies tuberculosis case finding through mass contact tracing across 104 urban villages (kelurahan) and sets up 242 screening sites through mid-November 2026. Each site is expected to screen about 100 people—including family, neighbors, coworkers, and schoolmates of confirmed TB patients. The program starts from confirmed TB cases, with health workers tracing contacts to identify those potentially exposed. Field operations involve sub-district administrations and local health cadres to reach high-risk groups. Screened individuals undergo initial evaluation; those with symptoms or suspected infection proceed to sputum testing for diagnosis. Positive cases receive prompt treatment; those testing negative receive education on transmission prevention and proper cough etiquette. Expanded early detection aims to shorten delays in treatment and curb TB transmission, with public participation encouraged.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,地方保健当局による通常の結核対策プログラムの告知記事であり、新規アウトブレイクや異常事態を示すものではない。,
