aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZGlhcmlvZGVjdWlhYmEuY29tLmJyL2NpZGFkZXMvY3VpYWJhLXNlLWFwcm94aW1hLWRlLW1pbC1jYXNvcy1kZS1kZW5ndWUtZW0tMjAyNi83NjE3NDU=,DISMISS,デング熱・チクングニア熱は例年ブラジルで季節的に発生しており、前年比微増(4.2%)で死亡例もなく、異常性・重症度・社会的関心の高まりは確認できない。,Zika; Chikungunya; Dengue,Mato Grosso; Cuiabá; Federative Republic of Brazil,"Cuiabá nears 1,000 dengue cases in 2026.",Cuiabá se aproxima de mil casos de dengue em 2026,2026-11-04T04:00:21+00:00,https://www.diariodecuiaba.com.br/cidades/cuiaba-se-aproxima-de-mil-casos-de-dengue-em-2026/761745,PORTUGUESE,humans; vectors; environment,"As of epidemiological week 42 (week ending Oct 29, 2026), Cuiabá, Brazil, reports 931 locally acquired dengue cases in 2026, nearing 1,000 and up 4.2% from the same period in 2025. Six new dengue cases were confirmed in week 42, with 41 earlier records added to the annual total. Autochthonous chikungunya totals reach 65; no chikungunya deaths; no new Zika cases that week and no Zika deaths this year. Dengue, chikungunya, and Zika are transmitted by Aedes aegypti. Dengue symptoms include high fever, muscle and head pain, retro-orbital pain, and rash; warning signs such as intense abdominal pain, persistent vomiting, bleeding, and dizziness require urgent medical evaluation. Prevention emphasizes eliminating indoor breeding sites, with ~80% of foci found inside homes. Residents should inspect yards, keep water tanks covered, clean gutters, and remove water-holding containers like tires and bottles. Health teams have conducted 958,373 environmental inspections, treating 100,614 properties, 114,317 deposits, and eliminating 29,015 potential breeding sites; continued community participation is essential.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,No,No,No,流行は媒介蚊により継続中だが、症例増加率は小幅で死亡例なし。地方行政による通常の防疫活動が報告されているのみ。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmV3aW5kaWFuZXhwcmVzcy5jb20vY2l0aWVzL2JodWJhbmVzd2FyLzIwMjYvTm92LzA0L2phdW5kaWNlLXNjYXJlLWF0LXV0a2FsLXVuaXZlcnNpdHktYXMtMTItc3R1ZGVudHMtdGVzdC1wb3NpdGl2ZS1mb3ItaGVwYXRpdGlzLWE=,WATCH,大学キャンパス内の限定的なA型肝炎集団発生で、当局による対応（水質検査・衛生啓発・隔離等）が進行中だが、国際的拡大リスクは低く、続報を注視する段階。,Hepatitis A,Bhubaneshwar; State of Odisha; Republic of India,,Jaundice scare at Utkal University as 12 students test positive for Hepatitis A,2026-11-04T04:07:39+00:00,https://www.newindianexpress.com/cities/bhubaneswar/2026/Nov/04/jaundice-scare-at-utkal-university-as-12-students-test-positive-for-hepatitis-a,ENGLISH,humans; environment,"Hepatitis A triggers a jaundice outbreak at Utkal University in Bhubaneswar, with 12 of 19 samples testing positive. Infection may stem from contaminated food or water; campus water samples are being tested, and officials also suspect campus feasts during recent elections. After two initial cases among Girls' Hostel 7 boarders, who are hospitalized, the university postponed mid-semester exams and intensified hostel screening while banning street food on campus. Registrar Swati Mishra said a university team is inspecting hostels and coordinating with health authorities under close surveillance. Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation’s Urban Surveillance Unit collected water and blood samples, and conducted awareness on hand hygiene, safe drinking water, and sanitation. Preventive measures include cleaning more than 10 water tanks, opening a control room, a pharmacy and public health facility; 1,500 litres of drinking water is being supplied, and students are advised to drink boiled water.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,Yes,Yes,No,単一大学キャンパス内での局地的な水系感染症アウトブレイクであり、地方自治体（Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation）が主体的に対応中。重症例や死亡の報告はなく、現時点では国際的な公衆衛生上の脅威とは評価されない。,
