aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc2F0aHlhbW9ubGluZS5jb20vbmV3cy9uZXdzLWtlcmFsYW0va290dGF5YW0tMTI3ODE2Mzg=,PICKUP,ケララ州でデング熱の確定例・死亡例が前年を上回るペースで増加しており、持続的な降雨によるベクター媒介リスクの継続とともに公衆衛生上の懸念が高まっているため。,Dengue,State of Kerala; Republic of India,"Dengue fever cases and the death rate are rising in the state; the number of people seeking treatment with symptoms is also increasing. Dengue fever has been confirmed in 13,108 people in the state this year. 44 people have died.","സംസ്ഥാനത്ത് ഡെങ്കിപ്പനി ബാധയും മരണ നിരക്കും ഉയരുന്നു; രോഗലക്ഷണങ്ങളോടെ ചികിത്സ തേടുന്നവരുടെ എണ്ണത്തിലും വർധനവ്. 13,108 പേർക്കാണ് സംസ്ഥാനത്ത് ഈ വർഷം ഡെങ്കിപ്പനി സ്ഥിരീകരിച്ചത്. 44 പേർ മരണപ്പെടുകയും ചെയ്തു",2026-11-04T04:16:53+00:00,https://www.sathyamonline.com/news/news-keralam/kottayam-12781638,MALAYALAM,humans; vectors; environment,"As of October 30, 2026, dengue fever has been confirmed in 13,108 people across the state, with 44 deaths attributed to dengue and a rising number of people seeking treatment for dengue-like symptoms, including in Kottayam district. The year 2026 surpasses 2025, which had 10,909 confirmed cases. Suspected dengue cases reached 35,192 by Oct 30, 2026, up from 29,060 in 2025, with suspected dengue deaths at 35 this year (versus 6 last year). Intermittent rains have persisted, creating standing water that sustains mosquito breeding. Health authorities urge intensified cleaning and vector-control measures to curb larval growth. Given ongoing rainfall, the public should eliminate stagnant water and promptly seek care at health facilities for fever or dengue-like symptoms rather than self-treat.",Yes,No,No,No,1,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,デング熱はケララ州で毎年季節的に発生する疾患だが、今年は確定症例数・死亡者数ともに前年（2025年）を上回っており、継続的な降雨によるベクター発生リスクが指摘されている。国際的拡大・渡航制限のリスクは低いが、州内の公衆衛生対応強化が求められる状況。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hMS5yby9uZXdzL3NvY2lhbC9yZWd1bGktbm9pLXBlbnRydS1wYXNhZ2VyaWktY2FyZS1jYWxhdG9yZXNjLWluLXN1YS1wZS1mb25kdWwtcmlzY3VsdWktZGUtZWJvbGEtZGVjbGFyYXRpYS1jYXJlLWxpLXNlLWNlcmUtaW5haW50ZS1kZS1pbWJhcmNhcmUtaWQxMTY1OTM0Lmh0bWw=,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国でのエボラ出血熱流行を受け、米国が入国時に渡航歴申告を義務化するなど、国際的な渡航制限措置が実施されており、IHR基準に複数該当する。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States; Romania,"New rules for passengers traveling to the United States, amid the Ebola risk? The declaration required before boarding.","Reguli noi pentru pasagerii care călătoresc în SUA, pe fondul riscului de Ebola? Declarația care li se cere înainte de îmbarcare",2026-11-04T05:30:00+00:00,https://a1.ro/news/social/reguli-noi-pentru-pasagerii-care-calatoresc-in-sua-pe-fondul-riscului-de-ebola-declaratia-care-li-se-cere-inainte-de-imbarcare-id1165934.html,ROMANIAN,humans,"New pre-boarding declaration required for all passengers traveling to the United States amid the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC). Travelers must sign a declaration stating they were not present in the DRC in the 21 days before their flight; transit through a DRC airport also counts. The rule applies regardless of citizenship, including Americans returning home. Those who refuse to sign will not be allowed to board. Airlines must retain the completed documents for at least 42 days after arrival. The declaration is an official confirmation of the traveler's information; deliberate false statements can carry legal penalties. The 21‑day window matches Ebola's maximum incubation period. Some airlines (e.g., Delta) use electronic systems, while others (e.g., KLM) provide paper forms at the airport. Romanians traveling to the U.S. should check with their carrier, as forms may be online or on paper.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,記事はコンゴ民主共和国でのエボラ出血熱流行を受けた米国の渡航対策（搭乗前申告義務化）に関するもの。米国・ルーマニアは発生国ではなく、渡航規制の実施・情報提供先として言及されているのみのため対象国から除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9qYWJhci5pZG50aW1lcy5jb20vbmV3cy9qYXdhLWJhcmF0LzkwLXBlcnNlbi1haXItYmFrdS1kaS1rb3RhLWJhbmR1bmctZGlkdWdhLXRlcmNlbWFyLWJha3RlcmktZS1jb2xpLTAwLTl5N3lsLTB2bXMzOQ==,WATCH,実際の感染症症例報告ではなく河川の水質汚染に関する環境・衛生インフラの懸念記事であるが、下痢症等の感染症リスクにつながる可能性があるため経過観察とする。,Tuberculosis; E. coli,Jawa Barat; Bandung; Republic of Indonesia,Drinking Water in Bandung City Allegedly Contaminated with Escherichia coli,Air Baku di Kota Bandung Diduga Tercemar Bakteri E-coli,2026-11-04T04:30:16+00:00,https://jabar.idntimes.com/news/jawa-barat/90-persen-air-baku-di-kota-bandung-diduga-tercemar-bakteri-e-coli-00-9y7yl-0vms39,INDONESIAN,humans; environment,"Bandung City is reviewing raw-water quality after suspected Escherichia coli (E. coli) contamination. An NGO monitoring Bandung rivers reported E. coli levels near 90% in several waterways. Mayor Muhammad Farhan seeks data confirmation but warns that sanitation-related pollution threatens public health, especially children. The issue stems from households discharging human waste into rivers; of about 600,000 homes near riverbanks, roughly 200,000 lack septic tanks. If unresolved, contamination could compromise drinking-water safety and child health, including diarrhea—dangerous for infants under two months—and potentially affect growth and immune development, with TB vulnerability noted. DLHK Bandung’s 2024 measurements show Sungai Cikapundung’s water quality index below 50, making river water unfit for consumption and not suitable for children’s play, underscoring the need for sanitation infrastructure improvements.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,不明,2,Yes,Yes,No,記事は実際の感染症発生ではなく、河川水質汚染（大腸菌検出）による衛生インフラ不足の懸念を報じたもの。具体的な症例数・死亡者数の報告はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hbGxhZnJpY2EuY29tL3N0b3JpZXMvMjAyNjExMDQwMDk4Lmh0bWw=,PICKUP,エボラ出血熱がDRC国内で8番目の州に拡大しており、深刻な公衆衛生上の影響と国際支援の必要性が明確であるため、フルリスク評価に進むべきシグナルと判断する。,Ebola,Goma; Province du Nord-Kivu; Isiro; Ituri; Bunia; Democratic Republic of the Congo,,"Congo-Kinshasa: Ebola Spreads to Eighth DRC Province As WFP Delivers Food, Builds Treatment Centres and Keeps Supplies Moving",2026-11-04T05:13:22+00:00,https://allafrica.com/stories/202611040098.html,ENGLISH,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, Ebola has spread to the eighth province of the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC). WFP coordinates food and logistics to support patients, families and health teams amid insecurity and poor roads. The six‑month plan provides dry rations for over 500,000 relatives and hot meals for affected households. WFP has delivered 744,000 hot meals in 59 facilities and moved over 3,000 metric tons of food to families. UNHAS has flown 1,255 flights, carrying 10,272 responders and 483 metric tons of cargo. The Logistics Cluster runs bases in Isiro and across Ituri and Haut‑Uélé, storing 3,417 metric tons for 43 partners and delivering 2,653 metric tons by air/road. Musienene hosts the first ETC; Bunia’s is under construction; four more ETCs, including one in Goma, are planned. WFP seeks USD 214 million, including USD 78.6 million for meals. Challenges: insecurity, roads, weather; funding needed to sustain containment.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はDRC国内でのエボラ拡大とWFP等の人道支援活動に焦点を当てている。治安悪化や道路状況、資金不足が封じ込めの課題として挙げられており、2億1400万ドルの資金要請がなされている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmFpZHVuaWEuY29tL21hZGh5YS1wcmFkZXNoL3NhdG5hLXNhdG5hLW1hbi13aG8tcmV0dXJuZWQtZnJvbS1wdW5lLWRpZXMtb2YtZGVuZ3VlLXByZWduYW50LXdpZmUtYWxzby1pbmZlY3RlZC04NDc0NTMz,DISMISS,単発の個別症例報告であり、地域的拡大や異常性を示す情報もなく、デング熱はインドで季節的に発生する既知の風土病であるため、社会的関心や国際的懸念も低いと判断される。,Malaria; Dengue,State of Mahārāshtra; Madhya Pradesh; Rewa; Pune; Satna; Republic of India,Satna man who returned from Pune dies of dengue fever; his pregnant wife is also infected; notices issued to two pathology operators.,"पुणे से लौटे सतना के युवक की डेंगू से मौत, गर्भवती पत्नी भी संक्रमित; दो पैथोलॉजी संचालकों को नोटिस",2026-11-04T06:03:08+00:00,https://www.naidunia.com/madhya-pradesh/satna-satna-man-who-returned-from-pune-dies-of-dengue-pregnant-wife-also-infected-8474533,HINDI,humans,"Dengue fever case in Satna, Madhya Pradesh: A 30-year-old Rajesh Kori alias Bunakar, a Siddharth Nagar resident, died of dengue after returning from Pune on Oct 29 with his seven-month pregnant wife Priyanka, who also tested dengue-positive. The Malaria Department reports that Rajesh’s antigen test was conducted at Vidya Pathology and Priyanka’s at Central Pathology; both were positive for dengue, but the health department was not informed. Rajesh, admitted to a district hospital, had dengue confirmed and was also diagnosed with kidney stones; he died while being transported to Rewa Medical College on Nov 1. Health authorities plan action after replies; it is mandatory to log dengue cases on the IHI portal. A six-member Malaria team found no dengue larvae at their Siddharth Nagar residence; temephos was sprayed in the drain and parathram in the house. Priyanka’s treatment requires careful monitoring; five family members will be ELISA-tested.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,地元保健当局（マラリア部門）が既に対応（幼虫調査、消毒薬散布、家族のELISA検査）しており、地域的な集団発生の兆候は報告されていない。デング熱届出未遂に関する行政的な問題（病理検査施設への通知）が中心の記事。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubWF0aWNob24uY28udGgvbG9jYWwvcXVhbGl0eS1saWZlL25ld3NfNTk2MDU1MQ==,WATCH,タイでのエムポックス累計症例（470例、死亡3例）やWHOの世界的流行状況を伝える内容だが、新規の異常な増加や重症化傾向を示す情報はなく、既存の継続的流行の経過報告・医療ガイダンスに留まるため、フルRRAには至らず経過観察が妥当。,Mpox; Mpox Clade I; Mpox Clade II,Kingdom of Thailand,Monkeypox: No hospitalization required for every case! Doctor says you can isolate at home; urges prompt testing if you notice a rash or lesions.,ฝีดาษวานรไม่ต้องนอน รพ.ทุกราย! หมอชี้แยกกักตัวที่บ้านได้ ย้ำพบผื่น-ตุ่มรีบตรวจ,2026-11-04T05:59:02+00:00,https://www.matichon.co.th/local/quality-life/news_5960551,THAI,humans,"Monkeypox in Thailand totals 470 confirmed cases and 3 deaths as of 31 October 2026, with ongoing global transmission. WHO data reported 68,096 confirmed cases and 272 deaths across 107 countries from 1 January 2025 to 31 August 2026. Most patients recover with symptomatic care; hospitalization is not required for every case, and home isolation is advised for those who can be adequately separated and monitored. Early symptoms include fever, headache, and lymphadenopathy, followed by a skin rash or vesiculopustular lesions that can appear on the body, face, genitals, or anal region; some patients have only a few lesions. Diagnosis relies on PCR testing of lesion material; routine blood tests are not confirmatory. Prevention focuses on avoiding direct contact with lesions, not sharing personal items, and practicing hand hygiene and masking during care. Prompt testing after suspicious rash aids timely management.",No,No,Yes,不明,1,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,不明,No,記事はタイ国内のエムポックス累計データと一般的な医療ガイダンス（自宅隔離可能、PCR検査推奨等）を伝える内容で、新規アウトブレイクや急増を示す情報は含まれていない。既存の継続監視対象としてWATCHと判断。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmV3c3J1LmNvLmlsL2hlYWx0aC80bm92MjAyNi9lYm9sYTMwOC5odG1s,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ出血熱の発生を受け、米国が入国制限措置（健康申告義務）を実施しており、渡航制限リスクとIHR複数基準に該当するためフルRRAへ進むべき。,Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States,"Due to Ebola fever, passengers flying to the United States are required to fill out a health declaration form.","Из-за лихорадки Эбола пассажиры, вылетающие в США, обязаны заполнить декларацию о состоянии здоровья",2026-11-04T06:22:41+00:00,https://www.newsru.co.il/health/4nov2026/ebola308.html,RUSSIAN,humans,"From November 3, 2026, all passengers flying to the United States must complete and sign a health declaration before boarding, prompted by an Ebola fever outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. Issued by the U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, the rule applies to everyone, regardless of citizenship, departure country, or prior Africa travel. Passengers must confirm they have not been in the DRC within the previous 21 days; time spent in a Congolese airport during a layover counts as being there, while transiting over Congo without entry does not. The requirement also applies to transit passengers routing through the U.S. to other destinations. Those who have been in the DRC within 21 days must wait 21 days after leaving before flying. Airlines are responsible for enforcement; those without a declaration will be denied boarding, and false statements carry criminal penalties. Declarations are integrated into online check-in; minors sign via a guardian. It does not replace visas or ESTA. Valid until December 18, 2026, unless extended.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,米国は対象国リストに含まれないため除外。発生地域としてUnited StatesとAfrica大陸も付与されているが、実際の感染症発生国はDRCのみであり、米国は渡航制限措置の実施国として言及されているに過ぎない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYWdlbmNlZWNvZmluLmNvbS9hY3R1YWxpdGVzLzA0MTEtMTQzMDczLXphbWJpZS0yMTMtbWlsbGlvbnMtcG91ci1jb25zdHJ1aXJlLWxhLXByZW1pZXJlLXVzaW5lLWRlLXZhY2NpbnMtY29udHJlLWxlLWNob2xlcmE=,PICKUP,"ザンビアで2026年にコレラ流行が悪化し7州で1,958例・40死亡、南部アフリカ地域でも4,320例・56死亡と拡大しており、IHR基準の深刻性・国際拡大の観点で該当するためフルRRAへの移行を推奨する。",Cholera,Lusaka; Lusaka Province; Republic of Zambia,Zambia: $213 million to build the first cholera vaccine factory.,Zambie : 213 millions $ pour construire la première usine de vaccins contre le choléra,2026-11-04T06:24:38+00:00,https://www.agenceecofin.com/actualites/0411-143073-zambie-213-millions-pour-construire-la-premiere-usine-de-vaccins-contre-le-cholera,FRENCH,humans; environment,"Cholera outbreak in Zambia worsened in 2026 with 1,958 cases, 303 confirmed, and 40 deaths across seven provinces as of November 2, 2026. Regional data show five Southern African countries reporting 4,320 cases and 56 deaths from January 1 to February 15, 2026, linked to floods, displacement, and limited water and sanitation. Zambia’s Industrial Development Corporation (IDC) and China’s Jijia International Medical Technology have formed ZAMVAX Limited to develop a cholera vaccine manufacturing plant in the Lusaka-South Special Economic Zone. Total project investment is about $213 million; an initial $24.13 million will establish an oral cholera vaccine filling/packaging unit, with a planned capacity of 20 million doses per year (half for Zambia, half for export, subject to regulatory approvals). IDC will hold 60% and Jijia 40%. Preparatory work will take place over the next 12 months; no commercial production date announced. Long-term plans include pediatric and veterinary vaccines, contingent on feasibility, funding, and approvals, expanding a 2024 agreement for a smaller facility.",Yes,不明,Yes,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,不明,Yes,Yes,記事は主にザンビアと中国企業によるコレラワクチン工場建設計画を報じているが、背景情報としてザンビア及び南部アフリカ地域での深刻なコレラ流行状況（洪水・衛生環境悪化に起因）が含まれている。中国はワクチン製造の事業パートナーとして言及されているのみで、感染症の発生国ではないためverified_locationsから除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9wYXB1YXRlbmdhaC5hbnRhcmFuZXdzLmNvbS9iZXJpdGEvOTE2NzkvYmFsYWkta2FyYW50aW5hLW11c25haGthbi1heWFtLXRhbnBhLWRva3VtZW4tY2VnYWgtcGVudWxhcmFuLXZpcnVzLWRpLW1hbm9rd2FyaQ==,DISMISS,鶏の感染確認報告はなく、書類不備の鶏の予防的処分という行政措置に関する記事であり、実際の鳥インフルエンザ発生・感染拡大の証拠がないため見送りとする。,Human Infection with Avian Influenza; Avian Influenza,Manokwari; Provinsi Papua Barat,Quarantine Office destroys chickens without documents to prevent virus transmission in Manokwari - ANTARA News Central Papua,Balai Karantina musnahkan ayam tanpa dokumen cegah penularan virus di Manokwari - ANTARA News Papua Tengah,2026-11-04T06:33:47+00:00,https://papuatengah.antaranews.com/berita/91679/balai-karantina-musnahkan-ayam-tanpa-dokumen-cegah-penularan-virus-di-manokwari,INDONESIAN,animals,"On 4 November 2026, in Manokwari, West Papua, the Quarantine Office for Animals, Fish and Plants (BKHIT Papua Barat) destroyed ten chickens that entered the area without official documents to prevent avian influenza transmission. BKHIT official Suryatmoko RH Putro said the health status of the birds was unknown due to missing documents from the place of origin, posing a risk. The birds were seized after PT Pelni ship security reported finding ten chickens without documents during passenger-ticket checks before docking at Manokwari Port; with no owner reported, the seized birds were slated for destruction three working days after seizure. The action follows Bupati Manokwari Instruction 07/INS/Bup/Mkw/2004 banning shipment of adult poultry, poultry meat, and eggs from areas infected with avian influenza. Provincial rules also restrict entry of certain animals and products into Papua Barat; only day-old chicks and poultry products with proper documents are allowed.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,不明,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,記事は鳥インフルエンザの実際の発生ではなく、書類不備の鶏の検疫・予防的処分に関する行政対応の報告。感染確認事例なし。,
aHR0cHM6Ly90YW1pbC5hYnBsaXZlLmNvbS9uZXdzL3RhbWlsLW5hZHUvdGhlYXRlcnMtYW5kLWZhY3Rvcmllcy1pbi1uYWdhaS1oYXZlLWJlY29tZS1icmVlZGluZy1ncm91bmRzLWZvci1kZW5ndWUtY2FycnlpbmctbW9zcXVpdG9lcy10aGUtaGVhbHRoLWRlcGFydG1lbnQtaGFzLXRha2VuLXN3aWZ0LWFjdGlvbi1ieS1pbXA=,DISMISS,デング熱媒介蚊の発生源に対する通常の行政的取締り・罰金事例であり、症例急増や異常な流行拡大の報告はなく、公衆衛生上の重大な懸念は認められない。,Dengue,Nagapattinam; State of Tamil Nādu; Republic of India,"Theatres and factories in Nagai have become breeding grounds for dengue mosquitoes: Health Department imposes Rs. 11,500 fine.","நாகையில் டெங்கு கொசுக்களின் புகலிடமாக மாறிய தியேட்டர், தொழிற்சாலைகள்: ரூ.11,500 அபராதம் விதித்து சுகாதாரத்துறை அதிரடி!",2026-11-04T06:24:13+00:00,https://tamil.abplive.com/news/tamil-nadu/theaters-and-factories-in-nagai-have-become-breeding-grounds-for-dengue-carrying-mosquitoes-the-health-department-has-taken-swift-action-by-imposing-a-fine-of-rs-11-500-tnn-278891,TAMIL,environment; humans; vectors,"Nagapattinam, Tamil Nadu faces dengue risk after health officials found Aedes mosquito larvae breeding in stagnant water inside a private cinema theatre, an ice plant, several factories, and a lathe workshop within Nagapattinam Municipality. Under the Tamil Nadu Public Health Act 1939, authorities levied a total fine of Rs 11,500: cinema Rs 5,000; ice plant Rs 5,000; factory Rs 1,000; lathe workshop Rs 500. Aedes, the dengue vector, is described as biting during the day. Preventive actions include removing standing water, cleaning waste such as old tires and plastic containers, covering water storage tanks, and maintaining clean surroundings. Dengue prevention and awareness drives are being intensified in Nagapattinam, with warnings of further action if violations persist. The investigation underscores shared responsibility of businesses and the public to maintain hygiene to curb dengue transmission.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,記事は蚊の繁殖地に対する罰金執行という日常的な公衆衛生対策の報道であり、デング熱症例数や流行状況についての具体的データは含まれていない。,
aHR0cDovL2hlYWx0aC5jbndlc3QuY29tL2prc2gvYS8yMDI2LzExLzA0LzIzNDY2NTUyLmh0bWw=,DISMISS,西安市内の幼稚園における季節性の一般的な小児感染症（手足口病・ノロウイルス・水痘）に関する啓発記事であり、異常性や国際的拡大リスクは認められない。,Norovirus; Enterovirus 71; Foot And Mouth Disease; Varicella,Shaanxi; Xi’an; People's Republic of China,"In autumn and winter, infectious diseases are on the rise; protect children's health.",秋冬季传染病高发，守护好孩子健康,2026-11-04T06:28:03+00:00,http://health.cnwest.com/jksh/a/2026/11/04/23466552.html,CHINESE,humans,"Autumn–winter rises in infectious diseases in Xi’an. Hand, foot and mouth disease (HFMD), norovirus, and varicella (chickenpox) are entering peak periods. At a Huyi District Sunshine Kindergarten, health staff and clinicians from Xi’an Children’s Hospital and Xi’an Jiaotong University Second Affiliated Hospital outlined prevention and control. HFMD mostly affects children under five (peaking at ages 2–3); transmission is primarily fecal–oral with additional droplet and contact routes. Contagiousness is strongest in the first week. An EV71 vaccine (6 months–5 years) reduces severe disease; two doses before 12 months are encouraged. Control measures include frequent handwashing, disinfection, and isolating cases until symptoms resolve for about a week. Norovirus, highly infectious in schools, spreads via contaminated food/water and vomitus aerosols; no vaccine; management is rehydration and isolation until 72 hours after symptom resolution. Varicella spreads via droplets; vaccination remains key; infected students stay home and return with medical clearance after crusting.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,No,No,季節性の流行期における予防啓発記事であり、特定のアウトブレイクや異常事態を報告するものではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9mci5hZnJpY2FuZXdzLmNvbS8yMDI2LzExLzA0L2Vib2xhLWxlcy12b3lhZ2V1cnMtdmVycy1sZXMtZXRhdHMtdW5pcy1kZXZyb250LWRlc29ybWFpcy1yZW1wbGlyLXVuZS1kZWNsYXJhdGlvbi1zYW5pdGFpci8=,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラアウトブレイクを受け、米国が入国制限・健康申告義務化などの渡航制限措置を講じており、IHR基準の複数（深刻性・国際的拡大懸念・渡航制限）に該当するため。,Ebola,Georgia; Virginia; Atlanta; New York; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States; Republic of Uganda; Republic of the Sudan,Ebola: Travelers to the United States will now have to fill out a health declaration.,Ebola : les voyageurs vers les États-Unis devront désormais remplir une déclaration sanitaire,2026-11-04T06:47:15+00:00,https://fr.africanews.com/2026/11/04/ebola-les-voyageurs-vers-les-etats-unis-devront-desormais-remplir-une-declaration-sanitair/,FRENCH,humans,"From November 3, 2026 at 23:59 EST, all passengers on international flights to the United States, including transit, must sign a CDC health attestation before boarding, confirming they have not traveled to the Democratic Republic of the Congo in the prior 21 days. Airlines may deny boarding without it. The requirement applies to commercial, private, and general aviation; minors or those unable to sign may be represented. It coincides with an Ebola outbreak in the DRC; no U.S. cases detected, and population risk deemed low. Foreign nationals who recently traveled to Uganda or South Sudan remain barred from entry; U.S. citizens returning from those countries may be admitted but must undergo health screening at designated airports (Washington Dulles, Atlanta, JFK). Attestations must be kept for 42 days and provided upon request. The measure is temporary through December 18, 2026, unless extended.",Yes,No,Yes,Yes,3,No,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,3,Yes,Yes,不明,記事の主題はDRCでのエボラアウトブレイクに対する米国の渡航対応措置。米国・ウガンダ・南スーダン・ジョージア州・バージニア州・アトランタ・ニューヨークは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。DRCでの感染状況の詳細（症例数、死亡者数等）は本文に記載がなく不明。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZWNvZmluYWdlbmN5LmNvbS9uZXdzLWZpbmFuY2VzLzA0MTEtNjA0NTYtemFtYmlhLXBsYW5zLTIxMy1taWxsaW9uLWNob2xlcmEtdmFjY2luZS1wbGFudC13aXRoLWNoaW5lc2UtcGFydG5lcg==,PICKUP,"ザンビアで7州にわたり1,958例（40死亡）のコレラアウトブレイクが継続中であり、南部アフリカ地域全体でも拡大（4,320例・56死亡）している。深刻な公衆衛生影響と地域的拡大リスクがありIHR基準を複数満たす。",Cholera,Lusaka; Lusaka Province; Republic of Zambia,,Zambia Plans $213 Million Cholera Vaccine Plant With Chinese Partner,2026-11-04T06:51:45+00:00,https://www.ecofinagency.com/news-finances/0411-60456-zambia-plans-213-million-cholera-vaccine-plant-with-chinese-partner,ENGLISH,humans; environment,"Zambia plans its first cholera vaccine manufacturing facility via ZAMVAX Limited, a joint venture between IDC (60%) and Jijia International Medical Technology (40%). Total investment is $213 million, with about $24.13 million in the first phase to build an oral cholera vaccine filling and packaging plant in Lusaka South Multi-Facility Economic Zone. Target annual capacity: 20 million doses, split 10 million for domestic use and 10 million for export, pending regulatory approvals. Preparatory work will take about 12 months; commercial production start date has not been announced. The project follows a cholera outbreak in Zambia declared July 28, 2026; by Nov 2, 2026, 1,958 cases (303 confirmed), and 40 deaths across seven provinces. Regional data show 4,320 cases and 56 deaths across five Southern African countries Jan–Feb 2026. The venture could later expand to pediatric and veterinary vaccines, subject to feasibility and approvals.",Yes,不明,Yes,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"記事の主題は新規ワクチン製造施設建設計画だが、背景として7月28日宣言のコレラアウトブレイクの最新状況（7州、1,958例、40死亡）および南部アフリカ地域全体の流行状況（5か国で4,320例、56死亡）が報告されており、公衆衛生上重要な情報を含む。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGhlYmFuZ2tva2luc2lnaHQuY29tL25ld3MvbGlmZXN0eWxlL3dlbGxuZXNzLzE3MTY2MTMv,DISMISS,季節性RSVの通常の疫学報告であり、公衆衛生上の異常性や国際的拡大リスクは認められず、社会的関心の高まりも確認できない。,Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV) Infection,Kingdom of Thailand,RSV cases surge 30%; not just a children's disease—elderly at risk of severe pneumonia,เตือน RSV ผู้ป่วยพุ่ง 30% ย้ำไม่ใช่แค่โรคเด็ก ผู้สูงอายุเสี่ยงปอดอักเสบรุนแรง - The Bangkok Insight,2026-11-04T06:45:55+00:00,https://www.thebangkokinsight.com/news/lifestyle/wellness/1716613/,THAI,humans,"Thailand reports 5,683 RSV cases from Jan 1 to Aug 15, 2026 (8.63 per 100,000), up 30% from the same period in 2025. Disease affects all ages, with 0–4-year-olds having the highest incidence, but elderly (≥60 years) and those with chronic conditions are at risk of severe disease. About 40% of patients require hospitalization; risk factors include age, chronic lung/heart/kidney disease, and immunocompromise. RSV can cause lower respiratory tract infections such as bronchiolitis and pneumonia, presenting initially with fever, cough, and runny nose, potentially leading to dyspnea and hypoxemia; some cases need ICU care or ventilation. There is no RSV-specific antiviral; treatment is supportive. Preventive measures include hand hygiene, masks, and avoiding close contact with the sick. For those aged 50+ or with comorbidities, consult a physician about RSV vaccination (adjuvanted or non-adjuvanted), effective against RSV A and B. Vaccination confusion with pneumococcal vaccines is noted. RSV Awareness Week 2026 highlights these risks in Thailand.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,RSV啓発週間に合わせた季節性感染症の通常の統計報告記事であり、緊急対応を要する内容ではない。,
