aHR0cHM6Ly9lY29ub3RpbWVzLmNvbS9UaGFpbGFuZC1SZXBvcnRzLTQ3MC1NcG94LUNhc2VzLVRocmVlLURlYXRocy1pbi0yMDI2LVRocm91Z2gtT2N0LTMxLTE3NzA1NDA=,WATCH,既知の流行性疾患（Mpox）に関する定期的な症例集計報告であり、新規の異常事態や急激な拡大を示す情報はないが、性的接触を含むヒト-ヒト感染が継続しているため経過観察とする。,Mpox; Mpox Clade I; Mpox Clade II,Kingdom of Thailand,,"Thailand Reports 470 Mpox Cases, Three Deaths in 2026 Through Oct. 31 | EconoTimes",2026-11-04T07:09:26+00:00,https://econotimes.com/Thailand-Reports-470-Mpox-Cases-Three-Deaths-in-2026-Through-Oct-31-1770540,ENGLISH,humans,"Mpox (monkeypox) in Thailand reports 470 cases and 3 deaths in 2026 through Oct 31, per the Department of Disease Control. A Nov 3 notice outlines transmission via close contact with an infected person, contact with contaminated objects, and sexual contact. Individuals with fever or unusual skin lesions, including on the face, genitals, or around the anus, are urged to seek medical assessment and disclose potential exposures to clinicians; prompt evaluation aids care planning and limits transmission. Thailand classifies mpox as a communicable disease under surveillance (Communicable Diseases Act 2015) with a 2022 Ministry of Public Health notification. Globally, WHO’s Sept 14 situation report covers 65,784 confirmed cases and 264 deaths across 105 countries from Jan 1, 2025, to Jul 31, 2026, with moderate public health risk.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,タイ保健省（DDC）による定期的なサーベイランス報告であり、2022年の省令・2015年感染症法に基づく既存の監視体制下での集計。WHOの世界的な中程度リスク評価と整合しており、新規の警戒事態とは言えない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9qYXRlbmcuYW50YXJhbmV3cy5jb20vYmVyaXRhLzY1MjAzOS9rdWR1cy1rb21pdG1lbi10dW50YXNrYW4tdmFrc2luYXNpLTE1MDAtdGVybmFrLXVudHVrLW1lbmNlZ2FoLXBlbnlha2l0LXBtaw==,DISMISS,動物の口蹄疫に関するワクチン接種推進の記事であり、現在ヒトへの影響や新規感染拡大は報告されていない。家畜疾病でありIHR・WPRO基準の該当性は低い。,Foot And Mouth Disease,Provinsi Jawa Tengah; Kudus; Republic of Indonesia,"Kudus commits to completing vaccination of 1,500 livestock to prevent foot-and-mouth disease (FMD).",Kudus komitmen tuntaskan vaksinasi 1.500 ternak untuk mencegah penyakit PMK,2026-11-04T07:06:27+00:00,https://jateng.antaranews.com/berita/652039/kudus-komitmen-tuntaskan-vaksinasi-1500-ternak-untuk-mencegah-penyakit-pmk,INDONESIAN,animals,"Foot-and-mouth disease (FMD), PMK in Indonesian, vaccination effort in Kudus Regency, Central Java, targets 1,500 livestock to complete vaccination this year, on top of 4,500 already vaccinated out of 6,000 planned for cattle and buffalo. With two months remaining, central-government vaccine shipments via the Central Java provincial government are supporting due to stockouts. Local personnel are deployed to accelerate the campaign. There are no current PMK cases, though 24 cattle were previously infected; seven were culled after testing, while the rest recovered with treatment. Farmers are urged to maintain hygiene and immediately isolate any animals showing PMK-like symptoms for prompt care. Arin Nikmah, head of Livestock at Kudus Regency’s Department of Agriculture and Food, emphasizes vigilance as vaccination continues through November 2026.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,家畜（牛・水牛）の口蹄疫に関するワクチン接種キャンペーンの進捗報告。現在新規感染例はなく、公衆衛生上の緊急性は低い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9qYWJhci50cmlidW5uZXdzLmNvbS9tZXRyby1iYW5kdW5nLzExODkwMDIvdGluZ2thdC1wZW5jZW1hcmFuLWJha3RlcmktZWNvbGktZGktc3VuZ2FpLWRpLWJhbmR1bmctY2FwYWktOTAtcGVyc2VuLWZhcmhhbi11bmdrYXAtcGVueWViYWJueWE=,DISMISS,河川の環境衛生問題に関する報道であり、具体的な感染症の集団発生やヒト感染事例の急増は報告されていないため、現時点でシグナルとしての該当性は低い。,Tuberculosis; E. coli,Jawa Barat; Bandung; Republic of Indonesia,"E. coli Bacterial Contamination Level in Bandung's Rivers Reaches 90 Percent, Farhan Reveals the Cause.","Tingkat Pencemaran Bakteri E.coli di Sungai di Bandung Capai 90 Persen, Farhan Ungkap Penyebabnya",2026-11-04T07:04:41+00:00,https://jabar.tribunnews.com/metro-bandung/1189002/tingkat-pencemaran-bakteri-ecoli-di-sungai-di-bandung-capai-90-persen-farhan-ungkap-penyebabnya,INDONESIAN,humans; environment,"As of 4 November 2026, E. coli contamination in Bandung’s rivers reaches almost 90%, according to an NGO report presented to Mayor Muhammad Farhan, prompting official action. The finding raises public health concerns across Bandung, West Java, as E. coli–associated diarrhea endangers residents, especially infants. Farhan attributes pollution to household sanitation gaps, noting that 27% of toilets still discharge directly or lack septic tanks, despite Open Defecation Free (ODF) awareness. The NGO highlighted potential downstream effects: diarrhea in infants under two months can lead to weight loss, weakened immunity, and subsequent stunting and even tuberculosis risk. Bandung City plans to tighten environmental sanitation controls and step up monitoring of refill water depots (galon) to prevent waterborne exposure. The Ministry of Trade reports about 800 refill galon outlets in Bandung meeting health standards, reinforcing ongoing public health measures.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,No,No,1,Yes,Yes,No,本記事は感染症のアウトブレイクではなく、河川の大腸菌汚染という環境衛生問題を扱っている。下痢や結核リスクへの言及はあるが、具体的な症例数や集団発生の報告はない。地方自治体による監視強化の方針が示されている段階。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9pbmsuY29tL2FydGljbGVzLzY3MDAyOC9vaWtvbm9taWtpLWJvaXRoZWlhLWV1cjEwMDAwMC1hcG8tdGluLWt5cHJvLXN0by1rb25na28tZ2lhLXRpLW1haGkta2F0YS10b3ktZW1wb2xh,WATCH,エボラ流行自体は既知の継続事案であり、本記事は国際支援（資金拠出）に関する内容で新規の公衆衛生リスク情報は含まれないが、DRCでのエボラ流行継続状況として経過観察の対象とする。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Cyprus,"Cyprus provides €100,000 in financial aid to Congo to fight Ebola",Οικονομική βοήθεια €100.000 από την Κύπρο στο Κονγκό για τη μάχη κατά του Έμπολα - ink,2026-11-04T07:28:41+00:00,https://ink.com/articles/670028/oikonomiki-boitheia-eur100000-apo-tin-kypro-sto-kongko-gia-ti-mahi-kata-toy-empola,GREEK,humans,"On 4 November 2026, the Cypriot Ministry of Foreign Affairs announced a €100,000 contribution to Ebola response in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, channelled via the World Health Organization and the CyprusAid mechanism to support humanitarian and health efforts addressing the Ebola epidemic there. The ministry described the donation as a practical expression of solidarity with affected populations and reaffirmed Cyprus’s commitment to international efforts to manage humanitarian and health emergencies. The funding highlights ongoing international cooperation to combat Ebola in the DRC and aligns Cyprus with WHO-led containment and response efforts.",不明,No,不明,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,Yes,3,No,Yes,Yes,記事は資金援助に関する報道であり、エボラ流行の最新疫学情報（症例数・死亡数等）は含まれていない。既存のDRCエボラ流行の継続状況確認のため、続報・公式発表の注視が必要。キプロスは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9zdWNraG9lZG9pc29uZy52bi9ob24tNzAwLWNodXllbi1naWEtc2UtdGhhbS1kdS1ob2ktbmdoaS1zb3QteHVhdC1odXlldC1kZW5ndWUtMjAyNi10aHVjLWRheS11bmctZHVuZy1raG9hLWhvYy10cm9uZy1jb25nLXRhYy1waG9uZy1jaG9uZy1kaWNoLWJlbmgtMTY5MjYxMTA0MTQxODQyODQ4Lmh0bQ==,DISMISS,本記事はデング熱対策に関する国際会議の開催案内であり、実際の感染拡大や公衆衛生上の緊急事態を報じるものではない。,Dengue,Hanoi; Thành Phố Hà Nội,"Over 700 experts will attend the Dengue Fever Conference 2026, promoting the application of science in disease prevention and control.","Hơn 700 chuyên gia sẽ tham dự hội nghị sốt xuất huyết Dengue 2026, thúc đẩy ứng dụng khoa học trong công tác phòng chống dịch bệnh",2026-11-04T07:55:00+00:00,https://suckhoedoisong.vn/hon-700-chuyen-gia-se-tham-du-hoi-nghi-sot-xuat-huyet-dengue-2026-thuc-day-ung-dung-khoa-hoc-trong-cong-tac-phong-chong-dich-benh-169261104141842848.htm,VIETNAMESE,humans; vectors; environment,"Dengue fever remains a global public health challenge, including Vietnam, with transmission shaped by climate change and urbanization. The Dengue Summit 2026 in Hanoi on 5–6 November 2026 will host nearly 700 delegates from domestic and international health sectors, including representatives from 34 provincial health departments. The two-day event, organized by Vietnam’s Ministry of Health’s Department of Prevention with Hanoi Medical University and Takeda Vietnam, aims to promote science-based applications, research, and technical exchanges to strengthen dengue prevention, surveillance, vector control, diagnosis, treatment, and outbreak response nationwide. Sessions cover epidemiology, updated treatment guidelines, data sharing, and digital surveillance with early warning, plus risk communication and policy integration. International speakers include Rosana Richtmann (Brazil) on proactive dengue prevention in Brazil’s Expanded Immunization Program; Jarir At Thobari (Indonesia) on integrating health-technology evidence into policy; and Shane Fairlie (WHO) on risk-based communication. Over 60 domestic posters will be presented at Lotte Hanoi Hotel.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,記事はベトナム・ハノイで開催されるデング熱対策国際会議の案内であり、具体的な感染事例や流行状況の報告ではないため、対象国での実際の発生イベントとしては扱わない。ブラジル・インドネシアは講演者の出身国として言及されているのみで、当該国での発生報告ではない。,
