aHR0cHM6Ly9jeXBydXMtbWFpbC5jb20vMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9jeXBydXMtZG9uYXRlcy10by13aG8tZWJvbGEtY2FtcGFpZ24=,PICKUP,"DRCでのエボラ出血熱アウトブレイクは感染者1万人超、死者5,100人超と史上2番目の規模であり、公衆衛生上深刻かつ異常事態と判断されるためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Cyprus,,Cyprus donates to WHO Ebola campaign,2026-11-04T07:48:22+00:00,https://cyprus-mail.com/2026/11/04/cyprus-donates-to-who-ebola-campaign,ENGLISH,humans,"Cyprus, via the CyprusAid mechanism, donates €100,000 to the World Health Organization to support humanitarian and health response efforts addressing the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo. The contribution reflects Cyprus’ solidarity with affected populations and commitment to international public health emergencies. Since the outbreak was declared in May, the Democratic Republic of Congo has recorded over 10,000 Ebola infections and more than 5,100 deaths, making it the second-largest Ebola outbreak on record. The report focuses on funding and international response; it does not provide details on symptoms, laboratory confirmation, infection sources, or specific imported/exported cases.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"記事自体はキプロスの寄付に関する報道だが、背景にあるDRCのエボラアウトブレイクは既に大規模化しており（感染者1万人超、死者5,100人超）、継続的な国際支援が必要な深刻な公衆衛生イベントである。キプロスは対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations から除外。",
aHR0cDovL3d3dy54aW5odWFuZXQuY29tL2hlYWx0aC8yMDI2MTEwNC9hM2Y2MDY0MTg5MDg0MDdkYTc5YjQ3NzA5Y2QyMDM1MS9jLmh0bWw=,DISMISS,手足口病の季節性流行に関する一般的な予防啓発記事であり、異常事態や重症例急増の報告はなく、既存の公衆衛生対応の範囲内である。,Enterovirus 71; Enterovirus Syndrome,People's Republic of China,Autumn small peak of hand-foot-mouth disease: key protective measures for schools and childcare institutions,手足口病秋季小高峰，学校、托幼机构防护要点,2026-11-04T00:00:00+00:00,http://www.xinhuanet.com/health/20261104/a3f606418908407da79b47709cd20351/c.html,CHINESE,humans,"Hand-foot-mouth disease (HFMD) shows an autumnal small peak in China, especially in nurseries and schools. It is caused by multiple enteroviruses, with Coxsackievirus A6, A16, A10, and Enterovirus A71 being major circulating strains; EV-A71 is more prone to severe disease. HFMD can occur year-round, but southern regions experience a fall peak (September–November) while northern areas have a summer peak (April–July). Autumn resurgence is tied to increased clustering and seasonal immune fluctuations in children. Preventive measures in child care and school settings include enhanced ventilation, hygiene education, and disinfection: toys and surfaces with 500 mg/L chlorine disinfectant for 30 minutes; boiling tableware for 15 minutes; alcohol-based disinfectants are ineffective; vomitus requires 1000–2000 mg/L chlorine disinfectant. Daily morning/afternoon health checks; immediate isolation of suspected cases and parental notification; confirmed cases should recover at home and return after symptoms disappear and at least 14 days from onset (generally one week after symptom resolution).",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,No,No,毎年繰り返される季節性の手足口病に関する予防啓発記事であり、新規の公衆衛生リスクを示すものではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucmlvdGltZXNvbmxpbmUuY29tL2doYW5hLWVib2xhLXNjcmVlbmluZy1hbGwtYWlycG9ydC1hcnJpdmFscy0yMDI2Lw==,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で発生したブンディブギョ株エボラのアウトブレイクが1万人超の症例・5千人超の死亡に達し、ウガンダ・ケニア・ナイジェリア・フランスへも波及、米国やガーナが渡航制限・検疫措置を導入するなどIHR基準を複数満たすためフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Africa; Accra; Greater Accra Region; United States; Republic of France; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria,,Ghana Screens All Arrivals for Ebola,2026-11-04T08:09:47+00:00,https://www.riotimesonline.com/ghana-ebola-screening-all-airport-arrivals-2026/,ENGLISH,humans,"Ghana begins Ebola screening at Accra International Airport: all arrivals face non-contact temperature checks and a health declaration; Port Health, with follow-up by the Ghana Health Service, deems the measures precautionary as no Ebola cases have been confirmed in Ghana. The Bundibugyo-strain outbreak in parts of Africa drives the precaution. Travelers from countries with ongoing transmission are monitored for up to 21 days and must report symptoms; hotels and conference venues must report guests from affected countries and keep contact records. From 3 November 2026, US-bound travelers must sign a Congo-attestation not to have been in Congo in the prior 21 days. CDC data as of 1 November 2026: globally 10,563 cases, 5,130 deaths; Congo 10,532/5,126; outside Congo: Uganda 20, Kenya 9, Nigeria 1, France 1; no active cases in Uganda or France.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ガーナは予防的空港スクリーニングを実施しているのみで、国内でのエボラ症例確認はされていないため発生国からは除外。対象国リスト外（ウガンダ、ケニア、ナイジェリア、フランス、米国）での症例・対応は参考情報として記載したが、verified_locationsには含めていない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYWZyaWNhLW5ld3Nyb29tLmNvbS9wcmVzcy9kZS1sYS1wZXVyLWEtbGVzcG9pci0tbGUtY29tYmF0LWRlLWphY3F1ZWxpbmUtYmFnYWJvLWNvbnRyZS1lYm9sYS1lbi1yZXB1YmxpcXVlLWRlbW9jcmF0aXF1ZS1kdS1jb25nbw==,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国イトゥリ州で発生中のエボラ出血熱が4,800人超の死者を出しており、国境封鎖など社会経済への影響も深刻であるためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Ituri; Bunia; Democratic Republic of the Congo,From Fear to Hope: Jacqueline Bagabo's Battle Against Ebola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo,De la peur à l'espoir : le combat de Jacqueline Bagabo contre Ebola en République Démocratique du Congo,2026-11-04T07:32:57+00:00,https://www.africa-newsroom.com/press/de-la-peur-a-lespoir--le-combat-de-jacqueline-bagabo-contre-ebola-en-republique-democratique-du-congo,FRENCH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in Ituri province, Democratic Republic of the Congo, centered in Bunia. By Oct 24, 2026, Ebola had caused over 4,800 deaths, with women making up about 54% of reported cases. Jacqueline Bagabo, executive director of Women Need Peace, leads community prevention and advocacy. When unexplained deaths appeared, misconceptions spread until May 2026 when analyses confirmed Ebola. Her organization launched awareness campaigns reaching about 1,800 people and distributed handwashing kits, hydroalcoholic gel, and disinfection supplies in schools and community spaces. Women, as primary caregivers and traders, bore the economic and caregiving burden, worsened by border closures. Survivors faced stigma; psychosocial support and community campaigns helped rebuild trust, including sign-language outreach for deaf and mute students at the Ephphatha school in Bunia. Nyagoma, 20, and Shukuru, 25, survivors pursuing sewing training; one machine for ~40 learners. Bagabo insists women must be central to the Ebola response.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"記事はコミュニティ主導の予防・啓発活動を紹介する人間ドラマ的内容だが、背景にある大規模エボラ流行（累計死者4,800人超、女性が主な感染者層・介護者）はIHR基準・WPRO基準いずれにも強く該当する既知の大規模公衆衛生危機である。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cueWFuZ3RzZS5jb20vbmV3cy9qay8yMDI2MTEvdDIwMjYxMTA0XzQwOTI3Ni5odG1s,DISMISS,単一症例の臨床症例報告であり、公衆衛生上の異常事態や集団感染、社会的関心の高まりを示す要素がないため見送りと判断する。,Tuberculosis,Taizhou; Jiangsu Sheng; Nanjing,Bedridden woman for ten years with a nonhealing pressure ulcer found to be caused by latent tuberculosis; Traditional Chinese Medicine intangible heritage therapy relieves the chronic illness.,"女子卧床十载压疮难愈竟因结核""隐身""， 中医非遗疗法解沉疴",2026-11-04T08:42:18+00:00,https://www.yangtse.com/news/jk/202611/t20261104_409276.html,CHINESE,humans,"A fifty-something bedridden woman from Taizhou developed a nonhealing left hip pressure ulcer, following paralysis caused by a psoas abscess. Weeks of standard wound care failed, and a wound culture at Nanjing Integrated Traditional Chinese and Western Medicine Hospital’s Wound Clinic revealed Mycobacterium tuberculosis in the exudate, identifying a tuberculous pressure ulcer—rare and treatment-challenging. After diagnosis, clinicians implemented a combined approach: systemic anti-tuberculosis therapy to control infection, surgical debridement of the ulcer, and Xu’s Ulcer Therapy (a traditional Chinese medicine external application and dressing method) to promote granulation. The ulcer rapidly improved, exudate decreased, and healthy tissue formed, leading to complete healing and discharge. The case highlights that pressure ulcers in long-term bedridden patients can harbor uncommon infections and should be evaluated at experienced centers if healing remains stalled beyond one month.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,個人の臨床症例報告（結核性褥瘡）であり、公衆衛生イベントとしての性質はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly90cmlidW5lLm5ldC5waC8yMDI2LzExLzA0L2ZsdS1saWtlLWlsbG5lc3Nlcy1qdW1wLTMxLWluLXR3by13ZWVrcy1kb2gtcmVwb3J0cw==,DISMISS,インフルエンザ様疾患(ILI)の増加は季節性変動の範囲内であり、年間累計は前年を下回り致死率も低い。デング熱・レプトスピラ症も通常の定期サーベイランス報告の範囲であり、異常性や国際的拡大リスクは認められない。,Influenza; Leptospirosis; Dengue,Mimaropa; Western Visayas; National Capital Region; Republic of the Philippines,,"Flu-like Illnesses Surge by 31% Nationwide, DOH Urges Preventive Measures",2026-11-04T08:55:51+00:00,https://tribune.net.ph/2026/11/04/flu-like-illnesses-jump-31-in-two-weeks-doh-reports,ENGLISH,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, the Department of Health reports a 31% nationwide surge in influenza-like illness (ILI), with 15,042 cases logged from 1–14 October, up from 11,517 in 17–30 September. Year-to-date ILI totals reach 139,031, still 19% below the 171,506 cases in the same period in 2025, and the case-fatality rate stands at 0.06%. The DOH urges continued preventive measures to curb respiratory illnesses. Dengue infections rose 6% to 23,842 (1–14 October) from 22,575 in the prior two weeks. Leptospirosis declined by 54%, from 1,198 (17–30 September) to 554 (1–14 October). The largest relative ILI increases occurred in Western Visayas, Central Visayas, and MIMAROPA, with 17 provinces and several highly urbanized cities, many in Metro Manila, reporting localized upticks. Overall, differing trends are noted among monitored diseases.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,DOHによる定期的な感染症サーベイランス報告。ILIは前年同期比で19%減少しており、季節的な変動と解釈される。致死率0.06%は低く、重症化や異常なクラスターの報告はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly92b3Yudm4veGEtaG9pL3Rpbi0yNGgvdGhhaS1uZ3V5ZW4tdGFuZy1jdW9uZy1waG9uZy1jaG9uZy1kaWNoLXRhLWxvbi1jaGF1LXBoaS1wb3N0MTM0NzIzOC52b3Y=,WATCH,動物疾病（アフリカ豚熱）であり直接的なヒトへの健康影響はないが、ベトナム国内で広範に発生しており養豚業への経済的影響と食料安全保障上のリスクから継続監視が必要。,African Swine Fever,Tỉnh Lạng Sơn; Tỉnh Thái Nguyên; Hiệp Lực; Thái Nguyên; Socialist Republic of Vietnam,Thai Nguyen strengthens prevention and control of African swine fever.,"Thái Nguyên tăng cường phòng, chống dịch tả lợn châu Phi",2026-11-04T08:46:38+00:00,https://vov.vn/xa-hoi/tin-24h/thai-nguyen-tang-cuong-phong-chong-dich-ta-lon-chau-phi-post1347238.vov,VIETNAMESE,animals,"African swine fever (ASF) outbreaks in Thái Nguyên Province, Vietnam, prompted a strong response. On 18 September in Hiệp Lực commune, 15 pigs fell ill; 5 died, with 8 other households in 3 villages reporting deaths from the same cause. In total 76 pigs were culled or died, about 2.8 tons, with losses around 170 million VND. Local authorities culled infected stock, carried out disinfection, and lime-dusted facilities; officials urged ongoing surveillance and strict biosecurity. Nationwide, VAHIS records from the start of the year to 25 Oct show 1,251 ASF outbreaks in 31 provinces, affecting over 16,000 pigs. Thai Nguyen faces small, sporadic outbreaks; risk is higher in areas with prior outbreaks or weaker biosecurity. On 21 Oct the province ordered reinforced controls and a second 2026 vaccination round to reach at least 80% coverage; strict sourcing, quarantine of breeding stock, and prompt reporting are emphasized. Cam Giang and Yen Phong areas are monitoring deaths, and authorities have prosecuted transporting ASF-positive pigs in Thai Nguyen.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,No,"ASF（アフリカ豚熱）はヒトに感染しない動物疾病であり、IHR基準には該当しない。ベトナム全国で年初来1,251件の発生、16,000頭超に影響しており、養豚業・経済への影響として動向を注視する価値がある。",
aHR0cHM6Ly9iYi5sdi9zdGF0amEvbmFzaGEtbGF0dmlqYS8yMDI2LzExLzA0L3R1YmVya3VsZXotb2JuYXJ1emlsaS11LXJhYm90bmlrYS1yaXpza29pLWtlYmFibm9pLW9wYXNuby1saS1ieWxvLWVzdC1wcmlnb3Rvdmxlbm51aXUtaW0tZWR1,DISMISS,ラトビアにおける個別の輸入結核・A型肝炎症例であり、対象国（インド等）での発生事例ではないため対象外。公衆衛生上の深刻な影響や国際的拡大のリスクも認められない。,Hepatitis A; Tuberculosis,Riga; Rīga; Islamic Republic of Pakistan; Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal; Republic of Latvia; Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka; Bangladesh,Tuberculosis detected in an employee of a Riga kebab shop. Was it dangerous to eat the food he prepared?,Туберкулез обнаружили у работника рижской кебабной. Опасно ли было есть приготовленную им еду?,2026-11-04T06:09:16+00:00,https://bb.lv/statja/nasha-latvija/2026/11/04/tuberkulez-obnaruzili-u-rabotnika-rizskoi-kebabnoi-opasno-li-bylo-est-prigotovlennuiu-im-edu,RUSSIAN,humans,"Two infectious-disease cases involving foreign workers in Riga raised food-safety and medical-screening concerns. An Indian citizen employed at a Riga kebab shop was diagnosed with tuberculosis (TB) after arrival in Latvia and hospitalized in serious condition; authorities emphasize that food prepared by a TB patient does not transmit TB, which spreads mainly via airborne droplets from active cases. Latvia reports 219 TB cases year-to-date, including 16 among foreigners; the Indian TB case is the only registered Indian TB case this year. A separate Hepatitis A case was reported among a foreign worker at a Riga university catering facility. The Centre for Disease Prevention and Control notes that TB can develop after initial screening, as latent-to-active progression is possible. For certain third-country nationals (including India, Pakistan, Sri Lanka, Bangladesh, Nepal), residence-permit processes require chest X-ray screening and a physician’s declaration of no active TB; post-employment, foreign workers follow the same health checks as other food-service workers, with two years of contact monitoring and periodic chest radiographs.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,Yes,No,No,事例はラトビア（リガ）で発生した個別の輸入症例であり、患者の出身国であるインドでの発生事例ではないため、対象国リストの国での発生とは認められない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmF0dXJlLmNvbS9hcnRpY2xlcy9zNDE1NDEtMDI2LTAxNjA4LTQ=,DISMISS,本記事はニパウイルスワクチン・治療薬開発に関する専門家会合の成果をまとめた学術論文であり、実際の症例・アウトブレイク情報は含まれていないため、シグナルとしての該当性はない。,Nipah,State of Mahārāshtra; New Delhi; National Capital Territory of Delhi; Delhi; Faridabad; State of Haryāna; Pune; United States; Bangladesh; Malaysia; Republic of Singapore; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,Stakeholder-informed use cases and target product characteristics for vaccines and therapeutics for Nipah virus disease - npj Vaccines,2026-11-04T00:00:00+00:00,https://www.nature.com/articles/s41541-026-01608-4,ENGLISH,humans; animals,"Stakeholder-informed use cases and target product characteristics for Nipah virus disease vaccines and therapeutics were developed through an expert consultation workshop funded by the Coalition for Epidemic Preparedness Innovations (CEPI). The effort reflects a broad, multinational collaboration spanning Bangladesh (icddr,b; IEDCR), India (ICMR-NIV Pune; CDSCO New Delhi; NCDC Delhi; ICMR-NIE; NITVAR Pune; THSTI Faridabad), the United Kingdom (University of Oxford; ISARIC; CEPI), the United States (CDC; FDA; Johns Hopkins; PATH; FIND; Mapp Biopharmaceutical), Singapore (HSA), Malaysia (Institute for Medical Research; University of Malaya), and additional partners. NAVIPP, funded by UKRI under Horizon Europe and EU Project 101137506, coordinates funding and governance. The article emphasizes stakeholder input in shaping vaccine and therapeutic development and provides no Nipah case counts, outbreak details, or laboratory-confirmed data in the text; it presents the views of the authors and funders.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事はワクチン・治療薬開発のための多国間専門家協議の報告であり、ニパウイルスの実際の発生・症例報告は含まれていないため、対象国における発生事例として扱わない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9tLjE2My5jb20vZHkvYXJ0aWNsZS9MQVRDTUkxNTA1MTQ5NVJMLmh0bWw=,DISMISS,帯状疱疹は既知の一般的疾患で、季節的な啓発記事であり、公衆衛生上の異常性や国際的拡大リスクはない。,Varicella,Jingzhou; Hubei Sheng,"Once infected, you’ll be a lifelong carrier! This virus is entering a period of high incidence.",一旦感染，终身携带！这种病毒进入高发期,2026-11-04T07:45:24+00:00,https://m.163.com/dy/article/LATCMI15051495RL.html,CHINESE,humans,"Shingles (herpes zoster), caused by reactivation of the varicella-zoster virus, is entering a high-incidence period in autumn–winter in Jingzhou, Hubei Province, China. After primary infection (chickenpox), the virus remains latent in dorsal root ganglia and can reactivate to cause painful vesicular rashes along nerve distributions. Lesions are not confined to the waist; they can affect the head, neck, chest, eyes, ears, and sometimes the face. Transmission occurs via the live virus in vesicle fluid; while most adults have prior VZV exposure, unvaccinated children should avoid direct contact with active lesions. Prompt antiviral treatment within 72 hours of rash onset, adequate dosing, and analgesia are essential to limit nerve damage and reduce postherpetic neuralgia. Vaccination markedly lowers incidence and complications, and immune health—regular sleep, moderate exercise, and chronic disease management (e.g., diabetes, COPD)—helps prevention. Source: National Emergency Broadcast, Jingzhou Media Center.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,帯状疱疹（水痘帯状疱疹ウイルス再活性化）に関する一般的な健康啓発記事であり、アウトブレイクや異常事態ではない。,
