aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cub3RlbXBvLmNvbS5ici9zYXVkZS1lLWJlbS1lc3Rhci8yMDI2LzExLzQvbW9ydGUtcG9yLXNhcmFtcG8tZW0tbnktZXZpZGVuY2lhLWltcG9ydGFuY2lhLWRhLXZhY2luYWNhby1jYXNvcy1kb2JyYW0tbm8tYnJhc2lsLWVtLWRvaXMtbWVzZXM=,WATCH,ブラジルでは麻疹排除状態を維持しているが輸入例による症例増加が見られ、排除status喪失のリスクが指摘されているため、続報を注視する必要がある。,Measles,New York; United States; Federative Republic of Brazil,Death from measles in New York highlights the importance of vaccination; cases double in Brazil in two months.,Morte por sarampo em NY evidencia importância da vacinação; casos dobram no Brasil em dois meses,2026-11-04T09:06:56+00:00,https://www.otempo.com.br/saude-e-bem-estar/2026/11/4/morte-por-sarampo-em-ny-evidencia-importancia-da-vacinacao-casos-dobram-no-brasil-em-dois-meses,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Measles death in New York State highlights vulnerability as US vaccination coverage drops below the 95% target; 2026 cases in the United States total 4,852 with three deaths through Oct 29, and about 96% of cases occur in individuals not vaccinated or with unknown immunization status. In Brazil, 61 confirmed measles cases in 2026 (61 by early November), more than double August’s 27, marking the highest since 2022, with transmission tied to importations. Brazil remains non-endemic since regaining elimination in November 2024, but imports risk sustained transmission; Minas Gerais reports zero cases in 2026 but had 158 (2019) and 22 (2020) previously. Health authorities stress vaccination and containment, including dose zero for under-1s in affected areas. SBIm warns that Brazil could lose measles-free status if transmission becomes sustained, though current case management and surveillance continue. Brazil’s vaccination history shows fluctuations, with 2025 first-dose coverage above 93% after years below the target and ongoing emphasis on access, outreach, and misinformation countering.",不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,Yes,No,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,No,米国ニューヨーク州の麻疹死亡事例が主なトピックだが、対象国リストに米国は含まれないため除外。ブラジルは輸入例による症例増加（8月27件→11月61件）が報告されており、排除status喪失のリスクが懸念される。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZm9vZGFncmlidXNpbmVzcy53b3JsZC9wb3VsdHJ5L2JyYXppbC1mYWNlcy1wb3RlbnRpYWxseS1jb3N0bHktcG91bHRyeS1leHBvcnQtcmVzdHJpY3Rpb25zLWFmdGVyLW5ld2Nhc3RsZS1kaXNlYXNlLW91dGJyZWFr,WATCH,動物疾病（ニューカッスル病）による貿易制限が複数国で発生しているが、ヒトへの公衆衛生影響は報告されておらず、IHR基準・社会的関心は限定的。経済・貿易への影響は継続監視が必要。,Newcastle Disease,Rio Grande; Paraná; Santa Catarina; Rio Grande do Sul; United States; Federative Republic of Brazil; Republic of Chile; Malaysia; Kingdom of Saudi Arabia; Mexico,,Brazil could face costly poultry export restrictions after Newcastle disease outbreak,2026-11-04T09:15:20+00:00,https://www.foodagribusiness.world/poultry/brazil-faces-potentially-costly-poultry-export-restrictions-after-newcastle-disease-outbreak,ENGLISH,animals,"Newcastle disease outbreak in Brazil triggers costly export restrictions across key markets. Mexico banned imports of Brazilian poultry on Oct 19, affecting Brazil’s roughly 244,000 tonnes imported in 2025 (about US$777 million) and Mexico’s 22.8% share of Brazilian chicken, second only to the United States. Mexican officials said domestic supplies suffice and the restriction would not impact the home market. Saudi Arabia limited imports to Santa Catarina, Brazil’s third-largest export market, after a partial restriction. Malaysia, Chile and China also imposed limits; China remains the major concern. After a 2024 outbreak, China previously restricted imports from Rio Grande do Sul, with Brazil regaining disease-free status in Oct 2024, but China kept restrictions until Jan 2026. From Jan–Sep 2026 China imported about 420,000 tonnes, making it Brazil’s largest market. Affected production capacity includes Santa Catarina, which accounted for 13.7% of 2025 chicken slaughter, second to Paraná.",No,No,Yes,Yes,2,No,No,不明,不明,No,0,No,Yes,No,本事案は家禽疾病（動物衛生）であり、ヒト感染症としての公衆衛生リスクは記事内で言及されていない。主に貿易・経済への影響が焦点。IHR上の貿易制限基準には該当するが、ヒトへの重大な公衆衛生影響は不明なためWATCH判定とした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9ibmV3cy52bi92aW5oLWxvbmcta2llbS1zb2F0LWRpY2gtdGEtbG9uLWNoYXUtcGhpLXZhLWtodXllbi1jYW8ta2hvbmctdGFpLWRhbi80NDMxMjYuaHRtbA==,DISMISS,アフリカ豚熱(ASF)はヒトに感染しない動物疾病であり、記事内でも人への感染リスクがないことが明記されている。公衆衛生上の深刻な影響や国際的拡大リスクは認められず、養豚業への経済的影響に留まるためIHR基準・WPRO基準いずれも該当性が低い。,African Swine Fever,Socialist Republic of Vietnam,Vĩnh Long controls African swine fever and advises against restocking.,Vĩnh Long kiểm soát dịch tả lợn châu Phi và khuyến cáo không tái đàn,2026-11-04T09:27:23+00:00,https://bnews.vn/vinh-long-kiem-soat-dich-ta-lon-chau-phi-va-khuyen-cao-khong-tai-dan/443126.html,VIETNAMESE,animals,"African swine fever (ASF) remains active in Vĩnh Long. On 3 November, outbreaks were reported in 9 households across 5 communes (Quới An, Vĩnh Kim, Long Hiệp, Ngũ Lạc, Tân Long Hội), with 217 pigs culled and over 12.7 tons destroyed. Since 29 September, ASF has affected 124 households in 78 rural hamlets (ấp, khóm) within 32 communes, totaling 3,098 pigs culled and more than 182 tons removed. Nationwide, the disease has caused 1,360 outbreaks in 826 administrative units across 31 of 34 provinces/cities, with 177,265 pigs dead or culled; 25 provinces/cities report outbreaks not yet past 21 days. Authorities urge intensified outbreak containment, biosafety, surveillance, testing, and strict control of pig transport, trading, and slaughter. Farmers should avoid restocking until safe conditions are confirmed; authorities will support disposal, sanitation, and traceability, while warning against public alarm about ASF not infecting humans.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,ASFはブタの疾病でヒトへの感染性はなく、記事も人体への影響がないことを明示的に否定している。ベトナム国内の養豚業に対する経済的・農業的影響としての注視は妥当だが、公衆衛生上のシグナルには該当しない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmV3czlsaXZlLmNvbS9pbmRpYS9hc3NhbS1vdmVyLTUwLXN0dWRlbnRzLWF0LWVuZ2luZWVyaW5nLWNvbGxlZ2UtZmFsbC1pbGwtZGVhZC1tb25rZXktZm91bmQtaW4td2F0ZXItdGFuay0zMDIxNzI1,DISMISS,給水タンクの汚染による局地的な胃腸炎症状の集団発生であり、全員安定し退院済み。狂犬病タグは咬傷を受けた学生1名へのワクチン接種に起因するもので、疾患としての狂犬病アウトブレイクではない。,Rabies,Guwahati; Assam,,"Assam: Over 50 students at engineering college fall ill, dead monkey found in water tank",2026-11-04T09:17:38+00:00,https://www.news9live.com/india/assam-over-50-students-at-engineering-college-fall-ill-dead-monkey-found-in-water-tank-3021725,ENGLISH,humans; environment,"In Guwahati, Assam, 52 students from Hostel 7 at Assam Engineering College fell ill after using water from a tank in which a dead monkey was found, prompting foul-smelling water concerns. The illness, beginning after Durga Puja vacation, included vomiting, stomach pain, fever, with 30–40 students reporting dysentery-like symptoms. They were treated at Government Ayurvedic College and Hospital; 3 were referred for further care, but all 52 were stable and discharged. The college cleaned the tank and moved the mess to another hostel; classes resumed. No deaths were reported. The campus lies near a hill with a large monkey population, contributing to safety concerns and a recent rabies vaccination for a bitten student. The administration has alerted the forest department about the monkey menace.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,疾患タグは狂犬病だが、記事の主題は給水タンク汚染による胃腸炎症状の集団発生。咬傷学生への狂犬病ワクチン接種は付随的な記述であり、対象国リストの狂犬病アウトブレイクには該当しないためverified_locationsは空とした。,
