aHR0cHM6Ly9ibmV3cy52bi9uZ3V5LWNvLWRpY2gtYmVuaC1jYW4tdGV0LWRvbmctdGhhcC1raGFuLXRydW9uZy1iYW8tdmUtZGFuLXZhdC1udW9pLzQ0MzEzNy5odG1s,WATCH,ベトナム・ドンタップ省での豚熱・H5N6鳥インフルエンザ等の家畜疾病発生が報告されているが、ヒトへの感染事例はなく、省レベルで防疫措置（殺処分・ワクチン接種）が進行中であるため、現時点でのヒト公衆衛生への直接的影響は確認されない。H5N6はズーノーシスポテンシャルがあるため継続監視が必要。,African Swine Fever; Avian Influenza; Lumpy Skin Disease; Human Infection with Avian Influenza A H5N6; Human Infection with Avian Influenza,Socialist Republic of Vietnam,Risk of disease outbreaks around Tet; Dong Thap urgently protects its livestock.,"Nguy cơ dịch bệnh cận Tết, Đồng Tháp khẩn trương bảo vệ đàn vật nuôi",2026-11-04T10:13:01+00:00,https://bnews.vn/nguy-co-dich-benh-can-tet-dong-thap-khan-truong-bao-ve-dan-vat-nuoi/443137.html,VIETNAMESE,animals,"Dong Thap Province, Vietnam, faces persistent animal-disease threats ahead of Tet and the 2027 Lunar New Year. In October 2026, the province recorded six African swine fever outbreaks, one avian influenza outbreak, and one case of lumpy skin disease. Notably in Ba Lắm hamlet, Tan Phú Đông commune, a A/H5N6 avian flu outbreak affected 562 poultry (560 ducks, 2 chickens); 167 birds were infected (90 sick, 77 dead) with onset Oct 12–17. By Oct 24, officials culled 518 birds (844 kg) and implemented outbreak-control measures. The province mandates intensified surveillance, mass vaccination (including a second 2026 round) and vaccination for new or unvaccinated stock; biosafety, hygiene, disinfection, and regulated transport/slaughter of animals and products. Border controls, public communications, and training are being deployed; authorities urge rapid reporting of sick or dead animals and strict containment to protect food safety and livestock supply during year-end and Tet.",No,No,不明,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,記事は家畜（アヒル・鶏・豚・牛）の疾病発生と省による防疫対応に関する内容であり、ヒト感染例の報告はない。H5N6はヒトへの感染事例が過去に報告されている株であるため、今後の人獣共通感染症としての進展を注視する必要がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2llbm1hZy5jb20vbnMxLWJhc2VkLWlnZy1lbGlzYS13aXRoLW9kLXJhdGlvLWltcHJvdmVzLXppa3YtYW5kLWRlbmd1ZS1zZXJvbG9neS1pbi1lbmRlbWljLXJlZ2lvbnMv,DISMISS,本記事は診断検査法の研究論文であり、アウトブレイクや公衆衛生上の緊急事態を報告するものではないため、トリアージ基準に該当しない。,Zika; Coccidioidomycosis; Dengue,,,NS1-based IgG ELISA with OD ratio improves ZIKV and dengue serology in,2026-11-04T10:41:04+00:00,https://scienmag.com/ns1-based-igg-elisa-with-od-ratio-improves-zikv-and-dengue-serology-in-endemic-regions/,ENGLISH,humans,"Thailand researchers evaluated an in-house NS1-based IgG ELISA to distinguish past ZIKV infections from past DENV infections in a dengue-endemic setting. Using RT-PCR–confirmed ZIKV or DENV samples, they compared three ZIKV antigens—envelope protein domain III and NS1 from African-lineage MR766 and Asian-lineage SV0127—and applied three ZIKV/DENV ratio metrics (positive-to-negative, optical density, and relative optical density). The Asian SV0127 NS1 antigen with the relative OD ratio yielded the best discrimination. Validation with a Youden index cut-off of 2.35 produced an AUC of 0.7083 (95% CI 0.6335–0.7831), sensitivity 58.3%, and specificity 79.2%. Compared with a commercial Zika IgG ELISA, the in-house NS1-based assay demonstrated better discrimination despite lower overall signal. The approach aims for surveillance and retrospective serology in settings where neutralization tests are impractical and is not a replacement for PRNT.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,本記事は研究手法（血清学的検査法の評価）に関するものであり、実際の感染症発生事例の報告ではないため、発生地域（Thailand）はverified_locationsに含めない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYmx1ZXdpbi5jaC9kZS9saWZlc3R5bGUvd2lzc2VuL3ZpZXItbG9rYWxlLWZhZWxsZS12b24tY2hpa3VuZ3VueWEtZmllYmVyLWltLXRlc3Npbi1iZXN0YWV0aWd0LWxpLjM2NjEwNDE=,PICKUP,スイス・ティチーノ州で初めてチクングニア熱の自国内（非渡航者）感染が確認され、媒介蚊の定着拡大という異常事態であり、社会的関心も高いためフルRRAへの移行が妥当。,Chikungunya,Ticino; Africa; Switzerland; Italian Republic; Republic of France,Dangerous tropical virus transmitted in Switzerland for the first time.,Gefährliches Tropenvirus erstmals in der Schweiz übertragen,2026-11-04T10:32:51+00:00,https://www.bluewin.ch/de/lifestyle/wissen/vier-lokale-faelle-von-chikungunya-fieber-im-tessin-bestaetigt-li.3661041,GERMAN,vectors; humans,"Chikungunya virus has been locally transmitted for the first time in Ticino, Switzerland, with affected individuals reporting no recent travel to endemic areas. Transmission occurred via Aedes mosquitoes, including the Asian tiger mosquito, now established in parts of Switzerland. Classic symptoms are sudden high fever and severe joint and muscle pain, sometimes with headaches and a rash; onset typically 7–9 days after a bite. Although usually not life-threatening, joint pain and fatigue can persist for weeks or months. Chikungunya is common in tropical and subtropical regions, notably Africa, India, Southeast Asia, the Caribbean, and Central/South America. Europe has seen local outbreaks in Italy and France. Transmission requires infected mosquitoes and suitable climate; Switzerland had previously been considered to have very low risk.",No,Yes,不明,No,1,Yes,No,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,不明,No,記事の主題はスイス（ティチーノ州）での初の局地感染事例であり、インド・アフリカ・イタリア・フランスはチクングニア熱の一般的流行地域として言及されているのみで、本イベントの発生地ではないため対象国リストには該当しない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly90dW9pdHJlLnZuL2FuLWdpYW5nLWxhbS1naS1kZS1raWVtLXNvYXQtYmVuaC1kaWNoLXRhLWhlby1jaGF1LXBoaS0xMDAyNjExMDQxNjEwNTkwOTMuaHRt,WATCH,動物感染症（ASF）であり人への健康影響はないが、ベトナム国内での豚肉流通・越境移動によるさらなる拡大リスクがあり、経過観察が妥当。,African Swine Fever,Thôn Vĩnh Thông; Tỉnh Kiến Giang; Socialist Republic of Vietnam,What is An Giang doing to control African swine fever?,An Giang làm gì để kiểm soát bệnh dịch tả heo châu Phi?,2026-11-04T09:52:00+00:00,https://tuoitre.vn/an-giang-lam-gi-de-kiem-soat-benh-dich-ta-heo-chau-phi-100261104161059093.htm,VIETNAMESE,animals,"African swine fever (ASF) control in An Giang Province, Vietnam, reports 660 ASF-affected pigs culled, weighing over 35.3 tons, from Aug 25 to Oct 31. An Giang encompasses about 54,902 pigs on 140 farms and 2,108 households, with 80 slaughter establishments (6 centralized, 74 small). Slaughter surveillance remains weak in some communes, boosting biosafety and food-safety risks, while cross-border animal movements and unregulated trade threaten spread. One incident involved transporting 54 ASF-infected piglets in Vĩnh Thông Ward; two slaughter facilities were flagged as potential spreaders. Authorities are coordinating with border districts and the Border Guard to monitor cross-border movement. Separately, the Department of Domestic Market Management and Development reported nearly 1 ton of pork and pork products flagged for food-safety violations, with laboratory tests confirming ASF virus in 7 of 9 samples.",No,No,Yes,不明,1,No,不明,Yes,Yes,不明,2,不明,Yes,不明,ASFは動物感染症であり、人獣共通感染症ではないためヒトへの公衆衛生影響は直接的にはない。ただし豚肉の食品安全・流通管理上の懸念と越境拡大リスクがあるため監視継続が適切。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9uZXdzLm15ZHJpdmVycy5jb20vMS8xMTYzLzExNjMyMTcuaHRt,DISMISS,四川省での住血吸虫病の排除達成を発表するポジティブなニュースであり、新規感染拡大や公衆衛生上の脅威を示すものではない。,Schistosomiasis,Shanghai Shi; People's Republic of China,Once threatened more than 13 million people! Officially confirmed: Sichuan has eliminated schistosomiasis.,曾威胁1300多万人！官方正式确认：四川已消除血吸虫病,2026-11-04T10:37:50+00:00,https://news.mydrivers.com/1/1163/1163217.htm,CHINESE,vectors; animals; humans; environment,"As of 2026-11-04, Sichuan Province has been officially confirmed to eliminate schistosomiasis (Schistosoma japonicum) by the National Center for Disease Control and Prevention and other ministries. Historically one of China’s most affected regions, Sichuan’s outbreak spanned 11 prefectures/cities and 63 counties, putting about 13 million people at risk. The disease was first reported in 1924; the snail Oncomelania was identified in 1939, and cattle infection confirmed in 1943. Cumulative cases reached about 1.28 million; more than 30,000 late-stage patients; about 200,000 cattle infected. Schistosomiasis is a zoonosis; late-stage symptoms include severe abdominal distension. Transmission requires water contaminated with eggs, the snail intermediate host, and skin contact with infectious water—common activities include swimming, fishing, washing, farming, aquaculture, and floods. Snails remain widespread in the Yangtze basin and southern areas; risk is higher April–October. National transmission interruption was achieved in 2023, with elimination targeted by 2030.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事は過去の流行の歴史と排除達成を報告する内容であり、現在進行中のアウトブレイクではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmV3c3dlZWsuY29tL25ldy1lYm9sYS10cmF2ZWwtcnVsZS1raWNrcy1pbi1mb3ItYWxsLXBhc3NlbmdlcnMtaGVhZGluZy10by11cy0xMjY2MTA1Ng==,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ（ブンディブギョ種）アウトブレイクが1万人超の症例・5千人超の死者を出し、ケニア・ナイジェリアへの国際的な拡大も確認され、米国が渡航制限措置を導入するなどIHR基準を複数満たすため。,Ebola,United States; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria,,New Ebola travel rule kicks in for all passengers heading to US,2026-11-04T10:27:56+00:00,https://www.newsweek.com/new-ebola-travel-rule-kicks-in-for-all-passengers-heading-to-us-12661056,ENGLISH,humans,"Bundibugyo Ebola virus outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) prompts a new CDC rule for travelers to the United States. From 11:59 p.m. ET on November 3, all international and connecting flights must have an attestation that the traveler has not been in the DRC in the previous 21 days; transiting through DRC counts. Airlines must deny boarding to noncompliant passengers and keep attestations for 42 days. The rule runs through 11:59 p.m. ET on December 18 unless extended and carries penalties for false statements. The outbreak began in May, with Uganda’s outbreak declared over in August; imported cases have appeared in Kenya (first case Oct 6, two deaths) and Nigeria (Oct 20). As of Nov 1, the ECDC reports 10,532 confirmed DRC cases and 5,126 deaths. The CDC says no U.S. cases to date, but travel-related spread has occurred elsewhere.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"発生地域にUnited States, Kenya, Uganda, Nigeriaが含まれるが、対象国リストに該当するのはDRCのみ。主たる発生国はDRCであり、ケニア・ナイジェリアは輸入症例、米国は渡航規制の対象国として言及されているのみ。",
aHR0cHM6Ly9uZXdzLnJlcHVibGlrYS5jby5pZC9iZXJpdGEvdG56NTBzNDMwL2NhcmEta2VtZW5rZXMtcHV0dXMtcmFudGFpLXBlbnVsYXJhbi10YmMtZGktcG9ucGVz,DISMISS,既知の風土病である結核対策の政府プログラムに関する報道であり、異常性や国際的拡大リスクは認められず、通常の公衆衛生施策として扱われるべき内容である。,Tuberculosis,North Sumatra; Republic of Indonesia,How the Ministry of Health Breaks the TB Transmission Chain at an Islamic boarding school.,Cara Kemenkes Putus Rantai Penularan TBC di Ponpes |Republika Online,2026-11-04T10:55:40+00:00,https://news.republika.co.id/berita/tnz50s430/cara-kemenkes-putus-rantai-penularan-tbc-di-ponpes,INDONESIAN,humans; environment,"Indonesia's Ministry of Health launches the Pesantren Bebas Tuberkulosis (TBC) program, integrating it with nationwide Free Health Check (CKG) at Islamic boarding schools (pondok pesantren) to curb airborne tuberculosis transmission in densely populated santri communities. The initiative prioritizes periodic airborne case tracing in communal pockets, enabling early detection and free treatment, with patients referred to local clinics (puskesmas) for medication support until cure. The program seeks to substantially boost national active TB case finding, targeting up to a 90% increase in 2026, and intensifies detection in North Sumatra cluster areas to shrink transmission. The kickoff was held at Pondok Pesantren Mawaridussalam, Deli Serdang Regency, North Sumatra, on 4 November 2026, with plans to replicate the model across Indonesia through cross-sector collaboration among Kemenkes, Kemenag, and Kemendagri. TB is framed as a social, nutritional, and living-environment challenge, not merely a medical one.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,No,Yes,No,結核は既知の風土病であり、本記事は新規アウトブレイクではなく既存の国家プログラムの展開に関する内容。密集した寄宿学校環境での持続的曝露リスクはあるが、通常の公衆衛生対策の枠内。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY2RubmV3cy5jb20udHcvYXJ0aWNsZXMvMTQ4NTEzMA==,DISMISS,台湾・宜蘭県における季節性ノロウイルスの集団感染で、学校や施設での散発的な事例であり、国際的拡大や渡航制限のリスクは認められない。対象国での発生でもない。,Norovirus,Heilongjiang Sheng; Yilan Xian; Taiwan,Prevent Norovirus: Start with Hand Hygiene,防範諾羅病毒 從落實手部清潔做起 | 中華日報|中華新聞雲,2026-11-04T10:52:07+00:00,https://www.cdnnews.com.tw/articles/1485130,CHINESE,humans,"Norovirus drives diarrheal clusters in Yilan County, Taiwan, with cases concentrated in schools, institutions, dining-out events, and travel-related settings. Health authorities collected specimens; laboratory results indicate norovirus as the cause in most clusters. Norovirus is highly infectious, requiring as few as 10 to 100 viral particles to cause infection. Common symptoms include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and abdominal cramps; fever, chills, fatigue, headache, and myalgia may occur. Most people recover spontaneously in 1–3 days with no long-term consequences, but dehydration from severe vomiting or diarrhea can be dangerous, especially in infants, the elderly, the immunocompromised, or those needing long-term care, potentially leading to seizures if treatment is delayed. Health Commissioner Xu Nai-wei urges strict hand hygiene as a key preventive measure, noting many people wash hands after bathroom use but skip thorough soap washing.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,Yes,No,1,No,No,No,発生地域に黒龍江省（中国）が含まれるが、記事本文は台湾・宜蘭県での事例を主題としており、中国本土での発生ではない。台湾・中国本土ともに対象国リストに該当する発生地ではないため、verified_locationsは空とした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9qb3JuYWxyYXphby5jb20vc2F1ZGUvc2FudGEtY2F0YXJpbmEtY29uZmlybWEtcXVhcnRvLWZvY28tZGEtZG9lbmNhLWRlLW5ld2Nhc3RsZS1lbS1hdmVz,WATCH,動物衛生事象（家禽ニューカッスル病）であり、ヒトへの直接的な公衆衛生上の脅威は報告されていないが、同一地域での発生拡大（4例目）が続いており貿易・畜産業への影響の観点から経過観察が妥当。,Newcastle Disease,Santa Catarina; Federative Republic of Brazil,Santa Catarina confirms the fourth outbreak of Newcastle disease in birds.,Santa Catarina confirma quarto foco da doença de Newcastle em aves,2026-11-04T11:00:36+00:00,https://jornalrazao.com/saude/santa-catarina-confirma-quarto-foco-da-doenca-de-newcastle-em-aves,PORTUGUESE,animals,"Nova Erechim, in western Santa Catarina, Brazil, reported a new Newcastle disease focus in a poultry facility on November 3, 2026. The outbreak lies within the already delineated restricted area under the zoosanitary emergency, and this is the fourth detection since the emergency was declared. The Ministry of Agriculture and Livestock (MAPA) confirms the establishment's inclusion in the restricted zone. The Surveillance and Official Veterinary Service will perform an epidemiological investigation and implement surveillance and containment measures per emergency zoosanitary protocols within the emergency area.",No,No,不明,Yes,1,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,本事象は家禽における動物疾病であり、ヒト感染症としてのリスクは報告されていない。ただし家禽業への影響や貿易規制の可能性があるため、続報を注視する必要がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hZmFtaWx5LnZuL3Z1YS1kaS1uZ29haS1kdW9uZy12ZS1kYS1iZS1jb24tZGFuZy1zby1tdWktdmFuLW9tLWFwLWJlLW5odW5nLXRob2ktcXVlbi1kZS1sYW0tbGF5LXJzdi1jaG8tdHJlLTIzNjI2MTEwNDEyNTYwMDI5Ny5jaG4=,DISMISS,季節性RSVに関する一般的な予防啓発記事であり、異常な流行や公衆衛生上の緊急事態を示す情報はない。,Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV) Infection,Thành Phố Hà Nội; Hanoi,"Just back from the street, holding my child, with a runny nose, still cuddling the baby: Habits that easily spread RSV (respiratory syncytial virus) to children","Vừa đi ngoài đường về đã bế con, đang sổ mũi vẫn ôm ấp bé: Những thói quen dễ làm lây RSV cho trẻ",2026-11-04T11:00:00+00:00,https://afamily.vn/vua-di-ngoai-duong-ve-da-be-con-dang-so-mui-van-om-ap-be-nhung-thoi-quen-de-lam-lay-rsv-cho-tre-236261104125600297.chn,VIETNAMESE,humans,"Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV) infection remains common in Vietnam, with Hanoi reporting seasonal peaks in March–April and September–November. RSV causes bronchiolitis and pneumonia in children under 2 years, especially those under 6 months. Transmission occurs via respiratory droplets and contact with contaminated surfaces; adults and older children may have mild cough or runny nose, facilitating household spread. Alarm signs in infants include poor feeding with rapid breathing, chest retractions, or fatigue; blue lips, apnea, or lethargy require emergency care. Prevention centers on hand hygiene, surface cleaning, masking around babies, limiting exposure to crowds, and ensuring ventilation. WHO-recommended preventive options are maternal RSV vaccination in late pregnancy and postnatal long-acting monoclonal antibodies. Guidance from Hanoi Children’s Hospital, Hung Vuong Hospital, and the WHO covers risk groups and vaccination/antibody strategies for RSV prevention.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事は季節性RSVに関する一般的な保健教育・予防啓発内容であり、特定の異常な感染拡大やアウトブレイクを報告するものではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaW5jaGVvbmlsYm8uY29tL25ld3MvYXJ0aWNsZVZpZXcuaHRtbD9pZHhubz0xMzM1OTk2,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で致死率51.6%・死者5,372人に達する大規模なエボラ流行が継続しており、米CDCが国際便に渡航制限措置を発動するなど国際的拡大・貿易渡航制限の両基準に該当するため、フルリスク評価が必要と判断。",Ebola,Atlanta; Georgia; Incheon; Los Angeles; Incheon; Seattle; San Francisco; California; New York; Washington; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Korea; United States,Incheon Airport makes Ebola virus pledge mandatory for U.S.-bound passengers.,"인천공항, 미국행 탑승객 에볼라 바이러스 서약 의무화",2026-11-04T10:50:00+00:00,https://www.incheonilbo.com/news/articleView.html?idxno=1335996,KOREAN,humans; environment,"Ebola virus pledge attestation becomes mandatory for all passengers on U.S.-bound flights departing Incheon Airport, effective 2026-11-04 13:59 Korea Time, under a U.S. CDC emergency administrative order. The Attestation requires travelers to declare in writing (paper or electronic) that they have not visited or stayed in the Democratic Republic of the Congo in the previous 21 days; signed and submitted to the airline before check-in. The order covers all passengers, crew, and third-country transfer passengers on U.S.-bound flights and is temporary through 2026-12-19, with possible extension based on health conditions. Incheon operates 17 U.S.-bound routes with about 41 daily flights (roughly 12,277 seats) to destinations including Los Angeles, San Francisco, New York, Seattle, Atlanta, and Guam. Congo's current Ebola outbreak severity: 14,414 cumulative confirmed cases and 5,372 deaths, CFR 51.6%, as of the 2nd; even transfers via Congo airport or not exiting the airport count toward stay history.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事は仁川空港における米国行き便の渡航者誓約義務化を主題としているが、感染症事象の実際の発生地はコンゴ民主共和国（DRC）。韓国・米国は対応措置の実施地であり発生地ではないため、対象国リストに該当する韓国・米国は含まれず、verified_locationsはDRCのみとした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9kZW1va3JhYXR0aS5maS9oa2Zvb2RzLWthcnNpaS1zaWthcnV0b3N0YS1taWxqb29uYW4tZXVyb24tdmVycmFu,DISMISS,フィンランドでの家畜疾病（ASF）による経済的影響を報じる記事であり、対象国における人の健康リスクや公衆衛生上の懸念は認められない。,African Swine Fever,Helsinki; Japan; Republic of Finland,HKFoods suffers from classical swine fever to the tune of one million euros.,HKFoods kärsii sikarutosta miljoonan euron verran,2026-11-04T11:05:46+00:00,https://demokraatti.fi/hkfoods-karsii-sikarutosta-miljoonan-euron-verran,FINNISH,animals,"African swine fever (ASF) weighs on HKFoods in Finland, cutting this year's operating profit by about €1 million. The company reports no contracted pork producers inside Finland’s infection zone, but export bans outside the EU have halted pork shipments to China and Japan. Competitor Atria estimates ASF-related losses of €4–5 million for the year, with about €2 million already incurred by late summer. HKFoods’ July–September comparable operating profit rose 5.3% to €12.4 million, as prepared foods and Kariniemen broiler products boosted sales; continuing operations revenue increased roughly 3% to €255 million. Following the earnings release, HKFoods’ stock gained about 5% in Helsinki. In Finland, pork consumption rose about 5% January–August, helped by summer grilling and a shift from beef to pork mince. The report highlights ASF’s economic impact and export restrictions affecting major markets.",No,No,No,Yes,1,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,ASFはフィンランドで発生しており、中国・日本は輸出禁止措置の対象国として言及されているのみで、発生国ではない。対象国リストにフィンランドは含まれないため、verified_locationsは空配列とした。,
