aHR0cHM6Ly9vcHJlc2VudGVydXJhbC5jb20uYnIvbWFwYS1jb25maXJtYS1xdWFydG8tZm9jby1kZS1uZXdjYXN0bGUtZW0tc2FudGEtY2F0YXJpbmEv,DISMISS,本事例は家きん（ニワトリ）を対象とした動物疾病（ニューカッスル病）であり、人への公衆衛生上の直接的な影響は確認されていない。既に防疫措置（淘汰・消毒・衛生空白期間）が実施され管理下にあるため、フルリスク評価の必要性は低い。,Newcastle Disease,Santa Catarina; Nova Itaberaba; Federative Republic of Brazil; Mexico,MAPA confirms fourth Newcastle disease outbreak in Santa Catarina.,Mapa confirma quarto foco de Newcastle em Santa Catarina,2026-11-04T11:05:28+00:00,https://opresenterural.com.br/mapa-confirma-quarto-foco-de-newcastle-em-santa-catarina/,PORTUGUESE,animals,"On 4 November 2026, MAPA confirmed a fourth Newcastle disease outbreak in Santa Catarina, Brazil. Three commercial foci were identified in Nova Itaberaba, Coronel Freitas, and Nova Erechim and underwent depopulation, cleaning, disinfection, and entry into a sanitary void. Inspections covered more than 2,700 mapped properties and 202 commercial poultry establishments; 91 laboratory analyses have been completed, with two samples awaiting genetic sequencing. Traffic control remains active with four sanitary barriers and about 68 professionals. Education efforts have reached thousands of students and dozens of farms. Timeline shows laboratorially confirmed cases between 18–26 October; depopulation between 21–30 October, eliminating over 47,000 birds with deep burial, followed by the sanitary void. By 1 November, inspections of mapped properties were completed; analyses are expected during the holiday to guide statistics and market reopening. Mexico signaled resumed imports of Brazilian poultry products, highlighting ongoing biosafety across the value chain.",No,No,No,Yes,1,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,ニューカッスル病は主に家きんに感染するウイルス性疾患であり、ヒトへの感染はまれで軽度（結膜炎等）に留まるため、本記事はEBSにおける人の感染症シグナルとしての優先度は低い。ただし家きん貿易（メキシコへの輸出再開等）への影響があるため、農業・貿易関連部門での継続的な情報モニタリングは有用。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9zaWNodWFuLnNjb2wuY29tLmNuL2dneHcvMjAyNjExLzgzMzUxMjU1Lmh0bWw=,DISMISS,本記事は四川省における住血吸虫症の撲滅達成を報告する内容であり、新規感染事例や公衆衛生上の脅威を示すものではない。,Schistosomiasis,Sichuan Sheng,A Century of Struggle with Schistosomiasis: Sichuan Officially Eliminates Schistosomiasis.,"与血吸虫病""较量""百年 四川正式消除血吸虫病",2026-11-04T11:26:19+00:00,https://sichuan.scol.com.cn/ggxw/202611/83351255.html,CHINESE,vectors; animals; humans; environment,"On 2026-11-04, Sichuan Province officially reached schistosomiasis elimination, confirmed by national health authorities. The upland-endemic area previously affected 11 prefectures/cities and 63 counties, with about 13 million people at risk. Historically, first cases were reported in 1924; Oncomelania snails were found in 1939; cattle infection confirmed in 1943. Cumulative patients reached 1.2757 million, with over 30,000 late-stage cases and more than 200,000 cattle infected. Milestones included transmission control in 2008, transmission interruption in 2017, and provincial elimination assessment in 2025; national multi-department confirmation followed in 2026. A party-led, cross-sector mechanism coordinated health, livestock, water resources, agriculture, forestry and other departments, with about 700 million yuan invested since 2016. Measures encompassed human and snail control, livestock-source management, ecological governance, and integrated prevention; ongoing province-city-county surveillance and early warning systems guard against importation and strengthen grassroots capacity.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,疾患の撲滅達成を報告するポジティブなニュースであり、新規発生・流行事例ではないため対象国として計上しない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9uZG1haXMuY29tLmJyL2Vjb25vbWlhL2Fncm9uZWdvY2lvcy9ub3ZvLWZvY28tZGUtbmV3Y2FzdGxlLWUtY29uZmlybWFkby1lbS1ncmFuamEtcXVlLWphLWVzdGF2YS1zb2ItcmVzdHJpY2FvLWVtLXNjLw==,WATCH,動物（家禽）の疾病で人への直接的な公衆衛生リスクは報告されていないが、ブラジルの養鶏産業への経済的影響と感染拡大が継続している点から経過観察が妥当。,Newcastle Disease,Santa Catarina; Nova Itaberaba; Federative Republic of Brazil,New Newcastle disease outbreak confirmed at a farm that was already under restriction in Santa Catarina.,Novo foco de Newcastle é confirmado em granja que já estava sob restrição em SC,2026-11-04T11:26:19+00:00,https://ndmais.com.br/economia/agronegocios/novo-foco-de-newcastle-e-confirmado-em-granja-que-ja-estava-sob-restricao-em-sc/,PORTUGUESE,animals,"New Newcastle disease focus confirmed on 2026-11-04 at a poultry operation in Nova Erechim, Oeste Santa Catarina, Brazil, within the restricted area established after the initial cases in the western part of the state. Authorities report the farm already located inside the restricted zone. Surveillance intensified as the Official Veterinary Service enforces emergency zoosanitary protocols, including epidemiological investigation and strict containment measures. Earlier foci in Nova Itaberaba, Coronel Freitas, and the first Nova Erechim establishment are under vazio sanitário, entailing removal of birds and cleansing, disinfection, and sanitary controls before activities resume. MAPA and state defense agencies coordinate to contain the outbreak and protect the regional poultry industry. Epidemiological work seeks links between farms and virus circulation to guide responses and prevent new registrations. Newcastle disease is a highly contagious avian viral disease with economic impacts.",No,No,No,Yes,1,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,No,ニューカッスル病は家禽の疾病であり人獣共通感染症としてのヒトへの感染リスクは一般的に低い。本イベントは動物衛生・貿易経済面の問題として評価した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYmFuZC5jb20uYnIvc2F1ZGUvY29tLW1haXMtZGUtMTAtbWlsLWNhc29zLXZhbGUtZG8tcGFyYWliYS1yZWdpc3RyYS0xOC1tb3J0ZXMtcG9yLWRlbmd1ZQ==,WATCH,ブラジルの一地域で季節性デング熱による症例・死亡が報告されているが、例年の流行パターンの範囲内であり、国際的拡大や渡航制限のリスクは低い。重症度（死亡者数）の面でWPRO基準に該当するため経過観察とする。,Dengue,São Paulo; Jacareí; Paraíba; Federative Republic of Brazil,"With more than 10,000 cases, Vale do Paraíba records 18 dengue deaths.","Com mais de 10 mil casos, Vale do Paraíba registra 18 mortes por dengue",2026-11-04T11:31:44+00:00,https://www.band.com.br/saude/com-mais-de-10-mil-casos-vale-do-paraiba-registra-18-mortes-por-dengue,PORTUGUESE,humans; vectors; environment,"Vale do Paraíba, Brazil, reports more than 10,000 dengue cases and 18 deaths as spring arrives and rainfall rises, heightening Aedes aegypti transmission. Aedes eggs can survive up to 450 days in dry conditions, re-emerging when water returns. Jacareí registered about 33,000 dengue cases and 83 deaths in 2024, around 4,500 in 2025, and 2,669 confirmations with 3 deaths in 2026 to date. São José dos Campos’ September 2026 Larval Density Assessment (ADL) measured an index of 1.2, equal to January and the year's highest. Dengue typically circulates October–May, with rain boosting breeding. Prevention emphasizes eliminating water-collecting containers, keeping tanks sealed, removing standing water from plant pots and dishes, discarding bottles and tires, cleaning gutters, and checking appliance trays and yards. Authorities warn that sustained rainfall could keep transmission elevated into next year.",No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,不明,不明,No,"デング熱はブラジルで毎年10月〜5月に季節的に流行する疾患であり、本記事はヴァレ・ド・パライバ地域（サンパウロ州）における2026年の症例報告。過去数年のデータ（2024年：約33,000例、83人死亡）と比較すると2026年は現時点で少ない水準。地域限定の季節性報道であり、国際的な関心の高まりを示す情報はない。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZm9saGFwZS5jb20uYnIvbm90aWNpYXMvbWluaXN0ZXJpby1jb25maXJtYS1ub3ZvLWZvY28tZGEtZG9lbmNhLWRlLW5ld2Nhc3RsZS1lbS1ncmFuamEvNTIyMjY0Lw==,WATCH,動物疾患（ニューカッスル病）のブラジル国内での継続的な発生拡大事例であり、ヒトへの直接的な公衆衛生影響は報告されていないが、家禽産業・貿易への影響可能性があるため経過観察とする。,Newcastle Disease,Santa Catarina; Nova Itaberaba; Federative Republic of Brazil,Ministry confirms new Newcastle disease outbreak on a commercial farm in Nova Erechim (SC).,Ministério confirma novo foco da doença de Newcastle em granja comercial de Nova Erechim (SC),2026-11-04T11:42:30+00:00,https://www.folhape.com.br/noticias/ministerio-confirma-novo-foco-da-doenca-de-newcastle-em-granja/522264/,PORTUGUESE,animals,"Newcastle disease (ND) has been confirmed on a commercial turkey farm in Nova Erechim, western Santa Catarina, Brazil, representing the fourth active ND case in the current Brazilian outbreak. Confirmation occurred on 3 November 2026; sampling followed investigations that began on 31 October 2026 within the zoosanitary emergency area. In total, four active ND cases are reported across three municipalities—Nova Itaberaba, Coronel Freitas, and Nova Erechim—within the same emergency zone; the first outbreak was identified on 18 October 2026. The Official Veterinary Service is implementing response measures, including epidemiological investigations, surveillance, and containment, with affected properties already under a sanitary vacuum. This is the fifth focus in commercial production in Brazil since 17 July 2024. Newcastle disease is a highly contagious viral disease of domestic and wild birds, causing respiratory signs followed by nervous symptoms; it is notifiable to the OIE.",No,No,No,Yes,1,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,No,本疾患は鳥類の動物疾患であり、ヒトへの感染・公衆衛生への直接影響については記事中に言及なし。家禽産業と貿易への影響のためOIE通報対象。,
