aHR0cHM6Ly9hcXVpLnVhaS5jb20uYnIvc2F1ZGUvYmgtbGV2YS12YWNpbmEtY29udHJhLXNhcmFtcG8tYXMtZXNjb2xhcy1hcG9zLWF1bWVudG8tZGUtY2Fzb3Mv,WATCH,ブラジルで麻疹症例が報告されているが規模は限定的で、ベロオリゾンテは2020年以降症例なし。予防的ワクチン接種強化の報道であり緊急性は低いが、米州全体での麻疹流行傾向は注視が必要。,Measles; Varicella,São Paulo; Amazonas; Rio de Janeiro; Rio de Janeiro; São Paulo; New York; United States; Federative Republic of Brazil,Belo Horizonte brings measles vaccine to schools after rise in cases.,BH leva vacina contra sarampo às escolas após aumento de casos,2026-11-04T12:36:12+00:00,https://aqui.uai.com.br/saude/bh-leva-vacina-contra-sarampo-as-escolas-apos-aumento-de-casos/,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Belo Horizonte, Brazil launches in-school vaccination against measles and varicella in municipal schools to strengthen child immunization and prevent virus circulation in the capital of Minas Gerais, which has had no measles cases since 2020. The program uses the Measles–Mumps–Rubella (triple viral) vaccine and varicella, with parental authorization. Outside schools, vaccines are available at 154 health centers, extra posts, and the Travel Health Service. Measles coverage in BH is 99.45% for the first dose and 86.54% for the second; varicella cases rose to 118 in 2025 and 102 through September 2026, with under-1-year coverage at 80.97%. Dosing guidance: people up to 29 years without immunization proof should receive two MMR doses; 30–59 years, one dose; health professionals, two doses. Brazil reported 52 measles cases in October 2026 (São Paulo 41, Amazonas 10, Rio de Janeiro 1); the Americas saw 23,165 cases by July 2026, with New York recording a measles death, highlighting ongoing outbreak risks and the role of vaccination.",No,No,Yes,No,1,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,No,"記事は予防接種キャンペーンが主題。ブラジル国内の麻疹症例数（10月52例）は限定的だが、米州全体（23,165例、ニューヨークで死亡例）の文脈で言及されており、地域的な流行拡大の兆候として継続監視が望ましい。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubnNjdG90YWwuY29tLmJyL3NhdWRlL25vdm8tZm9jby1kYS1kb2VuY2EtZGUtbmV3Y2FzdGxlLWUtY29uZmlybWFkby1lbS1zYy1lLW1vYmlsaXphLW5vdmFzLW1lZGlkYXMtZGUtY29udGVuY2FvLW5vLWVzdGFkbw==,DISMISS,家禽のニューカッスル病の発生であり、ヒトへの公衆衛生影響はほぼないため。複数国による家禽輸入停止という貿易制限は生じているが、IHR基準・WPRO基準の該当は限定的。,Newcastle Disease,Santa Catarina; Nova Itaberaba; Republic of Chile; Federative Republic of Brazil; Malaysia; Kingdom of Saudi Arabia; Mexico,"New Newcastle disease outbreak confirmed in Santa Catarina, spurring new containment measures in the state.",Novo foco da doença de Newcastle é confirmado em SC e mobiliza novas medidas de contenção no Estado,2026-11-04T12:38:35+00:00,https://www.nsctotal.com.br/saude/novo-foco-da-doenca-de-newcastle-e-confirmado-em-sc-e-mobiliza-novas-medidas-de-contencao-no-estado,PORTUGUESE,animals,"New Newcastle disease outbreak confirmed in Santa Catarina, Brazil. On Nov 3, 2026, a new outbreak was confirmed at a poultry facility in Nova Erechim. This brings four foci in the state, two in Nova Erechim and one in Nova Itaberaba and Coronel Freitas, since a zoosanitary emergency was declared. More than 47,000 birds have been culled. Farms are undergoing depopulation with cleaning and disinfection under Cidasc; most are in sanitary depopulation awaiting new stock. About 70 establishments have tested negative; further analyses will guide exports. Countries suspending Brazilian poultry imports include China, Mexico, Saudi Arabia, Malaysia and Chile. Mexico and Malaysia paused; Chile, Saudi Arabia and China restrict Santa Catarina-origin goods. Newcastle disease is a contagious viral infection in birds; severity varies by strain; symptoms include respiratory problems, diarrhea and neurological signs, with high mortality; transmission via secretions, feces, water, feed, equipment, or contaminated surfaces.",No,No,No,Yes,1,No,No,不明,No,不明,0,No,Yes,不明,ニューカッスル病は家禽の疾患でありヒトへの感染リスクは極めて低い。主な懸念は農業・貿易への経済的影響（中国、メキシコ、サウジアラビア、マレーシア、チリがブラジル産家禽の輸入を一部停止）。公衆衛生イベントとしてのフルRRAは不要と判断。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYnRhLmJnL2JnL25ld3Mvd29ybGQvMTIzOTY3OC12LWtpdGF5c2tpLXNhZC16YXBvY2huYS1kZWxvdG8tc3Jlc2h0dS1hbWVyaWthbnNraXlhLXNodGF0LW1pc3VyaS16YXJhZGktcGFuZGVtaQ==,DISMISS,COVID-19に関する新規の公衆衛生事象ではなく、訴訟・外交的な法的対立に関する報道であり、感染症の発生動向や公衆衛生リスクには該当しない。,COVID-19,Hubei Sheng; Missouri; Wuhan; United States,"In a Chinese court, the case against the U.S. state of Missouri began because of the COVID-19 pandemic.",В китайски съд започна делото срещу американския щат Мисури заради пандемията от КОВИД-19,2026-11-04T12:52:13+00:00,https://www.bta.bg/bg/news/world/1239678-v-kitayski-sad-zapochna-deloto-sreshtu-amerikanskiya-shtat-misuri-zaradi-pandemi,BULGARIAN,humans; environment,"November 4, 2026 — A Wuhan, China court began hearings in a $53 billion damages case against the U.S. state of Missouri over alleged harm to China's reputation during the COVID-19 pandemic. The Wuhan Municipal Court, in the city where the virus was first detected in late 2019, said the case had been publicly heard last Friday and remains ongoing. Plaintiffs—the Wuhan city government, the Chinese Academy of Sciences, and the Wuhan Institute of Virology—seek 356 billion yuan (about $53 billion) and a public apology, accusing Missouri and three current or former state attorneys general of reputational harm and economic losses from alleged false pandemic claims. This suit follows Missouri’s 2020 lawsuit against China. In March 2025, a U.S. court awarded Missouri about $24.5 billion after Chinese defendants did not appear; China rejects the allegations and seeks to overturn the ruling.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,本記事は2019年末のCOVID-19発生を背景にした中米間の損害賠償訴訟に関する法廷報道であり、現在の感染症発生・流行事象ではないため対象国の感染症発生地としては該当しない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYWluZG9uZXNpYS5jb20vamFiYXIvYmVyaXRhLzk1MjM3OC9pbmRvbmVzaWEtcGVybHUtbWVtcGVya3VhdC1kZXRla3NpLWRpbmktdGJjLWRlbGZ0LWltYWdpbmctZHVrdW5nLXBlbmFuZ2FuYW5ueWE=,DISMISS,既知の慢性的な結核流行に関する一般的な報道であり、新規性・異常性がなく、AIスクリーニング技術の紹介が主旨であるため、緊急のシグナルとは言えない。,Tuberculosis,Republic of Indonesia,"Indonesia Needs to Strengthen Early TB Detection, Delft Imaging Supports Its Management.","Indonesia Perlu Memperkuat Deteksi Dini TBC, Delft Imaging Dukung Penanganannya",2026-11-04T12:50:08+00:00,https://mediaindonesia.com/jabar/berita/952378/indonesia-perlu-memperkuat-deteksi-dini-tbc-delft-imaging-dukung-penanganannya,INDONESIAN,humans,"Early tuberculosis (TB) detection is pivotal in Indonesia, where TB remains a major public health challenge. Delft Imaging reports over 2 million Indonesians have undergone TB screening using CAD4TB, an AI-assisted chest X-ray analysis tool, developed through long-running partnerships with health providers, government programs, mining firms, and implementers to speed case finding and broaden screening nationwide. The WHO Global Tuberculosis Report 2024 notes Indonesia is one of eight countries that together account for about two-thirds of global TB cases, with an approximate 10% share of global TB burden. In 2025, WHO estimates >1 million TB cases in Indonesia and about 134,000 deaths annually. World TB Day 2026 figures from Indonesia’s Ministry of Health warn that two people are infected and one dies every minute and every four minutes, respectively. While expanding screening is vital, timely diagnostics, treatment access, and patient support are essential to reach TB elimination by 2030. Experts emphasize addressing undetected cases and targeting high-risk groups with AI-enhanced screening.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,No,No,No,結核は既知の風土病であり突発的な公衆衛生イベントではないため、トリアージの対象外（DISMISS）と判断。,
