aHR0cHM6Ly9uaGFuZGFuLnZuL3NpZXQtY2hhdC1waG9uZy1jaG9uZy1kaWNoLXRhLWhlby1jaGF1LXBoaS1wb3N0MTAwMDIzMC5odG1s,WATCH,アフリカ豚熱（ASF）は豚のみに感染し人への健康被害はないが、ベトナム・カントー市で拡大が続き食料安全保障への懸念があるため、動物衛生面での経過観察が必要。,African Swine Fever,Socialist Republic of Vietnam,Tighten prevention and control measures for African swine fever.,"Siết chặt phòng, chống dịch tả heo châu Phi",2026-11-04T12:51:28+00:00,https://nhandan.vn/siet-chat-phong-chong-dich-ta-heo-chau-phi-post1000230.html,VIETNAMESE,environment; animals,"ASF in Can Tho City, Vietnam, has spread to 31 communes/wards as of Oct 29, with nearly 2,000 pigs culled. Nineteen communes still report outbreaks beyond 21 days, signaling ongoing risk as year-end transport and slaughter rise. The city's pig herd surpassed 507,000 in September 2026, with pork output over 83,000 tons, underscoring food-security concerns ahead of Tet. Contributing factors include widespread smallholder farming, inadequate biosecurity, mixed housing of sows, piglets and fatteners, and increased movement of pigs and products; some farmers sell diseased pigs or slaughter without proper controls, risking environmental contamination. Authorities have invoked Decree 116/2025 and Resolution 44/2025, including 40,000 VND per kg for culled diseased pigs. About 20 of 103 communes lack veterinary staff; coordination gaps persist. Plans emphasize surveillance, rapid testing, prompt culling, tightened transport/slaughter controls, crackdown on illegal slaughter, vaccination, and data updates in the Vietnam Animal Disease Information Management System.",No,No,不明,不明,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,ASFは人獣共通感染症ではなく、IHR(2005)上の公衆衛生事象には該当しない。ただし養豚業への経済的影響・食料安全保障（Tet前の豚肉供給）への懸念があり、動物衛生当局の対応状況を注視する必要がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cua2lrYXIuY28uaWwvc2Nvb3AtbmV3cy85MDgxNQ==,DISMISS,疑い患者2名のエボラ検査結果は陰性であり、イスラエル国内での感染確認はないため、現時点でシグナルとしての重要性は低い。,Ebola,State of Israel,Ministry of Health: Negative Ebola test results for two patients.,משרד הבריאות: תוצאות שליליות לבדיקות אבולה של שני מטופלים,2026-11-04T12:46:10+00:00,https://www.kikar.co.il/scoop-news/90815,HEBREW,humans,"On 4 November 2026, Israel’s Ministry of Health announced that two patients hospitalized yesterday on suspicion of Ebola tested negative. Both individuals had returned from the Democratic Republic of Congo and developed fever after their return. The ministry stressed that there is currently no confirmed Ebola case in Israel. No further exposure or contact details were provided. Despite travel from an Ebola-affected region, the immediate concern for these cases has been resolved with negative laboratory results. The report underscores ongoing monitoring of travelers from high-risk regions and the importance of rapid testing to distinguish Ebola from other febrile illnesses. No other Ebola-related updates were provided.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事はイスラエル国内での疑い例が陰性と判明したことを報じており、DRCでの新たな発生状況については言及がないため、DRCも含め対象国は該当なしとした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmV3c3J1LmNvLmlsL2hlYWx0aC80bm92MjAyNi9lYm9sYV9pbF8xMzUuaHRtbA==,DISMISS,疑い症例は検査の結果陰性と確定しており、実際の感染事例は存在しないため、シグナルとしての対応は不要。,Ebola,State of Israel,Israel's Ministry of Health: suspicions of Ebola infection in two patients were not confirmed.,Минздрав Израиля: подозрения на заражение лихорадкой Эбола у двух пациентов не подтвердились,2026-11-04T12:43:56+00:00,https://www.newsru.co.il/health/4nov2026/ebola_il_135.html,RUSSIAN,humans,"Israel's Ministry of Health announced on November 4, 2026, that Ebola testing for two patients hospitalized yesterday with suspected infection returned negative. Both individuals had recently returned from the Democratic Republic of Congo and developed fever after their arrival in Israel, leading to their hospitalization and medical evaluation. They were examined in accordance with international protocols for dealing with highly dangerous infectious diseases. The ministry emphasizes that there are currently no confirmed Ebola cases in Israel.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,疑い例はイスラエルで発生したが検査陰性のため実際の感染確認なし。DRCでの発生は記事の主題ではなく、確定症例についての言及もないためverified_locationsには含めない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9ub3RpY2lhcy51b2wuY29tLmJyL3NhdWRlL3VsdGltYXMtbm90aWNpYXMvcmVkYWNhby8yMDI2LzExLzA0L3Jpby1jb25maXJtYS0yNjktY2Fzb3MtZGUtbXBveC1lLWVzcGVyYS1yZWZvcmNvLWRlLXZhY2luYXMuZ2h0bQ==,WATCH,リオデジャネイロ州でmpox症例が前年同期比で増加しているが死亡例はなく、既存の対策（ワクチン接種、優先グループへの対応）が継続されており緊急性は低いため経過観察とする。,Mpox; HIV,Rio de Janeiro; Rio de Janeiro; Federative Republic of Brazil,Rio de Janeiro confirms 269 mpox cases in 2026 and expects a vaccine boost.,Rio confirma 269 casos de mpox em 2026 e espera reforço de vacinas,2026-11-04T12:49:29+00:00,https://noticias.uol.com.br/saude/ultimas-noticias/redacao/2026/11/04/rio-confirma-269-casos-de-mpox-e-espera-reforco-de-vacinas.ghtm,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Rio de Janeiro state, Brazil, reports 269 mpox cases and no deaths in 2026 as of 3 November, higher than 92 cases through 3 November 2025. The Health Secretariat notes vaccination progress with 953 doses administered by 2 November 2026 and anticipates stock replenishment due to increased end-year mobility. The two-dose vaccine regimen uses a 28-day interval. Priority groups include laboratory workers handling Orthopoxviruses, people living with HIV/AIDS with immunosuppression, and direct contacts at medium or high risk of exposure after health surveillance assessment. Public guidance urges avoiding contact with individuals with skin or mucosal lesions, not sharing personal items, avoiding intimate contact during symptoms, and seeking care for suspected lesions.",No,No,不明,No,0,Yes,No,Yes,Yes,No,3,不明,Yes,No,症例数は前年比で約3倍に増加しているが死亡例はゼロであり、州保健当局による既存のワクチン接種プログラムやサーベイランス体制が機能している。HIV感染者など免疫抑制状態にある者が優先接種対象に含まれる点に留意。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cua2lrYXIuY28uaWwvaXNyYWVsLW5ld3MvZWJvbGEtdGVzdC1yZXN1bHRzLW5lZ2F0aXZlLWNvbmdvLXJldHVybmVlcw==,DISMISS,イスラエルでのエボラ疑い症例は検査の結果陰性と確定しており、DRCでの実際の感染拡大を示す情報もないため、シグナルとしての意義は低い。,Ebola,Tel Litwinsky; Tel Aviv District; Tel Aviv; State of Israel,Test results are in: two Ebola suspects who arrived from Africa are negative.,תוצאות הבדיקות הגיעו: שני החשודים באבולה שהגיעו מאפריקה - שליליים,2026-11-04T12:42:23+00:00,https://www.kikar.co.il/israel-news/ebola-test-results-negative-congo-returnees,HEBREW,humans,"Two individuals who returned from the Democratic Republic of Congo were hospitalized yesterday in Israel on suspicion of Ebola. Lab tests were completed today and the results were negative, with the Health Ministry confirming that there is no confirmed Ebola case in Israel. The patients were admitted under isolation, one at Sheba Medical Center in Tel Hashomer and the other at Ichilov Medical Center in Tel Aviv, both designated as centers for suspected high‑risk infections. An epidemiological investigation was conducted to identify relevant contacts; those who did not receive a Health Ministry outreach are not required to take any action. Ebola virus transmission occurs by direct contact with a symptomatic patient or with blood, body fluids, contaminated materials, or infected animals; it is not airborne. Tests followed professional and international guidelines, and negative results remove the suspicion of infection.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事はイスラエル国内での疑い症例の陰性確定を報じるものであり、DRCにおける実際のエボラ発生状況についての新規情報は含まれていないため、DRCもverified_locationsには含めない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaW5kZXBlbmRlbnQuY28udWsvbmV3cy91ay9ob21lLW5ld3MvZWJvbGEtb3V0YnJlYWstdWsta2VueWEtc3ltcHRvbXMtYjMwNzkwMzYuaHRtbA==,PICKUP,DRCで1万人超の症例・5千人超の死亡を伴う大規模なエボラ（ブンディブギョウイルス）流行が継続し、ケニア・ナイジェリアへの渡航関連症例が確認されるなど国際的拡大がみられるため、IHR基準を複数満たしフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,Could Ebola reach the UK? A microbiologist explains the risk,2026-11-04T12:39:24+00:00,https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/home-news/ebola-outbreak-uk-kenya-symptoms-b3079036.html,ENGLISH,humans; environment,"By Oct 31, 2026, the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) reported 10,467 Ebola cases and 5,103 deaths due to Bundibugyo virus, with Kenya and Nigeria confirming travel-associated cases and Uganda previously affected. Ongoing conflict and humanitarian crisis hinder detection, treatment, and contact tracing, while cross-border movement increases introduction risk to neighbouring countries. The UK risk is assessed as low by UKHSA; Europe’s risk is rated low. Ebola spreads through close contact with fluids from symptomatic patients; transmission via coughing or sneezing is not typical, and infectiousness begins after symptoms appear. There is no approved vaccine or specific treatment for Bundibugyo virus; options are under investigation. The UK has protocols for suspected imported cases, including diagnosis, lab testing, and contact tracing, and monitoring aid workers returning from areas, with specialist NHS centres prepared for isolation. International cooperation and rapid diagnosis remain critical to containment.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,発生地域にはケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリア・英国が含まれるが、これらは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。記事の主題であるDRCのみをverified_locationsとした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaW5mb3NhbHVzLmNvbS9zYWx1ZC1pbnZlc3RpZ2FjaW9uL25vdGljaWEtcmRjb25nby1icm90ZS1lYm9sYS1yZGMtc3VwZXJhLXVtYnJhbC0xMDUwMC1jYXNvcy1tZW5vcy1zZWlzLW1lc2VzLTIwMjYxMTA0MTM1NTAwLmh0bWw=,PICKUP,致死率約48.7%の大規模エボラ流行がDRC7州に拡大し、ケニア・ナイジェリアへの関連症例も報告されており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するため。,Ebola,Tshopo; South Kivu Province; Bas Uele; Haut Uele; Nord Ubangi; Province de l’Équateur; Ituri; Republic of the Sudan; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria,"DRC - The Ebola outbreak in DR Congo surpasses the 10,500 threshold.",RDCongo.- El brote de ébola en RDC supera el umbral de los 10.500...,2026-11-04T12:55:00+00:00,https://www.infosalus.com/salud-investigacion/noticia-rdcongo-brote-ebola-rdc-supera-umbral-10500-casos-menos-seis-meses-20261104135500.html,SPANISH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) has exceeded 10,500 cases, with 10,532 infections and 5,126 deaths; 65 cases and 23 deaths were reported in the last day. Case fatality rate stands at 48.7%. There are 961 patients hospitalised or in isolation, 2,834 recovered, and contact tracing coverage at 84%. The seven-province spread includes Ituri (epicenter, 70.6% of cases), North Kivu, South Kivu, Haut-Uele, Bas-Uele, Tshopo, North Ubangi, and South Ubangi. Ituri remains the epicenter, and the outbreak is the deadliest in DRC history, with projections that it could surpass 2014–2016 West Africa’s 11,325 deaths. Recent linked cases have appeared in Kenya and Nigeria; Uganda had declared itself virus-free earlier. Separately, UNICEF delivered 50 tonnes of supplies to South Sudan to bolster Ebola preparedness, including PPE and infection-control materials, and to reinforce prevention standards and community awareness.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ケニア・ナイジェリアでの関連症例、南スーダンへのUNICEF支援が言及されているが、これらは対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations には含めていない。DRC史上最悪の流行となる可能性が指摘されている。,
