、ウガンダの以前のエボラ終息宣言、南スーダンへのUNICEF支援物資提供が言及されているが、これらは対象国リストに含まれないか、または現時点で発生国として確認されていないため verified_locations には含めていない。2014-2016年西アフリカ流行（ギニア・リベリア・シエラレオネ）は歴史的比較として言及されているのみで現行の発生地域ではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYWluZG9uZXNpYS5jb20vamFiYXIvYmVyaXRhLzk1MjQwNS90ZXJpbWEtbGFwb3Jhbi1wZW5jZW1hcmFuLWJha3RlcmktZS1jb2xpLXBlbWtvdC1iYW5kdW5nLXBlcmtldGF0LWtlYmVyc2loYW4tc2FuaXRhc2k=,DISMISS,河川の大腸菌汚染と衛生インフラの課題に関する行政対応の記事であり、ヒトの急性感染症アウトブレイクの報告ではないため、IHR・WPRO基準のいずれにも明確に該当しない。,E. coli,Jawa Barat; Bandung; Republic of Indonesia,Bandung City Government Tightens Sanitation Standards After Reports of E. coli Contamination,"Terima Laporan Pencemaran Bakteri E-Coli, Pemkot Bandung Perketat Kebersihan Sanitasi",2026-11-04T13:22:24+00:00,https://mediaindonesia.com/jabar/berita/952405/terima-laporan-pencemaran-bakteri-e-coli-pemkot-bandung-perketat-kebersihan-sanitasi,INDONESIAN,humans; environment,"Bandung, Indonesia — In response to NGO findings that nearly 90% of rivers surveyed in Bandung show E. coli contamination, the Bandung City Government tightened environmental sanitation and drinking-water quality oversight to reduce diarrheal infections and risk of stunting in children. The city coordinates with relevant agencies to maintain water hygiene standards. The Ministry of Trade states that thousands of drinking-water refill outlets meet health standards, with 800 refill-gallon outlets in Bandung confirmed compliant. The administration also maps municipal sanitation, noting about 27% of households still dispose of wastewater directly without septic tanks. Although public awareness of avoiding open defecation is high, infrastructure gaps remain and require phased improvements. E. coli infections threaten early childhood growth and immune health, prompting enhanced surveillance and sanitation investments as of November 4, 2026.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,No,No,1,No,Yes,No,具体的な感染者数・症例報告はなく、環境モニタリング結果に基づく予防的な衛生対策の記事。急性アウトブレイクの兆候はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZWxiYWxhZC5uZXdzLzcxNjc5NDA=,PICKUP,DRCで継続中のエボラ流行に関する国際的な注目度が高く、フランスによる支援活動や他国での疑い例発生など社会的・政治的関心が高いため、フルRRAでの確認が望ましい。,Ebola,Paris; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Bunia; State of Israel; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of France,Ebola virus in Israel... Urgent statement from the Occupation's Health Ministry regarding the dangerous epidemic.,فيروس إيبولا في إسرائيل.. بيان عاجل من صحة الاحتلال بشأن الوباء الخطير,2026-11-04T13:13:51+00:00,https://www.elbalad.news/7167940,ARABIC,humans,"Two suspected Ebola cases in Israel, recently returned from the Democratic Republic of Congo, tested negative after hospital admission yesterday with fever. Israeli Health Ministry confirmed no confirmed Ebola cases in Israel at this time, with tests conducted per professional protocols and international guidelines for high-consequence diseases. The Democratic Republic of Congo continues to face an Ebola outbreak, centered in Kinshasa and Bunia. France announced a shipment of 1.5 tonnes of medicines to support NGOs on the outbreak’s front lines in the DRC, during Paris talks between Jean-Noël Barrot and Therese Wagner, the DRC’s minister of state for foreign affairs, cooperation and Francophonie. The shipment followed Barrot’s month-long visit to Kinshasa and Bunia, reaffirming France’s solidarity with Congolese authorities and people.",Yes,No,不明,不明,1,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事の主眼はイスラエルでの疑い例（陰性確定）だが、イスラエルは対象国リスト外のため除外。実際の感染発生国はDRC（キンシャサ・ブニア中心の継続中アウトブレイク）であり、フランスからの医薬品支援など国際的関心が示されている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9qYWJhci5qcG5uLmNvbS9qYWJhci10ZXJraW5pLzM0MTU1L3NrcmluaW5nLXRiYy1iZXJiYXNpcy1haS1qYW5na2F1LTItanV0YS1vcmFuZy1rYXN1cy1iZWx1bS10ZXJkZXRla3NpLWphZGktdGFudGFuZ2Fu,DISMISS,既知の慢性的な結核流行に関する公衆衛生施策・啓発報道であり、突発的・異常な感染症イベントではないため、シグナルとしての基準を満たさない。,Tuberculosis; HIV,Jawa Barat; Bandung; Republic of Indonesia,"AI-Based TB Screening Reaches 2 Million People, Undetected Cases Remain a Challenge.","Skrining TBC Berbasis AI Jangkau 2 Juta Orang, Kasus Belum Terdeteksi Jadi Tantangan",2026-11-04T13:18:00+00:00,https://jabar.jpnn.com/jabar-terkini/34155/skrining-tbc-berbasis-ai-jangkau-2-juta-orang-kasus-belum-terdeteksi-jadi-tantangan,INDONESIAN,humans,"Indonesia faces an estimated 1.09 million tuberculosis (TB) cases annually, with undetected infections hindering early treatment and fueling transmission, a barrier to eliminating TB by 2030. As of November 4, 2026, AI-based TB screening has reached 2 million people, signaling progress but not closing the detection gap. Professor Erlina Burhan warns that delayed diagnosis increases transmission risk and access barriers persist. She calls for expanded active screening, especially among high-risk groups such as household contacts of TB patients, people living with HIV, infants and children, the elderly, and those with weakened immune systems. The remarks, reported from Kota Bandung and Indonesia, highlight the urgent need to boost detection and timely treatment to curb spread and move toward elimination.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,No,No,No,結核は既知の地域流行病であり、本記事はAIスクリーニング事業の進捗報告。急性・異常な感染症アウトブレイクではないためDISMISS相当だが、結核の継続的な感染曝露の観点からWPRO基準の『長期曝露』のみ該当。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9ub3RpY2lhcy5yNy5jb20vYnJhc2lsaWEvZGYtbm8tYXIvdmlkZW8vY2h1dmEtcmVmb3JjYS1hbGVydGEtcGFyYS1wcmV2ZW5jYW8tZGEtZGVuZ3VlLW5vLWRpc3RyaXRvLWZlZGVyYWwtMDQxMTIwMjYv,DISMISS,通常の季節性デング熱予防啓発記事であり、異常な流行や重症例の急増を示す情報はなく、公的機関の定例的な予防活動の報告に留まる。,Dengue,Federative Republic of Brazil,Rain heightens dengue-prevention alert in the Federal District.,Chuva reforça alerta para prevenção da dengue no Distrito Federal,2026-11-04T13:37:47+00:00,https://noticias.r7.com/brasilia/df-no-ar/video/chuva-reforca-alerta-para-prevencao-da-dengue-no-distrito-federal-04112026/,PORTUGUESE,humans; vectors; environment,"As of 2026-11-04, dengue prevention efforts in Brazil's Federal District intensify amid ongoing rainfall. Water accumulation in bottles, pots, backyards, and abandoned lots promotes Aedes aegypti, the dengue vector. Environmental Surveillance agents urge residents to wash containers with soap and water, scrubbing their rims to remove potential mosquito eggs. Health authorities also employ larvicide-dispensing traps and perform residual spraying in areas with high human activity. More than 40,000 youths aged 10–14 who received the first vaccine dose have not yet returned to complete the immunization schedule. The weather-driven risk underscores the need for household vigilance and vector-control measures to curb transmission, alongside vaccination completion to strengthen population immunity.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,No,記事は雨季によるデング熱媒介蚊の繁殖リスクへの注意喚起と、ワクチン接種未完了者への呼びかけが主内容。症例数の急増や異常事態の報告はなし。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9rdXJpci5tay92ZXN0aS9zdmV0L2tpcGFyLWtlLW9kdm9pLTEwMC0wMDAtemEtcG9tb3NoLXphLXNwcmF2dXZhbmUtc28tZXBpZGVtaWphdGEtbmEtZWJvbGEtdm8tZHIta29uZ28v,WATCH,エボラ出血熱はIHR基準に該当しうる重大疾患だが、本記事はキプロスの資金拠出に関する内容でDRC国内の最新疫学情報（症例数・拡大状況等）が含まれておらず、既知の流行への国際支援表明に留まるため続報を注視する。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Cyprus,"Cyprus will allocate 100,000 for aid to combat the Ebola epidemic in the DRC.",Кипар ќе одвои 100.000 за помош за справување со епидемијата на ебола во ДР Конго,2026-11-04T13:41:43+00:00,https://kurir.mk/vesti/svet/kipar-ke-odvoi-100-000-za-pomosh-za-spravuvane-so-epidemijata-na-ebola-vo-dr-kongo/,MACEDONIAN,humans,"Cyprus will allocate €100,000 through the CyprusAid humanitarian mechanism managed by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, to be channeled via the World Health Organization to support humanitarian and health activities addressing the Ebola epidemic in the Democratic Republic of Congo. The commitment, announced by the Cypriot MFA and reported by the Athens-based MIA correspondent, is dated 2026-11-04. The funds aim to bolster the international response in DRC, though the article does not specify the exact activities, beneficiaries, or outbreak milestones. No Cyprus-specific case counts, laboratory confirmations, or infection sources are mentioned. This action underscores Cyprus's contribution to global Ebola response efforts through multilateral channels.",Yes,不明,不明,不明,1,不明,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,3,No,Yes,Yes,キプロスは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。DRCのエボラ流行自体の最新状況（症例数・地域拡大等）は本記事に記載なく、国際支援表明のみの内容。,
