aHR0cHM6Ly9iYW90aW50dWMudm4vZGUteS1uaHVuZy12aWVjLW5oby1kZS1kYXktbHVpLWRpY2gtc290LXh1YXQtaHV5ZXQtaGlldS1xdWEtcG9zdDEzOTk5MjYuaHRtbA==,WATCH,ハノイでの季節性デング熱流行が継続し症例数は多いが死亡例はなく、異常性や国際的拡大の兆候は見られないため、続報を注視する段階と判断。,Dengue,Ngọc Trụ; Thành Phố Hà Nội; Hanoi; Dại Mõ; Socialist Republic of Vietnam,Pay attention to the small things to effectively curb the dengue outbreak.,Để ý những việc nhỏ để đẩy lùi dịch sốt xuất huyết hiệu quả,2026-11-04T10:28:27+00:00,https://baotintuc.vn/de-y-nhung-viec-nho-de-day-lui-dich-sot-xuat-huyet-hieu-qua-post1399926.html,VIETNAMESE,vectors; humans; environment,"Dengue outbreak in Hanoi, Vietnam: Hanoi CDC reports hundreds of dengue cases weekly; last week 550 new cases across 97 wards/communes with 12 new clusters; previous week 429; total 5,839 cases since start of 2026, across 121 wards/communes; no fatalities. Transmission by Aedes mosquitoes; risk persists if larval habitats are not detected and eliminated. Vector-control measures include environmental sanitation, larval source elimination, and adulticide spraying at high-risk locations, including areas with active cases. Local authorities in Ngoc Tru, Dai Mo, and Cau Giay are conducting campaigns; surveillance by health stations and community teams; households asked to inspect and clean water containers, drain and cover tanks, rinse and replenish water in decorative pots, add fish in decorative ponds, flip unused containers. Dengue vaccine is available; residents urged to get vaccinated. People with sudden high fever, headache, bleeding under the skin should seek medical care promptly; avoid self-treatment. Community involvement is essential.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,記事は季節性デング熱に関する公衆衛生啓発記事であり、地元当局による媒介蚊対策・ワクチン接種呼びかけが中心。死亡例なく、重症度や社会的関心の高まりについての明確な記載はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9uYXNpb25hbC5rb21wYXMuY29tL3JlYWQvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC8yMDI5NDc2MS9rZW1lbmtlcy1rYXN1cy1pc3BhLWFraWJhdC1rYXJodXRsYS10ZW1idXMtNDAxNTg2LWRpLTctcHJvdmluc2k=,WATCH,森林火災によるスモッグが原因の急性呼吸器症状であり感染症のヒト-ヒト感染ではないが、症例数が40万件超と大規模かつ脆弱層への健康影響が継続しているため経過観察とする。,Unknown Illness,Provinsi Kalimantan Timur; Provinsi Kalimantan Tengah; Provinsi Kalimantan Barat; Kabupaten Kotawaringin Timur; Provinsi Riau; Sumatera Selatan; Palangkaraya; Republic of Indonesia,"Ministry of Health: Acute Respiratory Infection (ARI) cases due to forest and land fires reach 401,586 in seven provinces.",Kemenkes: Kasus ISPA akibat Karhutla Tembus 401.586 di 7 Provinsi,2026-11-04T13:29:47+00:00,https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2026/11/04/20294761/kemenkes-kasus-ispa-akibat-karhutla-tembus-401586-di-7-provinsi,INDONESIAN,humans; environment,"Acute Respiratory Infection (ARIs) linked to forest and land fires in Indonesia has risen to 401,586 cumulative cases across seven provinces and 63 districts/cities as of 2 November 2026 at 16:00 WIB, per the Ministry of Health; the daily increase on that date was 3,906 cases. Children 0–5 years account for 91,913 cases, ages 6–9 for 87,704, and adults 60+ for 56,092. Vulnerable groups include 590 pregnant women, 1,530 asthma patients, and 8,086 outdoor workers at risk due to smoke exposure. Regional trends vary: decreases in Central Kalimantan, South Sumatra, and Riau; increases in East Kalimantan and West Kalimantan, with East Kalimantan of particular concern. Air quality (ISPU) on 3 November 2026 shows two jurisdictions with hazardous PM2.5 and 15 with unhealthy levels; Kotawaringin Timur PM2.5 580 and Palangka Raya 348 are flagged as hazardous. Pneumonia risk remains a serious concern for the vulnerable.",Yes,No,No,No,1,No,Yes,Yes,No,不明,2,Yes,Yes,不明,本事例は森林・泥炭火災による大気汚染（PM2.5）に起因する急性呼吸器感染症であり、感染症（病原体によるヒト-ヒト感染）ではなく環境要因による健康影響である。インドネシアでは毎年の乾季に繰り返される季節性の事象であり、国際的な感染拡大リスクは低いが、大規模な症例数・脆弱層（乳幼児、高齢者、妊婦、喘息患者）への影響・有害な大気質レベルが継続している点から注視が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9mci5hbGxhZnJpY2EuY29tL3N0b3JpZXMvMjAyNjExMDQwNDY3Lmh0bWw=,PICKUP,DRCで進行中の第17次エボラ出血熱アウトブレイクおよびコレラ流行に対するWHOの物資支援に関する記事であり、IHR基準（深刻性・異常性・国際拡大リスク）を複数満たすためフルリスク評価に進むべきと判断。,Cholera; Ebola,Kindu; Province du Maniema; Democratic Republic of the Congo,Africa: WHO allocates at least 7 tonnes of medical supplies to strengthen preparedness against Ebola and cholera in Maniema.,Afrique: L'OMS octroie au moins 7 tonnes d'intrants médicaux pour renforcer la préparation contre Ebola et le choléra au Maniema,2026-11-04T13:36:59+00:00,https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202611040467.html,FRENCH,humans; environment,"WHO delivered at least 7 tonnes of medical supplies on November 3 in Kindu, Maniema Province, Democratic Republic of the Congo, to the Provincial Division of Health to bolster preparedness and response to Ebola virus disease and to improve cholera management in a high-risk area. The consignment includes emergency health kits, essential medicines, cholera treatment inputs, and infection prevention and control equipment. The handover supports the ongoing 17th Ebola outbreak in the DRC and cholera outbreaks, strengthening infection prevention in health facilities and patient care. The WHO notes Maniema is among provinces at risk of Ebola spread and urges provincial authorities to prioritize these inputs to outbreak-affected zones. Dr. Jad Kabeya emphasizes prudent use and targeted allocation to the most affected health zones, as part of WHO's broader effort to bolster Congo's public health readiness for Ebola and cholera and other emergencies.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,不明,Yes,Yes,本記事は既に報告されているDRCの第17次エボラアウトブレイク及びコレラ流行への物資支援に関するものであり、新規イベントではないが、継続する公衆衛生上のリスクとしてフルRRAでの経過確認が妥当。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9mci5hbGxhZnJpY2EuY29tL3N0b3JpZXMvMjAyNjExMDQwNDY1Lmh0bWw=,DISMISS,新規の症例報告や疫学的変化を伴わない、既存のエボラ対応プログラムにおける研修活動の紹介記事であり、新たなシグナルとしての該当性は低い。,Ebola,Butembo; Province du Nord-Kivu; Democratic Republic of the Congo,DRC: North Kivu - IRC strengthens the capacity of community actors to better protect populations affected by Ebola.,Congo-Kinshasa: Nord-Kivu - L'IRC renforce les capacités des acteurs communautaires pour mieux protéger les populations affectées par Ebola,2026-11-04T13:36:58+00:00,https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202611040465.html,FRENCH,humans,"Two-day training in Butembo for about 30 community actors and health professionals aims to bolster protection of vulnerable groups—women, children, and families affected by Ebola—in North Kivu, DRC. Ebola virus disease brings health risks plus stigma, violence, abuse, and psychological distress. Trainees will identify vulnerabilities, provide initial psychosocial support, and refer cases to appropriate services while safeguarding confidentiality. IRC says the initiative makes the response safer and more humane by helping responders detect distress and risks of violence or exploitation and offer immediate support. Participants will be better prepared to address gender-based violence, child protection, and abuse within the Ebola response in the Grand North, and to engage communities to ease concerns and mistrust of Ebola treatment centers. Survivors and affected families will receive improved support from more trained staff handling sensitive information. Funded by Irish Aid.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,不明,不明,No,0,No,No,No,記事はエボラ対応の人道支援活動（IRCによる研修プログラム）を報じるもので、新規発生や症例数の変化など疫学的な新情報は含まれていない。既存の北キブ州でのエボラ対応状況の一環としての活動報告。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYW50YXJhbmV3cy5jb20vYmVyaXRhLzU4MzIyNzUvd2FtZW5rZXMtaW5kb25lc2lhLXRlbXBhdGktdXJ1dGFuLWtlZHVhLWthc3VzLXRiLXRlcmJhbnlhay1kaS1kdW5pYQ==,DISMISS,既知の慢性疾患である結核の国内対策・政策発表に関する内容であり、突発的・異常な公衆衛生事象ではないため、シグナルトリアージの対象外と判断。,Tuberculosis,North Sumatra; Republic of Indonesia,Deputy Health Minister: Indonesia ranks second in the world for TB cases.,Wamenkes: Indonesia tempati urutan kedua kasus Tb terbanyak di dunia,2026-11-04T13:44:28+00:00,https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5832275/wamenkes-indonesia-tempati-urutan-kedua-kasus-tb-terbanyak-di-dunia,INDONESIAN,humans,"Indonesia ranks second globally for tuberculosis (TB) cases after India, per Deputy Health Minister dr Benjamin Paulus Octavianus. In response, President Prabowo Subianto orders intensified TB management. At the launch of the National Pesantren Free-TB movement and the National Free Health Check program 2026, held at Mawaridussalam Pesantren in Desa Tumpatan, Deli Serdang, North Sumatra, the government notes that over 114 million Indonesians have used Free Health Check services (Cek Kesehatan Gratis). The initiative aims to make pesantren TB-free and empower santri as Health Ambassadors. The administration plans about Rp120 trillion to rehabilitate 441 regional hospitals and upgrade 1,988 Puskesmas nationwide starting next year. Deputy Home Affairs Akhmad Wiyagus and Vice Minister of Religious Affairs Romo Muhammad Syafii underscore local-government coordination with Health and Religious Affairs to sustain prevention, early detection, and treatment within pesantren communities.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,記事は結核の国内有病率と政府の対策プログラム（プサントレン結核フリー運動、医療施設改修等）に関する報道であり、新規アウトブレイクや異常事態ではない。インドが言及されているのは比較統計のためであり、インド国内の発生事例ではないため verified_locations から除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudHVuaXNpZW51bWVyaXF1ZS5jb20vZWJvbGEtcHJlcy1kZS01LTAwMC1tb3J0cy1sZS1yaXNxdWUtZHVuZS1wcm9wYWdhdGlvbi1tb25kaWFsZS1pbnF1aWV0ZS8=,PICKUP,DRCイツリ州でのエボラ流行（ブンディブギョ株）について、Africa CDCが国際的拡大リスクを警告しており、複数国への拡大報告がある。ただし感染者数・死者数は未検証・公式発表なしと明記されており、フルリスク評価での事実確認が必要。,Ebola,Africa; Ituri; Republic of France; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,"Ebola: nearly 5,000 deaths, the risk of a global spread is worrying - Tunisie Numerique.","Ebola : près de 5 000 morts, le risque d'une propagation mondiale inquiète - Tunisie Numerique",2026-11-04T13:45:00+00:00,https://www.tunisienumerique.com/ebola-pres-de-5-000-morts-le-risque-dune-propagation-mondiale-inquiete/,FRENCH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo’s Ituri province, declared May 15 with early transmissions dating back to February, involves the Bundibugyo strain. Africa CDC director Jean Kaseya warns of a risk of international spread, with the United Kingdom cited as a possible destination. Reported totals reach about 10,100 cases and 4,900 deaths, though independent verification is not available and no official bulletin is cited. The summary also notes deaths in Uganda and Kenya and reported cases in Nigeria and France, with dates and circumstances needing corroboration from health authorities. Transmission occurs mainly through direct contact with blood or other infectious fluids, including handling the body of a deceased patient; airborne spread is not the primary mode. Prevention centers on rapid detection, case management, contact tracing, protection of health workers, and vaccination when indicated.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,不明,3,Yes,不明,不明,"記事内で報告されている約10,100症例・4,900死亡という数値は独立した検証ができず、公式発表（WHO等）の引用もないため信頼性に強い疑問がある。ウガンダ・ケニア・ナイジェリア・フランスでの症例報告も対象国リスト外または未確認情報であり、verified_locationsには含めていない。フルRRAにおいてWHO・Africa CDCの公式情報源との照合が必須。",
aHR0cHM6Ly9zaWNodWFuLnNjb2wuY29tLmNuL2dneHcvMjAyNjExLzgzMzUxMzI4Lmh0bWw=,DISMISS,単発の個別症例報告であり、ヒト-ヒト感染性もなく公衆衛生上の深刻な拡大リスクは認められない。,Leptospirosis,Chengdu; Sichuan Sheng,"Sixty-something man admitted to ICU after an outdoor outing; was a tiny cut while washing his hands the culprit? Doctors warn to beware ""hookworm disease"".","郊游后六旬老人住进ICU，问题出在洗手时的一道小划伤？医生提醒警惕""钩体病""",2026-11-04T13:57:04+00:00,https://sichuan.scol.com.cn/ggxw/202611/83351328.html,CHINESE,humans; environment; animals,"Leptospira infection (leptospirosis) in Chengdu, Sichuan, China, hospitalized elderly woman after outdoor family outing. She developed high fever, severe fatigue, calf pain, and decreased urine; condition rapidly worsened with infection-related organ dysfunction and septic shock, leading to ICU admission. Metagenomic next-generation sequencing (mNGS) of clinical samples rapidly confirmed Leptospira as the causative pathogen. The exposure likely occurred when she sustained a minor skin puncture washing hands at an outdoor pond with contaminated water/soil from rodents. With sensitive antibiotics and multidisciplinary management, she recovered and was discharged. The disease is zoonotic, with rodents and pigs as reservoirs; emphasize prevention: avoid contact with stagnant water after rain, wear waterproof boots and gloves when wading or cleaning mud, cover wounds, and reduce exposure to animal urine.",No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,No,No,1,No,No,No,単一症例の健康啓発記事であり、集団発生や感染拡大の情報はない。対象国リストに中国は含まれるが、本事例は散発的個別症例であり地域的な公衆衛生イベントとは言えないため地域検証はスキップ可能だが念のため確認:中国(1814991)での発生だが個別症例のため重大性は低い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly94ZXUubXgvbmFjaW9uYWwvMTQzOTA4My9ldS1lbmR1cmVjZS1jb250cm9sZXMtZW4tdnVlbG9zLXBvci1icm90ZS1kZS1lYm9sYS1xdWUtcGFzYS1zaS12dWVsYXMtZGVzZGUtbWV4aWNv,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で発生したエボラ出血熱（ブンディブギョ株）の流行を受け、米国が渡航制限措置を導入しており、IHR基準の複数（深刻性・異常性・国際的拡大リスク・渡航制限）に該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,United States; Republic of the Sudan; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Uganda; Mexico,EU tightens flight controls due to an Ebola outbreak. What happens if you fly from Mexico?,EU endurece controles en vuelos por brote de ébola ¿Qué pasa si vuelas desde México?,2026-11-04T08:07:12+00:00,https://xeu.mx/nacional/1439083/eu-endurece-controles-en-vuelos-por-brote-de-ebola-que-pasa-si-vuelas-desde-mexico,SPANISH,humans; environment,"US health authorities impose new air-travel controls amid an Ebola outbreak caused by Bundibugyo ebolavirus in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. Effective November 3, 2026, travelers must declare they have not been in the DRC in the prior 21 days; those who transited or stayed there are barred from boarding flights to the United States. Additional checks target travelers who stayed in Uganda or South Sudan, with US citizens arriving from those countries required to use designated airports and undergo health screenings, and foreign nationals who have been in these zones face entry restrictions. The measures run through December 18, 2026, with possible adjustments as epidemiology evolves. There is no general quarantine for all travelers; individuals from Mexico, Europe, and other countries not in restricted zones are not automatically subjected to isolation. As of November 2, no confirmed US cases and overall risk remains low.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,"発生地域にUnited States, Sudan, Uganda, Mexicoが含まれるが、記事の主題である実際の発生国はDRC（コンゴ民主共和国）のみ。米国・ウガンダ・南スーダン・メキシコは渡航制限措置の対象国として言及されているに過ぎず、対象国リストにも含まれないため除外した。",
aHR0cHM6Ly9iYWxsb29uLWp1aWNlLmNvbS8yMDI2LzExLzA0L3BsYWd1ZXMtcGFuZGVtaWNzLXVwZGF0ZS1ub3ZlbWJlci00LTIwMjYv,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国におけるエボラ出血熱の流行が同国史上最大規模（症例6,000件超、死者5,000人超）に達し、8州67保健区域に拡大、新規感染の約8割が監視外の感染経路から発生しているため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。",COVID-19; Ebola; Influenza,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States; Canada; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,"Balloon Juice - Plagues & Pandemics Update - November 4, 2026",2026-11-04T13:56:53+00:00,https://balloon-juice.com/2026/11/04/plagues-pandemics-update-november-4-2026/,ENGLISH,humans; environment,"Flu surge in the United States with mid-October lab-confirmed hospitalizations at a 16-year high, fueling calls to get the flu shot. COVID-19 vaccination updates: experts urge taking the new vaccine; last year’s vaccine cut hospitalizations by about 55% and helped prevent ED visits and severe illness, with ongoing emphasis on protecting against Long COVID. COVID-19 trends as of Oct 28, 2026 show 22 states with rising infections, 6 declining, 14 unchanged. Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo: over 6,000 cases and more than 5,000 deaths, described as the largest in Congo’s history, spreading across 8 provinces and 67 health zones; about 80% of new cases arise from transmission chains outside monitored contacts, underscoring vaccination, surveillance, and containment needs, with no confirmed US wastewater detections yet. Paxlovid within 5 days linked to a 12% lower risk of Long COVID in high-risk adults, with no clear benefit for lower-risk individuals. Canadian activity is described as moderate; UK updates are noted without detailed figures.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事は米国のインフルエンザ流行、COVID-19ワクチン動向、Paxlovid研究など複数トピックを含む総合記事だが、公衆衛生上最も重大なのはコンゴのエボラ流行。米国・カナダ・英国は対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations から除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9leHByZXNzLjI0c2F0YS5oci90b3AtbmV3cy9zaXJpLXNlLXNtcnRvbm9zbmktdmlydXMtZ290b3ZvLTEwLTAwMC16YXJhemVuaWgtemFzdG8tZ2EtbmUtbW9ndS1zdXpiaXRpLTM0NDEz,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国でブンディブギョ・エボラウイルスによる大規模アウトブレイク（感染者約1万人、死者約5000人）が発生し、WHOが緊急事態を宣言するなど、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するため。,Tuberculosis; Ebola; Malaria,Democratic Republic of the Congo,"A deadly virus is spreading: nearly 10,000 infected, why can't it be contained?","Širi se smrtonosni virus: Gotovo 10.000 zaraženih, zašto ga ne mogu suzbiti?",2026-11-04T00:00:00+00:00,https://express.24sata.hr/top-news/siri-se-smrtonosni-virus-gotovo-10-000-zarazenih-zasto-ga-ne-mogu-suzbiti-34413,CROATIAN,humans; environment,"Bundibugyo virus drives one of Ebola’s largest outbreaks, centered in the DRC. About 10,000 infected and roughly 5,000 deaths; no specific vaccine is approved. By Oct 20, 2026, the DRC reported 9,704 confirmed cases and 4,687 deaths; later counts exceeded 10,000. The outbreak began early 2026, with patients showing fever, weakness, vomiting, and diarrhea, often mistaken for malaria or TB. Early tests for other ebolaviruses missed Bundibugyo in some cases; some patients do not hemorrhage. Transmission is via direct contact with blood, body fluids, or contaminated materials, not airborne. Over 300 health workers infected; 48 dead by Oct. PPE shortages and distrust hinder response; at least 12 attacks on health workers in three months; two aid volunteers killed in June in eastern DRC. Factors include poverty, conflict, displacement, and mobility; more than 90% of infections originate from unidentified sources. WHO declared a May 2026 emergency. The article notes USAID cuts harming the response.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,WHOは2026年5月に緊急事態を宣言。医療従事者300人以上が感染、48人死亡。USAID資金削減が対応を阻害していると報告されている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hY3AuY2QvcHJvdmluY2UvZWJvbGEtZW4taXR1cmktbGEtbW9udXNjby1yZW5mb3JjZS1sYS1wcm90ZWN0aW9uLWRlcy1wb2xpY2llcnMv,PICKUP,DRC・イチュリ州でエボラ出血熱の発生に対しMONUSCOが警察への防護資機材供与を実施しており、既存のアウトブレイク対応が継続中であることを示す。エボラは重篤度・国際的関心が高く、IHR基準・WPRO基準を複数満たす。,Ebola,Ituri; Bunia; Democratic Republic of the Congo,Ebola in Ituri: MONUSCO Strengthens Police Protection - ACP,Ebola en Ituri : la Monusco renforce la protection des policiers - ACP,2026-11-04T14:21:04+00:00,https://acp.cd/province/ebola-en-ituri-la-monusco-renforce-la-protection-des-policiers/,FRENCH,humans; environment,"MONUSCO provides Ebola-protection equipment to the Congolese National Police in Bunia, Ituri, DR Congo, as of 4 November 2026, to limit police exposure during Ebola response and safeguard communities. The equipment, delivered via UNPOL, includes 500 FFP2/N95 masks, 20 infrared thermometers, 100 hand sanitizers, 125 liquid soap units, ten 100-liter handwashing stations, gloves, chlorine powder, trash bags, and Ebola prevention leaflets (700) and posters (100). Five Ituri PNC units—the provincial police, Bunia Police School, the urban police station, the Mobile Intervention Group, and the Squad against crime and drugs—will use it to strengthen checkpoint management and response operations in coordination with health authorities. The provincial police commissioner urged proper use and adherence to prevention measures. MONUSCO will continue supporting the PNC to protect populations and bolster operational capacity.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はエボラ対応における警察への防護資機材提供の報道であり、感染者数や死亡者数など疫学データの具体的記載はない。既存のアウトブレイクの継続対応と見られるが、発生規模・拡大状況については続報の確認が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYWluZG9uZXNpYS5jb20va2VzZWhhdGFuLzk1MjQ1MS9pbmRvbmVzaWEtcGVyaW5na2F0LTItdHViZXJrdWxvc2lzLXBlbmFuZ2FuYW4tZGktcGVzYW50cmVuLWRpZ2VuY2Fya2Fu,DISMISS,既知の慢性的な結核流行状況に関する政府の既存対策強化の報道であり、突発的・異常な公衆衛生事象ではないため。,Tuberculosis,North Sumatra; Republic of Indonesia,"Indonesia Ranks No. 2 in Tuberculosis, Treatment at Pesantrens Intensified.","Indonesia Peringkat 2 Tuberkulosis, Penanganan di Pesantren Digencarkan",2026-11-04T14:26:53+00:00,https://mediaindonesia.com/kesehatan/952451/indonesia-peringkat-2-tuberkulosis-penanganan-di-pesantren-digencarkan,INDONESIAN,humans,"Indonesia ranks second worldwide in tuberculosis (TB) cases after India, prompting President Prabowo Subianto to order intensified TB control nationwide. On Nov 4, 2026, at Pondok Pesantren Mawaridussalam in Desa Tumpatan, Deli Serdang, North Sumatra, Deputy Health Minister Benjamin Paulus Octavianus launched the National Pesantren Free TB Movement and the National Free Health Check (CKG) 2026. He noted that over 114 million Indonesians have used the Free Health Check service. The program aims to make pesantren TB-free and to empower santri as Health Ambassadors in their communities. Beyond TB, the government will allocate about Rp120 trillion to rehabilitate 441 regional hospitals and upgrade 1,988 Puskesmas starting next year. Inter-ministerial and regional cooperation is emphasized to ensure health education, early detection, periodic screenings, and proper treatment.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,No,Yes,No,結核はインドネシアにおける既知のエンデミック疾患であり、本記事は政府の既存対策（プサントレンでのTBフリー運動、無料健康診断拡充など）の発表に関する内容。インドはTB罹患数比較で言及されているのみで、インド国内の発生事象ではないためverified_locationsから除外。,
