aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYnJlaXRiYXJ0LmNvbS9hZnJpY2EvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9lYm9sYS1tb3J0YWxpdHktcmlzZXMtb3Zlci01MC1pbi1kci1jb25nby8=,PICKUP,WHOがPHEICを宣言した大規模エボラ流行（1万例超、致死率51.6%）で、ケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリア・フランス・イスラエルへの越境事例も確認されており、IHR基準を複数満たすためフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Province du Nord-Kivu; Butembo; Lubero; Ituri; Republic of France; Democratic Republic of the Congo; State of Israel; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria,,Ebola Mortality Rises over 50% in DR Congo,2026-11-04T13:16:56+00:00,https://www.breitbart.com/africa/2026/11/04/ebola-mortality-rises-over-50-in-dr-congo/,ENGLISH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) linked to Bundibugyo strain shows 10,414 cases with 5,372 deaths (51.6% mortality) per the DRC Ministry of Public Health, Hygiene and Social Welfare; Africa CDC reports over 10,000 cases and about 5,376 deaths. The mortality rise is attributed to retrospective data adjustment, not greater lethality. WHO declared a public health emergency in eastern DRC in May. No specific treatments or vaccines exist for Bundibugyo. Transmission is via bodily fluids, not airborne. Response hampered by remoteness, ongoing conflict, and hostility toward aid workers. Affected areas include Ituri and North Kivu (notably Beni, Butembo, Lubero) with treatment centers at capacity and rising pediatric cases. Imported/exported cases include Kenya (2), Uganda (2); Nigeria and France also reported Bundibugyo cases; Israel isolated a potentially exposed patient.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,致死率上昇は後方視的データ調整によるもので、病原性自体の増加ではないと報告されている。ケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリア・フランス・イスラエルは対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations から除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9jb25nbHkudm4vZGllbi1iaWVuLXNhbi1zYW5nLXBodW9uZy1hbi11bmctcGhvLXRoaWVuLXRhaS1kaWNoLWJlbmgtdmEta2h1bmctaG9hbmctYW4tbmluaC01NDYyMzMuaHRtbA==,DISMISS,実際の感染症発生ではなく、複合災害対応訓練・計画に関する行政文書であり、具体的な疾病事例の報告がない。,Unknown Illness,Tỉnh Ðiện Biên,"Điện Biên is ready with a plan to respond to natural disasters, disease outbreaks, and security crises.","Điện Biên sẵn sàng phương án ứng phó thiên tai, dịch bệnh và khủng hoảng an ninh",2026-11-04T14:12:01+00:00,https://congly.vn/dien-bien-san-sang-phuong-an-ung-pho-thien-tai-dich-benh-va-khung-hoang-an-ninh-546233.html,VIETNAMESE,humans; environment,"On November 4, 2026, Dien Bien Province issued a framework and response plans for a Level-2 multi-crisis scenario, prioritizing protection of life and health, disease control, misinformation management, and public order. The exercise imagines simultaneous hazards: protracted rainstorms causing floods, landslides, and isolation of villages; outbreaks of infectious diseases; and misinformation-driven unrest with price volatility in essential goods. The response emphasizes maintaining electricity, water, and health services while preventing crises from spreading. The three-stage process covers information intake, initial handling, and risk assessment, followed by emergency action under the '4-at-site' principle, relief, infrastructure repair, production recovery, and social welfare. Commune-level forces organize evacuations and shelters; the provincial police assess risk, advise activation, and coordinate rescue, traffic restoration, disease control, and online misinformation countermeasures. The provincial People's Committee assigns the police as the standing body to lead drills and ensure inter-agency coordination to avoid paralysis in complex, concurrent events.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,不明,不明,No,0,No,Yes,No,記事は具体的な感染症アウトブレイクではなく、ベトナム・ディエンビエン省の危機管理計画（防災・疫病・治安）の策定に関する行政報道。実際の疾病発生地域ではないためverified_locationsは空とした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZWNvbm9teS5iZy93b3JsZC92aWV3LzY1NDE5LzUzMDAtc2Etc215cnRuaXRlLXNsdWNoYWktb3QtZWJvbGE=,PICKUP,"DRCを中心にケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリアへ越境拡大し、10,000人超感染・5,300人超死亡という大規模流行で、承認されたワクチン・治療法もなくIHR基準を複数満たす。",Hemorrhagic Fever; Ebola,Abuja; Federal Capital Territory; Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Federal Republic of Nigeria; Republic of Uganda; Republic of Kenya,"5,300 Ebola deaths",5300 са смъртните случаи от ебола - Economy.bg,2026-11-04T14:33:25+00:00,https://www.economy.bg/world/view/65419/5300-sa-smyrtnite-sluchai-ot-ebola,BULGARIAN,humans,"Bundibugyo ebolavirus outbreak in Africa has infected over 10,000 people and caused about 5,376 deaths (as of 31 October), with 5,372 in the Democratic Republic of Congo and 2 in Kenya and 2 in Uganda. The outbreak began in May in DRC and is the fastest-growing, most widespread Ebola event recorded. Uganda reports 20 cases, largely linked to travelers from DRC; the country was declared Ebola-free in August. Kenya reported 9 cases in October, its first Ebola cases. Nigeria reported a single imported case: a 42-year-old Swiss woman whose husband works at the embassy in Abuja; the couple had traveled to Uganda before returning home. There is no approved vaccine or treatment for Bundibugyo ebolavirus. Transmission is via bodily fluids, causing hemorrhagic fever. Ervebo vaccine trials have begun and have shown efficacy against the Zaire strain.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリアは対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations から除外。DRCが流行の中心かつ対象国のため記載。,
