aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWdhcG9saXRhbi5rb21wYXMuY29tL3JlYWQvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC8yMTQ1NTYzMS9tZW55aXNpci1nYW5nLW1lbmNhcmktYW5hYnVsLXNhYXQta2xpbmlrLWhld2FuLWtlbGlsaW5nLWphZ2EtamFrYXJ0YQ==,DISMISS,ジャカルタは2004年以降狂犬病フリーであり、本記事は予防・啓発活動の紹介であって、実際の症例発生や公衆衛生上の異常事態を報告するものではない。,Rabies,Jawa Barat; Banten; Cempaka Putih; Daerah Khusus Ibukota Jakarta; Rawasari; Jakarta,Combing the Alleys in Search of Pets: As Mobile Veterinary Clinics Keep Jakarta Rabies-Free,Menyisir Gang Mencari Anabul: Saat Klinik Hewan Keliling Jaga Jakarta Bebas Rabies,2026-11-04T14:45:56+00:00,https://megapolitan.kompas.com/read/2026/11/04/21455631/menyisir-gang-mencari-anabul-saat-klinik-hewan-keliling-jaga-jakarta,INDONESIAN,animals; humans,"Mobile Veterinary Clinics began operating in Jakarta on July 13, 2026, and by November 4, 2026 have run for nearly four months, using van-based teams to bring veterinarians closer to residents and animal shelters. Operated by Jakarta Province’s Food Security, Maritime, and Agriculture Agency (KPKP), the service serves both owned pets and stray animals, while strengthening rabies prevention through examinations, owner education, and accessible care. Jakarta has been rabies-free since 2004, with ongoing surveillance to prevent reintroduction; no positive rabies cases have been reported to date. In 2024 and 2025, vaccination of rabies reached 59,855 and 61,643 animals, respectively, supporting herd immunity. Dr. Mufid Hadi, stationed in Rawasari, Cempaka Putih, Central Jakarta, notes clinics treat both owned and stray animals, underscoring the program’s role in maintaining Jakarta’s rabies-free status.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事は狂犬病症例の発生ではなく、ジャカルタの狂犬病清浄地域維持のための予防活動（移動診療・ワクチン接種）を報じるポジティブな内容。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc2VjcmV0Y2hpbmEuY29tL25ld3MvYjUvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC8xMTA2OTk3Lmh0bWw=,PICKUP,中国全土でA(H3N2)・A(H1N1)・B(Victoria)の複数株が同時流行し、季節外れの早期流行拡大と病院の混雑・重症化（脳炎・心筋炎リスク）が報告されており、IHR基準とWPRO基準の複数に該当するためフルリスク評価に進むべき。,Human Infection with Swine Influenza A H1N1; Unknown Encephalitis; Human Infection with Swine Influenza A H3N2; Influenza,Shanghai Shi; Shandong Sheng; Shanghai; Beijing Shi; Sichuan Sheng; Zhejiang Sheng; Beijing; People's Republic of China,Influenza viruses prevalent in Mainland China; multiple strains circulating simultaneously; hospitals overwhelmed in many areas (Photo Gallery),大陸流感病毒盛行 多種毒株同活躍 多地醫院爆滿(組圖),2026-11-04T14:51:55+00:00,https://www.secretchina.com/news/b5/2026/11/04/1106997.html,CHINESE,humans,"Influenza activity is severe across Mainland China with simultaneous circulation of multiple strains and hospitals overwhelmed in many areas. Since July, both A(H3N2) and B Victoria lineage have co-circulated, with A(H3N2) the dominant A-subtype and A(H1N1) also present. Week 43 (Oct 19–25) data show a rapid rise: influenza-like illness (ILI) positive rate at sentinel hospitals 14.7%, and 145 weekly ILI outbreak events (up from 28). Among positives, A accounts for 67.6% (H3N2 within A 67.2% and H1N1 32.8%), B/Victoria 32.4%; overall three strains circulating concurrently. Regions affected include Shanghai, Zhejiang, Beijing, Shandong, and Sichuan, with hospitals reported as crowded. Common syndromes include high fever with rapid return after antipyretics, persistent fever >5 days, severe cough, chest tightness, dyspnea, and pneumonia risk; children may experience drowsiness or vomiting and risk encephalitis, while young adults risk myocarditis. The season shows earlier onset and increased indoor crowding contributing to transmission.",Yes,Yes,不明,No,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,4,Yes,Yes,不明,記事は中国本土（上海、浙江、北京、山東、四川など）での季節性インフルエンザの急拡大を報じており、対象国は中国のみ。国際的拡大や渡航制限への言及はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hY3AuY2QvcHJvdmluY2UvZWJvbGEtbGVzLWVucXVldGVzLWNvbW11bmF1dGFpcmVzLWFpZGVudC1saXR1cmktYS1yZXBvbmRyZS1hdXgtYWxlcnRlcy1saWVlcy1hdXgtZGVjZXMv,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国イトゥリ州ニジ保健区でエボラ出血熱が継続的に発生しており、累計827例確定・488例死亡（うち59%が地域内死亡）、10月にも119例確定・51例地域内死亡が報告されるなど、重大な公衆衛生上の脅威かつ感染拡大リスクが継続している。,Ebola,Ituri; Nizi; Democratic Republic of the Congo,Ebola: Community Investigations Help Ituri Respond to Death-Related Alerts - ACP,Ebola : les enquêtes communautaires aident l'Ituri à répondre aux alertes liées aux décès - ACP,2026-11-04T14:56:38+00:00,https://acp.cd/province/ebola-les-enquetes-communautaires-aident-lituri-a-repondre-aux-alertes-liees-aux-deces/,FRENCH,humans,"Ebola virus disease in Ituri's Nizi health zone, Democratic Republic of the Congo, prompts community-led investigations that inform response. From August 10–18, 2026, with WHO support, four health areas were surveyed to identify social and cultural drivers of resistance to Ebola interventions and to address community deaths. Findings highlighted practices facilitating transmission: self-medication, reliance on traditional healers, home-based care, and handling bodies during funeral rites, prompting adapted risk communication. Following the assessment, local leaders, religious figures, and community authorities led sensitization sessions to promote preventive behaviors and safer burials. Nizi had 827 confirmed cases and 488 deaths by July 2026, with 59% of deaths occurring in the community; in October, 119 confirmed cases and 51 community deaths were reported. Families are urged to report deaths promptly, limit contact with corpses, and refer suspected cases to care facilities to interrupt transmission; WHO supports culturally tailored prevention strategies.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,エボラ出血熱はIHR常時通報対象疾患であり、高致死率・地域内死亡の多さ・伝統的埋葬慣行等によるヒト-ヒト感染リスクの継続が確認されている。WHO支援下での対応が進行中。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc2VjcmV0Y2hpbmEuY29tL25ld3MvZ2IvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC8xMTA2OTk3Lmh0bWw=,PICKUP,複数のインフルエンザ株（H3N2、H1N1、B型）が同時流行し、陽性率上昇・病院逼迫・重症化（肺炎、脳炎、心筋炎）の報告があり、公衆衛生への影響が深刻かつ季節性インフルエンザとしては異常な規模・重症度を示しているためフルリスク評価が必要。,Human Infection with Swine Influenza A H3N2; Influenza B; Plague; Influenza; Human Infection with Swine Influenza A H1N1; Influenza A; Unknown Encephalitis,Shanghai Shi; Shandong Sheng; Zhejiang Sheng; Sichuan Sheng; Shanghai; Hangzhou; People's Republic of China,Influenza viruses prevalent in Mainland China; multiple strains co-circulating; hospitals in many regions overwhelmed (Photo Gallery).,大陆流感病毒盛行 多种毒株同活跃 多地医院爆满(组图),2026-11-04T14:49:26+00:00,https://www.secretchina.com/news/gb/2026/11/04/1106997.html,CHINESE,humans,"Influenza activity is elevated across Mainland China with simultaneous circulation of three strains: Influenza A (H3N2 and H1N1) and Influenza B (Victoria lineage). Sentinel data show a 14.7% influenza-positive rate among outpatient/ED respiratory specimens in Week 43 (Oct 19–25), with 145 influenza-like outbreaks that week, up from 28. Southern regions report earlier and stronger activity than the north, with hospitals crowded in Shanghai, Zhejiang (Hangzhou), Shandong, and Sichuan. National sequencing indicates H3N2 dominates within A (67.2% of A; ~45% of all positives), B/Victoria about 32.4%, and H1N1 about 22% of positives. Common symptoms include high fever lasting beyond antipyretic relief, severe cough, chest tightness, dyspnea, and pneumonia risk; children may present lethargy and vomiting with encephalitis risk, adults chest pain and possible myocarditis. An October official note mentions one plague death with few details.",Yes,Yes,No,No,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,4,Yes,Yes,不明,ペストによる死亡例についても言及があるが詳細不明。上海・浙江（杭州）・山東・四川など複数地域で病院逼迫が報告されている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hY3AuY2QvcHJvdmluY2UvZWJvbGEtZW4taXR1cmktbGVuZ2FnZW1lbnQtY29tbXVuYXV0YWlyZS11bi1mYWN0ZXVyLWluY29udG91cm5hYmxlLWRhbnMtbGEtcmlwb3N0ZS1kci1taWNoZWwtbXV2dWRpLw==,PICKUP,DRCで継続中の第17次エボラ出血熱アウトブレイクに関する内容であり、疾患自体の重篤性とヒト-ヒト感染の可能性、国際機関（世界銀行）の関与など社会的・政治的関心が認められるため、既知のアウトブレイクではあるがフルリスク評価による継続監視が妥当と判断。,Ebola,Ituri; Bunia; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"Ebola in Ituri: Community Engagement, a Key Factor in the Response (Dr. Michel Muvudi) - ACP.","Ebola en Ituri : l'engagement communautaire, un facteur incontournable dans la riposte (Dr. Michel Muvudi) - ACP",2026-11-04T15:00:02+00:00,https://acp.cd/province/ebola-en-ituri-lengagement-communautaire-un-facteur-incontournable-dans-la-riposte-dr-michel-muvudi/,FRENCH,humans,"On 4 November 2026 in Bunia, Ituri, northeastern Democratic Republic of the Congo, the endgame of the 17th Ebola virus disease outbreak hinges on community engagement, according to a World Bank specialist. Dr. Michel Muvudi told a community forum that success in interrupting transmission requires local leaders and residents to co-create risk messages and tailor response measures to fit local realities. He stressed that communities, directly bearing the epidemic's impact, should be partners rather than passive recipients, capable of identifying what to do and what to avoid. The discussion included chiefs of Bahema Banywagi and Bahema d'Irumu, a civil-society vice-coordinator for Ituri, and community relay agents. The emphasis on locally owned communication and partnerships highlights a pathway to reduce transmission and bring the outbreak to a close.",Yes,No,No,No,1,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事は第17次エボラ出血熱アウトブレイクの終息段階における地域社会エンゲージメントの重要性を扱う内容で、新規症例や死亡者数など疫学的な新情報は含まれていない。既存アウトブレイクの継続監視の一環として位置づけられる。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cueHhjYi5jbi9kZXRhaWxzLzJxOGJpU1lnQjZhZWIwM2QyODQyMDE3NmUxMzBhZDM1My5odG1s,DISMISS,季節性インフルエンザ等の通常の流行状況報告であり、専門家も「全体的に安定・制御可能」と評価しており、異常性や国際的拡大リスクは認められない。,Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV) Infection; Human Infection with Swine Influenza A H3N2; Influenza; Human Infection with Swine Influenza A H1N1; Haemophilus Influenzae Infection; Pneumococcus; Varicella,Hunan Sheng; People's Republic of China,What is the autumn–winter trend of respiratory infectious diseases in Hunan Province? CDC experts: overall stable and controllable; four protective tips to learn.,秋冬季湖南呼吸道传染病流行态势如何？疾控专家：总体平稳可控，可学习4个防护妙招 | 潇湘晨报网,2026-11-04T15:08:04+00:00,https://www.xxcb.cn/details/2q8biSYgB6aeb03d28420176e130ad353.html,CHINESE,humans,"Influenza remains active in Hunan Province during autumn–winter, with rising activity. Dominant strains are A/H3N2 and B Victoria lineage; occasional A/H1N1 detected. Children aged 5–14 show the highest positivity. Rhinovirus is rising; infants and young children are at risk for severe disease, with rhinovirus ranking among top pathogens in outpatient influenza-like illness and severe acute respiratory infection. Other pathogens — Streptococcus pneumoniae, respiratory syncytial virus (RSV), and Haemophilus influenzae type b (Hib) — circulate at typical levels. Four protective tips: 1) dress in layers; 2) reduce crowding, especially for children, the elderly, and those with chronic diseases; 3) maintain hand hygiene and ventilation; 4) vaccines: routine ones (MMR, DTP, meningococcal) and non‑routine ones (influenza, pneumococcal, varicella) to reduce infection and severe disease. Source: Hunan CDC briefing, Nov 4, 2026.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,湖南省CDCによる季節性報告であり、通常の季節性呼吸器感染症（インフルエンザ、RSV、肺炎球菌等）の流行状況と予防啓発が内容。異常事態の報告ではない。,
