aHR0cDovL3BhbmV0LmNvbS9zdG9yeS80MzEwMzMx,DISMISS,イスラエルで検査された疑い例はエボラ陰性と確定しており、DRCでの新規エボラ発生を示す情報も記事内にないため、シグナルとしての根拠がない。,Ebola,State of Israel,Ministry of Health: Negative results for Ebola tests conducted on the two patients who were admitted to the hospital yesterday.,وزارة الصحة: نتائج سلبية لفحوصات الإيبولا التي أُجريت للمريضين اللذين أُدخلا إلى المستشفى أمس,2026-11-04T15:09:50+00:00,http://panet.com/story/4310331,ARABIC,humans,"Israel's Ministry of Health announces negative Ebola test results for two patients admitted yesterday. Both individuals had recently returned from the Democratic Republic of Congo and developed fever upon their return, prompting clinical suspicion of Ebola. Diagnostic testing was carried out in accordance with professional procedures and international guidelines for managing highly contagious diseases. The Ministry notes that, to date, Israel has not registered a confirmed Ebola case. The findings underscore ongoing vigilance for imported infectious threats and adherence to established protocols to rapidly assess travelers from regions with Ebola activity. Health authorities continue to monitor contacts and advise on risk and preventive measures.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事はイスラエルでの疑い例が陰性であったことを報告しているのみで、DRCにおけるエボラ発生そのものについての具体的情報（新規症例、流行状況等）は記載がない。イスラエルは対象国リストに含まれず、DRCも本記事の主題ではないため verified_locations は空とした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hY3AuY2QvcHJvdmluY2UvdHNob3BvLTk1LWNhcy1jb25maXJtZXMtZGVib2xhLWVucmVnaXN0cmVzLWRlcHVpcy1sZS1kZWJ1dC1kZS1sZXBpZGVtaWUv,PICKUP,エボラ出血熱のアウトブレイクが継続中で、致死率40%、医療従事者への感染も多数発生しており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルRRAへの移行が必要。,Ebola,Tshopo; Bafwasende; Mangobo; Province du Nord-Kivu; Kisangani; Lubunga; Kabondo; Democratic Republic of the Congo,Tshopo: 95 confirmed Ebola cases recorded since the start of the outbreak - ACP.,Tshopo : 95 cas confirmés d'Ebola enregistrés depuis le début de l'épidémie - ACP,2026-11-04T15:03:10+00:00,https://acp.cd/province/tshopo-95-cas-confirmes-debola-enregistres-depuis-le-debut-de-lepidemie/,FRENCH,humans,"Ebola virus disease outbreak in Tshopo province, northeastern Democratic Republic of Congo, Kisangani. As of 3 November 2026, 95 laboratory-confirmed Ebola cases have been recorded since outbreak declaration, with 38 deaths, 44 recoveries, and 5 probable cases, yielding a case fatality ratio of 40%. Distributed across health zones: Makiso-Kisangani leads with 33 cases, Kabondo 21, Bafwasende 20, Mangobo 11, Tshopo 8, while Wanie-Rukula and Lubunga have one each. Frontline healthcare workers accounted for 25 confirmed cases, including 20 survivors and 5 deaths. Eight patients are currently treated at the Ebola Treatment Center in Météo. The information is reported by the provincial health division via ACP, reflecting ongoing transmission in the province since the epidemic declaration.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,致死率40%、医療従事者25例感染（5名死亡）と高いリスクを示す。複数の保健区にまたがる拡大傾向があり、国際的な支援ニーズが高いと考えられる。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9pYmkub25nLmJyL25vdGljaWEvMjY1NjM0L2dvdmVybm8tZGUtc3AtbW9iaWxpemEtNjQ1LW11bmljaXBpb3MtcGFyYS1pZGVudGlmaWNhci1jYXNvcy1zdXNwZWl0b3MtZGUtc2FyYW1wby1lLXJ1YmVvbGE=,PICKUP,ワクチン未接種率が高い集団での麻疹流行継続（41例確認、61%が2歳未満）があり、ヒト-ヒト感染のリスクと社会的・行政的関心の高さからWPRO基準とsocio-political関心の双方に該当する。,Rubella; Measles; Mumps; Varicella,São Paulo; São Paulo; Guarulhos; Federative Republic of Brazil,São Paulo state government mobilizes 645 municipalities to identify suspected cases of measles and rubella.,Governo de SP mobiliza 645 municípios para identificar casos suspeitos de sarampo e rubéola,2026-11-04T15:11:50+00:00,https://ibi.ong.br/noticia/265634/governo-de-sp-mobiliza-645-municipios-para-identificar-casos-suspeitos-de-sarampo-e-rubeola,PORTUGUESE,humans,"São Paulo state mobilizes 645 municipalities for the 6th Dia S (National Day of Active Searches for Measles and Rubella), running November 4–14, 2026. The effort reviews patient records, serology results, and outreach to identify cases not yet notified, including home visits to schools and workplaces. It uses three modalities: Institutional Active Search (BAI), Community Active Search (BAC), and Laboratory Active Search (BAL). By October 2026, 41 measles cases were confirmed in São Paulo: 37 in the capital, 2 in São Bernardo do Campo, 1 in Guarulhos, and 1 in Santo André; 31 patients had no vaccination or incomplete schedules; about 61% were under 2 years old. Vaccination via SUS uses the measles-mumps-rubella vaccine: first dose at 12 months, second at 15 months (preferably tetraviral with varicella); ages 5–29: two doses; 30–59: one dose if not previously vaccinated; health workers: two doses. Vaccines are free at UBS; pregnancy is contraindicated.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,Yes,Yes,No,本件はブラジル・サンパウロ州における麻疹・風疹の能動的症例探索キャンペーン（Dia S）に関する内容で、国家規模の定例的公衆衛生活動である。国際的拡大や渡航制限のリスクは記載されておらず、死亡例や重症例の言及もないが、未接種者における麻疹の継続的な感染拡大リスクが懸念される。,
aHR0cHM6Ly95b3VybmV3cy5jb20vMjAyNi8xMS8wNC83MjUyMjg5L2NvbmdvLWVib2xhLWRlYXRoLXRvbGwtc3VycGFzc2VzLTUwMDAtYXMtaGVhbHRoLW9mZmljaWFscy1yZWNvbmNpbGUv,PICKUP,"致死率約50%の大規模エボラ(ブンディブギョ株)アウトブレイクで死者5,000人超、ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダへの国際的な輸出例も報告されており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Tshopo; South Kivu Province; Province du Nord-Ubangi; Province du Sud-Ubangi; Ituri; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Federal Republic of Nigeria; Republic of Uganda; Republic of Kenya,,"Congo Ebola Death Toll Surpasses 5,000 as Health Officials Reconcile Conflicting Mortality Figures - [your]NEWS",2026-11-04T14:59:16+00:00,https://yournews.com/2026/11/04/7252289/congo-ebola-death-toll-surpasses-5000-as-health-officials-reconcile/,ENGLISH,humans,"DR Congo’s Bundibugyo Ebola outbreak, which began in May 2026, has killed more than 5,100 people as of early November, with conflicting mortality figures being reconciled. The National Institute of Biomedical Research reports 5,372 deaths among 10,414 confirmed infections (case fatality rate 51.6%) as of Oct 30, while the European Centre for Disease Prevention and Control records 5,126 deaths among 10,532 confirmed cases through Nov 1 (CFR ~48.7%). A retrospective mortality review in Ituri caused 314 deaths to be added, not reflected in the latest reports, explaining the discrepancy. Ituri and North Kivu drive the outbreak: 7,431 infections/3,492 deaths in Ituri; 2,518 infections/1,395 deaths in North Kivu; Haut-Uélé 467/205. Transmission extends to Tshopo, South Kivu, Bas-Uélé, Sud-Ubangi, Nord-Ubangi. Kenya reports the first imported Bundibugyo case (Oct 6); 9 infections and 2 deaths in Kenya; Nigeria and Uganda report imports. Bundibugyo has no licensed vaccine or virus-specific treatment; care is supportive.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダへの輸入例が報告されているが、対象国リストに含まれないためverified_locationsには含めていない。ワクチン・特異的治療法が存在しない点も重大なリスク要因。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubjNuZXdzLmNvbS5ici8yMDI2LzExL21wb3gtYXZhbmNhLW5vLXJpby1jb20tMjY5LWNhc29zLWVtLTIwMjY=,WATCH,リオデジャネイロ州でMpox症例が前年比約3倍に増加しているが、死亡例はなく、国際的拡大や渡航制限等の明確な兆候は見られないため経過観察とする。,Mpox; HIV,Rio de Janeiro; Rio de Janeiro; Federative Republic of Brazil,Mpox advances in Rio de Janeiro with 269 cases in 2026.,Mpox avança no Rio com 269 casos em 2026,2026-11-04T15:09:00+00:00,https://www.n3news.com.br/2026/11/mpox-avanca-no-rio-com-269-casos-em-2026,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Mpox in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, has 269 confirmed cases in 2026 through November 3, with no deaths reported. This marks a substantial rise from 92 cases by the same date in 2025. As of November 2, the state had administered 953 vaccine doses against mpox; officials anticipate a stock reinforcement to meet higher year-end activity. The vaccination scheme consists of two doses with a 28-day interval. Priority groups include laboratory workers handling Orthopoxviruses, people living with HIV/AIDS with immunosuppression, and direct contacts at medium or high risk of exposure after health surveillance assessment. Public health guidance urges avoiding contact with people with skin or mucosal lesions, not sharing personal items, avoiding intimate contact during symptoms, and seeking medical care for suspected lesions. The surge underscores the need to expand vaccine coverage and maintain preventive measures amid upcoming year-end travel.",No,Yes,不明,No,1,Yes,No,Yes,Yes,不明,3,不明,Yes,不明,ブラジルは対象国リストに含まれるため検証地域として記載。症例数増加の背景やワクチン供給状況など続報の注視が必要。,
