ているが、いずれも対象国リストに含まれないためverified_locationsには含めていない。Africa CDCが国際的な監視・資金提供の強化を呼びかけている点も重要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaGVhbHRoZGVzay5pdC9jcm9uYWNoZS9jb25nby1sYW50cmFjZS1mYS1zdHJhZ2UtaXBwb3BvdGFtaS10ZW1lLWx1b21v,PICKUP,DRCでの炭疽菌感染による野生動物の大量死が継続し、エボラ・コレラが同時流行する中で人への感染リスクが指摘されており、社会的・行政的関心も高いと考えられるため。,Cholera; Anthrax; Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Uganda,"Congo: Anthrax Decimates Hippos, Fears for Humans.","Congo: l'antrace fa strage di ippopotami, si teme per l'uomo",2026-11-04T14:54:02+00:00,https://www.healthdesk.it/cronache/congo-lantrace-fa-strage-ippopotami-teme-luomo,ITALIAN,environment; humans; animals,"Anthrax decimates hippos in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, with at least 30 hippos dead in the last 30 days, confirmed as Bacillus anthracis by laboratory analysis. First carcasses were found in September in Virunga National Park in eastern DRC. No human cases reported yet, but authorities and international bodies remain alert: risk to people arises from handling infected carcasses or consuming contaminated meat. While the organism is environmental, silent transmission cannot be ruled out. Experts note that in 2025 a similar outbreak killed about 65 hippos in DRC, and in Uganda that year 15 people tested positive with 2 deaths. Although wildlife surveillance and safe carcass disposal are underway, and vaccination campaigns for livestock continue, these measures are costly. The episode coincides with ongoing Ebola and cholera epidemics in the country, amid insecurity and conflict.",不明,Yes,不明,No,1,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はDRCのヴィルンガ国立公園での炭疽によるカバ大量死を主題としており、ウガンダの事例は2025年の過去の参考事例として言及されているのみで現事例の発生地ではない。人への感染例は未報告だが、同国で進行中のエボラ・コレラ流行と治安不安が重なり、監視強化が必要とされている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYW50YXJhbmV3cy5jb20vYmVyaXRhLzU4MzI2MjcvOTU5Ny1wZW5naWRhcC10YmMtYmVyaGFzaWwtdGVyZGV0ZWtzaS1kaS1qYWtiYXI=,DISMISS,通常の公衆衛生プログラムによる結核検出・治療の進捗報告であり、異常事態や新規脅威ではないため見送り。,Tuberculosis,Daerah Khusus Ibukota Jakarta; Jakarta,"9,597 TB patients successfully detected in West Jakarta",9.597 pengidap TBC berhasil terdeteksi di Jakbar,2026-11-04T15:33:57+00:00,https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5832627/9597-pengidap-tbc-berhasil-terdeteksi-di-jakbar,INDONESIAN,humans,"TB in West Jakarta, Indonesia: The West Jakarta Health Office (Sudinkes Jakbar) detected and treated 9,597 tuberculosis (TB) patients in 2026, with 7,378 cases found and treated from Jan 1 to Oct 31, from 69,512 people screened or evaluated. This reflects progress toward Jakarta Barat's 2026 TB detection target of 11,955 cases and the broader DKI Jakarta elimination goal by 2030. Detection relied on active and passive case finding: active through community health screenings, Free Health Check (CKG), and TB Cadres on the ground; passive via suspects presenting at healthcare facilities. Diagnostics combined sputum testing and radiology (X-ray) per clinical indications to confirm cases. All treated patients receive standard-of-care therapy, with adherence monitoring and contact tracing. Close contacts receive TB Preventive Therapy (TPT). Public health messaging includes PHBS, cough etiquette, immunization, and service access.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,結核は既知の疾患で、記事は通常の検診・治療プログラムの実績報告。対象国リストにインドネシアは含まれるが、本件は定例的な保健活動報告でありシグナルとしての緊急性はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuanBvc3QuY29tL2hlYWx0aC1hbmQtd2VsbG5lc3MvYXJ0aWNsZS05MTM4MzM=,PICKUP,DRCで1万人以上が感染し5000人超が死亡する大規模なエボラアウトブレイクが継続しており、既に複数国へ拡大、渡航制限も発生していることからIHR基準を複数満たす。,Ebola,Republic of the Sudan; Republic of Angola; Central African Republic; Republic of Rwanda; State of Israel; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; United Republic of Tanzania; Republic of Burundi; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria,,"Suspected patients test negative for Ebola after returning to Israel from DRC, Health Ministry says",2026-11-04T15:37:32+00:00,https://www.jpost.com/health-and-wellness/article-913833,ENGLISH,humans; animals,"Two suspected Ebola patients returning from the Democratic Republic of the Congo were placed in isolation at Sheba Medical Center and Ichilov Medical Center in Israel, and both tested negative for Ebola. Israel's Health Ministry said there are no confirmed Ebola cases in the country. The DRC Ebola outbreak has infected over 10,000 people and killed more than 5,000 since it was first declared in May. The outbreak has spread to Uganda, Kenya, and Nigeria, prompting travel advisories by the Health Ministry, urging avoidance of nonessential travel to several countries including South Sudan, the Central African Republic, Rwanda, Burundi, Tanzania, Zambia, and Angola. The outbreak is caused by the Ebola Bundibugyo virus, for which there is no vaccine or cure. Transmission occurs via close contact with symptomatic patients or bodily fluids, contaminated objects, or infected animals.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はDRCで継続中のエボラ（ブンディブギョ・ウイルス）アウトブレイクが主題。イスラエルでの疑い例は陰性確認済み。Zambia等は渡航回避勧告の対象国として言及されているのみで、実際の発生国ではないためverified_locationsから除外。ウガンダ・ケニア・ナイジェリアへの拡大が言及されているが、これらは対象国リストに含まれない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly92b3Yudm4veGEtaG9pL2tpZW0tc29hdC1zb3QteHVhdC1odXlldC1iYXQtZGF1LXR1LXR1eWVuLWNvLXNvLXBvc3QxMzQ3MzcwLnZvdg==,WATCH,ベトナム南部でデング熱が季節的に流行し死亡例も報告されているが、例年の流行パターンの範囲内であり国際的拡大のリスクは低いため、経過観察とする。,Dengue,Ho Chi Minh City; Ho Chi Minh City; Socialist Republic of Vietnam,Dengue fever control starts at the grassroots level.,Kiểm soát sốt xuất huyết bắt đầu từ tuyến cơ sở,2026-11-04T15:21:34+00:00,https://vov.vn/xa-hoi/kiem-soat-sot-xuat-huyet-bat-dau-tu-tuyen-co-so-post1347370.vov,VIETNAMESE,humans; vectors; environment,"Grassroots dengue control escalates as cases rise in Ho Chi Minh City (HCMC) and Bình Dương Province. Authorities stress that dengue prevention must be a community effort, with local government, organizations, and residents eliminating larval habitats and seeking timely care for fever. In Bình Dương’s Thuận Giao ward, 2026 has recorded 469 dengue cases, 194 outbreaks, and 3 risk points needing surveillance. Notable clusters include Thuận Giao 17 Street near Hoa Lân 2 and a nearby waste-transfer site (4 cases) and Thuận Giao 7 Street near a banana garden (5 cases). Inspections of dormitories found water-holding containers such as air-conditioner pans and buckets. The ward has mobilized cleaning, requiring landlords and tenants to remove standing water; more than 6 tons of waste were collected at five sites. Dengue is described as endemic in HCMC; weekly 10–15 minute household inspections are urged. Đồng Nai reports two dengue deaths within 24 hours.",No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,No,デング熱はベトナム（HCMC、ビンズオン省、ドンナイ省）の風土病であり、毎年の流行シーズンにおける症例増加・死亡例の報告。国内の地方自治体レベルでの対策強化が主題であり、国際的な公衆衛生上の緊急事態には該当しない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9rZW5oMTQudm4vY3V1LXNvbmctdHJlLXNvLXNpbmgtMTctbmdheS10dW9pLXNvYy1zb3QteHVhdC1odXlldC10b24tdGh1b25nLWdhbi1uYW5nLTIxNTI2MTEwNDIwNDAwMTg4Mi5jaG4=,DISMISS,単一症例の臨床報告であり、デング熱はベトナムで既知の風土病であるため、異常性や国際的拡大リスクは認められない。,Dengue,Ho Chi Minh City; Ho Chi Minh City; Socialist Republic of Vietnam,Rescuing a 17-day-old neonate with dengue shock and severe liver injury.,"Cứu sống trẻ sơ sinh 17 ngày tuổi sốc sốt xuất huyết, tổn thương gan nặng",2026-11-04T14:26:00+00:00,https://kenh14.vn/cuu-song-tre-so-sinh-17-ngay-tuoi-soc-sot-xuat-huyet-ton-thuong-gan-nang-215261104204001882.chn,VIETNAMESE,humans,"On 2026-11-04, a 17-day-old male neonate from Tan Vinh Loc, Ho Chi Minh City, was treated at Ho Chi Minh City Children’s Hospital for dengue shock syndrome with severe liver injury. He presented after two days of fever with lethargy, irritability, a generalized rash and petechiae, and shock (blood pressure 60/40 mmHg). Laboratory results showed hematocrit 45%, platelets 24,000/mm3, AST 1369 U/L, and ALT 245 U/L. Diagnosed with dengue shock syndrome with severe hepatic injury, he received aggressive resuscitation: 6% Volulyte fluids, transfusion of packed red cells and platelets, albumin, liver support, and respiratory support including oxygen and CPAP. After 72 hours, hemodynamic status and liver injury improved; no further bleeding; he was awake and feeding well. Neonatal dengue can present non-specifically, requiring careful neonatal specialty assessment and tailored treatment to optimize outcomes.",No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,No,No,1,No,No,No,単一の新生児症例報告であり、デング熱の流行拡大や異常事態を示す情報はない。患児は治療により回復しており、公衆衛生上の緊急性は低い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZWxjb25maWRlbmNpYWwuY29tL3NhbHVkLzIwMjYtMTEtMDQvYnJvdGUtZWJvbGEtcmVwdWJsaWNhLWRlbW9jcmF0aWNhLWNvbmdvLTF0cHNfNDQ1ODkyMS8=,PICKUP,IHR基準のうち深刻性・異常性・国際拡大の3つに該当し、DRC史上最悪規模（1万532例、致死率48.7%）のエボラ流行で国際的関心・支援の必要性も高いため、フルリスク評価に進むべき。,Ebola,Tshopo; South Kivu Province; Bas Uele; Haut Uele; Nord Ubangi; Province de l’Équateur; Province du Nord-Ubangi; Ituri; Republic of the Sudan; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria,"The Ebola outbreak in the DRC surpasses the 10,500-case threshold in less than six months.",El brote de ébola en RDC supera el umbral de los 10.500 casos en menos de seis meses,2026-11-04T15:26:00+00:00,https://www.elconfidencial.com/salud/2026-11-04/brote-ebola-republica-democratica-congo-1tps_4458921/,SPANISH,humans; environment,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo has surpassed 10,500 cases, with 10,532 infections and 5,126 deaths as of the latest INSP bulletin. In the last day, 65 new cases and 23 deaths were reported, with a case fatality rate of 48.7%. Currently, 961 patients are hospitalized or in isolation and 2,834 have recovered; contact tracing stands at 84%. Eight provinces are affected: Ituri (epicenter, 70.6% of cases), North Kivu, South Kivu, Haut-Uele, Bas-Uele, Tshopo, Nord-Ubangi, and Ubangi. UNICEF delivered 50 tons of supplies to South Sudan for Ebola preparedness, including PPE and infection-control resources, emphasizing prevention in health facilities and communities, information dissemination, and training for workers and communities. The outbreak is the deadliest in DRC’s history and could surpass West Africa’s 2014–2016 outbreak per WHO. Kenya and Nigeria report linked cases; Uganda declared the country virus-free after two deaths and 20 cases.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事ではケニア・ナイジェリアでの関連症例やウガンダでの終息宣言、南スーダンへの支援物資輸送も言及されているが、いずれも対象国リストに含まれないか、DRCからの波及として言及されているのみのため verified_locations には含めなかった。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYWluZG9uZXNpYS5jb20va2VzZWhhdGFuLzk1MjQ4Mi9tZW5nZW5hbC1pbXVuaXNhc2ktZHQtZGFuLXRkLXVudHVrLW1lbGluZHVuZ2ktYW5hay1kYXJpLWRpZnRlcmktZGFuLXRldGFudXM=,DISMISS,特定のアウトブレイク報告ではなく、学校免疫月間の定期ワクチン接種に関する一般的な啓発記事であり、異常事態や公衆衛生上の緊急性を示す内容ではない。,Diphtheria; Tetanus,,Understanding DT and Td Immunizations to Protect Children from Diphtheria and Tetanus,Mengenal Imunisasi DT dan Td untuk Melindungi Anak dari Difteri dan Tetanus,2026-11-04T15:39:13+00:00,https://mediaindonesia.com/kesehatan/952482/mengenal-imunisasi-dt-dan-td-untuk-melindungi-anak-dari-difteri-dan-tetanus,INDONESIAN,humans,"Indonesia's School Immunization Month (BIAS) DT and Td vaccines aim to sustain protection as children grow. DT is given to elementary grade 1 students (typically 7 years old) as an early booster against diphtheria and tetanus; Td, the follow-on booster replacing TT, is administered to students in grade 2 and grade 5 (or ages 8 and 11 for non-scholars) each November, extending protection into adolescence and beyond. Antibody titers wane after infancy, so these boosters raise protection above 90%, helping prevent diphtheria (Corynebacterium diphtheriae) and tetanus (Clostridium tetani) and their dangerous complications—diphtheria can cause severe throat pain with a grey-white pseudomembrane and possible heart and kidney failure; tetanus causes severe muscle spasms and breathing difficulties. Success depends on collaboration among health, education, religious, and local authorities, schools, and parents who complete health screening, ensure meals before vaccination, and monitor post-immunization, strengthening herd immunity in Indonesia.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事は定期予防接種プログラム（BIAS）の説明であり、具体的な感染症発生や流行の報告ではないため、対象国の発生地域としては計上しない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9maW9jcnV6LmJyL25vdGljaWEvMjAyNi8xMS93ZWJpbmFyaW8tYXByZXNlbnRhLXByb2plY29lcy1wYXJhLXRlbXBvcmFkYS0yMDI3LWRlLWRlbmd1ZQ==,DISMISS,実際の感染症アウトブレイクの報告ではなく、将来シーズンの予測モデルに関するウェビナー開催告知であり、トリアージ基準に該当しない。,Chikungunya; Dengue,,Webinar presents projections for the 2027 dengue season | Fiocruz Portal.,Webinário apresenta projeções para a temporada 2027 de dengue | Portal Fiocruz,2026-11-04T13:30:00+00:00,https://fiocruz.br/noticia/2026/11/webinario-apresenta-projecoes-para-temporada-2027-de-dengue,PORTUGUESE,humans; environment,"Projected 2027 dengue season in Brazil anticipates a potential transmission rise driven by a very strong El Niño and above-average temperatures, following a 2024 record outbreak and a below-expected 2026 season in much of the country. A webinar on dengue-season preparation for 2027 is scheduled for 6 November 2026 at 10:00, online with simultaneous Portuguese, English and Spanish translation. Promoted by Fiocruz, FGV, Mosqlimate, InfoDengue, KWAR-AI, and TGHN LAC, it centers on forecasts from the Infodengue-Mosqlimate (IMDC) Challenge, which in 2026 expanded to 27 teams from eight countries and added municipal-level dengue and chikungunya predictions. The ensemble model combines multiple projections for public health planning. InfoDengue provides current municipality/state bulletins; forecast results are compiled into a report for the Ministry of Health. Audience includes researchers, health managers, data scientists, regulators, and journalists.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,不明,Yes,No,1,No,No,No,記事は2027年シーズンの予測・準備に関する学術的ウェビナーの告知であり、現在進行中のアウトブレイク報告ではない。デング熱・チクングニア熱の流行可能性は一般論として存在するためepidemic_proneをYesとしたが、具体的な発生事例ではないためverified_locationsは空とした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYW5hY2FvLmN2L25vdGljaWEvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9lYm9sYS1jYWJvLXZlcmRlLXJlZm9yY2EtdmlnaWxhbmNpYS1ub3MtYWVyb3BvcnRvcy1lLWltcGxlbWVudGEtcXVhcmVudGVuYS1kb21pY2lsaWFyaWEv,PICKUP,WHOがナイジェリアでのエボラ出血熱確定例を発表したことを受け、カーボベルデが空港検疫強化・渡航者への陰性証明義務化・自宅隔離を導入しており、国際的拡大・渡航制限のリスクを伴う公衆衛生上重大な事案であるため。,Ebola,Concelho da Praia; Dakar; Dakar; Praia; Federal Republic of Nigeria; Republic of Cabo Verde; Republic of Senegal,Ebola: Cabo Verde strengthens airport surveillance and implements home quarantine.,Ébola: Cabo Verde reforça vigilância nos aeroportos e implementa quarentena domiciliária,2026-11-04T00:00:00+00:00,https://www.anacao.cv/noticia/2026/11/04/ebola-cabo-verde-reforca-vigilancia-nos-aeroportos-e-implementa-quarentena-domiciliaria/,PORTUGUESE,humans; environment,"Ebola preparedness in Cabo Verde tightens airport surveillance and home quarantine after the WHO-confirmed case in Nigeria. The National Health Directorate activated the contingency plan at four international airports—Praia, São Vicente, Sal, and Boa Vista—requiring travel-history questionnaires, PPE for frontline staff, and thermal screening of arrivals. Following a US directive, all passengers entering or leaving Cabo Verde must have a negative Ebola test; testing will occur at the National Institute of Public Health, with rapid tests to be introduced and expanded to health centers. A five-member delegation from the Democratic Republic of Congo’s boxing federation arrived on a flight, was asymptomatic, and placed under mandatory home surveillance for up to 21 days (three in Praia, one in São Vicente), with daily health visits. Cabo Verde has no Ebola cases to date; samples needing confirmation are sent to Dakar under cooperation with the Public Health Institute.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事の主題はナイジェリアで確認されたエボラ症例を受けたカーボベルデの水際対策強化である。コンゴ民主共和国（DRC）のボクシング連盟代表団が到着し自宅待機となったが無症状であり、DRC国内での発生事例ではないため、対象国リストに該当する発生地域はなし（カーボベルデ・ナイジェリアは対象国リスト外）。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY2xpY2tndWFydWxob3MuY29tLmJyLzIwMjYvMTEvMDQvc3AtbW9iaWxpemEtbXVuaWNpcGlvcy1wYXJhLWlkZW50aWZpY2FyLWNhc29zLXN1c3BlaXRvcy1kZS1zYXJhbXBvLWd1YXJ1bGhvcy10ZW0tdW0tY2Fzby1jb25maXJtYWRvLw==,PICKUP,麻疹排除国であるブラジルで集団発生が確認され、州政府が645市町村を動員した積極的症例探索キャンペーンを実施しており、ヒト-ヒト感染拡大のリスクと行政的関心の高さからシグナルとして識別する。,Rubella; Measles,São Paulo; São Paulo; Guarulhos; Federative Republic of Brazil,São Paulo mobilizes municipalities to identify suspected measles cases; Guarulhos has a confirmed case - Click Guarulhos.,SP mobiliza municípios para identificar casos suspeitos de sarampo; Guarulhos tem um caso confirmado - Click Guarulhos,2026-11-04T15:42:02+00:00,https://www.clickguarulhos.com.br/2026/11/04/sp-mobiliza-municipios-para-identificar-casos-suspeitos-de-sarampo-guarulhos-tem-um-caso-confirmado/,PORTUGUESE,humans,"By October 2026, São Paulo state had 41 measles cases (37 in São Paulo city, 2 in São Bernardo do Campo, 1 in Guarulhos, 1 in Santo André); Guarulhos has a confirmed case. In response, SES-SP mobilizes 645 municipalities for the 6th National Day of Active Case Finding for Measles and Rubella (Dia S), running November 4–14 to identify suspected cases not yet diagnosed or notified. Teams will review medical records and lab results and conduct community searches, including home visits and outreach in schools and workplaces. The effort uses three modalities—Institutional (BAI), Community (BAC), and Laboratory (BAL)—with training for health workers. Vaccination with free MMR vaccine at UBSs follows schedules: children 12 and 15 months (preferably tetraviral); ages 5–29: two doses, 30 days apart; 30–59: one dose if not previously vaccinated; health workers: two doses. Measles and rubella symptoms are outlined; pregnancy remains a contraindication for vaccination; rapid case finding is emphasized.",不明,Yes,No,No,1,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,不明,サンパウロ州で41例（うちグアルリョス1例）の麻疹症例が報告され、州保健局が積極的症例探索（Dia S）を実施。重症度・死亡情報は記事中に記載なし。,
aHR0cHM6Ly8yNC5odS90dWRvbWFueS8yMDI2LzExLzA0L2hpdi1pbmpla2Npby1sZW5hY2F2YXBpci1qb3ZhaGFneWFzYS8=,DISMISS,HIV予防薬（レナカパビル）の承認・普及に関するポジティブな医療ニュースであり、公衆衛生上の緊急事態や異常な感染拡大を示すものではない。,HIV,United States,"The HIV injection, which reduces the risk of infection by 99.9%, is now available.","Elérhetővé vált a HIV-injekció, ami 99,9 százalékkal csökkenti a fertőzés esélyét",2026-11-04T16:08:57+00:00,https://24.hu/tudomany/2026/11/04/hiv-injekcio-lenacavapir-jovahagyasa/,HUNGARIAN,humans,"lenacavapir, an injectable HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis agent, received FDA approval in the United States and is expected to expand global access by making a cheaper generic version available from Dr. Reddy's Laboratories (India) and Unitaid. The injectable reduces the risk of HIV transmission by 99.9% compared with unprotected exposure, with dosing every six months, replacing daily oral PrEP regimens. The branded product previously cost over $14,000 per dose, limiting uptake; the generic will be available at about $20 per dose. With FDA clearance, regulators in many countries are likely to accelerate approvals, making this injectable accessible in roughly 120 low- and middle-income countries, potentially within weeks in some places. WHO estimates: in 2025, about 41 million people living with HIV worldwide and 570,000 HIV-related deaths. The generic rollout could reach about 20 million people at risk.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事はHIV予防薬の承認・価格低下に関する医薬品アクセスのニュースであり、インドは製造国（Dr. Reddy's Laboratories）として言及されているのみで、インド国内での感染症発生事例ではないため verified_locations には含めない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYmJjLmNvbS90YW1pbC9hcnRpY2xlcy9jNnJteTl2bjR5NzBv,WATCH,タミル・ナードゥ州クダロール県で大量の鶏が死亡しているが、低病原性鳥インフルエンザは否定され、原因（毒性物質や熱ストレスなど）は調査中のため、続報を注視する必要がある。,Human Infection with Avian Influenza; Avian Influenza,Namakkal; Cuddalore; State of Tamil Nādu; Chennai; Republic of India,Why did thousands of chickens die in Cuddalore in a single week?,கடலூரில் ஒரேவாரத்தில் பல்லாயிரம் கோழிகள் உயிரிழந்தது ஏன்?,2026-11-04T15:55:51+00:00,https://www.bbc.com/tamil/articles/c6rmy9vn4y70o,TAMIL,animals,"Six coastal poultry farms in Cuddalore district, Tamil Nadu, have reported thousands of chicken deaths over the past week around the Diwali period. Farmers claim more than 9,000 birds died across six farms; one farmer says about 4,000 of 5,000 on his farm died in a week, with district losses potentially around 30,000. Government investigators collected carcasses and sent samples to laboratories in Chennai and Namakkal; results are expected in 2–3 days. Tests have ruled out low-virulence avian influenza, while authorities are testing for toxins or other causes. Seasonal factors such as heat stress and rising humidity on coastal farms are considered. Officials have advised reporting any unusual symptoms or sudden deaths and have restricted bringing new chicks pending results; compensation decisions will follow the investigations.",不明,Yes,No,No,1,Yes,不明,不明,不明,不明,1,Yes,Yes,不明,記事では低病原性鳥インフルエンザは否定されており、原因は毒性物質や季節的な熱ストレスの可能性が検討されている。検査結果待ちの段階であり、人への感染報告はない。,
