aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubGJjLmNvLnVrL2FydGljbGUvYnJpdGlzaC1jaXRpemVuLXBvc2l0aXZlLWVib2xhLWNvbmdvLTVIamRrc21fMi8=,PICKUP,エボラというIHR Annex2の即時通知対象疾患であり、英国への患者の国際移送（渡航に関わる事案）を伴うため国際的拡大リスクがあり、社会的関心も高いと判断される。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,British citizen tests positive for Ebola in DR Congo,2026-11-04T16:20:15+00:00,https://www.lbc.co.uk/article/british-citizen-positive-ebola-congo-5Hjdksm_2/,ENGLISH,humans,"A British citizen in the Democratic Republic of Congo has tested positive for Ebola, confirmed on 4 November 2026. The patient tested positive on Wednesday, and a UK government spokesperson said the risk to the UK public remains low. Reuters reported that the individual will be evacuated to the United Kingdom for treatment and will receive care there after evacuation from DR Congo. The report emphasizes that the public health risk to the UK remains low despite the confirmed case. No further clinical details or exposure information are provided in the article. This is a developing, breaking story with more updates expected.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,英国への患者移送が報じられているが、感染発生自体はDRC国内で確認されたものであり、UKは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。続報（感染経路・接触者追跡状況等）の確認が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9ydGVuZnJhbmNhaXMudHYvbmV3cy8xMzk3MTAtZXhwZXJ0cy1vbXMtcmVjb21tYW5kZW50LWFqb3V0LWRldXgtbm91dmVhdXgtdmFjY2lucy1jb250cmUtZWJvbGEtZXNzYWlzLWNsaW5pcXVlcw==,DISMISS,WHO専門家によるワクチン臨床試験への追加推奨に関する研究開発ニュースであり、具体的な症例数や発生地域の報告がなく、実際の感染症アウトブレイクシグナルではない。,Ebola,Oxford; England; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,WHO experts recommend adding two new Ebola vaccines to clinical trials.,Des experts de l'OMS recommandent l'ajout de deux nouveaux vaccins contre l'Ebola aux essais cliniques,2026-11-04T16:24:28+00:00,https://rtenfrancais.tv/news/139710-experts-oms-recommandent-ajout-deux-nouveaux-vaccins-contre-ebola-essais-cliniques,FRENCH,humans,"On 4 November 2026, WHO experts urged adding two Ebola vaccines to ongoing clinical trials: the ChAdOx1 vaccine from the University of Oxford in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India, and Moderna’s mRNA-1469. The WHO press release notes this is the first time vaccines specifically designed to protect against Bundibugyo virus will be evaluated during an active health crisis. The recommendation broadens the experimental Ebola vaccine portfolio under assessment, aiming to accelerate protective options for Ebola virus species. The article does not provide case counts or geographic details beyond the Bundibugyo virus, and no approvals are reported; the focus is on incorporating these candidates into trials to improve readiness for emerging outbreaks.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,不明,不明,No,0,No,No,No,記事はブンディブギョウイルスに対するワクチン候補（ChAdOx1、mRNA-1469）の臨床試験組み入れに関するWHOの推奨についてであり、インドとイギリスはそれぞれワクチン製造元（インド血清研究所）および開発元（オックスフォード大学）として言及されているのみで、実際の発生地域ではないため verified_locations には含めない。症例数や地理的発生情報も記載なし。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hY3AuY2QvcHJvdmluY2UvZWJvbGEtYS1raXNhbmdhbmktZGVzLWFjdGl2aXRlcy1kZS1yaXBvc3RlLXJlYWp1c3RlZXMtYS1saXNzdWUtZGUtbGEtcmV2dWUtaW50cmEtYWN0aW9uLw==,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国キサンガニで進行中のエボラ出血熱アウトブレイクに関する続報であり、対応システムの脆弱性やIPC不備が指摘されているため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当しフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Kisangani; Tshopo; Democratic Republic of the Congo,Ebola in Kisangani: Readjusted response activities following the intra-action review.,Ebola à Kisangani : des activités de riposte réajustées à l'issue de la revue intra-action. - ACP,2026-11-04T16:24:51+00:00,https://acp.cd/province/ebola-a-kisangani-des-activites-de-riposte-reajustees-a-lissue-de-la-revue-intra-action/,FRENCH,humans; environment,"As of 4 November 2026, Ebola virus disease response in Kisangani, Tshopo province, northeastern Democratic Republic of the Congo, has been readjusted after an intra-action review. The review found the initial response system fragile, contributing to a delayed outbreak declaration due to limited laboratory capacity and logistics, with ongoing surveillance weaknesses. Private health facilities in Kisangani were identified as transmission foci because Infection Prevention and Control (IPC) protections for health workers were inadequate. To address these gaps, authorities will intensify collaboration with the most affected zones for the response and bolster preparedness in at-risk areas. The provincial government, with partners, aims to strengthen IPC to better protect health personnel and sustain Ebola control efforts in the region. The report does not provide case counts, deaths, or specific laboratory confirmations.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事は既知のエボラアウトブレイクに対する対応活動の見直しに関する続報。症例数・死亡者数の具体的記載はないが、医療従事者への感染防止策の不備や検査・物流体制の脆弱性が指摘されており、継続的な監視が必要。,
