aHR0cHM6Ly9hY3AuY2QvcHJvdmluY2UvZWJvbGEtYS1tYW5kaW1hLXF1YXRyZS1ub3V2ZWF1eC1ndWVyaXMtcG9ydGVudC1sZS1jdW11bC1hLTYzLw==,PICKUP,DRCイトゥリ州マンディマで進行中のエボラ出血熱アウトブレイクに関する続報であり、重症度・人対人感染リスクが高い疾患のため継続的なリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Ituri; Democratic Republic of the Congo,Ebola in Mandima: four new recoveries bring the total to 63 - ACP.,Ebola à Mandima : quatre nouveaux guéris portent le cumul à 63 - ACP,2026-11-04T16:24:51+00:00,https://acp.cd/province/ebola-a-mandima-quatre-nouveaux-gueris-portent-le-cumul-a-63/,FRENCH,humans,"On 4 November 2026, in Mandima health zone of Ituri province, northeastern Democratic Republic of the Congo, four patients treated for Ebola virus disease were discharged, bringing total recoveries in Mandima to 63. Dr. David Robo, deputy chief of the health zone, announced the four new healings and thanked the patients for consenting to care at the treatment center. He urged recovered individuals to serve as ambassadors against Ebola, educating their communities on clinical signs and the value of early treatment. Medicines are available and care is free, and the health authorities encouraged anyone with suspected symptoms to seek prompt care to improve survival chances. The doctor also called for mobilization by civil society, communities, and response teams to defeat the outbreak.",Yes,No,不明,不明,1,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,本記事は既存のエボラアウトブレイク（マンディマ保健ゾーン）における回復者数の更新報告。新規発生ではないが、エボラは致死率が高く人-人感染のリスクがあるため、既存イベントとして継続的な監視・評価が妥当。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubWlycm9yLmNvLnVrL25ld3MvdWstbmV3cy9lYm9sYS1icml0aXNoLWNpdGl6ZW4tZHItY29uZ28tMzc4NDM3NTE=,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ流行は死者5000人超で過去最悪規模とされ、英国への輸入症例も発生しており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland; Republic of Angola,,Brit tests positive for Ebola and is heading to the UK after evacuation,2026-11-04T16:18:01+00:00,https://www.mirror.co.uk/news/uk-news/ebola-british-citizen-dr-congo-37843751,ENGLISH,humans,"British citizen tests positive for Ebola in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) and will be treated in the UK after evacuation. The infection is linked to the Bundibugyo virus. The UK Foreign Office says the risk to the UK public remains low. The patient’s evacuation marks an imported case from the DRC, with treatment planned in Britain. More than 5,000 people have died this year in the DRC’s Ebola outbreak, described as the deadliest outbreak in the country to date. World Health Organization warnings suggest the outbreak is on course to surpass West Africa’s 2014–2016 epidemic, which killed more than 11,000 people. The report underscores the ongoing severity of the DRC outbreak and the need for continued international attention to Ebola, including monitoring exported and imported cases.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国および アンゴラは発生地域に含まれるが、記事の主題である感染拡大・死亡の中心はDRCであるため、verified_locationsにはDRCのみを記載。英国は輸入症例の治療先、アンゴラへの言及は記事本文中には見られない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubWFya2V0c2NyZWVuZXIuY29tL25ld3MvYnJpdGlzaC1oZWFsdGhjYXJlLXdvcmtlci13aXRoLWVib2xhLXRvLWJlLWV2YWN1YXRlZC1mcm9tLWNvbmdvLXRvLXVrLWRvY3VtZW50LXNob3dzLWNlNzg1ZmRmZGM4ZmYzMjE=,PICKUP,DRCで進行中のエボラ流行はすでに1万例・死亡5000人近くに達する過去2番目の規模のアウトブレイクであり、英国人医療従事者の感染・国際搬送という形で国際的拡大が現実化しているためIHR基準を複数満たす。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,"British healthcare worker with Ebola to be evacuated from Congo to UK, document shows",2026-11-04T16:18:47+00:00,https://www.marketscreener.com/news/british-healthcare-worker-with-ebola-to-be-evacuated-from-congo-to-uk-document-shows-ce785fdfdc8ff321,ENGLISH,humans,"British healthcare worker infected with Ebola evacuated from the Democratic Republic of Congo to the United Kingdom for specialist treatment; the patient has tested positive and is in stable condition, expected to arrive in Britain on Wednesday or Thursday before transfer to a high-consequence infectious disease unit. British authorities say the risk to the UK public remains low and no travel or trade disruption is anticipated. The patient, a British citizen, was sent to Congo by a humanitarian organisation to support outbreak response; this is the first British national case linked to the current outbreak. Other European countries have reported cases. Ebola spreads via direct contact with infected bodily fluids; the World Health Organization notes about 50% fatality on average, with variation. Imported UK cases are rare (four since 1976). The Congo outbreak is the second-largest on record, with more than 10,000 confirmed cases and nearly 5,000 deaths by late October.",Yes,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,DRCにおける大規模エボラ流行（第2位規模、1万例超・死亡約5000人）が主題。英国への患者搬送は人道支援従事者の輸入症例であり、英国自体は対象国リストに含まれないためverified_locationsから除外。欧州他国でも症例報告があるとされるが詳細不明。,
