aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc3RhLnNpL2h0dHAucGhwP2lkPTM2MTg1NDE=,PICKUP,"アフリカ全域で5,300人以上の死者を出しているエボラ出血熱の大規模流行であり、WHOがDRCでのワクチン臨床試験を承認するなど国際的対応が進行中であるため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。",Ebola,Genève; Genève; Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Switzerland,WHO approved testing of two new vaccines against Ebola.,WHO odobril testiranje dveh novih cepiv proti eboli,2026-11-04T16:35:00+00:00,https://www.sta.si/http.php?id=3618541,SLOVENIAN,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, Geneva reports that the World Health Organization has approved clinical testing of two new Ebola vaccines. The testing follows an Africa-wide outbreak that has claimed more than 5,300 lives, with the Democratic Republic of the Congo singled out for vaccine trials. The WHO approval signals accelerated efforts to assess safety and potential protection against Ebola while frontline clinicians continue outbreak management and patient care in affected regions. The report emphasizes the ongoing international response to the Ebola crisis and the role of vaccination research in halting transmission. No further details on trial phase or laboratory confirmation are provided in the article.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,発生地域にGenève/Switzerlandが含まれるが、これはWHO本部所在地であり実際の発生国ではないため除外。記事はDRCを含むアフリカ全域での大規模エボラ流行とそれに対するWHOのワクチン試験承認を報じている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZWx1bml2ZXJzYWwuY29tLm14L211bmRvL29tcy1hcHJ1ZWJhLWVuc2F5b3MtY2xpbmljb3MtZGUtbnVldmFzLXZhY3VuYXMtY29udHJhLWVsLWVib2xhLWVwaWRlbWlhLWVuLWFmcmljYS1oYS1tYXRhZG8tYS1tYXMtZGUtNS1taWwtMzAwLXBlcnNvbmFzLw==,PICKUP,"DRCにおけるエボラ流行で5,300人以上の死者が出ており、公衆衛生への深刻な影響と国際的拡大リスクが認められるため、IHR基準複数該当でフルRRAへ進めるべき。",Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"WHO approves clinical trials of new Ebola vaccines; Ebola epidemic in Africa has killed more than 5,300 people.",OMS aprueba ensayos clínicos de nuevas vacunas contra el ébola; epidemia en África ha matado a más de 5 mil 300 personas,2026-11-04T16:27:00+00:00,https://www.eluniversal.com.mx/mundo/oms-aprueba-ensayos-clinicos-de-nuevas-vacunas-contra-el-ebola-epidemia-en-africa-ha-matado-a-mas-de-5-mil-300-personas/,SPANISH,humans,"As of November 4, 2026, the World Health Organization approved clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccine candidates. Expert groups recommended adding these two candidates to vaccine trials launched in late October in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC). WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus announced the move. The Ebola epidemic in Africa has killed more than 5,300 people. The approval reflects an ongoing effort to expand vaccination options amid the outbreak in the DRC. The development aims to improve protection against Ebola by evaluating the safety and efficacy of the two additional vaccine candidates within the established trial framework. These trials represent an escalation in vaccination strategy as authorities monitor performance in affected populations.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"死者数5,300人超という既存の大規模流行の継続情報であり、ワクチン臨床試験承認は対応策の進展を示す。既にフルRRA対象となっている可能性が高いが、続報として重要。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZGFpbHltYWlsLmNvbS93aXJlcy9hZnAvYXJ0aWNsZS0xNjI2NTY3Ny9XSE8tYXBwcm92ZXMtY2xpbmljYWwtdHJpYWxzLXR3by1uZXctRWJvbGEtdmFjY2luZXMuaHRtbA==,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で進行中のブンディブギョウイルス(エボラ属)流行は致死率50%超、感染者約10,444人・死者5,300人超と深刻であり、国境管理も導入されておりIHR基準を複数満たすためフルRRAへ進むべき。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,,WHO approves clinical trials on two new Ebola vaccines,2026-11-04T16:32:35+00:00,https://www.dailymail.com/wires/afp/article-16265677/WHO-approves-clinical-trials-two-new-Ebola-vaccines.html,ENGLISH,humans,"WHO approves clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccines in the Democratic Republic of Congo amid an ongoing Bundibugyo virus outbreak that has killed more than 5,300 people and infected about 10,444 cases, with a fatality rate above 50%. Last month, the Ervebo vaccine—approved for Ebola virus—began a trial but is not approved for Bundibugyo virus. The two additional candidates, ChAdOx1 BDBV (Oxford University with Serum Institute of India) and Moderna's mRNA-1469, are being tested specifically against Bundibugyo virus. The DRC's National Institute for Biomedical Research leads the trial with WHO backing. Border controls have been introduced as governments seek to halt spread. WHO stresses vaccines are powerful tools but not substitutes for early care, contact tracing, isolation, safe and dignified burials, and community engagement.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドはSerum Institute of Indiaがワクチン開発に協力しているとの記載のみで、感染事例発生国ではないためverified_locationsから除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9ub3RpY2lhcy5yNy5jb20vc2F1ZGUvdmFuaXR5LWJyYXNpbC9ob3J0b2xhbmRpYS1jb25maXJtYS1wcmltZWlyby1jYXNvLWRlLWxlaXNobWFuaW9zZS12aXNjZXJhbC1lbS1jYWNob3Jyby1lLWluaWNpYS10ZXN0ZXMtZW0tMTAzLWFuaW1haXMtMDQxMTIwMjYv,DISMISS,犬1頭での内臓リーシュマニア症確認に過ぎず、ヒトへの感染拡大は確認されていない。既知の風土病であり国際的な懸念も低い。,Leishmaniasis; Visceral Leishmaniasis,São Paulo; Hortolândia; Campinas; São Paulo; Federative Republic of Brazil,Hortolândia confirms first case of visceral leishmaniasis in a dog and begins testing on 103 animals.,Hortolândia confirma primeiro caso de leishmaniose visceral em cachorro e inicia testes em 103 animais,2026-11-04T16:37:34+00:00,https://noticias.r7.com/saude/vanity-brasil/hortolandia-confirma-primeiro-caso-de-leishmaniose-visceral-em-cachorro-e-inicia-testes-em-103-animais-04112026/,PORTUGUESE,environment; humans; vectors; animals,"Visceral leishmaniasis confirmed in a dog in Hortolândia, São Paulo, Brazil, marking the first canine case in the city. A confirmatory test is awaited; 103 dogs in Jardim Santa Clara do Lago II are being screened. Blood collection runs Nov 3–5, 2026, with samples sent to Instituto Adolfo Lutz in Campinas for laboratory analysis. UVZ teams registered dogs and educated residents about transmission by the sand fly. Hortolândia has recorded one human visceral leishmaniasis case in 2016. Leishmaniasis is a serious parasitic disease affecting liver and spleen in humans; dogs show appetite loss, weight loss, lethargy, skin lesions around the nose and ears, hair loss, abdominal distention, ocular issues, vomiting, and diarrhea. Free treatment is available via SUS for humans and animals; preventive measures include environmental sanitation and removal of organic waste to curb sand fly breeding.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,No,No,No,動物（犬）での症例確認が主体で、ヒトの新規感染例は報告されていない。サンドフライ媒介の既知の風土病に対する地域的な予防措置が中心。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9jb3JyZWlvZG9lc3RhZG8uY29tLmJyLzIwMjYvMTEvMDQvc2VzLXZhY2luYS10cmFiYWxoYWRvcmVzLWRlLWFlcm9wb3J0by1wYXJhLXByZXZlbmlzLWVudHJhZGEtZG8tc2FyYW1wby1lbS1tcy5odG1s,PICKUP,ブラジル全国で麻疹感染が拡大しており（2026年61例確認、複数州で活動中）、ヒトーヒト感染力が高く空港という人流拠点での予防接種対応が取られている。州・国レベルの行政対応（関心）が確認できるためフルRRAでの評価が妥当。,Measles,Campo Grande; Mato Grosso do Sul; São Paulo; Amazonas; São Paulo; Tabatinga; Federative Republic of Brazil,State Health Secretariat vaccinates airport workers to prevent measles from entering Mato Grosso do Sul.,SES vacina trabalhadores de aeroporto para prevenis entrada do sarampo em MS,2026-11-04T12:23:00+00:00,https://correiodoestado.com.br/2026/11/04/ses-vacina-trabalhadores-de-aeroporto-para-prevenis-entrada-do-sarampo-em-ms.html,PORTUGUESE,humans,"At Campo Grande International Airport in Mato Grosso do Sul, Brazil, on November 4, 2026, the State Health Secretariat vaccinated airport workers and travelers against measles, administering 30 doses and distributing guidance on symptoms and prevention. The campaign targets importation and spread as measles activity rises nationwide. Brazil has 61 confirmed measles cases in 2026 as of October 22, with active transmission in São Paulo, Santo André (SP), and Tabatinga (AM); MS has no confirmed cases this year, but two suspects remain under investigation. Investigations collect blood, urine, and respiratory secretions, with possible Fiocruz lab confirmation; the process can take about 30 days. Between Oct 4 and Nov 4, 79 MS municipalities conducted active record searches; results are due by Nov 27, with a state report to MoH by Dec 1. SUS vaccines are free; the airport vaccination aims to boost protection for workers and travelers.",No,No,No,No,0,不明,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,マトグロッソ・ド・スル州自体に確定例はなく疑い例2件が調査中。感染確認地域はサンパウロ州、アマゾナス州（タバチンガ）。全国的な麻疹活動の高まりを受けた予防的対応であり、重症度や死亡情報は記事に記載なし。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYWEuY29tLnRyL2VuL2hlYWx0aC93aG8tc2F5cy0yLW5ldy1jYW5kaWRhdGUtdmFjY2luZXMtdG8tam9pbi1lYm9sYS10cmlhbC1pbi1kci1jb25nby80MTExODIw,PICKUP,"DRCのエボラ流行は10,000例・5,000人死亡を超え新規感染拠点も出現しており、IHR基準（深刻性・国際拡大リスク・渡航制限関連）を複数満たすためフルRRAへの移行が妥当。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of the Sudan,,WHO says 2 new candidate vaccines to join Ebola trial in DR Congo,2026-11-04T16:31:32+00:00,https://www.aa.com.tr/en/health/who-says-2-new-candidate-vaccines-to-join-ebola-trial-in-dr-congo/4111820,ENGLISH,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, the WHO announced two additional Ebola vaccine candidates will join Congo’s Bundibugyo virus trial: ChAdOx1 BDBV (Oxford University with Serum Institute of India) and Moderna’s mRNA-1469, to be added alongside Ervebo which began the trial last month for Zaire ebolavirus. In the Democratic Republic of Congo, Ebola totals exceed 10,000 cases and 5,000 deaths, with new infection hotspots continuing to emerge. Tedros urged lifting travel restrictions to foster transparent reporting and said WHO will support neighboring countries in preparing for possible importations. In climate-health context ahead of COP31, the WHO emphasizes climate action as a health crisis, potentially preventing 1.6 million deaths annually and delivering about $9.3 trillion in benefits. Separately, WHO notes over 230 attacks on healthcare in Sudan since the war began, with more than 2,000 deaths and ongoing access challenges.",Yes,No,Yes,Yes,3,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドはワクチン製造企業（Serum Institute of India）の所在地として言及されているのみで発生国ではない。スーダンは別件（医療施設への攻撃）であり、本記事のエボラ発生国はDRCのみ。既存の継続的流行であるため「異常・予想外」はNoと評価したが、新規ホットスポット出現と近隣国への拡大懸念は重要な継続監視ポイント。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY29ycmVpb2RvcG92by5jb20uYnIvbm90JUMzJUFEY2lhcy9zYSVDMyVCQWRlL29tcy1hcHJvdmEtZW5zYWlvcy1jbGluaWNvcy1kZS1kdWFzLW5vdmFzLXZhY2luYXMtY29udHJhLW8tZWJvbGEtMS4xNzYxNzM5,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で進行中のエボラ出血熱アウトブレイクが5,300人超の死者を出しており、IHR基準の深刻性・異常性・国際拡大リスクに該当するためフルRRAへ進むべきシグナルと判断。",Hemorrhagic Fever; Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,WHO approves clinical trials of two new Ebola vaccines,OMS aprova ensaios clínicos de duas novas vacinas contra o ebola,2026-11-04T00:00:00+00:00,https://www.correiodopovo.com.br/not%C3%ADcias/sa%C3%BAde/oms-aprova-ensaios-clinicos-de-duas-novas-vacinas-contra-o-ebola-1.1761739,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Two Ebola vaccine candidates have been approved by the World Health Organization to enter clinical trials in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, where the current Ebola outbreak has caused over 5,300 deaths, the majority in the DRC. Trials began in late October 2026, following the outbreak declaration on May 15, 2026, though experts say the virus circulated for months earlier. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus announced the inclusion of the two vaccines in the ongoing trial program. Ebola is transmitted by contact with bodily fluids and causes severe hemorrhagic fever. Africa-wide, Ebola has caused more than 15,000 deaths over the past five decades, with the worst RDC outbreak (2018–2020) recording about 2,300 deaths and 3,500 cases. The current efforts aim to accelerate vaccination options amid this central African outbreak.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"記事はWHOによるワクチン臨床試験承認が主題だが、背景として大規模なエボラアウトブレイク（5,300人超死亡）が進行中であり、既存の公衆衛生危機として評価対象とした。",
aHR0cHM6Ly9uei5uZXdzLnlhaG9vLmNvbS9icml0aXNoLWNpdGl6ZW4tdGVzdHMtcG9zaXRpdmUtZWJvbGEtMTYxNjU3MjgxLmh0bWw=,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ流行（1万人超の症例、約5000人の死亡、史上2番目の規模）に加え、英国人への感染・国際医療搬送という国際的拡大が確認されており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,British health worker tests positive for Ebola in Democratic Republic of Congo,2026-11-04T16:32:12+00:00,https://nz.news.yahoo.com/british-citizen-tests-positive-ebola-161657281.html,ENGLISH,humans,"British health worker tests positive for Ebola in the Democratic Republic of Congo, the first case among a British national linked to the current outbreak. The unnamed patient is being medically evacuated to the UK for specialist treatment and is in stable condition; arrival is expected Wednesday or Thursday to be transported to a high-consequence infectious disease unit. The DRC outbreak, caused by the Bundibugyo strain, has surpassed 10,000 cases and nearly 5,000 deaths since May. The individual was deployed to Congo by a humanitarian organisation to support the response. UK officials say the risk to the UK public remains low, imported cases are rare (four confirmed since 1976), and no disruption to international travel or trade is anticipated. Transmission is via direct contact with infected bodily fluids; mortality varies, and the Bundibugyo outbreak is the second-largest on record with over 10,000 cases and ~5,000 deaths by October.",Yes,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国への症例輸出は確認されているが、英国はトリアージ対象国リストに含まれないためverified_locationsから除外。DRCでの流行自体が主題であり、同国のみを計上。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9zYTI0LmNvL3Nob3c3NzI1NjQyMzguaHRtbA==,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で進行中のエボラ出血熱（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクに関する国際的なワクチン治験のニュースであり、疾患の重篤性・ヒト-ヒト感染可能性・国際支援の必要性からPICKUPと判断。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,World Health Organization: Two candidate vaccines to join Ebola vaccination trials for the Bundibugyo strain,الصحة العالمية لقاحان مرشحان للانضمام لتجربة تطعيمات إيبولا لسلالة بونديبوجيو,2026-11-04T16:54:42+00:00,https://sa24.co/show772564238.html,ARABIC,humans,"Two candidate Ebola vaccines were recommended by WHO expert groups to join the ongoing Tomini vaccine trial in the Democratic Republic of Congo, targeting the Bundibugyo strain driving the current outbreak. The two vaccines are ChAdOx1, developed by University of Oxford with Serum Institute of India, and mRNA-1469 from Moderna. The WHO Independent Technical Advisory Group on Vaccines prioritized further clinical evaluation this week, based on available early clinical and preclinical data. Companies were notified on Monday, and both candidates are slated to begin additional assessment within the week as part of the trial in DRC. This represents the first time vaccines designed specifically to protect against Bundibugyo are being evaluated in the outbreak context, alongside the Tomini vaccine.",Yes,不明,不明,不明,1,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はDRCで継続中のエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクに対するワクチン治験拡大の発表。インド（Serum Institute of India）・英国（Oxford大学）はワクチン開発・製造拠点であり、発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cueW91bTcuY29tL3N0b3J5LzIwMjYvMTEvNC8lRDglQTclRDklODQlRDglQjUlRDglQUQlRDglQTktJUQ4JUE3JUQ5JTg0JUQ4JUI5JUQ4JUE3JUQ5JTg0JUQ5JTg1JUQ5JThBJUQ4JUE5LSVEOSU4NCVEOSU4MiVEOCVBNyVEOCVBRCVEOCVBNyVEOSU4Ni0lRDklODUlRDglQjElRDglQjQlRDglQUQlRDglQTc=,PICKUP,DRCで進行中のブンディブギョ株エボラアウトブレイクに対し、WHOが新規ワクチン候補の治験参加を承認するなど国際的な対応が継続しており、既知のアウトブレイクに関する重要な続報としてフルRRA対象とすべきと判断。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,World Health Organization: Two candidate vaccines to join an Ebola vaccination trial for the Bundibugyo strain.,الصحة العالمية: لقاحان مرشحان للانضمام لتجربة تطعيمات إيبولا لسلالة بونديبوجيو,2026-11-04T16:48:13+00:00,https://www.youm7.com/story/2026/11/4/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B5%D8%AD%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%84%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%AD%D8%A7%D9%86-%D9%85%D8%B1%D8%B4%D8%AD%D8%A7%D9%86-%D9%84%D9%84%D8%A7%D9%86%D8%B6%D9%85%D8%A7%D9%85-%D9%84%D8%AA%D8%AC%D8%B1%D8%A8%D8%A9-%D8%AA%D8%B7%D8%B9%D9%8A%D9%85%D8%A7%D8%AA-%D8%A5%D9%8A%D8%A8%D9%88%D9%84%D8%A7-%D9%84%D8%B3%D9%84%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A9-%D8%A8%D9%88%D9%86%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A8%D9%88%D8%AC%D9%8A%D9%88/7606287,ARABIC,humans,"Two Ebola vaccine candidates—ChAdOx1 (Oxford University) and mRNA-1469 (Moderna)—were recommended by WHO expert groups to join the Tomani ring-vaccination trial in the Democratic Republic of Congo, the first evaluation of vaccines designed specifically against the Bundibugyo Ebola strain during this outbreak. The WHO SAGE panel urged further clinical assessment this week based on available early data; developers were notified Monday, and trials will begin after national approvals. Tomani tests multiple vaccines in a single trial by vaccinating contacts of confirmed Bundibugyo cases. It uses a ring vaccination approach and builds on prior experience with Ervebo (Ebola Zaire vaccine) in Tomani. Four vaccination groups exist, consisting of contacts of infected or deceased individuals; additional groups are being prepared. Separately, the PARTNERS trial is evaluating MBP134 monoclonal antibody and remdesivir, alone or in combination, with Obildivisir added soon for post-exposure prophylaxis. Results are expected: treatments in coming months, vaccines in early 2027.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,本記事はDRCで進行中のブンディブギョ株エボラアウトブレイクに対するワクチン・治療薬治験（Tomani試験、PARTNERS試験）に関するWHOの発表内容であり、既存アウトブレイクの対応進展を示す続報。アウトブレイクの規模・症例数・死亡者数など詳細情報は本記事に含まれていないため不明。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZGFpbHlzdGFyLmNvLnVrL25ld3MvbGF0ZXN0LW5ld3MvYnJlYWtpbmctYnJpdC10ZXN0cy1wb3NpdGl2ZS1lYm9sYS0zNzg0Mzg3MQ==,PICKUP,DRCでエボラウイルス病に感染した英国人医療従事者が本国搬送されるという、国際的な感染拡大・越境移送を伴う事例であり、IHR基準の複数項目に該当するためフルRRAへの移行が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,Brit tests positive for Ebola and 'will be sent back to UK for treatment',2026-11-04T16:50:43+00:00,https://www.dailystar.co.uk/news/latest-news/breaking-brit-tests-positive-ebola-37843871,ENGLISH,humans,"A British healthcare worker in the Democratic Republic of Congo has tested positive for Ebola virus disease and will be repatriated to the United Kingdom for treatment. The patient, a British citizen on duty in the DRC, contracted Ebola while serving as a healthcare worker. The Foreign Office confirmed the positive test and said the risk to the UK public remains low. The story is breaking news with updates expected; no further details on symptoms, case counts, transmission, or laboratory confirmation are provided. The incident reflects an imported case to the UK, with treatment to be administered on arrival. No timeline for repatriation is stated, and no mortality or symptom details are provided.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国への搬送は輸入症例であり、発生国はDRC。英国(UK)は対象国リストに含まれないためverified_locationsから除外。症状詳細・感染経路・検査確定情報など多くが不明であり、続報の確認が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYmJjLmNvLnVrL25ld3MvYXJ0aWNsZXMvY3JxOG5qN3hxZHY5bw==,PICKUP,DRCで史上最悪規模のエボラアウトブレイク（1万人超の症例、致死率48.6%）が継続中で、英国人医療従事者の感染・国際搬送という国際的拡大の兆候が確認されたため。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,UK national tests positive for Ebola virus in DR Congo,2026-11-04T16:53:02+00:00,https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crq8nj7xqdv9o,ENGLISH,humans,"British national in the Democratic Republic of Congo has tested positive for Ebola, confirmed by the UK government on 4 November 2026. This marks the first confirmed case of a UK national contracting Ebola during the current outbreak in DR Congo, which has produced more than 10,000 confirmed cases and over 5,000 deaths since May. The UK states it has well-established procedures and that the public risk remains low as these procedures are activated. Reuters reported the patient is a healthcare worker and would be brought to the UK for treatment, though the Foreign Office has not confirmed repatriation. The DR Congo outbreak is described as the deadliest in the country's history, with a fatality rate of 48.6% at the end of October. No infection source is disclosed.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国は対象国リストに含まれないため、verified_locationsからは除外。感染源は未公表。英国本土への感染拡大リスクは低いとされているが、国際搬送事例として国際的拡大の懸念材料となる。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hcXVpbm90aWNpYXMuY29tL3ZpdmEtdmlkYS9zYXVkZS1lLWJlbS1lc3Rhci9lbC1uaW5vLXBvZGUtYXVtZW50YXItY2Fzb3MtZGUtZGVuZ3VlLW5vLWJyYXNpbC12ZWphLWNvbW8tcHJldmVuaXIv,WATCH,将来予測（2027年）に基づく将来的なデング熱増加リスクの報道であり、現時点での急性アウトブレイクではないが、流行拡大の可能性があるため経過観察とする。,Dengue,Federative Republic of Brazil,El Niño could increase dengue cases in Brazil; see how to prevent.,El Niño pode aumentar casos de dengue no Brasil; veja como prevenir,2026-11-04T16:03:29+00:00,https://aquinoticias.com/viva-vida/saude-e-bem-estar/el-nino-pode-aumentar-casos-de-dengue-no-brasil-veja-como-prevenir/,PORTUGUESE,humans; environment,"Brazil could face up to 5.6 million dengue cases in 2027 as El Niño intensifies heat and rainfall, Fiocruz’s InfoDengue projections show. Nationwide estimates range 1.7–5.6 million, with the Southeast potentially up to 60% higher and the South about 20% under an intense El Niño. LIRAa indicates 49.2% of assessed municipalities are at alert or risk. Transmission largely occurs in homes from breeding sites such as plant pot trays, refrigerator drip pans, AC condensate collectors, gutters, drains, and uncovered water containers. Prevention emphasizes removing standing water, cleaning gutters/drains, sealing tanks, protecting plant trays, safeguarding bottles, installing screens, and using registered repellents. Dengue symptoms include fever, headache, myalgias, rash, and fatigue; warning signs require urgent care. Qdenga vaccination is available via SUS for 10–14-year-olds, two doses 3 months apart.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,不明,No,記事はFiocruz/InfoDengueによる2027年に向けた将来予測・予防啓発記事であり、現在進行中のアウトブレイク報告ではない。デング熱はブラジルで季節性・流行性が高く、エルニーニョによる増加予測は継続的な注視が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hZnJpY2EuYnVzaW5lc3NpbnNpZGVyLmNvbS9sb2NhbC9tYXJrZXRzL3doaWxlLWJhdHRsaW5nLWVib2xhLW91dGJyZWFrLWFuZC1mYWNpbmctdXMtcmVzdHJpY3Rpb25zLWNvbmdvLWlzLWhpdC1ieS1hbm90aGVyLzZjNmw2ZGo=,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で史上2番目に大規模なエボラ流行（1万例超、死亡約5,100人）が継続中であり、米国が渡航歴申告を義務化するなど国際的対応が取られている。加えてカバ28頭が炭疽で死亡し人への感染拡大リスクも指摘されており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルリスク評価へ進むべき事案。",Anthrax; Ebola,Province du Nord-Kivu; Butembo; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States,,"While battling Ebola outbreak and facing U.S. restrictions, Congo is hit by another anthrax but brave survivors enter deadly isolation wards to comfort infected children",2026-11-04T16:51:57+00:00,https://africa.businessinsider.com/local/markets/while-battling-ebola-outbreak-and-facing-us-restrictions-congo-is-hit-by-another/6c6l6dj,ENGLISH,environment; humans; animals,"Anthrax has killed 28 hippopotamuses along the Semuliki River in Virunga National Park, eastern Democratic Republic of Congo, signaling potential spillover risk to humans via contact with sick or dead wildlife or consumption of meat. Bacillus anthracis confirmation underpins the wildlife outbreak, with hippo deaths observed since mid-September and continuing over about a month. In parallel, Congo reports the second-largest Ebola epidemic on record, with more than 10,000 cases and about 5,100 deaths; no vaccine or approved specific treatment exists, and the outbreak has prompted heightened border screening as the United States requires travelers from Congo to declare travel history within the prior 21 days. In hospitals such as Kitatumba Reference Hospital in Butembo, recovered Ebola survivors—like 29-year-old Jerkis Mahamba, who spent 18 days ill—are entering isolation wards to comfort infected children, helping fight stigma and restore hope.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事は主にコンゴのエボラ流行と炭疽（カバの大量死）の2つの公衆衛生事象を扱っている。米国は対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations から除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGhlc3VuLmNvLnVrL2hlYWx0aC80MDkxNTMzMy9icml0YWluLWVib2xhLWNvbmdvLXRocmVhdC1wb3NpdGl2ZS8=,PICKUP,DRCで史上2番目の規模・最速拡大のエボラ流行が継続し、英国人感染者や近隣国(ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダ)への拡大が報告されており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルRRAへ進むべき。,Ebola,Africa; Republic of Angola; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,Brit tests positive for Ebola as experts warn outbreak 'poses threat worldwide',2026-11-04T16:18:25+00:00,https://www.thesun.co.uk/health/40915333/britain-ebola-congo-threat-positive/,ENGLISH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has reached 10,060 confirmed cases and 4,887 deaths, the fastest-growing and second-largest Ebola outbreak on record, behind West Africa's 2014-16 epidemic (28,616 cases; >11,000 deaths). A British citizen in the DRC has tested positive; Kenya reports nine cases and two deaths as of Oct 23, with Nigeria confirming cases, and Uganda having infections earlier in the summer. The Bundibugyo strain carries a 30-50% mortality rate and there is currently no approved vaccine or treatment. The UK Foreign Office says the risk to the public remains low. WHO notes conflicts, hard-to-reach areas, the rainy season, and misinformation as containment barriers. Africa CDC planned a meeting on Oct 28 to discuss regional health-security implications. The outbreak began mid-May and continues to spread in the DRC and neighboring countries.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"発生地域にはAngola, Kenya, Uganda, Nigeria, UK等が含まれるが、対象国リストに該当するのはDRCのみ。記事の主題はDRCでの大規模流行であり、他国は二次的な症例報告にとどまる。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubm90aWNpYXNhb21pbnV0by5jb20vbXVuZG8vMzA3ODU1NS9lYm9sYS1kdWFzLXZhY2luYXMtY29udHJhLWJ1bmRpYnVneW8tZW50cmFtLWVtLWVuc2Fpby1jbGluaWNv,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国でのエボラ出血熱（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクは既に5,100人以上の死者を出し同国史上最悪规模とされ、国際的なワクチン試験・WHO関与が続く重大な公衆衛生事案であるため。",Ebola,Republic of Sierra Leone; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Liberia; Republic of Guinea,Ebola: Two vaccines against Bundibugyo virus enter clinical trials.,Ébola: Duas vacinas contra Bundibugyo entram em ensaio clínico,2026-11-04T16:52:09+00:00,https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/mundo/3078555/ebola-duas-vacinas-contra-bundibugyo-entram-em-ensaio-clinico,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Two vaccines specifically developed for Bundibugyo virus will enter clinical trials in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, where Ebola has caused more than 5,100 deaths and about 10,500 infections. The World Health Organization announced after independent experts recommended adding vaccines from Oxford University (in collaboration with Serum Institute of India) and Moderna to the Tumaini trial in the DRC, ongoing since late October. This is the first time Bundibugyo-specific vaccines are evaluated during an Ebola outbreak. Tumaini uses ring vaccination, testing several candidates among contacts of confirmed Bundibugyo cases. The platform also evaluates an existing Ebola vaccine against the Zaire strain for potential protection against Bundibugyo. The DRC outbreak is the deadliest in the country’s history, with projections that it could surpass the 2014–2016 West Africa outbreak of 28,616 cases and 11,325 deaths in Guinea, Liberia, and Sierra Leone.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はワクチン臨床試験に関する報道だが、背景となるDRCのエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクは同国史上最悪規模で進行中。シエラレオネ・リベリア・ギニアは2014-2016年の西アフリカ流行への歴史的言及であり、現アウトブレイクの発生地ではないため除外。インドはワクチン製造元（Serum Institute of India）としての言及のみで発生地ではないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc2F3dGJlaXJ1dC5jb20vd29ybGQtbmV3cy8lRDglQTUlRDglQjUlRDglQTclRDglQTglRDglQTktJUQ5JTg1JUQ5JTg4JUQ4JUE3JUQ4JUI3JUQ5JTg2LSVEOCVBOCVEOCVCMSVEOSU4QSVEOCVCNyVEOCVBNyVEOSU4NiVEOSU4QS0lRDglQTglRDklODElRDklOEElRDglQjElRDklODglRDglQjMtJUQ4JUE=,PICKUP,進行中のDRCエボラ流行の中で外国籍（英国人）感染者が確認されたことは国際的拡大リスクと渡航制限リスクを示唆し、IHR基準を複数満たすためフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,A British citizen infected with the Ebola virus in the Democratic Republic of the Congo... How did London respond?,إصابة مواطن بريطاني بفيروس إيبولا في الكونغو الديمقراطية.. كيف علّقت لندن؟,2026-11-04T16:55:09+00:00,https://www.sawtbeirut.com/world-news/%D8%A5%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%A8%D8%A9-%D9%85%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%B7%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%8A-%D8%A8%D9%81%D9%8A%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3-%D8%A5%D9%8A%D8%A8%D9%88%D9%84%D8%A7-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%A7/,ARABIC,humans,"Ebola virus infection confirmed in a British citizen in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. A UK government spokesperson said laboratory tests confirmed the British national is infected with Ebola while currently in the DRC; the spokesperson stressed that the risk to the UK population remains low. The statement did not provide further details on the patient's health condition or circumstances of infection. The announcement highlights that the confirmed case is located within the DRC outbreak area and does not indicate onward transmission in Britain. Officials did not specify exposure timing or potential travel to the UK, and no additional case numbers or fatalities were disclosed. The situation is being monitored as of 4 November 2026.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,感染は英国人がDRC滞在中に発生したものであり、発生地域としてはDRCのみを対象国とした。英国は対象国リストに含まれないため除外。感染経路・曝露時期・帰国有無など詳細情報は不明であり、続報の確認が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9nci5ldXJvbmV3cy5jb20vMjAyNi8xMS8wNC93aG8tYmFja3MtdHJpYWxzLWZvci10d28tbmV3LXZhY2NpbmVzLWFnYWluc3QtZWJvbGEtb3V0YnJlYWs=,PICKUP,"DRCを中心に感染者1万人超・死者5,300人超という深刻なエボラ流行が継続し、複数国への拡大と渡航制限も発生しているためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Oxford; England; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,The WHO supported clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccines.,Ο ΠΟΥ στήριξε κλινικές δοκιμές για δύο νέα εμβόλια Έμπολα,2026-11-04T17:08:51+00:00,https://gr.euronews.com/2026/11/04/who-backs-trials-for-two-new-vaccines-against-ebola-outbreak,GREEK,humans,"WHO-backed clinical trials will evaluate two new Ebola vaccine candidates specifically developed for Bundibugyo Ebola virus, as an outbreak across several African countries continues. The outbreak, which began in May in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), has infected more than 10,000 people and killed over 5,300, with the DRC accounting for about 5,103 deaths as of 31 October. Cases have also been reported in Kenya, Nigeria, and Uganda. The two vaccines—developed by the University of Oxford in collaboration with Serum Institute of India and Moderna—will be tested in a trial led by the National Institute for Biomedical Research (NIBR) in the DRC, with international partners including WHO. WHO cautioned that vaccines complement but do not replace established measures such as timely care, contact tracing, isolation, safe burials, and community engagement. Some countries have imposed travel restrictions on arrivals from the DRC, which WHO and Africa CDC oppose.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダへの症例報告があるが対象国リスト外のため除外。インド（Serum Institute of India）と英国（Oxford大学）はワクチン開発機関としての関与でありアウトブレイク発生地ではないため除外。,
