aHR0cHM6Ly9oc2Jub3RpY2lhcy5jb20vbm90aWNpYXMvbnVldm9zLWNhc29zLWRlLW1hbGFyaWEtZW4tZWwtdmFsbGU=,DISMISS,コンゴ民主共和国への渡航歴を持つコロンビア人における輸入マラリア症例であり、対象国での発生ではなく、ヒト-ヒト感染やアウトブレイクの兆候もないため見送りとする。,Malaria Falciparum; Ebola; Malaria,Cali; Departamento del Valle del Cauca; Palmira; Republic of Colombia,New Malaria Cases in the Valley | HSB Noticias,Nuevos casos de malaria en el Valle | HSB Noticias,2026-11-04T17:07:50+00:00,https://hsbnoticias.com/noticias/nuevos-casos-de-malaria-en-el-valle,SPANISH,humans,"Four imported malaria cases caused by Plasmodium falciparum have been confirmed in Valle del Cauca, Colombia, following recent travel to the Democratic Republic of the Congo. A 33-year-old man died on October 31 in a Palmira hospital; a 50-year-old man in Cali remains under specialist treatment. The remaining two infections were identified through epidemiological surveillance after the initial cases, and both patients show malaria-compatible symptoms and are under treatment. Health authorities, including the Ministry of Health and the National Institute of Health, are maintaining coordination with local secretariats to strengthen follow-up, control, and monitoring of these imported cases. As part of the epidemiological investigation, additional tests ruled out other infectious diseases, including Ebola; no Ebola cases have been confirmed. Contact tracing and travel-route reconstruction continue to determine exposure factors and preventive actions.",No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,No,No,1,No,No,No,症例はコロンビアで確認された輸入マラリア（渡航先はDRC）であり、DRCでの発生事例ではないため対象国として計上しない。コロンビアは対象国リストに含まれない。エボラは検査で否定されている。,
