aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaXMuZmkva290aW1hYS9hcnQtMjAwMDAxMjM4OTQ0Ny5odG1s,PICKUP,IHR基準(深刻性・異常性・国際拡大)が3つ該当し、DRCでの進行中のエボラ流行に関連した国際的な症例拡大が確認されるためフルRRAへ進める。,Hemorrhagic Fever; Ebola,Switzerland; Republic of France; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,Ebola diagnosed in a British citizen,Britannian kansalaisella todettu ebola,2026-11-04T17:15:00+00:00,https://www.is.fi/kotimaa/art-2000012389447.html,FINNISH,humans,"A British citizen has been diagnosed with Ebola, the first known infection among a UK national linked to the current epidemic. The patient, a healthcare worker, was evacuated from the Democratic Republic of Congo to Britain for treatment; the condition is stable and arrival in the UK is expected on Wednesday or Thursday (as of 4 November 2026). Local authorities say the case is unlikely to significantly affect Britain’s overall health situation. The patient’s identity has not been disclosed; he had previously left Congo through a humanitarian organization to help combat the outbreak. Europe has seen imported cases before, including Switzerland’s evacuation of an Ebola patient from Nigeria and France’s first confirmed case in June in a doctor who had returned from Congo. UKHSA notes only four confirmed imported Ebola cases in Britain since 1976. Ebola causes hemorrhagic fever and is transmitted via bodily fluids, with a case fatality around 50%, varying by outbreak.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はDRCで進行中のエボラ流行に関連した医療従事者の輸入症例（英国搬送）を報じている。スイス・フランス・英国・ナイジェリアは輸入先/過去事例として言及されているが対象国リストに含まれないか、発生国ではないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaW5kZXBlbmRlbnQuY28udWsvbmV3cy9oZWFsdGgvaXMtdGhlcmUtYW4tZWJvbGEtdmFjY2luZS1iMjk5NjQzMy5odG1s,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国東部で782例確認・181例死亡（致死率約40%）のブンディブギョ株エボラ流行が継続しており、承認された治療・ワクチンが存在しないため、公衆衛生上深刻かつ国際的拡大リスクを伴う重大シグナルと判断。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,,The treatments being developed for the Bundibugyo strain of Ebola,2026-11-04T17:17:29+00:00,https://www.independent.co.uk/news/health/is-there-an-ebola-vaccine-b2996433.html,ENGLISH,humans,"Bundibugyo ebolavirus (BDBV) outbreak in eastern Democratic Republic of Congo reports 782 confirmed cases and 181 fatalities as of Sunday. There are no approved medical interventions for Bundibugyo, unlike Zaire Ebola, with a fatality rate up to about 40%. Global health authorities are testing experimental vaccines and therapies; none have completed human trials, and emergency/compassionate-use authorisations may be needed. WHO prioritizes candidate vaccines: rVSVΔG/BDBV-GP, a single-dose vaccine from IAVI, potentially ready for clinical trial assessment in seven to nine months; and ChAdOx1 Bundibugyo from Oxford/Serum Institute, with two to three months before efficacy assessment, possibly with one- or two-dose regimens. Antibody therapies include MBP134 from Mapp Biopharmaceutical for pan-ebolavirus activity, supported by BARDA, and Regeneron’s maftivimab, with Inmazeb components stock in DRC for potential use. Survivors’ antibodies like BDBV289-N show animal efficacy; antiviral drug details are listed but not completed in the report.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ブンディブギョ株エボラ（BDBV）は致死率が高く承認治療法がないため、WHOが複数の実験的ワクチン・抗体療法の優先開発を進めている。既に782例確認・181例死亡という大規模流行であり、フルリスク評価が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly91ay5uZXdzLnlhaG9vLmNvbS9icml0aXNoLWNpdGl6ZW4tdGVzdHMtcG9zaXRpdmUtZWJvbGEtMTYxNjU3MjgxLmh0bWw=,PICKUP,DRCで継続中のエボラ(ブンディブギョ株)アウトブレイクは1万人超の症例・約5000人の死亡を伴う史上2番目の規模であり、英国人医療従事者の感染・本国搬送という国際的拡大の実例が生じているため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当しフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,British health worker tests positive for Ebola in Democratic Republic of Congo,2026-11-04T17:07:40+00:00,https://uk.news.yahoo.com/british-citizen-tests-positive-ebola-161657281.html,ENGLISH,humans,"British healthcare worker in the Democratic Republic of Congo has tested positive for Ebola (Bundibugyo strain), the first British national linked to the current outbreak. The patient is evacuated to the UK for specialist treatment and is in stable condition, due to arrive midweek and will be transported by specialist ambulance to a high-consequence infectious disease unit. The DRC outbreak, ongoing since May, is the second-largest on record, with more than 10,000 cases and about 5,000 deaths across four African countries. There is no approved vaccine or treatment for Bundibugho (Bundibugyo). The patient was sent to Congo by a humanitarian organization to support the response. UK authorities say the risk to the public remains low; imported cases are rare (four confirmed in Britain since 1976). Ebola spreads via direct contact with infected fluids, with incubation of 2–21 days and symptoms ranging from fever to bleeding.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国への患者搬送は発生地域には含まれるが、感染事象自体はDRCで発生しているため、対象国としてはDRCのみを計上。UKは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ2JuZXdzLmNvbS9uZXdzL3dvcmxkL2Vib2xhLW91dGJyZWFrLWJyaXRpc2gtY2l0aXplbi10ZXN0cy1wb3NpdGl2ZS1kci1jb25nbw==,PICKUP,史上最大規模とされるエボラ出血熱アウトブレイクで、致死率約49%、複数国への拡大（ケニア、英国人患者の本国搬送）が確認されており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,British citizen tests positive for Ebola in DR Congo as outbreak rages in Africa,2026-11-04T16:13:28+00:00,https://www.gbnews.com/news/world/ebola-outbreak-british-citizen-tests-positive-dr-congo,ENGLISH,humans,"Ebola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) fuels the largest outbreak on record, driven by Bundibugyo strain. DR Congo has reported more than 10,500 confirmed cases and about 5,100 deaths in eight provinces, and Kenya is reporting cases. The fatality rate is around 49%. The UN warns it is among the fastest-growing Ebola outbreaks, with reports that someone dies about every 30 minutes. No vaccine or specific treatment is approved for this strain. Transmission is by direct contact with infected bodily fluids; early symptoms—fever, headache and fatigue—appear 2–21 days after exposure and may progress to vomiting, diarrhoea and organ failure. A British citizen infected in the DRC has been evacuated to the United Kingdom for care, remains stable, and is due to arrive midweek before transfer to a specialized infectious disease unit. UK risk remains low; the patient was deployed to support outbreak response by a humanitarian organization.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ケニアおよび英国は感染拡大先として記載されているが、対象国リストに含まれないためverified_locationsには含めていない。英国人患者の本国搬送は国際的拡大の懸念材料として評価に反映した。,
