への言及のみで対象国リストにも含まれない。DRCでの発生が新規アウトブレイクか既存アウトブレイクの一部かは記事から不明。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hdHZibC5ycy9tYWdhemluL3pkcmF2bGplL29kb2JyZW5lLWtsaW5pY2tlLXByb2JlLXphLW5vdmUtdmFrY2luZS1wcm90aXYtZWJvbGUvMjM2ODEyNQ==,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で致死率50%超、確認症例10,444件、直近1週間で約5,300人死亡というエボラ出血熱の大規模流行が継続しており、WHOが新規ワクチン臨床試験を承認するなど国際的対応が進行中であるため、フルリスク評価が必要と判断。",Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,Approved clinical trials for new Ebola vaccines.,Одобрене клиничке пробе за нове вакцине против еболе,2026-11-04T17:41:00+00:00,https://atvbl.rs/magazin/zdravlje/odobrene-klinicke-probe-za-nove-vakcine-protiv-ebole/2368125,SERBIAN,humans,"World Health Organization approves clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccines. Trials began last month with Ervebo, approved for Ebola virus but not for Bundibugyo strain circulating in the Democratic Republic of Congo, with two additional vaccines to be added to the trial. WHO's expert group recommended expanding the trial to include these vaccines. Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus cautioned that vaccines are powerful tools but do not replace life-saving measures such as early diagnosis and care, contact tracing, isolation, safe and dignified burials, and strong community engagement. Africa CDC reports about 5,300 Ebola deaths this week, most in the Democratic Republic of Congo, with 10,444 confirmed cases and a case-fatality rate above 50%.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はDRCで継続中のエボラ出血熱流行（Bundibugyo株、致死率50%超）とWHOによる新規ワクチン臨床試験承認を報じている。アフリカ大陸全体は発生地域に含まれるが、サマリー上の主題国はDRCのみのため、verified_locationsはDRCのみとした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuamFncmFuLmNvbS9wdW5qYWIvZmF0ZWhnYXJoLXNhaGliLWhhbnNsYS1yaXZlci1wb2xsdXRpb24tZmF0ZWhnYXJoLXNhaGliLXN0cC1mYWlscy1zdGFuZGFyZHMtNDA0Mjc2OTguaHRtbD9hcHA9dHJ1ZQ==,WATCH,実際の感染症患者発生ではなく、下水処理施設の不備による河川汚染とそれに伴うコレラ・腸チフス・肝炎等の潜在的健康リスクを報じた環境報道であるため、現時点でのピックアップ基準には達しないが継続的な汚染曝露のリスクがあるため経過観察とする。,Hepatitis; Cholera; Typhoid,Fatehgarh Sahib; State of Punjab; Republic of India,Toxic water flowing in the Pavitra Hansla River; lab report reveals it; dangerous bacteria found ten times above the standard.,"पवित्र हंसला नदी में बह रहा जहरीला पानी, लैब रिपोर्ट में खुली पोल; मानक से 10 गुना ज्यादा अधिक मिला खतरनाक बैक्टीरिया",2026-11-04T17:24:00+00:00,https://www.jagran.com/punjab/fatehgarh-sahib-hansla-river-pollution-fatehgarh-sahib-stp-fails-standards-40427698.html?app=true,HINDI,humans; environment,"Untreated sewage from a 5 MLD Sewage Treatment Plant has polluted the Hansla River (Sarhind Drain) in Fatehgarh Sahib, Punjab. PPCB lab results, obtained via RTI, show alarming pollution: BOD 15 mg/L (NGT standard <10), Total Suspended Solids 24 mg/L (standard <20), fecal coliform 2100 MPN (standard 230). The district administration had claimed the plant was in ‘under testing/stabilization mode’ and that treated water would be diverted to soil-conservation irrigation, but the PPCB outlet sample contradicts this, with the river receiving contaminated effluent. The National Green Tribunal is hearing a related case, with government agencies yet to submit responses. Health and ecological risks are severe: high BOD depletes dissolved oxygen, fecal bacteria rise, and exposure can lead to cholera, typhoid, hepatitis, and skin infections; irrigation of crops could introduce toxins and bacteria into the food chain, potentially causing cancer and liver diseases. The case underscores administrative inaction and ongoing environmental hazard as of 2026.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,Yes,Yes,No,記事は実際の感染症アウトブレイクではなく、未処理下水による河川汚染とそれに起因する将来的な健康リスク（コレラ・腸チフス・肝炎）を警告する環境報道。国家緑色裁判所(NGT)で係争中の案件であり、行政の対応不備が指摘されている。感染症患者の発生報告があれば再評価が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hcmFiaWMuZXVyb25ld3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMTEvMDQvZXVyb3Blcy10cm9waWNhbC1kaXNlYXNlLXRocmVhdC1pcy1tb3Zpbmctbm9ydGgtY2FuLWl0LXN0b3AtbW9zcXVpdG9lcy1pbi10aGVpci10cmFja3M=,DISMISS,本記事の主題はポルトガル・イタリア・フランスなど欧州域内でのヒトスジシマカ媒介性疾患（デング熱等）の北上拡大であり、タイ・ブラジルは旅行者の感染経路として言及されているのみで、実際の発生地域ではないため、対象国における感染症イベントとは認められない。,Zika; Chikungunya; Dengue,Distrito de Lisboa; Lisbon; Italian Republic; Republic of France; Portuguese Republic,Europe faces a northward expansion of tropical diseases... will it succeed in curbing the spread of mosquitoes?,أوروبا تواجه تمدد الأمراض المدارية شمالاً.. هل تنجح في كبح انتشار البعوض؟,2026-11-04T17:39:01+00:00,https://arabic.euronews.com/2026/11/04/europes-tropical-disease-threat-is-moving-north-can-it-stop-mosquitoes-in-their-tracks,ARABIC,humans; vectors,"Europe faces northward expansion of tropical diseases as travel-related virus introductions raise local transmission risk. In Portugal, Lisbon released 30,000 sterilized male Aedes albopictus by irradiation to suppress the Asian tiger mosquito, a vector for dengue, chikungunya and Zika. The goal is to curb local spread while Europe strengthens preparedness as cases rise. Italy has 76 locally acquired dengue cases by end-October 2026, and France eight—nearly doubling 2025—highlighting escalating autochthonous transmission. The Asian tiger mosquito can move about 60 km per year northward, with outbreak clusters up to 120 km/year, increasing exposure for millions. Travelers returning from tropical regions, such as Thailand and Brazil, can seed local transmission and complicate diagnosis for clinicians unfamiliar with tropical diseases. EU’s Health Emergency Preparedness and Response Authority (HERA) is investing €10 million to develop diagnostics and fund antivirals and vaccines for these diseases.",No,No,Yes,No,1,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,Yes,Yes,No,記事は欧州（ポルトガル・イタリア・フランス）における熱帯病媒介蚊の北上と自国内感染拡大がテーマであり、タイ・ブラジルは感染症の輸入元（旅行者由来）として言及されているのみで、当該国内での発生事例ではないため対象国リストには含めない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9odS5ldXJvbmV3cy5jb20vMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9ldXJvcGFiYW4tZWd5cmUtZXN6YWthYmJyYS10b2xvZGlrLWEtdHJvcHVzaS1iZXRlZ3NlZ2VrLXZlc3plbHll,DISMISS,本イベントの実際の発生地域は欧州（ポルトガル、イタリア、フランス）であり、対象国リストに含まれる国（タイ、ブラジル）は感染者の渡航元として言及されているのみで、発生地ではないため対象外と判断。,Zika; Chikungunya; Dengue,Distrito de Lisboa; Lisbon; Italian Republic; Republic of France; Portuguese Republic,"In Europe, the threat of tropical diseases is moving further north.",Európában egyre északabbra tolódik a trópusi betegségek veszélye,2026-11-04T17:38:51+00:00,https://hu.euronews.com/2026/11/04/europaban-egyre-eszakabbra-tolodik-a-tropusi-betegsegek-veszelye,HUNGARIAN,humans; vectors,"Portugal released 30,000 sterilized male Aedes albopictus mosquitoes in Lisbon in September to suppress the invasive Asian tiger mosquito, a vector for dengue fever, chikungunya, and Zika. This second release aims to curb local transmission as tropical diseases move north with warmer seasons. Europe reports rising dengue activity: Italy had 76 locally acquired infections by end-October 2026; France eight, about double 2025. The Asian tiger mosquito, originating in Southeast Asia, has spread across southern Europe; they travel with vehicles and can be reintroduced by infected travellers, including arrivals from Thailand or Brazil. The species expands north roughly 60 km per year, with outbreaks advancing up to 120 km annually, risking up to 50 million people exposed to tropical diseases. Diagnostic gaps persist; the EU’s HERA is investing €10 million in new diagnostics and funding antivirals and vaccines.",No,Yes,Yes,No,2,Yes,No,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,No,記事の主題は欧州における蚊媒介感染症（デング熱、チクングニア熱、ジカ熱）の北上であり、タイ・ブラジルは感染者の渡航元・再導入リスクとして言及されているに過ぎず、発生国ではない。対象国リストに該当する発生国はないため verified_locations は空配列とした。欧州域内のサーベイランス事案としては注視価値があるが、本トリアージ対象地域外のためDISMISSと判定。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9wdC5ldXJvbmV3cy5jb20vMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9wb3J0dWdhbC1saWJlcnRhLW1vc3F1aXRvcy1lc3RlcmlsaXphZG9zLWVtLWxpc2JvYS1wYXJhLXRyYXZhci1kZW5ndWUtZS1vdXRyYXMtZG9lbmNhcy10cm8=,DISMISS,記事はポルトガル・イタリア・フランスにおける蚊媒介感染症対策に関する内容であり、対象国（タイ・ブラジル）は渡航者の出身地として言及されているのみで、実際の発生国ではないため対象外と判断。,Zika; Chikungunya; Dengue,Distrito de Lisboa; Lisbon; Italian Republic; Republic of France; Portuguese Republic,Portugal releases sterilized mosquitoes in Lisbon to curb dengue and other tropical diseases.,Portugal liberta mosquitos esterilizados em Lisboa para travar dengue e outras doenças tropicais,2026-11-04T17:38:37+00:00,https://pt.euronews.com/2026/11/04/portugal-liberta-mosquitos-esterilizados-em-lisboa-para-travar-dengue-e-outras-doencas-tro,PORTUGUESE,humans; vectors,"Portugal released 30,000 irradiated male Aedes albopictus mosquitoes in Lisbon in September to suppress the invasive tiger mosquito that transmits dengue, chikungunya, and Zika. It is Portugal’s second use of the sterile insect technique. With warmer Europe, locally acquired dengue cases are emerging: Italy reported 76 locally acquired infections and France 8 by end-October 2026, nearly double 2025. The tiger mosquito is moving north at about 60 km per year, with outbreaks expanding up to 120 km/year, increasing local transmission risk as travelers return from tropical regions such as Thailand and Brazil. Clinicians may misdiagnose tropical infections in patients without travel history, prompting EU HERA to invest €10 million in diagnostics and to support antivirals and vaccines to address imported cases and potential autochthonous transmission.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,不明,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事の主題はヨーロッパ（ポルトガル・イタリア・フランス）における蚊媒介感染症の予防対策であり、タイ・ブラジルは渡航者の出身地としての言及のみで実際の発生国ではないため、対象国リストに基づきverified_locationsは空配列とした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc2hvcm91a25ld3MuY29tL25ld3Mvdmlldy5hc3B4P2NkYXRlPTA0MTEyMDI2JmlkPTUwZmQyMTkyLWFkZjQtNDlhNS04MGMzLWRmZjEzMmE1ZWI2NA==,PICKUP,"DRCで発生中のエボラ（ブンディブギョ株含む）アウトブレイクは死者5,300人超、致死率50%超と極めて深刻であり、IHR基準の複数該当（深刻な公衆衛生影響・異常性）およびWPRO基準も複数該当するためフルRRAへ進むべき案件。",Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,World Health Organization approves clinical trials of two new Ebola vaccines.,الصحة العالمية تجيز إجراء تجارب سريرية للقاحين جديدين لفيروس إيبولا,2026-11-04T17:40:00+00:00,https://www.shorouknews.com/news/view.aspx?cdate=04112026&id=50fd2192-adf4-49a5-80c3-dff132a5eb64,ARABIC,humans,"WHO approves clinical trials of two new Ebola vaccines for Bundibugyo ebolavirus as Africa faces an ongoing outbreak, with more than 5,300 deaths, most in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. Last month trials began with the Ervebo vaccine (rVSV-ZEBOV) against Ebola, but not for Bundibugyo; experts now recommend adding two additional candidates. The vaccines are ChAdOx1 BDBV (Oxford University, in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India) and mRNA-1469 (Moderna), both targeting BDBV. Overall, 10,444 Ebola cases have been reported with a case-fatality rate above 50%. The new trials aim to expand immune protection and bolster outbreak control efforts amid the current epidemiological situation in the DRC.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"記事はワクチン臨床試験承認が主題だが、背景にあるDRCのエボラ流行（累計症例10,444件、死者5,300人超、CFR50%超）は既存の大規模アウトブレイクであり継続的な監視・評価が必要。インドは血清研究所（SII）がワクチン製造協力先として言及されているのみで発生地ではないため、verified_locationsから除外。UKも同様に発生地ではない。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2FsZXNvbmxpbmUuY28udWsvbmV3cy91ay1uZXdzL2JyaXQtdGVzdHMtcG9zaXRpdmUtZWJvbGEtZHItMzQ4NjQxMTM=,PICKUP,"DRCで進行中のエボラ(ブンディブギョ株)アウトブレイクは死者5,026人・感染者10,351人に達し史上2番目の規模であり、英国人医療従事者の感染・本国搬送という国際的拡大事例も発生しているためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Ituri; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland; Republic of Angola,,Brit healthcare worker tests positive for Ebola and is flown to UK,2026-11-04T17:26:25+00:00,https://www.walesonline.co.uk/news/uk-news/brit-tests-positive-ebola-dr-34864113,ENGLISH,humans,"UK repatriates Ebola-positive British healthcare worker from DR Congo; the patient contracted Ebola while working in the DRC and is in stable condition, expected to arrive in the UK on 5 November 2026 via specialist ambulance to an infectious disease unit (facility undisclosed); Foreign Office says UK risk remains low. DR Congo's ongoing Bundibugyo Ebola outbreak, declared mid-May, has caused 5,026 deaths among 10,351 infections, with 2,788 recoveries; about 50 of 67 health zones across eight provinces reporting active cases; epicentres are Ituri and North Kivu. This outbreak is the second-deadliest on record after West Africa's 2014–2016 epidemic; there is no vaccine or specific treatment for Bundibugyo. The case highlights imported/exported risk but remains a contained concern for the UK.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"英国およびアンゴラは発生地域に含まれているが、記事の主題である感染拡大・流行はDRC国内（特にIturi, North Kivu）で発生しているため、verified_locationsからは除外した。英国人患者はDRCで感染し英国へ搬送された二次的な事例。",
aHR0cHM6Ly9wdW5jaG5nLmNvbS93aG8tYXBwcm92ZXMtY2xpbmljYWwtdHJpYWxzLW9uLXR3by1uZXctZWJvbGEtdmFjY2luZXMv,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国でのスーダンエボラ（ブンディブギョ）アウトブレイクは致死率50%超、死者5,300人以上、ナイジェリアへの越境輸入例（スイスへの患者搬送も発生）があり、国際的拡大リスクが明確で、WHOがワクチン臨床試験承認するなど国際的対応が進行中。",Ebola,Lagos State; Port Harcourt; Lagos; Rivers State; Switzerland; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,WHO approves clinical trials on two new Ebola vaccines,2026-11-04T17:35:16+00:00,https://punchng.com/who-approves-clinical-trials-on-two-new-ebola-vaccines/,ENGLISH,humans,"WHO approves clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccines targeting Bundibugyo virus amid a Democratic Republic of Congo outbreak that has killed more than 5,300 people and confirmed about 10,444 cases (case fatality rate >50%). Ervebo remains approved for Ebola virus but not Bundibugyo. The two candidates—ChAdOx1 BDBV (Oxford University with Serum Institute of India) and Moderna’s mRNA-1469—were developed specifically for Bundibugyo and added to the trial led by the DRC’s National Institute for Biomedical Research, with WHO support. Vaccines are not substitutes for measures like early care, contact tracing, isolation, safe and dignified burials, and community engagement. Nigeria reports an imported Bundibugyo case from Uganda; lab-confirmed Oct 20, patient evacuated to Switzerland Oct 26 with husband. As of Nov 3, Nigeria has 1 confirmed case, 0 deaths, 62 contacts, 57 quarantined. Nigeria’s 2014 Lagos-Port Harcourt outbreak involved 20 cases and 8 deaths; the country was declared Ebola-free on Oct 20, 2014.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ナイジェリア・ウガンダ・スイスでの症例/搬送は本病原体の主要流行地ではなく国境を越えた波及事例。インドはワクチン製造元（Serum Institute of India）としての関与であり疾病発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9ub3RpY2lhc3ZlbmV2aXNpb24uY29tL25vdGljaWFzL3NhbHVkL29tcy1yZWNvbWllbmRhLXByb2Jhci1kb3MtbnVldmFzLXZhY3VuYXMtY29udHJhLWNlcGEtZGVsLWVib2xhLXF1ZS1jaXJjdWxhLWVuLWxhLXJkYw==,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）流行は既に1万人超の確定症例・5000人超の死者を出しており、公衆衛生上深刻かつ国際的対応（WHOによるワクチン試験推奨）が行われているためフルRRA対象とする。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,WHO recommends testing two new vaccines against the Ebola strain circulating in the DRC.,OMS recomienda probar dos nuevas vacunas contra cepa del ébola que circula en la RDC,2026-11-04T17:49:00+00:00,https://noticiasvenevision.com/noticias/salud/oms-recomienda-probar-dos-nuevas-vacunas-contra-cepa-del-ebola-que-circula-en-la-rdc,SPANISH,humans,"Two experimental Ebola vaccines, ChAdOx1 (Oxford University with Serum Institute of India) and mRNA-1469 (Moderna), targeting Bundibugyo Ebola virus, will be added to an ongoing clinical trial in the Democratic Republic of Congo during the current outbreak that has exceeded 10,000 confirmed cases and 5,000 deaths. An independent WHO expert group recommended their inclusion based on preclinical data. The trial, led by the National Institute of Biomedical Research in the DRC with WHO and international partners, also evaluates Ervebo, a vaccine effective against the Zaire Ebola variant but not confirmed for Bundibugyo. Pending approvals from DRC authorities, the study will assess multiple candidates concurrently. Results are expected in early 2027. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus underscored that vaccines may be an important tool but not a standalone solution.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドはワクチン開発元（Serum Institute of India）として言及されているのみで、感染発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外した。,
