aHR0cHM6Ly90cmlidW5lLm5ldC5waC8yMDI2LzExLzA0L2RvaC1sb2dzLTMxLWZsdS1saWtlLWlsbG5lc3Nlcy1zdXJnZQ==,WATCH,季節性ILIの増加だが致死率は低く2025年比でも減少傾向にあり、IHR基準には該当しないが継続的なモニタリング対象として注視する。,Influenza; Leptospirosis; Dengue,Mimaropa; Western Visayas; National Capital Region; Republic of the Philippines,,DoH logs 31% flu-like illnesses surge,2026-11-04T17:46:51+00:00,https://tribune.net.ph/2026/11/04/doh-logs-31-flu-like-illnesses-surge,ENGLISH,humans,"Influenza-like illnesses (ILI) in the Philippines rose 31% to 15,042 cases for 1–14 October, from 11,517 in the preceding two weeks. Local spikes were reported in Western Visayas, Central Visayas, and MIMAROPA, with 17 provinces and highly urbanized cities—primarily Metro Manila—showing increases. Nationwide ILI totals reach 139,031 for 2026, with a case-fatality rate of 0.06%; 2026 cases remain 19% lower than 171,506 in the same period in 2025. The DoH is strengthening preventive measures and monitoring to control respiratory illnesses. The report also notes a dengue uptick to 23,842 cases (1–14 October), up 6% from 22,575 (17–30 September), while leptospirosis declines to 554 cases (1–14 October), a 54% drop from 1,198 in the previous two weeks.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,No,ILI、デング熱、レプトスピラ症の定期サーベイランス報告。季節的な変動の範囲内であり、致死率0.06%と低く、前年同期比では減少している。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9pbmZvcm1hdGlvbi50djVtb25kZS5jb20vc2NpZW5jZS9lYm9sYS1lbi1yZGMtbG9tcy1kb25uZS1sZS1mZXUtdmVydC1hdXgtZXNzYWlzLWNsaW5pcXVlcy1kZS1kZXV4LW5vdXZlYXV4LXZhY2NpbnMtMjg0NDQ3NA==,PICKUP,"DRCでのエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）流行が5か月以上継続し、1万例超・死者5,300人超と甚大な被害が出ており、ナイジェリア・ケニア・ウガンダへの越境拡大も確認されているためIHR基準・WPRO基準を複数満たす。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,Ebola in the DRC: the WHO gives the green light to clinical trials of two new vaccines.,Ebola en RDC : l'OMS donne le feu vert aux essais cliniques de deux nouveaux vaccins,2026-11-04T15:54:14+00:00,https://information.tv5monde.com/science/ebola-en-rdc-loms-donne-le-feu-vert-aux-essais-cliniques-de-deux-nouveaux-vaccins-2844474,FRENCH,humans,"Ebola in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) continues with Bundibugyo strain; the WHO has approved extending clinical trials to two new vaccines alongside Ervebo (Zaire ebolavirus) to test candidates ChAdOx1 (adenoviral vector by Oxford University and Serum Institute of India) and Moderna's mRNA vaccine. Trials use ring vaccination targeting contacts of laboratory-confirmed Bundibugyo cases; the outbreak has persisted for over five months with more than 10,400 cases and over 5,300 deaths. Additional recent cases include Nigeria (1 case in October), Kenya (9 cases, 2 deaths); Uganda reports 20 cases and 2 deaths but remains Ebola-exempt per WHO. Therapeutics under study include MBP134 monoclonal antibody and remdesivir, with maftivimab soon added and post-exposure prophylaxis with obeldevisir. Therapeutic results expected in coming months; vaccine results expected early 2027.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"記事中の『India』はSerum Institute of India（ワクチン製造企業）としての言及であり、発生国ではないため verified_locations には含めていない。同様にKenya, Uganda, Nigeria, UKも対象国リスト外または主題でないため除外。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYW9sLmNvLnVrL2FydGljbGVzL2hvcnJvci1icml0LXRlc3RzLWRlYWRseS1lYm9sYS0xNzA4MDAwMDAuaHRtbA==,PICKUP,"DRCで史上2番目に深刻なエボラ流行が継続中（致死率約48.6%、10,351症例・5,026死亡）、かつ英国人患者の国際移送により国際拡大リスクが顕在化しているためフルRRAへ進むべき。",Ebola,Ituri; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,Horror as Brit tests for deadly Ebola and warning over 'worldwide outbreak threat' issued,2026-11-04T17:39:57+00:00,https://www.aol.co.uk/articles/horror-brit-tests-deadly-ebola-170800000.html,ENGLISH,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, a British citizen in the Democratic Republic of Congo tested positive for Ebola (Bundibugyo virus) and will be evacuated to the UK for treatment; patient is stable and expected to arrive midweek. This is the first UK national infection in the current outbreak, which has killed 5,026 of 10,351 cases in DRC, and has no vaccine or specific treatment—care is supportive. Since May, spread has reached 67 of 178 health zones across eight provinces, with 50 zones currently reporting active cases. Ituri and North Kivu are the epicentres, recording 9,782 confirmed cases and 4,792 deaths. About 2,788 people have recovered. The outbreak is the second deadliest in Ebola history, after the 2014–2016 West Africa epidemic. UK risk remains low; authorities have activated established response procedures.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国（UK）は対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations から除外。イギリス人患者の帰国治療は国際拡大懸念の根拠として記載するが、発生自体はDRC国内に限定。ワクチン・特異的治療法がなく支持療法のみという点からも管理可能性に懸念あり。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9qb3JuYWxkZWJyYXNpbGlhLmNvbS5ici9ub3RpY2lhcy9zYXVkZS9vbXMtYXByb3ZhLWVuc2Fpb3MtY2xpbmljb3MtZGUtZHVhcy1ub3Zhcy12YWNpbmFzLWNvbnRyYS1vLWVib2xhLTIv,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で5,300人超の死亡、10,400例超の大規模エボラ流行が継続中で、既に複数国（ナイジェリア、ケニア）に拡大しており、国際的な公衆衛生上の重大イベントであるためフルRRAが必要。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Federal Republic of Nigeria; Republic of Uganda; Republic of Kenya,WHO Approves Clinical Trials of Two New Vaccines Against Ebola,OMS aprova ensaios clínicos de duas novas vacinas contra o ebola,2026-11-04T17:45:43+00:00,https://jornaldebrasilia.com.br/noticias/saude/oms-aprova-ensaios-clinicos-de-duas-novas-vacinas-contra-o-ebola-2/,PORTUGUESE,humans,"On 4 November 2026, the World Health Organization approved clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccines targeting the Bundibugyo strain amid an outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo that has caused over 5,300 deaths and more than 10,400 cases in just over five months. A trial with Ervebo (Zaire ebolavirus) had begun earlier but does not cover Bundibugyo. The two candidates recommended for trials are: 1) a ChAdOx1 adenoviral-vector vaccine developed by the University of Oxford with the Serum Institute of India; 2) Moderna’s messenger RNA (mRNA) vaccine. Nigeria reported one case; Kenya recorded nine cases (including two deaths) in October; Uganda reported 20 cases (one fatal) but was declared Ebola-free by the WHO. Vaccines are powerful tools but must complement public health measures such as early care, contact tracing, isolation, safe burials, and community engagement.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はDRCでの大規模エボラ流行（Bundibugyo株）に対する新規ワクチン臨床試験承認が主題。ナイジェリア・ケニア・ウガンダへの拡大も言及されているが、これらは対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations には含めていない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYW9sLmNvbS9hcnRpY2xlcy91ay1uYXRpb25hbC10ZXN0cy1wb3NpdGl2ZS1lYm9sYS0xNjUzNDcwMDAuaHRtbA==,PICKUP,"DRコンゴのエボラ流行は10,000例超・死者5,000人超・致死率48.6%で深刻化し、ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダへの国際的拡大、さらに英国人感染者も確認されたため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当し社会的関心も高い。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,UK national tests positive for Ebola virus in DR Congo,2026-11-04T17:44:36+00:00,https://www.aol.com/articles/uk-national-tests-positive-ebola-165347000.html,ENGLISH,humans; environment,"A British national in the Democratic Republic of Congo has tested positive for Ebola, the first confirmed case of a UK national in the DR Congo outbreak. The UK risk to the public remains low, with established procedures activated; it is not yet confirmed whether the patient will be repatriated, though past cases have been flown back. The DR Congo outbreak has surpassed 10,000 cases since May and more than 5,000 deaths, making it the second deadliest outbreak in DR Congo history, with a 48.6% fatality rate reported at the end of last month. The Bundibugyo variant has no approved vaccine. Ebola spreads via infected bodily fluids, with early symptoms such as vomiting and diarrhoea, potentially progressing to organ failure. Cases have also been confirmed in Kenya, Nigeria and Uganda. The UK has four prior imported cases: one in 1976 and three during the 2014–2015 West Africa outbreak.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダ・英国での症例も報告されているが、対象国リストに含まれるのはDRコンゴのみ。Bundibugyo株には承認済みワクチンがなく、流行拡大のリスクが高い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9mci5zcHV0bmlrbmV3cy5hZnJpY2EvMjAyNjExMDQvMTA5MDY0NzU4Ni5odG1s,DISMISS,本記事はコレラの流行・症例報告ではなく、ワクチン製造工場への投資計画に関する経済・産業ニュースであり、感染症アウトブレイクの兆候は示されていない。,Cholera,Lusaka; Lusaka Province,Zambia will invest 213 million dollars in a cholera vaccine factory.,La Zambie investira 213 millions de dollars dans une usine de vaccins contre le choléra,2026-11-04T16:43:00+00:00,https://fr.sputniknews.africa/20261104/1090647586.html,FRENCH,humans; environment,"Zambia will invest 213 million dollars in ZAMVAX, a cholera vaccine factory to be built in the Lusaka-South Economic Zone. An agreement signed on November 2 outlines a two-phase project aiming to boost local production and regional supply. Phase 1, valued at about 24.13 million dollars, will establish an oral cholera vaccine packaging unit with annual capacity up to 20 million doses, with production split evenly between domestic use and exports. Phase 2 aims to locally manufacture vaccine active ingredients to reduce import dependence. In the long term, the facility could expand to pediatric and veterinary vaccines, strengthening Zambia’s health autonomy and contributing to regional vaccination capacity. The plan indicates emphasis on self-sufficiency and broader supply chains for cholera vaccines in the region.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,記事はコレラワクチン製造施設建設への投資発表であり、現時点でのコレラ流行や症例報告ではないため、感染症シグナルとしては該当しない。,
