aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2VsaW5nZWxpY2h0ZWtyaW5nZW4ubmwvc2FtZW5sZXZpbmcvd2hvLWdlZWZ0LXRvZXN0ZW1taW5nLXZvb3ItcHJvZWYtbWV0LW5pZXV3ZS1lYm9sYXZhY2NpbnM=,PICKUP,DRCで進行中のエボラ(Bundibugyo変異株)アウトブレイクは死者5000人超・感染者10000人超に達し、国際的な感染拡大（英国人医療従事者の感染・搬送）も発生しており、IHR基準の複数項目に該当する。,Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,WHO approves a trial of new Ebola vaccines,WHO geeft toestemming voor proef met nieuwe ebolavaccins,2026-11-04T18:05:49+00:00,https://www.welingelichtekringen.nl/samenleving/who-geeft-toestemming-voor-proef-met-nieuwe-ebolavaccins,DUTCH,humans,"WHO approves clinical trials of two new Ebola vaccines targeting the Bundibugyo variant that has caused thousands of deaths in the Democratic Republic of Congo. The Oxford University– Serum Institute of India ChAdOx1 vaccine and Moderna’s mRNA-1469 are tested specifically for the Bundibugyo variant; existing vaccine Ervebo is also being evaluated for cross-protection. Africa CDC reports over 5,000 deaths and more than 10,000 infections in the current outbreak, the vast majority in the DRC. Separately, a British healthcare worker contracted Ebola in Congo and is being transported to the United Kingdom for specialized treatment. These trials reflect ongoing efforts to address a variant with no approved vaccine or treatment to date.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドは血清研究所がワクチン製造に関与しているのみで発生国ではない。英国は感染者が治療目的で搬送される先であり発生国ではないため、いずれもverified_locationsから除外した。既存のDRCエボラアウトブレイクに関する続報であり、ワクチン臨床試験承認と国際的感染拡大事例を含む重要な進展。,
aHR0cHM6Ly90b2IubmV3cy9yZWQtYWxlcnQtaW4tdGhlLWNhcGl0YWwtZGhhbm1vbmRpLWR1LWFuZC1kbWNoLXRvcC1oaWdoLXJpc2stZGVuZ3VlLWxpc3Qv,DISMISS,対象国（バングラデシュ）は評価対象国リストに含まれておらず、内容も幼虫サーベイに基づく予防的リスクマッピングであり、重症患者や死亡等の深刻な公衆衛生影響の報告はない。,Dengue,Dhanmondi; Khilgaon; Barisal Division; State of Jhārkhand; Shahjāhanpur; Hazāribāgh; Dhaka; Dhaka Division; Maulvibazar; Azimpur; Rajarbagh; Chittagong; Sylhet Division; West Rasūlpur; Uttar Pradesh; Bangladesh,,"Red alert in the capital: Dhanmondi, DU, and DMCH top high-risk dengue list",2026-11-04T18:00:41+00:00,https://tob.news/red-alert-in-the-capital-dhanmondi-du-and-dmch-top-high-risk-dengue-list/,ENGLISH,humans; vectors,"Dengue fever threat intensifies in Dhaka after a 12-day monsoon larval survey (Sept 27–Oct 8) by DSCC across 75 wards. Aedes larvae/pupae were found in 322 of 2,250 inspected premises. The highest risk hotspots are Ward 15 (Dhanmondi), Ward 20 (DMCH), and Ward 21 (Dhaka University), with Ward 16 (Bagan) and Wards 18–19 (Kakrail) among other elevated areas. Overall, 29 wards are high risk, 28 moderate, and 18 under standard monitoring. Zones span Khilgaon, Basabo-Fakirapul, Shahjahanpur, Malibagh, Rajarbagh, Hazaribagh, Lalbagh, Azimpur, Bakshibazar, Jhaurchar, West Rasulpur, Moulvibazar, West Jurain, Alambagh, plus North Kutubkhali and Adarshabag. Breteau, House, Container, and Pupa indices guided risk. Primary breeding grounds include plastic buckets (14.21%), drums (11.22%), stagnant basement water (9.98%), and plastic mugs (9.92%), with detached homes and multi-storey units most affected. DSCC uses red/yellow/green mapping, weekly fogging by 12 joint teams, and enforcement to curb spread.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,"記事はバングラデシュ・ダッカ市内の蚊幼虫サーベイとリスクマッピングに関する内容で、対象国リストに含まれる国（インド等）への言及はない。発生地域にインドの州（Jharkhand, Uttar Pradesh）が含まれているが、記事サマリー上これらはダッカ市内の地名（Rajarbagh, Hazaribagh等と誤認識された可能性）であり、インドでの実際の発生を示すものではない。",
aHR0cHM6Ly9oZXJhbGRvZGVtZXhpY28uY29tLm14L211bmRvLzIwMjYvMTEvNC9zZS1leHRpZW5kZS1sYS1hbWVuYXphLW1vcnRhbC12aXJ1cy1kZWwtZWJvbGEtY3J1emEtZnJvbnRlcmFzLWxsZWdhLW90cm8tY29udGluZW50ZS05MjI3MzIuaHRtbA==,PICKUP,DRCでの大規模アウトブレイク（1万人超感染、5千人死亡）に加え、英国人の国境を越えた感染・搬送例が確認されており、国際的拡大リスクが現実化しているためフルRRAが必要。,Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,The threat spreads: Deadly Ebola virus crosses borders and reaches another continent.,Se extiende la amenaza: Mortal virus del Ébola cruza fronteras y llega a otro continente,2026-11-04T18:08:00+00:00,https://heraldodemexico.com.mx/mundo/2026/11/4/se-extiende-la-amenaza-mortal-virus-del-ebola-cruza-fronteras-llega-otro-continente-922732.html,SPANISH,humans; environment,"As of 2026-11-04, the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo has surpassed 10,000 infections and about 5,000 deaths, with the virus remaining active primarily on the African continent. A health worker who contracted Ebola in the DRC was identified as a British national who was repatriated to the United Kingdom for treatment and isolation after testing positive for Ebola. The case marks the first time the current outbreak has crossed borders, reaching Europe. UK Foreign Office officials told the Daily Mail that the British citizen in question tested positive in the DRC. Africa CDC Director General Dr. Jean Kaseya warned that the virus could still spread to other regions and is not yet contained. The article notes the outbreak is centered in Africa, with cross-border transmission to Europe reported.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国への症例輸出が報告されているが、対象国リストに英国は含まれないため verified_locations には含めない。発生の主体はDRCである。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc3Rlcm4uZGUvbmV3cy93aG8tZ2VuZWhtaWd0LWtsaW5pc2NoZS1zdHVkaWVuLWZ1ZXItendlaS1uZXVlLWVib2xhLWltcGZzdG9mZmUtMzg1MDIxNTYuaHRtbA==,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で継続中のエボラ出血熱（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクに関し、感染者約1万人・死者5300人超と深刻な公衆衛生影響があり、IHR基準の複数（深刻性・異常性・国際的拡大）に該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,WHO approves clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccines.,WHO genehmigt klinische Studien für zwei neue Ebola-Impfstoffe,2026-11-04T17:56:05+00:00,https://www.stern.de/news/who-genehmigt-klinische-studien-fuer-zwei-neue-ebola-impfstoffe-38502156.html,GERMAN,humans,"WHO approves clinical trials for two Ebola vaccines amid the outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo. The vaccines, ChAdOx1 BDBV (developed by Oxford University with Serum Institute of India) and mRNA-1469 (Moderna), are tailored to the Bundibugyo variant currently circulating. Previously, only Ervebo had been studied, and it is approved only for the Zaire Ebola strain. The DRC outbreak was officially identified in mid-May, with Africa CDC reporting roughly 10,400 infections and over 5,300 deaths across Africa, the majority in the DRC. Transmission occurs via direct contact with body fluids, causing fever, muscle pains, diarrhea, internal bleeding, and organ failure. Over 50 years, Africa has recorded more than 15,000 Ebola deaths. The Bundibugyo variant has no approved vaccine or treatment yet; several candidates are in trials.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドはワクチン開発（Serum Institute of India）に関与する企業所在地として言及されているのみで、感染発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucG9saXRpa2EucnMvc2NjL2NsYW5hay83OTk3OTUvYnJpdGFuc2tpLXpkcmF2c3R2ZW5pLXJhZG5pay11LWtvbmd1LXBveml0aXZhbi1uYS1lYm9sdQ==,,,Ebola,London; Newcastle upon Tyne; England; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,British healthcare worker in Congo tests positive for Ebola.,Британски здравствени радник у Конгу позитиван на еболу,2026-11-04T18:08:05+00:00,https://www.politika.rs/scc/clanak/799795/britanski-zdravstveni-radnik-u-kongu-pozitivan-na-ebolu,SERBIAN,humans,"British healthcare worker in the Democratic Republic of Congo tests positive for Ebola and will be evacuated to the United Kingdom for treatment in a specialized infectious diseases unit. The patient, identity undisclosed, is in stable condition and is expected to arrive in the UK today or tomorrow, then be transported to one of two facilities: Royal Free Hospital, London, or Royal Victoria Infirmary, Newcastle. This marks the first Ebola case in a British citizen linked to the current outbreak, described as the second-largest globally. The UK Foreign Office confirmed the single national case and that the risk to the UK population remains low, with no anticipated disruption to travel or trade. The outbreak in DRC is centered around Beni and is caused by the Bundibugyo strain of Ebola, for which there are no approved vaccines or specific antivirals. Last week, deaths exceeded 5,000 and infections surpassed 10,000.",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,"no text block in response (blocks=['thinking'], stop_reason=end_turn, event_id=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucG9saXRpa2EucnMvc2NjL2NsYW5hay83OTk3OTUvYnJpdGFuc2tpLXpkcmF2c3R2ZW5pLXJhZG5pay11LWtvbmd1LXBveml0aXZhbi1uYS1lYm9sdQ==)"
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaW5zaWRlci5nci95Z2VpYS80MzE0OTAvZHlvLW5lYS15cG9wc2lmaWEtZW1ib2xpYS1zdGluLWtsaW5pa2ktbWVsZXRpLWthdGEtdG95LWVtcG9sYS1hcG8tdG9uLWlvLWJkYnY=,WATCH,既知のコンゴ民主共和国でのBDBVアウトブレイクに対するワクチン・治療薬の臨床試験進展に関する報道であり、新規の公衆衛生緊急事態を示すものではないが、進行中のアウトブレイク対応として経過観察が妥当。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Kingdom of Belgium,Two new candidate vaccines in the clinical trial against Ebola caused by Bundibugyo ebolavirus (BDBV).,Δύο νέα υποψήφια εμβόλια στην κλινική μελέτη κατά του Έμπολα από τον ιό BDBV,2026-11-04T18:11:23+00:00,https://www.insider.gr/ygeia/431490/dyo-nea-ypopsifia-embolia-stin-kliniki-meleti-kata-toy-empola-apo-ton-io-bdbv,GREEK,humans,"Two new Ebola vaccines targeting Bundibugyo ebolavirus (BDBV) are entering clinical testing in the Democratic Republic of Congo’s ongoing BDBV outbreak. The vaccines are ChAdOx1 (Oxford University in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India) and Moderna’s mRNA-1469. WHO experts recommended adding them to the Tumaini ring-vaccination trial, the first evaluation of vaccines specifically designed for BDBV during an outbreak. Tumaini conducts multi-vaccine testing within four vaccination rings that enroll contacts of confirmed BDBV cases, led by the Institut National de Recherche Biomédicale with support from the University of Antwerp, WHO, Epicentre, MSF, TropMed Antwerp, and African CDCs, funded by CEPI. Ervebo (rVSV-ZEBOV) is the first vaccine assessed in Tumaini against Bundibugyo. Therapeutics are also studied: PARTNERS tests MBP134 monoclonal antibody and remdesivir, with maftivimab added soon and a post-exposure prophylaxis study for obeldevisir underway. Results are expected early 2027.",不明,No,不明,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,Yes,記事はDRCで進行中のBDBVアウトブレイクに対するワクチン・治療薬の臨床試験（Tumaini試験）に関する内容。ベルギーとインドは研究機関・製薬協力先として言及されているのみで、発生国ではないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYWxraGFsZWVqLmFlLzIwMjYtMTEtMDQvJUQ4JUI5JUQ4JUIxJUQ4JUE4LSVEOSU4OCVEOCVCOSVEOCVBNyVEOSU4NCVEOSU4NS8lRDglQTclRDklODQlRDglQjklRDglQTclRDklODQlRDklODUvJUQ4JUE1JUQ4JUI1JUQ4JUE3JUQ4JUE4JUQ4JUE5LSVEOCVBOCVEOCVCMSVEOSU4QSVEOCVCNyVEOCVBNyU=,PICKUP,致死率の高いエボラ出血熱がコンゴ民主共和国で発生し、英国人という渡航者にも感染が確認されたことから国際的拡大リスクが示唆されるため、IHR基準複数該当としてフルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,Briton infected with Ebola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo — London: the risk is low.,"إصابة بريطاني بـ""إيبولا"" في الكونغو الديمقراطية.. ولندن: الخطر منخفض",2026-11-04T17:05:00+00:00,https://www.alkhaleej.ae/2026-11-04/%D8%B9%D8%B1%D8%A8-%D9%88%D8%B9%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85/%D8%A5%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%A8%D8%A9-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%B7%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%8A-%D8%A8%D8%A5%D9%8A%D8%A8%D9%88%D9%84%D8%A7-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%83%D9%88%D9%86%D8%BA%D9%88-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%85%D9%82%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%B7%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%88%D9%84%D9%86%D8%AF%D9%86-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AE%D8%B7%D8%B1-%D9%85%D9%86%D8%AE%D9%81%D8%B6,ARABIC,humans,"Ebola infection confirmed in a British national currently in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, according to the British government. The spokesperson said the individual has tested positive for Ebola, and the risk to the UK population remains low. The report does not provide details on symptoms, the exact location within the DRC, exposure source, or travel history beyond being in the DRC. There is no information about treatment, recovery status, or any deaths related to this case. This is a single abroad case with no indicated linkage to domestic transmission. UK authorities reaffirm that protective measures and surveillance remain in place, and they will monitor the situation and provide updates as needed.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,英国はリスク評価の対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations から除外。感染経路・感染地域の詳細、治療状況、関連死亡の有無など情報が不足しているため、続報を注視しつつフルRRAへ進めるべき案件。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaW5kZXBlbmRlbnQuY28udWsvbmV3cy9oZWFsdGgvZWJvbGEtdmFjY2luZS10cmVhdG1lbnQtYnVuZGlidWd5by1iMzA3OTMzNS5odG1s,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で発生中のブンディブギョ型エボラ出血熱が5,000人以上の死者・10,000人以上の感染者を出し、致死率最大40%かつ英国への感染拡大（医療従事者の国際搬送）も確認されており、IHR基準に複数該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,The treatments being developed for the Bundibugyo strain of Ebola,2026-11-04T18:17:32+00:00,https://www.independent.co.uk/news/health/ebola-vaccine-treatment-bundibugyo-b3079335.html,ENGLISH,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, a British healthcare worker treating the Bundibugyo ebolavirus outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has tested positive for Ebola and will be evacuated to Britain; the patient is stable and expected to arrive on Wednesday or Thursday. The Foreign Office said the risk to the UK public remains low. The ongoing outbreak linked to Bundibugyo ebolavirus (BDBV) has killed over 5,000 and infected more than 10,000, with BDBV fatality up to 40%. There are no approved vaccines or treatments specifically for BDBV, though several candidates are in development. The WHO prioritises rVSVΔG/BDBV-GP (single-dose) and ChAdOx1 Bundibyo (Bundibugyo) for trials, with efficacy assessments in 7–9 months and 2–3 months respectively, and two additional candidates (ChAdOx1 and Moderna's mRNA-1469) added to the Tumaini trial in the DRC. Antibody MBP134 from Mapp Biopharmaceutical is also prioritized for trials, though most options require emergency or compassionate-use authorization.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国への患者搬送は国際的拡大の一例として記載されているが、対象国リストに英国は含まれないためverified_locationsには含めていない。主たる発生地はDRCである。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubWFyY2EuY29tL2JpZW5lc3Rhci9zYWx1ZC8yMDI2LzExLzA0L2VlLXV1LWltcG9uZS1udWV2by1yZXF1aXNpdG8tcGFzYWplcm9zLWludGVybmFjaW9uYWxlcy1icm90ZS1lYm9sYS5odG1s,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国でのエボラ流行による死者が5,100人を超え、米国が渡航制限に相当する健康申告義務を導入しており、IHR基準の複数（深刻性・異常性・国際的拡大・渡航制限）に該当するためフルRRAへ進むべきシグナルと判断。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States,The United States imposes a new requirement on international passengers due to the Ebola outbreak.,EE.UU. impone un nuevo requisito a los pasajeros internacionales por el brote de ébola,2026-11-04T18:24:14+00:00,https://www.marca.com/bienestar/salud/2026/11/04/ee-uu-impone-nuevo-requisito-pasajeros-internacionales-brote-ebola.html,SPANISH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo has caused over 5,100 deaths. To curb potential US spread, the United States imposes a new health declaration for all international arrivals, effective November 4, 2026. Every traveler arriving on international flights must sign a declaration stating they have not been in the DRC in the 21 days prior to boarding the US-bound flight (the maximum incubation period). The CDC order, issued October 22, applies to commercial, cargo, private flights, and flight crews. Declarations may be paper or digital and will be collected by airlines, either before boarding or during check-in. Those who fail to present it cannot fly; falsification may be prosecuted and fines imposed. The measure is temporary, valid through December 18, 2026, but may be modified, extended, or withdrawn earlier.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,米国は対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations には含めず。記事の主題はDRCでのエボラ流行とその国際的影響（米国の渡航対策）である。,
aHR0cHM6Ly90aGVwcmludC5pbi93b3JsZC9icml0aXNoLWhlYWx0aGNhcmUtd29ya2VyLXdpdGgtZWJvbGEtdG8tYmUtZXZhY3VhdGVkLWZyb20tY29uZ28tdG8tdWstZG9jdW1lbnQtc2hvd3MvMzA5MDgzMi8=,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ流行は史上2番目の規模（1万人超の感染、約5000人死亡）であり、国際的な症例輸出（英国への患者搬送）も発生しているため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当し、フルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,"British healthcare worker with Ebola to be evacuated from Congo to UK, document shows",2026-11-04T16:30:16+00:00,https://theprint.in/world/british-healthcare-worker-with-ebola-to-be-evacuated-from-congo-to-uk-document-shows/3090832/,ENGLISH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo is the second-largest on record, with more than 10,000 confirmed cases and nearly 5,000 deaths by late October 2026. A British citizen in the DRC has tested positive for Ebola linked to this outbreak and will be evacuated to the United Kingdom. The patient was sent to Congo by a humanitarian organization to assist the response. UK health authorities say the risk to the public remains low, and the NHS has procedures for managing suspected/confirmed infections. Imported cases in Britain are rare, with four confirmed since 1976; this is the first case involving a British national tied to the current outbreak. Ebola spreads through direct contact with infected bodily fluids, with an average fatality rate around 50%, varying by outbreak.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国への症例輸出はIHR上の国際拡大の明確な証拠。渡航・貿易制限の有無については記事に明示的記載がないため不明とした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9ub3RpY2lhcy51b2wuY29tLmJyL3VsdGltYXMtbm90aWNpYXMvcmV1dGVycy8yMDI2LzExLzA0L3Byb2Zpc3Npb25hbC1kZS1zYXVkZS1icml0YW5pY28tY29tLWVib2xhLXNlcmEtbGV2YWRvLWRvLWNvbmdvLXBhcmEtby1yZWluby11bmlkby5odG0=,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国における大規模エボラアウトブレイク（1万人以上感染、死者約5000人）に関連し、英国人患者が国際搬送される事例であり、国際的拡大のリスクを示すためフルRRAへの移行が妥当。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,British healthcare worker with Ebola to be flown from the Congo to the United Kingdom.,Profissional de saúde britânico com Ebola será levado do Congo para o Reino Unido,2026-11-04T18:12:20+00:00,https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2026/11/04/profissional-de-saude-britanico-com-ebola-sera-levado-do-congo-para-o-reino-unido.htm,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Ebola virus disease: A British healthcare worker infected with Ebola is being transported from the Democratic Republic of Congo to the United Kingdom for specialist treatment. The patient is stable and expected to arrive in the UK on Wednesday or Thursday (4–5 November 2026) before transfer by a dedicated ambulance to a high‑risk infectious diseases unit. UK health authorities say there is no expected impact on public health or on international travel or trade. The patient, a British citizen, had been sent to Congo by a humanitarian organization to assist with the outbreak; identity is undisclosed. This is the first UK case linked to the current outbreak, though other Europeans have been infected. The DRC outbreak is the second largest on record, with over 10,000 confirmed cases and nearly 5,000 deaths by the end of October. Ebola transmits via bodily fluids; WHO notes about 50% fatality on average, with variability. Imported UK cases are rare, with four confirmed since 1976.",Yes,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事の主題はDRCで進行中の大規模エボラアウトブレイクに関連する英国人患者の国際搬送。英国（UK）は対象国リストに含まれないため、verified_locationsにはDRCのみを記載。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9lcy11cy5ub3RpY2lhcy55YWhvby5jb20vb21zLWFwcnVlYmEtZW5zYXlvcy1jbCVDMyVBRG5pY29zLXZhY3VuYXMtMTgyMTAzNzIzLmh0bWw=,PICKUP,"アフリカ全域でのエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）大規模アウトブレイク（症例10,400件超、死者5,300人超）で複数国への越境拡大が確認されており、IHR基準に複数該当する重大イベントである。",Ebola,Africa; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,The WHO approves clinical trials of two new vaccines against Ebola.,La OMS aprueba ensayos clínicos de dos nuevas vacunas contra el ébola,2026-11-04T18:21:03+00:00,https://es-us.noticias.yahoo.com/oms-aprueba-ensayos-cl%C3%ADnicos-vacunas-182103723.html,SPANISH,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, the World Health Organization approved clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccines targeting the Bundibugyo strain amid an Africa-wide outbreak that has reported over 10,400 cases and more than 5,300 deaths in five months. Ervebo, licensed for the Zaire ebolavirus strain, is already used in trials but not for Bundibugyo. The two additional candidates would be included in these trials: ChAdOx1, an adenovirus-vectored vaccine developed by the University of Oxford with the Serum Institute of India; and a Moderna mRNA vaccine. The Bundibugyo outbreak has seen cases exported to Nigeria and Kenya, with nine Kenyan cases and one death in October, plus 20 Ugandan cases (one fatal) though Uganda has now been declared Ebola-free by WHO. The WHO director-general Tedros emphasized vaccines complement proven outbreak-control measures like case finding, contact tracing, safe burials, and community engagement.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,実際の発生国はナイジェリア、ケニア、ウガンダ（ウガンダはWHOによりエボラ終息宣言済み）であり、対象国リストには含まれない。インドはワクチン製造元（Serum Institute of India）としての言及のみで、発生地域ではないため verified_locations には含めない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9iYW5na2EudHJpYnVubmV3cy5jb20vbG9rYWwvMTcwMTgzNC8xMTktcG9zeWFuZHUtaWxwLWRpLXBhbmdrYWxwaW5hbmctZGlwZXJrdWF0LXVudHVrLXNrcmluaW5nLXRiYy1oaW5nZ2EtaGl2YWlkcw==,DISMISS,これは既存の慢性感染症(結核・HIV・マラリア・肝炎)に対する地域保健体制強化の行政報道であり、新規アウトブレイクや異常事態を示す情報はない。,Hepatitis; Tuberculosis; Malaria; HIV,Daerah Khusus Ibukota Jakarta; Bangka; Pangkalpinang,119 ILP Posyandu in Pangkalpinang Strengthened for TB and HIV/AIDS Screening,119 Posyandu ILP di Pangkalpinang Diperkuat untuk Skrining TBC hingga HIV/AIDS,2026-11-04T03:46:40+00:00,https://bangka.tribunnews.com/lokal/1701834/119-posyandu-ilp-di-pangkalpinang-diperkuat-untuk-skrining-tbc-hingga-hivaids,INDONESIAN,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, Pangkalpinang, Bangka, has strengthened 119 Posyandu Integrasi Layanan Primer (ILP) to support community health services, including screening for HIV/AIDS, tuberculosis, malaria, and hepatitis (ATM-H). Cadres are being trained to perform early risk-factor screening and detect health issues at the community level, with cross-sector collaboration among NGOs, private sector, and district offices to sustain ATM-H prevention and response. Data from ILP screenings will feed health planning and program design, helping tailor services to local needs. Despite broad coverage, not all cadres yet meet the 25-targeted competencies, and capacity-building will continue to ensure uniform primary health service quality. Nine Puskesmas in Pangkalpinang have already implemented ILP standards.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,記事は公衆衛生プログラムの能力強化に関する内容であり、具体的な感染症の発生・流行を報告するものではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZHcuY29tL2VzL2xhLW9tcy1hcHJ1ZWJhLWVuc2F5b3MtY2wlQzMlQURuaWNvcy1kZS1kb3MtbnVldmFzLXZhY3VuYXMtY29udHJhLWVsLSVDMyVBOWJvbGEvYS03OTg1ODQyMg==,PICKUP,"DRCで進行中のエボラ(Bundibugyo株)アウトブレイクにより5,300人以上が死亡という深刻な公衆衛生上の影響があり、既存ワクチン(Ervebo)の有効性が不明なため新規ワクチン臨床試験が承認されるなど、国際的な対応が継続している重大事案。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,WHO Approves Clinical Trials of Two New Vaccines Against Ebola.,La OMS aprueba ensayos clínicos de dos nuevas vacunas contra el ébola,2026-11-04T18:31:54+00:00,https://www.dw.com/es/la-oms-aprueba-ensayos-cl%C3%ADnicos-de-dos-nuevas-vacunas-contra-el-%C3%A9bola/a-79858422,SPANISH,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, the World Health Organization authorized clinical trials of two experimental Ebola vaccines targeting the Bundibugyo variant driving an outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, which has caused more than 5,300 deaths. The candidates are ChAdOx1, developed by the University of Oxford with the Serum Institute of India, and mRNA-1469 from Moderna. Trials will occur during the ongoing outbreak, pending approvals from competent authorities in the DRC. Ervebo, a vaccine against the Zaire strain, has been deployed since October but its effectiveness against Bundibugyo is unproven; thus the new candidates will be evaluated in field settings. WHO Director-General Tedros emphasized vaccines as powerful tools, but not substitutes for prompt care, contact tracing, safe burials, and community engagement. Results could be available in early 2027.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"IndiaおよびUKはワクチン開発に関与する企業・大学の所在国であり、感染症の発生地ではないためverified_locationsから除外した。アウトブレイクはBundibugyo株によるものでDRCにて継続中、既に5,300人以上の死者が出ている極めて深刻な事案であり、既存のEBS対応下にある可能性が高いが、新規治験承認という重要な動きのため改めてPICKUPと判定した。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZnR2bmV3cy5jb20udHcvbmV3cy9kZXRhaWwvMjAyNkIwNVcwMDI1,PICKUP,数十年来最悪のコレラ流行で死者約1800人、致死率約3%と高く、エボラ流行との併発や紛争地域でのアクセス制限、キンシャサへの拡大リスクも指摘されておりIHR基準を複数満たすためフルリスク評価へ進むべき。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"The Democratic Republic of the Congo's worst cholera outbreak in decades has killed about 1,800 people.",剛果民主共和國爆發數十年最慘霍亂　奪走約1800條人命 - 民視新聞網,2026-11-04T18:30:59+00:00,https://www.ftvnews.com.tw/news/detail/2026B05W0025,CHINESE,humans; environment,"Cholera in the Democratic Republic of the Congo has caused about 1,800 deaths and 60,000 reported cases in 2026, making it the country's worst outbreak in decades. Most infections are concentrated in North Kivu and South Kivu, where ongoing armed conflicts and militia control limit access to hard-to-reach areas for medical relief. The outbreak coexists with a deadly Ebola epidemic, adding to the public health emergency. The World Health Organization warns that the Congo River basin region is now seeing cases along waterways, risking spread toward Kinshasa amid the rainy season. The case fatality rate is around 3%, relatively high for cholera. Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus stresses that expanding vaccine distribution in the eastern provinces is critical to controlling the outbreak and preventing wider transmission.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,エボラとコレラの併発流行、紛争による医療アクセス制限、雨季による水系感染拡大リスクがあり、WHOも警戒を表明している重大事案。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYW9sLmNvLnVrL2FydGljbGVzL2JyaXRpc2gtaGVhbHRoY2FyZS13b3JrZXItZWJvbGEtZXZhY3VhdGVkLTE4MTgzNzAwMC5odG1s,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国における史上最大規模のエボラ流行（1万例超・死者5000人超）が続いており、国際的な人の移動（英国、スイスへの患者搬送、ケニア・ウガンダへの拡大）を伴うため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当し社会的関心も高い。,Ebola,Switzerland; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,British healthcare worker with Ebola evacuated from DR Congo to UK,2026-11-04T18:27:48+00:00,https://www.aol.co.uk/articles/british-healthcare-worker-ebola-evacuated-181837000.html,ENGLISH,humans,"Ebola in DR Congo: A British healthcare worker contracted Ebola while assisting the DR Congo outbreak and is being evacuated to the United Kingdom for treatment. The British citizen, whose identity isn’t disclosed, tested positive in DR Congo and is in stable condition; arrival in the UK is anticipated on 4–5 November 2026, followed by transfer to a high‑consequence infectious disease unit. UK authorities say the risk to the public remains low, and NHS procedures to manage imported Ebola cases are in place. The current DR Congo outbreak—declared 15 May—has surpassed 10,000 cases and 5,000 deaths, is caused by Bundibugyo virus, and is the largest and deadliest Ebola outbreak in the country’s history; no approved treatment exists, though vaccine trials are ongoing. The virus spreads via contact with body fluids; the outbreak has also reached Kenya and Uganda, with Nigeria evacuating a positive case to Switzerland.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事の主題はDRCでの大規模エボラ流行であり、英国・スイス・ケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリアは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。DRC発のアウトブレイクが中心的事象。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubGFuYWNpb24uY29tLmFyL3NvY2llZGFkL3ZhY3VuYXMtZW4tY2FycmVyYS1jb250cmEtZWwtZWJvbGEtbGEtb21zLWFtcGxpYS1sb3MtZW5zYXlvcy1lbi1tZWRpby1kZS11bi1icm90ZS1xdWUteWEtZGVqby1tYXMtZGUtbmlkMDQxMTIwMjYv,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で5,300人以上の死者・10,400件超の確定症例を出す大規模エボラアウトブレイクが継続しており、ナイジェリア・ケニア・ウガンダへの国際的拡大も確認されているため、フルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Federal Republic of Nigeria; Republic of Uganda; Republic of Kenya,"Vaccines in a race against Ebola: WHO expands clinical trials amid an outbreak that has already claimed more than 5,300 lives.",Vacunas en carrera contra el ébola: la OMS amplía los ensayos en medio de un brote que ya dejó más de 5300 muertos,2026-11-04T18:33:54+00:00,https://www.lanacion.com.ar/sociedad/vacunas-en-carrera-contra-el-ebola-la-oms-amplia-los-ensayos-en-medio-de-un-brote-que-ya-dejo-mas-de-nid04112026/,SPANISH,humans,"By 2026-11-04, the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo remains among the worst in recent years, with over 5,300 deaths and more than 10,400 confirmed cases, concentrated in DRC. Imported cases include 1 in Nigeria and 9 in Kenya in October (2 of the Kenyan cases fatal); Uganda reported 20 cases with 1 death and has since been declared Ebola-free. The outbreak is dominated by the Bundibugyo variant, for which no vaccine is yet approved. The WHO recommended expanding clinical trials to include two experimental vaccines: a ChAdOx1-based adenoviral-vector vaccine developed by the University of Oxford with the Serum Institute of India, and Moderna’s mRNA vaccine. Ervebo, approved for the Zaire strain, is being tested against Bundibugyo. Public health authorities emphasize vaccines strengthen—not replace—measures like rapid detection, contact tracing, isolation, safe burials, and community engagement.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ナイジェリア・ケニア・ウガンダは輸入症例としてアウトブレイクに関連するが、対象国リストに含まれないためverified_locationsから除外。Bundibugyo株に対する承認ワクチンが未だ存在せず、2種類の実験的ワクチン（ChAdOx1アデノウイルスベクター、Modernaの mRNA）の臨床試験拡大が検討されている点が特筆される。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucG9saXRpa2EucnMvc3IvY2xhbmFrLzc5OTc5NS9icml0YW5za2ktemRyYXZzdHZlbmktcmFkbmlrLXUta29uZ3UtcG96aXRpdmFuLW5hLWVib2x1,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で進行中の大規模エボラ流行（死者5,000人超、感染者10,000人超）に関連し、英国人医療従事者の感染・国際搬送事例が発生しており、国際的拡大とIHR基準複数該当が認められる。",Ebola,London; Newcastle upon Tyne; England; Switzerland; Republic of France; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,British healthcare worker in Congo tests positive for Ebola,Britanski zdravstveni radnik u Kongu pozitivan na ebolu,2026-11-04T18:37:08+00:00,https://www.politika.rs/sr/clanak/799795/britanski-zdravstveni-radnik-u-kongu-pozitivan-na-ebolu,SERBIAN,humans,"Ebola virus, Bundibugyo strain, has been detected in a British healthcare worker in the Democratic Republic of Congo and the patient will be evacuated to the United Kingdom for treatment in a specialized infectious-disease unit. The individual is currently stable and expected to arrive in the UK today or tomorrow, to be admitted at either Royal Free Hospital in London or Royal Victoria Infirmary in Newcastle. UK Health Security Agency states the public risk remains low. This marks the first case in a British citizen linked to the ongoing outbreak, one of the world’s largest, with reports last week of over 5,000 deaths and more than 10,000 infections. The Bundibugyo Ebola virus has no approved vaccines or specific therapies. The patient was deployed to DR Congo via humanitarian aid to assist in outbreak response; related international evacuations include Switzerland from Nigeria and a French doctor infected after returning from Congo missions.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,発生地域リストには英国・スイス・フランス・ナイジェリア等が含まれるが、これらは患者の搬送先・関連国であり、実際のアウトブレイク発生地はコンゴ民主共和国のみ。ナイジェリアは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYWEuY29tLnRyL2ZyL2FmcmlxdWUvZWJvbGEtbGUtZ2hhbmEtaW5zdGF1cmUtdW4tZCVDMyVBOXBpc3RhZ2Utb2JsaWdhdG9pcmUtJUMzJUEwLWxhJUMzJUE5cm9wb3J0LWRhY2NyYS80MTExOTM0,PICKUP,"DRCでの大規模エボラ流行（死者約5000人、感染者10,170人以上）に加え、ナイジェリアへの輸入症例発生など国境を越えた拡大が確認されており、ガーナが空港での義務的検疫措置を導入するなど地域的な公衆衛生対応が強化されているため、フルリスク評価が必要と判断する。",Ebola,Accra; Greater Accra Region; Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Ghana; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria,Ebola: Ghana imposes mandatory screening at Accra airport.,Ebola : le Ghana instaure un dépistage obligatoire à l'aéroport d'Accra,2026-11-04T18:41:38+00:00,https://www.aa.com.tr/fr/afrique/ebola-le-ghana-instaure-un-d%C3%A9pistage-obligatoire-%C3%A0-la%C3%A9roport-daccra/4111934,FRENCH,humans,"Ghana imposes mandatory Ebola screening at Accra airport: all arriving passengers undergo contactless temperature checks, review of the health-declaration form, and travel-history verification. Symptomatic travelers are immediately routed to secondary evaluation and placed in temporary isolation; travelers with recent travel to Ebola-affected countries are also subjected to this regime. Those arriving directly from affected countries may be observed for up to 21 days, with post-observation follow-up. The measures follow a virtual Africa CDC meeting on Oct 28, 2026, urging strengthened cross-border surveillance while keeping borders open and investing in prevention. Ghana reports zero Ebola cases to date. Hospitality venues are asked to report guests from affected countries and maintain registries, with penalties for false information or refusal to screen. Nigeria has one imported case (Oct 20, 2026) from Uganda; Uganda declared Ebola-free in Aug 2026; Kenya and DRC are affected, with DRC reporting nearly 5,000 deaths and over 10,170 confirmed cases since May 2026.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ガーナ国内では症例ゼロだが、DRCでの大規模流行とナイジェリアへの輸入症例（ウガンダ由来）を受けた予防的措置として空港検疫を導入。地域的な越境拡大リスクが懸念されるため、DRC・ガーナを検証済み発生地域とした。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvLnVrL2dsb2JhbC1oZWFsdGgvc2NpZW5jZS1hbmQtZGlzZWFzZS9lYm9sYS1yaXNrLXRvLXRoZS11ay1yZW1haW5zLWxvdy1kZXNwaXRlLWluZmVjdGVkLWJyaXRvbi8=,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ発生に伴い英国人感染者が自国へ避難搬送されたことは国際的拡大のリスクを示しており、IHR基準の複数該当（重篤性・国際拡大）によりフルRRAへの移行が妥当。,Ebola,Central Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,Ebola risk to UK remains 'low' despite evacuation of infected Briton,2026-11-04T18:53:00+00:00,https://www.telegraph.co.uk/global-health/science-and-disease/ebola-risk-to-the-uk-remains-low-despite-infected-briton/,ENGLISH,humans,"Ebola risk to the UK remains low after a UK humanitarian worker infected with Ebola is evacuated from the Democratic Republic of Congo to Britain for treatment. Experts say the disease would be unlikely to spread easily on home soil, and authorities have stressed that the risk to the UK is low as of 4 November 2026. The patient contracted Ebola in the DRC and is being brought to Britain for medical care, illustrating ongoing efforts to isolate and treat imported cases while preventing transmission. The move highlights persistent concerns about Ebola outbreaks in Central Africa and the importance of rapid evacuation and strict infection-control measures in protecting other countries.",Yes,不明,Yes,不明,2,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事の主眼は英国への輸入症例だが、感染自体はDRCで発生しているため、対象国としてDRCのみを検証対象とした。英国は対象国リストに含まれないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY25uYnJhc2lsLmNvbS5ici9hZ3JvL2JyYXNpbC1kZXZlLWJhdGVyLXJlY29yZGUtZGUtZXhwb3J0YWNhby1kZS1mcmFuZ28tYXBlc2FyLWRlLW5ld2Nhc3RsZS8=,DISMISS,動物疾病（家禽）に関する経済・貿易分析記事であり、ヒトへの公衆衛生リスクの言及はなく、IHR基準・WPRO基準いずれも該当しない。,Human Infection with Avian Influenza; Newcastle Disease; Avian Influenza,Santa Catarina; Paraná; Federative Republic of Brazil,Brazil to break the record for chicken exports despite Newcastle disease.,Brasil deve bater recorde de exportação de frango apesar de Newcastle,2026-11-04T18:55:25+00:00,https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/agro/brasil-deve-bater-recorde-de-exportacao-de-frango-apesar-de-newcastle/,PORTUGUESE,animals,"Newcastle disease in Brazil is expected to have limited impact on poultry exports due to regionalization, which lets importers restrict purchases to affected areas rather than suspending all Brazilian shipments. Rabobank analyst Wagner Yanaguizawa notes shipments remain positive despite restrictions, though a concentration of slaughterhouses in the South hampers rapid redirection of volumes. Santa Catarina, where about 63% of production is export-oriented, may face temporary price pressure. Last year’s avian influenza episode caused a four-month export suspension and a 17% year‑on‑year drop. Rabobank projects Brazil’s chicken exports at 5.75 million tonnes in 2026 and 5.95 million tonnes in 2027 (about +3.5%), with production rising to 16.3 Mt and 16.7 Mt. Domestic per-capita consumption is seen at 50.7 kg (2026) to 51.5 kg (2027). Tilapia growth in Paraná could diversify protein supply, while feed costs stay slightly above this year’s average.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事はニューカッスル病（家禽）および過去の鳥インフルエンザによる輸出への影響を扱う農業・貿易記事であり、ヒト感染症としての公衆衛生シグナルではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cxLmZvbGhhLnVvbC5jb20uYnIvZXF1aWxpYnJpb2VzYXVkZS8yMDI2LzExL21pbmlzdGVyaW8tZGEtc2F1ZGUtcHJvamV0YS1hbHRhLWRhLWRlbmd1ZS1lbS0yMDI3LWUtcXVlci12b2x0YXItYS11c2FyLXZhY2luYS1kby1idXRhbnRhbi5zaHRtbA==,WATCH,ブラジルにおけるデング熱・チクングニア熱の将来予測（2027年）に関する記事であり、季節性・既知の感染症の予測情報であるため緊急性は低いが、気候変動による長期的な感染リスク上昇とワクチン政策の動向は注視が必要。,Chikungunya; Dengue,Federative Republic of Brazil; Türkiye,The government expects a rise in dengue cases in 2027 and aims to resume dengue vaccination.,Governo prevê alta de dengue em 2027 e quer retomar vacina,2026-11-04T15:47:00+00:00,https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/equilibrioesaude/2026/11/ministerio-da-saude-projeta-alta-da-dengue-em-2027-e-quer-voltar-a-usar-vacina-do-butantan.shtml,PORTUGUESE,humans; environment,"El Niño-driven climate effects are expected to raise dengue and chikungunya in Brazil in 2027, with the Health Ministry forecasting a 20–40% rise in dengue. Fiocruz projects about 1.5 million dengue cases in 2027, similar to 2025’s 1.66 million, not accounting for El Niño; under a strong El Niño scenario, regional increases by early 2027 are 49.1% in the Northeast, 68.9% in the North, 84.9% in the Southeast, 98.4% in the Central-West, and 138.2% in the South. By January 2026, 489,197 probable dengue cases were recorded. The government aims to resume the Butantan-DV dengue vaccine after suspending it in June following 42 severe adverse events, including two deaths; Qdenga remains the main option (4–60 years), with about 10 million doses bought in 2024. Anvisa approved Butantan-DV in late November 2025 for 12–59 years; 3.9 million doses were purchased. COP31 in Turkey will discuss SUS climate-response measures.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,Türkiyeは記事中でCOP31の開催地として言及されているのみで、デング熱・チクングニア熱の発生国ではないため除外。既知の季節性疾患に関する将来予測記事であり、ワクチン政策（Butantan-DV再開、Qdenga継続）の動向を継続的にフォローする価値がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY25uYnJhc2lsLmNvbS5ici9zYXVkZS9zYXVkZS1wcm9qZXRhLWF1bWVudG8tZGUtYXRlLTQwLW5vcy1jYXNvcy1kZS1kZW5ndWUtY29tLWVsLW5pbm8v,WATCH,ブラジルで毎年発生する風土病（デング熱）の季節的増加予測であり新規性・異常性は低いが、政府機関（保健省）による公式発表であり、ワクチン供給問題やチクングニア熱リスクも言及されているため経過観察とする。,Chikungunya; Dengue,São Paulo; Rio de Janeiro; Rio de Janeiro; São Paulo; Espírito Santo; Federative Republic of Brazil,Ministry of Health forecasts an increase of up to 40% in dengue cases with El Niño,Saúde projeta aumento de até 40% nos casos de dengue com El Nino,2026-11-04T18:53:50+00:00,https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/saude/saude-projeta-aumento-de-ate-40-nos-casos-de-dengue-com-el-nino/,PORTUGUESE,humans; vectors; environment,"Dengue in Brazil is projected to rise 20-40% over months due to El Niño, with the Southeast region (Minas Gerais, Rio de Janeiro, São Paulo, Espírito Santo) potentially hardest hit, up to a 40% increase, as heat and heavy summer rains boost Aedes aegypti proliferation. Health Minister Alexandre Padilha and epidemiology director Nilton Pereira emphasized preparations for arboviroses surveillance, noting chikungunya transmission risk via the same mosquito. The Instituto Butantan dengue vaccine remains unavailable this year after a June suspension following two deaths and other adverse events; an expert committee and Anvisa and the health ministry continue investigations. The SUS currently offers Takeda's Qdenga vaccine. A final assessment on reallocating the Butantan shot in SUS will follow study results, with hopes to reintroduce it next year. Projections also warn of about 1.7 million dengue cases in 2027 per InfoDengue/Fiocruz; Fiocruz studies indicate southward and central-west spread due to El Niño.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,不明,2,Yes,Yes,不明,季節性のデング熱増加予測記事。Butantan製ワクチンの供給停止（死亡例を受けた調査継続中）や2027年までに170万例のデング熱予測など、サーベイランス上の継続注視が必要な要素を含む。チクングニア熱は同じ蚊媒介のリスクとして言及されているのみで独立した発生報告ではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9kb2wuY29tLmJyL2NhcmFqYXMvbm90aWNpYXMvYnJhc2lsLzk2NzM2NS9icmFzaWwtcmVnaXN0cmEtNjY1LWNhc29zLWRlLW1wb3gtZW0tMjAyNg==,WATCH,Mpoxはブラジルで既知の流行性疾患であり、2026年の症例数が前年同期比で増加しているが、重症度は概ね軽度〜中等度で国際的拡大や渡航制限の兆候はないため、経過観察が妥当。,Mpox; Mpox Clade I; Mpox Clade II,São Paulo; Rio de Janeiro; Rio de Janeiro; Guará; Federative Republic of Brazil,Brazil records 665 Mpox cases in 2026,Brasil registra 665 casos de Mpox em 2026,2026-11-04T18:40:07+00:00,https://dol.com.br/carajas/noticias/brasil/967365/brasil-registra-665-casos-de-mpox-em-2026,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Brazil reports 665 Mpox (monkeypox) cases in 2026 as of November 3, with Rio de Janeiro state accounting for 269 infections (vs 92 in the same period in 2025). In the Federal District, a 32-year-old man from Guará is the year’s 13th case; symptoms began October 26 with fever, body pains and sore throat, followed by widespread lesions; diagnosis was confirmed November 2. Mpox, caused by MPXV, spreads mainly through close contact with infected skin lesions, mucous membranes, bodily fluids, or prolonged contact, including kissing, sex, and sharing contaminated items. Incubation is 3–16 days (up to 21); transmission can continue until all lesions heal. Most cases are mild to moderate; recovery in 2–4 weeks. Vaccination targets priority groups, including immunocompromised individuals, laboratory personnel, and high-risk contacts. Brazil’s 2022 outbreak totaled 10,821 cases; 2025 had 1,079 cases and two deaths. Ongoing surveillance and reducing stigma are urged.",No,不明,No,No,0,Yes,No,Yes,Yes,No,3,不明,不明,No,リオデジャネイロ州で前年比増加（269件 vs 92件）が見られるが、全体として既存のサーベイランス体制下での推移報告であり、新規の国際的懸念は確認されない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9iZXRvLmNkL2ZtaS1yZGMtYWNjb3JkLXNlcnZpY2VzLXF1YXRyaWVtZS1yZXZ1ZS1mZWMtdHJvaXNpZW1lLXJldnVlLWZyZC00LW5vdmVtYnJlLTIwMjYtZndhbWJhLTc3MS1taWxsaW9ucy1kb2xsYXJzLTI0MC1taWxsaW9ucy1lYm9sYS1jb25zZWlsLWFkbWluaXN0cmF0aW9uLW1pLWRlY2VtYnJlLw==,WATCH,記事はIMFの財政支援に関する内容で、エボラの再燃に言及しているが症例数・重症度などの疫学的詳細が不明であり、続報の確認が必要。,Ebola,Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"DRC: Fwamba announces $771 million from the IMF in December, of which $240 is for the Ebola response.","RDC: Fwamba annonce 771 millions de dollars du FMI en décembre, dont 240 pour la riposte Ebola",2026-11-04T18:44:16+00:00,https://beto.cd/fmi-rdc-accord-services-quatrieme-revue-fec-troisieme-revue-frd-4-novembre-2026-fwamba-771-millions-dollars-240-millions-ebola-conseil-administration-mi-decembre/,FRENCH,humans,"DRC secures IMF accord on the fourth ECF review and the third RSF review, with an expected December disbursement of about $771 million, including roughly $240 million for the Ebola response (2026 phase). IMF board review is planned mid-December; the mission (Oct 22–Nov 4) was led by Calixte Ahokpossi. The IMF cites three shocks—conflict in the East, resurgence of Ebola, and the Middle East war—and urges prudent, coordinated fiscal and monetary policy and accelerated reforms to preserve macro stability and inclusive growth. Kinshasa requests higher 2026–27 deficit ceilings and increased access to both the ECF (to cover Ebola costs and external financing needs) and the RSF (to cushion macro-budget risks from health shocks). The IMF notes earlier deficit ceiling miss and ongoing execution risks (revenue measures, wage bill control, prioritization). Inflation is projected near 9% by end-2026 due to higher oil prices; the December Board review will consider the requests.",不明,不明,不明,不明,0,不明,不明,不明,Yes,Yes,2,不明,Yes,Yes,記事はIMFの財政支援に関するもので、エボラの症例数や感染拡大状況など疫学的詳細は記載されていない。『エボラの再燃』という表現から既存の流行継続が示唆されるが、詳細情報は不明。,
