aHR0cHM6Ly9kZW5pa24uY3ovbWludXRhLzIyNDYwODcv,DISMISS,本記事はブンディブギョウ（エボラ）ウイルスに対するワクチン臨床試験の承認に関する内容であり、具体的な発生国・地域情報や新規の公衆衛生事象を示すものではない。インドと英国はそれぞれワクチン製造元（Serum Institute）と開発機関（Oxford大学）の所在地であり、実際の感染発生地ではない。,Ebola,United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,The World Health Organization approved clinical trials of two new vaccines developed against Bundibugyo virus.,Světová zdravotnická organizace schválila klinické testy dvou nových vakcín vyvinutých proti viru bundibugyo,2026-11-04T19:02:13+00:00,https://denikn.cz/minuta/2246087/,CZECH,humans,"WHO has, as of 4 November 2026, approved clinical trials for two new vaccines against Bundibugyo virus, the Ebola virus species involved in a current Ebola outbreak. One vaccine was developed by Oxford University in collaboration with Serum Institute of India; the other by Moderna. The approval enables initiating human trials to assess safety, immunogenicity, and preliminary efficacy; trial specifics such as design, populations, endpoints, and timelines are not detailed. The move reflects international collaboration to broaden preventive options against Bundibugyo virus–related outbreaks and to diversify vaccine platforms amid ongoing Ebola activity. This development highlights vaccine development efforts against distinct Ebola virus species.",不明,No,不明,No,0,No,不明,不明,不明,No,0,No,不明,No,記事はワクチン開発・臨床試験承認に関するニュースであり、実際のエボラ（ブンディブギョウ種）発生国は明記されていない。インド・英国は製造・開発拠点に過ぎず、対象国リストの実発生国としては該当しない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9idXNpbmVzc21pcnJvci5jb20ucGgvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9mbHUtbGlrZS1pbGxuZXNzLWNhc2VzLXJpc2UtMzEtaW4tdHdvLXdlZWtzLWRvaC8=,WATCH,季節性インフルエンザ様疾患の増加で、致死率は低く前年同期比でも低水準だが、一部地域での局所的増加が継続しているため経過観察とする。,Influenza,Mimaropa; Western Visayas; Republic of the Philippines,,Flu-like illness cases rise 31% in two weeks -- DOH | Claudeth Mocon-Ciriaco,2026-11-04T13:30:09+00:00,https://businessmirror.com.ph/2026/11/04/flu-like-illness-cases-rise-31-in-two-weeks-doh/,ENGLISH,humans,"Influenza-like illness (ILI) cases rose 31% nationwide in the Philippines during the first two weeks of October (Oct 1-14, 2026), with 15,042 cases, up from 11,517 in the prior two weeks (Sept 17-30). Year-to-date totals reach 139,013, still 19% lower than the 171,506 recorded during the same period in 2025. The case fatality rate remains 0.06%. The Department of Health flagged 17 provinces and highly urbanized cities across 10 regions for localized increases, with most of the flagged areas in the National Capital Region. Regionally, Western Visayas, Mimaropa, and Central Visayas reported the highest percentage increases. Ongoing heightened surveillance covers those 17 P/HUCs, reflecting a recent rise in flu-like illnesses even as the nationwide total remains below last year's level.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,No,DOHが17の州・高度都市化都市で監視を強化しているが、全国的には前年同期を下回る水準であり、重症度や異常性の報告はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9icmF0aXNsYXZhZGVuLnNrL2FrdHVhbG5lL2RvLWJvamEtcy1lYm9sb3UtcHJpYnVkbnUtZHZlLW5vdmUtdmFrY2lueS1lcGlkZW1pYS1tYS11ei12eXNlLTUtMzAwLW9iZXRpLW96bmFtaWxhLXdoby8=,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で発生中のエボラ出血熱（ブンディブギョ株）流行が5,300人以上の死者・致死率50%超と深刻で、アフリカ全域で1万例超が確認されており、国際的拡大と公衆衛生上の重大性が認められるためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"Two new vaccines will join the fight against Ebola; the epidemic has already claimed over 5,300 lives, WHO announced.","Do boja s ebolou pribudnú dve nové vakcíny, epidémia má už vyše 5 300 obetí, oznámila WHO",2026-11-04T19:12:39+00:00,https://bratislavaden.sk/aktualne/do-boja-s-ebolou-pribudnu-dve-nove-vakciny-epidemia-ma-uz-vyse-5-300-obeti-oznamila-who/,SLOVAK,humans,"WHO expanded clinical trials to two experimental Ebola vaccines targeting the Bundibugyo strain, as the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) experiences a major outbreak in Africa. The current epidemic has caused more than 5,300 deaths and a case fatality rate above 50%, with Africa CDC reporting 10,444 confirmed cases across Africa by Monday. Ervebo, an approved Ebola vaccine, is effective against some strains but not confirmed for Bundibugyo. The two new candidates are ChAdOx1 BDBV (Oxford University in collaboration with Serum Institute of India) and mRNA-1469 (Moderna), developed specifically against Bundibugyo. Trials are led by the DRC National Institute for Biomedical Research with WHO and partners. No vaccine exists yet for Bundibugyo, but these trials aim to determine whether vaccination can curb further spread, alongside proven public health measures like case finding, isolation, safe burials, and community engagement.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドはワクチン開発（Serum Institute of India）に関与しているのみで、アウトブレイク発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9taWRpYW1heC5jb20uYnIvc2F1ZGUvMjAyNi9tcG94LWF2YW5jYS1yaW8tamFuZWlyby1lbnF1YW50by1tcy1zZWd1ZS1zZW0tY2Fzb3MtcmVnaXN0cmFkb3MtMjAyNi8=,WATCH,リオデジャネイロ州でMpox症例が前年比倍増しているが、死亡例はなく重症度・国際的拡大の情報もないため、続報を注視する。,Mpox; HIV,Rio de Janeiro; Rio de Janeiro; Federative Republic of Brazil,"Mpox advances in Rio de Janeiro, while the Ministry of Health remains without registered cases in 2026.","Mpox avança no Rio de Janeiro, enquanto MS segue sem casos registrados em 2026",2026-11-04T19:08:37+00:00,https://midiamax.com.br/saude/2026/mpox-avanca-rio-janeiro-enquanto-ms-segue-sem-casos-registrados-2026/,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Mpox advances in Rio de Janeiro state, with 269 confirmed cases reported as of 3 November 2026, more than double the 119 diagnosed prior year. Mato Grosso do Sul reports 12 notifications with all cases discarded this year, and no confirmed or suspected mpox cases (2025 had 11 confirmed from 67 notifications). In Rio de Janeiro city, EpiRio shows 196 confirmed infections in 2026, versus 94 in 2025, with no mpox deaths in either period. Vaccination decisions remain with the Ministry of Health. Brazil began mpox vaccination in 2023 after Anvisa approved Jynneos/Imvanex; eligibility includes adults 18–49 with HIV/AIDS and lab workers with direct exposure, plus others exposed to the virus, with PrEP vaccination considered if vaccine is available. Transmission is via close contact with lesions, fluids, respiratory secretions, or contaminated fomites; prevention emphasizes isolation, PPE, hand hygiene, and surface cleaning. Symptoms include rash, lymphadenopathy, fever, headache, myalgias, chills, weakness.",No,不明,No,No,0,Yes,No,Yes,Yes,No,3,不明,Yes,No,記事はブラジル・リオデジャネイロ州における2026年のMpox症例増加（119→269件）を報告。死亡例なし、ワクチン接種は保健省方針継続中。国際的な波及や渡航制限の兆候は見られない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudmlqZXN0aS5iYS9jbGFuYWsvNzgyODYyL3doby1wb2RyemFvLWlzcGl0aXZhbmplLWR2aWplLW5vdmUtdmFrY2luZS1wcm90aXYtZWJvbGU=,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で発生したBundibugyoエボラウイルスによる大規模流行（感染者1万人超、死者5,300人超、致死率50%超）がケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダにも拡大しており、IHR基準の複数該当とWPRO基準も満たすため、フルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,WHO supported clinical trials of two new vaccines against Ebola.,WHO podržao ispitivanje dvije nove vakcine protiv ebole,2026-11-04T19:18:00+00:00,https://www.vijesti.ba/clanak/782862/who-podrzao-ispitivanje-dvije-nove-vakcine-protiv-ebole,CROATIAN,humans,"Two experimental Ebola vaccines, developed by the University of Oxford in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India and Moderna, are entering clinical trials in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) to address an outbreak caused by Bundibugyo ebolavirus, a rare strain with no approved vaccine. WHO expert groups recommended including these vaccines in trials, led by the National Institute for Biomedical Research (INRB) in the DRC with international partners including WHO. The epidemic began in May in the DRC; by 31 October there were more than 10,000 infections and a case-fatality rate above 50%. The outbreak’s death toll in the DRC totals 5,103, while the overall toll exceeds 5,300, with additional cases reported in Kenya, Nigeria, and Uganda. Vaccines are powerful tools but not a substitute for proven measures such as timely healthcare, contact tracing, isolation, safe and dignified burials, and community engagement.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドはワクチン製造元（Serum Institute of India）として言及されているのみで、発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外。ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダは流行拡大国として言及されているが対象国リストに含まれないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly90YXJvYmEuY29tLmJyL3R2L2xvbmRyaW5hL3Rhcm9iYS1jaWRhZGUvdmV0ZXJpbmFyaW9zLWFsZXJ0YW0tcGFyYS1hdW1lbnRvLWRlLWNhc29zLWRlLWxlcHRvc3Bpcm9zZS1lbS1jYWVzLWVtLWxvbmRyaW5h,DISMISS,犬における動物疾患の増加に関する地域的な獣医情報であり、ヒトの公衆衛生上の深刻な影響や国際的拡大の兆候は認められない。,Leptospirosis,Londrina; Paraná; Federative Republic of Brazil,Veterinarians warn of an increase in leptospirosis cases in dogs in Londrina.,Veterinários alertam para aumento de casos de leptospirose em cães em Londrina,2026-11-04T19:25:05+00:00,https://taroba.com.br/tv/londrina/taroba-cidade/veterinarios-alertam-para-aumento-de-casos-de-leptospirose-em-caes-em-londrina,PORTUGUESE,humans; environment; animals,"Leptospirosis cases in dogs are rising in Londrina, Brazil, with a veterinary clinic reporting weekly consultations for three to four months; no official data yet. Leptospirosis is a bacterial zoonosis transmitted mainly through rodent urine, with the rainy season increasing environmental risk as the bacterium can persist six months to a year. Exposure is outdoor dog food and water bowls left overnight, attracting rodents. Prevention centers on canine vaccination included in the Dectuple vaccine, protecting four leptospira serovars; owners should remove bowls after meals and monitor for apathy, loss of appetite, and vomiting. In advanced cases, jaundice, muscle stiffness, and sepsis may occur; treatment uses antibiotics and, if severe, IV therapy. Humans can acquire the infection from animal urine or contaminated environments; cats less often affected, and there are no vaccines for cats or humans. Keep dogs up to date on vaccination and seek care for suspected infection.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,No,No,No,主に犬のレプトスピラ症に関する地域的な獣医情報で、人への感染リスクは一般的な注意喚起レベル。公式統計データなし。,
