aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZWFkdC5jby51ay9uZXdzL25hdGlvbmFsLzI2NzAwNDAzLmJyaXRpc2gtbWFuLWluZmVjdGVkLWVib2xhLWZsb3duLWJhY2stdWsv,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で約5000人の死者を出す大規模なエボラ流行が継続しており、感染した英国人医療従事者が本国へ緊急搬送される国際的な症例輸出事例であるため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland; Republic of Angola,,British man infected with Ebola to be flown back to the UK,2026-11-04T19:32:11+00:00,https://www.eadt.co.uk/news/national/26700403.british-man-infected-ebola-flown-back-uk/,ENGLISH,humans,"As of 4 November 2026, a British citizen in the Democratic Republic of Congo tested positive for Ebola and will be evacuated to the United Kingdom for treatment. DR Congo reports an ongoing Ebola outbreak with about 5,000 deaths. The patient is described as a healthcare worker; a medical evacuation to Britain is planned, though no flight timing has been announced. UK officials say the risk to the UK public remains low and that established procedures have been activated for imported cases. In the UK, four Ebola cases have been confirmed historically, including three health workers who treated the 2014–2015 West Africa outbreak. The situation underscores international transfer of an exported Ebola case for treatment and reinforces the need for containment in the DRC outbreak.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国およびアンゴラはBluedotの発生地域に含まれるが、記事主題はDRCでの流行とそこからの症例輸出であり、英国は対象国リスト外、アンゴラは本文に言及なしのため除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly90aW1lc29maW5kaWEuaW5kaWF0aW1lcy5jb20vY2l0eS9rb2xoYXB1ci8yMC1uZXctbGVwcm9zeS1jYXNlcy1kZXRlY3RlZC1pbi1rb2xoYXB1ci1kaXN0cmljdC1kdXJpbmctc3BlY2lhbC1zdXJ2ZXkvYXJ0aWNsZXNob3cvMTM1NTUwNjQwLmNtcw==,DISMISS,ハンセン病は既知の風土病であり、通常の公衆衛生サーベイランス活動による発見であって、異常性・国際的拡大リスク・社会的関心の高まりは見られない。,Leprosy,Republic of India,,20 new leprosy cases detected in Kolhapur district during special survey,2026-11-04T19:25:00+00:00,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/kolhapur/20-new-leprosy-cases-detected-in-kolhapur-district-during-special-survey/articleshow/135550640.cms,ENGLISH,humans,"Twenty new leprosy cases were detected in Kolhapur district during a special survey conducted Sept 16–Oct 31, 2026. All 20 individuals were examined and started on treatment; health workers also screened contacts of leprosy patients diagnosed in the district over the past five years. Symptoms emphasized include pale or reddish patches on the skin, lumps, painless slow-healing wounds, thickened earlobes, loss of eyebrow hair, changes in nose shape, and nerve involvement with tingling or numbness in hands and feet, weakness, and loss of sensation that can cause footwear to slip off. Dr. Hemlata Palekar, assistant director of health services (leprosy), said the goal is to reduce spread to zero by 2027 and urged people with symptoms to visit a government hospital for early diagnosis and treatment.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,地域の通常の公衆衛生サーベイランス活動（特別調査）による既知疾患の発見であり、緊急の対応を要するものではない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hYmNhZ29yYS5jb20uYnIvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9zYW8tYmVybmFyZG8tYXRpdmEtdmFjaW5hY2FvLXNhcmFtcG8v,WATCH,麻疹は伝播性が高く地域でのワクチン接種格差が懸念されるが、症例数は限定的（市内2例、州内41例）で深刻な公衆衛生インパクトやIHR基準の複数該当は認められないため、続報を注視する。,Measles,São Paulo; São Paulo; Federative Republic of Brazil,São Bernardo Intensifies Active Case Finding and Measles Vaccination Through November 14,São Bernardo Intensifica Busca Ativa E Vacinação Contra O Sarampo Até 14 De Novembro,2026-11-04T19:40:57+00:00,https://abcagora.com.br/2026/11/04/sao-bernardo-ativa-vacinacao-sarampo/,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Measles in São Bernardo do Campo, Brazil, remains limited to two confirmed cases this year, with 41 cases in the State of São Paulo since July. The city is intensifying active case finding and measles vaccination through November 14 under the Ministry of Health’s Week S campaign to raise awareness of symptoms (fever, red rash, cough, conjunctivitis) and vaccination coverage. After the July confirmations, sanitary blocks were placed around affected residences with home screening and vaccination outreach. From August 3 to September 1, vaccination was offered to the entire population. Through November 6, Community Health Workers are engaging residents and checking vaccination status. On November 4, 170 Community Health Workers were trained at the Pinacoteca to improve outreach. Vaccination schedule: 12 and 15 months; ages 1–29 require two doses; 30+ at least one dose. All 36 Basic Health Units stock vaccines; hours extend.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,記事は保健省主導のワクチン接種キャンペーン（Week S）を報じるもので、症例数は限定的。州内での麻疹流行継続状況の推移を注視する必要がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYWxqYXplZXJhLmNvbS9uZXdzLzIwMjYvMTEvNC93aG8tYXBwcm92ZXMtdHJpYWxzLWZvci10d28tbmV3LWVib2xhLXZhY2NpbmVz,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で史上最大規模のブンディブギョ株エボラ流行（1万人超感染、致死率約50%）が発生し、ケニア・ナイジェリア・英国への国際的拡大と渡航制限議論も生じているため、フルリスク評価が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,WHO approves trials for two new Ebola vaccines,2026-11-04T19:22:09+00:00,https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/4/who-approves-trials-for-two-new-ebola-vaccines,ENGLISH,humans,"WHO approves two Bundibugyo-specific Ebola vaccine trials in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) amid the largest Bundibugyo outbreak in history. Since May, the outbreak has surpassed 10,444 confirmed cases and more than 5,300 deaths, with a case fatality rate around 50%. A trial using Ervebo (Zaire strain) began earlier, but the new trials target Bundibugyo directly. Led by the DRC’s National Institute for Biomedical Research with WHO and partners, the vaccines were developed by University of Oxford in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India and Moderna; results are expected in early 2027. Kenya reports nine cases (two deaths); Nigeria one case. Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus urged lifting travel restrictions to avoid dampening transparency and response. Separately, a British healthcare worker infected with Ebola is being evacuated to the UK for specialist care, stable, expected to arrive by Thursday for treatment at a high-consequence infectious disease unit.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドはワクチン開発（Serum Institute of India）に関与しているのみで、感染発生国ではないためverified_locationsから除外。ケニア・ナイジェリア・英国は対象国リストに含まれないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc21lLnNrL3N2ZXQvYy9kby1ib2phLXMtZWJvbG91LXByaWJ1ZG51LWR2ZS1ub3ZlLXZha2NpbnktZXBpZGVtaWEtbWEtdXotdnlzZS01LTMwMC1vYmV0aQ==,PICKUP,"DRCでのエボラ流行は死者5,300人・症例10,444人と極めて深刻な規模で、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当し、国際的な支援体制（WHO、国際ワクチン開発）も進行中であるため。",Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,"Two new vaccines will be added to the fight against Ebola; the epidemic already has more than 5,300 victims.","Do boja s ebolou pribudnú dve nové vakcíny, epidémia má už vyše 5 300 obetí",2026-11-04T19:09:33+00:00,https://www.sme.sk/svet/c/do-boja-s-ebolou-pribudnu-dve-nove-vakciny-epidemia-ma-uz-vyse-5-300-obeti,SLOVAK,humans,"Two new experimental Ebola vaccines expand clinical trials to target Bundibugyo virus, as the World Health Organization reports Africa’s current outbreak centered in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) has surpassed 5,300 deaths among about 10,444 confirmed cases (as of Monday, per Africa CDC). The Ervebo vaccine, approved for Ebola broadly, is not yet confirmed effective against Bundibugyo. The two candidate vaccines—ChAdOx1 BDBV (University of Oxford and Serum Institute of India) and Moderna's mRNA-1469—are being tested specifically against Bundibugyo. Trials are led by the DRC National Institute for Biomedical Research with WHO support and partners. WHO cautions vaccines are powerful but do not replace proven measures: prompt health care, contact tracing, patient isolation, safe burials, and community engagement, to curb transmission while vaccine development continues.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドとイギリスはワクチン開発機関（Serum Institute of India、University of Oxford）の所在地であり、感染発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外した。,
