aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubm90aWNpYXNhb21pbnV0by5jb20vbXVuZG8vMzA3ODY3MS9yZGNvbmdvLWVuZnJlbnRhLXBpb3ItZXBpZGVtaWEtZGUtY29sZXJhLWVtLWRlY2FkYXM=,PICKUP,WHOが数十年で最悪規模と警告するコレラ流行（6万例以上、死者1800人超）とエボラ流行（死者5300人超）が同時進行し、キンシャサへの拡大リスクもあるためIHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,DR Congo faces the worst cholera epidemic in decades.,RDCongo enfrenta pior epidemia de cólera em décadas,2026-11-04T19:27:58+00:00,https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/mundo/3078671/rdcongo-enfrenta-pior-epidemia-de-colera-em-decadas,PORTUGUESE,humans; environment,"World Health Organization warns the Democratic Republic of Congo is facing its worst cholera outbreak in decades, with more than 60,000 cases and 1,800 deaths since the year began. Alongside Ebola, which has caused over 5,300 deaths in more than 10,400 cases in about five months, cholera is concentrated in North Kivu and South Kivu in the eastern DRC, but reports now extend along the Congo River basin, risking spread to Kinshasa. While 2025 registered the most cholera cases in over 25 years, the current year is projected to be even more severe. Transmission is driven by hard-to-reach, conflict-affected areas, with the rainy season potentially accelerating spread, including in the capital. The case fatality rate is around 3%, highlighting treatment access challenges. Vaccination campaigns are prioritized; the Vaccine Provision Group approved 7.4 million doses for 2026 with Gavi funding, and a new request is under consideration.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,コレラとエボラが同時に流行しており、紛争地域での対応困難さと雨季による拡大リスク、首都キンシャサへの波及懸念が指摘されている。Gaviによるワクチン供給計画も進行中。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9uZXdzLnVuLm9yZy9ydS9zdG9yeS8yMDI2LzExLzE0NjkwNDc=,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で発生中のブンディブギョ・エボラウイルス病に対し、WHO主導でワクチン・治療薬の臨床試験が開始されており、国際的な関与と公衆衛生上の重大性が認められるためフルリスク評価が妥当。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Angola,Two new vaccines against Ebola have been included in clinical trials.,В клинические испытания включены две новые вакцины против Эболы,2026-11-04T19:40:09+00:00,https://news.un.org/ru/story/2026/11/1469047,RUSSIAN,humans,"Two Ebola vaccines, ChAdOx1 (Oxford University with Serum Institute of India) and Moderna’s mRNA-1469, have been endorsed by WHO expert groups to advance to field-based clinical evaluation in the Democratic Republic of the Congo for Bundibugyo virus disease. This marks the first field testing of vaccines specifically designed against Bundibugyo ebolavirus in real-world conditions, using a ring vaccination approach that enrolls contacts of laboratory-confirmed cases. An Ervebo benchmark from West Africa will be used to gauge effectiveness against Bundibugyo. Concurrently, therapeutic studies assess MBP134 monoclonal antibody, remdesivir, or their combination; maftivimab is planned for inclusion as a potential therapy, and post-exposure prophylaxis with obeldevisir is under investigation. Early treatment results are expected in coming months, with vaccine trial outcomes anticipated in early 2027.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,不明,Yes,Yes,記事はブンディブギョ型エボラウイルス病に対するワクチン・治療薬の臨床試験開始を報じており、DRCでの進行中のアウトブレイクを前提とした内容。アンゴラは本文中で言及されていないためverified_locationsから除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9zYW1waS5uZXQuYnIvYXJhY2F0dWJhL25vdGljaWFzLzMwMTY0MzgvYnJhc2lsLWUtbXVuZG8vMjAyNi8xMS9taW5pc3RlcmlvLWRhLXNhdWRlLXByb2pldGEtYWx0YS1kYS1kZW5ndWUtZW0tMjAyNy0=,WATCH,将来予測に関する行政発表であり、現時点での急性アウトブレイクの報告ではないが、デング熱・チクングニア熱の増加予測とワクチン安全性問題という継続的な公衆衛生課題として経過観察が妥当。,Chikungunya; Dengue,Federative Republic of Brazil,Folha da Região: Ministry of Health forecasts a rise in dengue in 2027.,Folha da Região: Ministério da Saúde projeta alta da dengue em 2027,2026-11-04T19:43:14+00:00,https://sampi.net.br/aracatuba/noticias/3016438/brasil-e-mundo/2026/11/ministerio-da-saude-projeta-alta-da-dengue-em-2027-,PORTUGUESE,humans; environment,"Brazil's Ministry of Health warns that El Niño–driven climate changes are likely to increase dengue and chikungunya in 2027. The projection underscores heightened arbovirus risk linked to climate variability, with potential regional impacts across Brazil. Health Minister Alexandre Padilha says he intends to resume the dengue vaccine developed by Instituto Butantan, which was suspended in June after reports of severe adverse reactions. Padilha emphasized that safety analyses are still pending and he did not provide a timeline for deciding whether to reinstate the Butantan-DV vaccine in Brazil’s public health system (SUS, Sistema Único de Saúde). The remarks reflect ongoing tensions between vaccine safety assessments and outbreak preparedness amid rising arboviral threat.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,不明,2,不明,Yes,No,本記事は2027年に向けた予測・政策的発言が中心であり、現在進行中の具体的な感染急増データは示されていない。ブタンタン研究所製デングワクチンの安全性問題（重篤な副反応報告）は継続的な注視が必要。,
