aHR0cHM6Ly9yYXBpZG9ub2FyLmNvbS5ici9ob3J0b2xhbmRpYS1pZGVudGlmaWNhLWNhc28tZGUtbGVpc2htYW5pb3NlLWVtLWNhby1lLWluaWNpYS1leGFtZXMtZW0tb3V0cm9zLTEwMy1hbmltYWlzLw==,DISMISS,動物（犬）における内臓リーシュマニア症の市内初症例報告であり、ヒトへの感染拡大や公衆衛生上の深刻な影響は報告されていない。局地的な動物検査対応で管理可能と見られる。,Leishmaniasis; Visceral Leishmaniasis,São Paulo; Hortolândia; Campinas; Federative Republic of Brazil,Hortolândia identifies a case of leishmaniasis in a dog and begins testing 103 additional animals.,Hortolândia identifica caso de leishmaniose em cão e inicia exames em outros 103 animais,2026-11-04T19:47:21+00:00,https://rapidonoar.com.br/hortolandia-identifica-caso-de-leishmaniose-em-cao-e-inicia-exames-em-outros-103-animais/,PORTUGUESE,humans; vectors; animals,"Visceral leishmaniasis identified in a dog in Hortolândia, Brazil—municipality's first case. The dog remains with its owner while the zoonoses surveillance unit awaits confirmatory contraprova. 103 additional dogs in Jardim Santa Clara do Lago II are being tested; blood collection began on Tuesday, November 3, and ends November 5. Samples are sent to Instituto Adolfo Lutz in Campinas; UVZ agents visit residences to register animals and advise residents. Transmission occurs via bite of an infected sand fly; there is no direct dog-to-human transmission, though infected dogs can serve as a parasite source for the vector. The disease is caused by Leishmania and can affect the liver and spleen. Dogs may be asymptomatic or show appetite loss, weight loss, weakness, skin lesions, hair loss, and thick nails. Humans may experience fever, weakness, weight loss, and anemia. SUS provides treatment; prevention focuses on reducing sand fly habitats and keeping yards clean.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,媒介動物（犬）での市内初発生例。地域の動物衛生当局が通常の監視・検査対応を実施中であり、ヒト症例の報告はない。,
