aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYmlvYmlvY2hpbGUuY2wvbm90aWNpYXMvY2llbmNpYS15LXRlY25vbG9naWEvbWVkaW8tYW1iaWVudGUtY3l0LzIwMjYvMTEvMDQvbWlzdGVyaW9zby1icm90ZS1kZS1hbnRyYXgtbWF0YS1oaXBvcG90YW1vcy1lbi1hZnJpY2EteS1wcmVvY3VwYS1wb3NpYmxlLWNvbnRhZ2lvLWVudHJlLWh1bWFub3Muc2g=,WATCH,DRCヴィルンガ国立公園でカバの炭疽菌集団死が発生し人間への感染リスクが懸念されているが、現時点で人間感染例は確認されておらず続報を注視する段階。,Cholera; Anthrax; Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Uganda,Mysterious anthrax outbreak kills hippos in Africa and raises concern about possible human-to-human transmission.,Misterioso brote de ántrax mata hipopótamos en África y preocupa posible contagio entre humanos,2026-11-04T20:06:12+00:00,https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/ciencia-y-tecnologia/medio-ambiente-cyt/2026/11/04/misterioso-brote-de-antrax-mata-hipopotamos-en-africa-y-preocupa-posible-contagio-entre-humanos.shtml,SPANISH,environment; humans; animals,"Anthrax outbreak in Virunga National Park, eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo, has killed at least 30 hippos over the past month; no human cases have been detected yet, but authorities monitor and urge not to touch or eat meat from dead animals. Bacillus anthracis, a soil-dwelling bacterium whose spores endure in the environment, was confirmed in lab tests after carcasses appeared in September. Prolonged drought and lack of rain may drive such spillovers, contributing to a decline of Virunga’s hippos from about 29,000 to around 2,700. Human risk lies in handling infected carcasses or consuming contaminated meat; antibiotics can be effective if treatment begins early. The outbreak coincides with large Ebola and cholera outbreaks and regional armed conflict, straining resources. In March 2025, Uganda reported about 65 hippos killed and 15 people positive, 2 deaths, linked to similar spillovers.",No,Yes,No,No,1,Yes,No,Yes,No,Yes,3,Yes,不明,Yes,ウガンダでの2025年3月の類似事例（カバ65頭死亡、人間15例感染・2例死亡）が言及されているが、今回の記事主題はDRCヴィルンガ国立公園での現在進行中のアウトブレイクであるため、verified_locationsはDRCのみとした。炭疽菌は通常ヒト-ヒト感染しないが、動物死骸の取扱いや肉の摂取によるリスクがあり、DRCは既にエボラ・コレラ・紛争で資源が逼迫している点に留意。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubWFnMi5jb20vcC9uZXdzLzY4ODY0Ng==,PICKUP,DRCで発生したエボラ出血熱（ブンディブギョ株）が1万人以上感染・5千人以上死亡と大規模化し、ウガンダ・ケニア・フランスへも越境拡大が確認されており、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。,COVID-19; Ebola,Africa; Republic of France; Republic of Angola; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda,"""'Zero Japanese deaths'—isn't that news? The government's blithe attitude: it continues to admit foreign tourists while domestic media fail to report Africa's Ebola hemorrhagic fever disaster that killed 5,000.""","「日本人の死者ゼロ」だからニュースにしない？アフリカで5千人が死亡した""エボラ出血熱禍""を報じぬ国内メディアと外国人観光客を入れ続ける政府の能天気",2026-11-04T20:00:28+00:00,https://www.mag2.com/p/news/688646,JAPANESE,humans; environment,"Ebola virus disease caused by the Bundibugyo strain is spreading from the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), where the outbreak was declared in May. By October 30, confirmed infections exceeded 10,000 with over 5,000 deaths. The epidemic has reached Uganda to the east, with Kenya reporting infections in October; France had a traveler-confirmed case in June, signaling international exposure. The Bundibugyo strain has no approved therapies or vaccines, and early treatment is crucial as the baseline fatality rate is about 60%, rising to 80–90% with delayed care. The piece notes border screening has waned (unlike during COVID-19), and compares to the 2014–2016 West Africa outbreak that infected about 28,600 and killed 11,000. It criticizes Japanese media for underreporting Africa’s Ebola crisis and urges heightened awareness.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,不明,不明,Yes,記事はDRC由来のエボラ出血熱（ブンディブギョ株）の大規模流行とウガンダ・ケニア・フランスへの拡大を報じる日本語論説記事。対象国リストに含まれるのはDRCのみ（ウガンダ・ケニア・フランス・アンゴラはリスト対象外のためverified_locationsから除外）。致死率60〜90%、ワクチン・治療薬未承認という点で極めて深刻な公衆衛生事案であり、WHO通知相当の可能性が高い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucmFkb3Iucm8vMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9leHBlcnRpaS1vbXMtcmVjb21hbmRhLWFkYXVnYXJlYS1hLWluY2EtZG91YS12YWNjaW51cmktaW1wb3RyaXZhLWVib2xhLWxhLXVuLXN0dWRpdS1jbGluaWMtYWZsYXQtaW4tZGVydWxhcmUtaW4tci1kLWNvbmdvLw==,WATCH,エボラワクチン臨床試験への追加という研究開発関連の情報であり、新規感染拡大や症例数増加等の緊急性を示す内容はないが、エボラという疾患の性質上、経過観察の対象とする。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,WHO experts recommend adding two more Ebola vaccines to an ongoing clinical trial in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.,Experţii OMS recomandă adăugarea a încă două vaccinuri împotriva Ebola la un studiu clinic aflat în derulare în R.D. Congo,2026-11-04T20:16:08+00:00,https://www.rador.ro/2026/11/04/expertii-oms-recomanda-adaugarea-a-inca-doua-vaccinuri-impotriva-ebola-la-un-studiu-clinic-aflat-in-derulare-in-r-d-congo/,ROMANIAN,humans,"WHO experts recommend adding two Ebola vaccines to an ongoing clinical trial in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. One vaccine is developed by the University of Oxford and the Serum Institute of India, and the other by Moderna. The vaccines will join the trial after approval by Congolese medical authorities. This move seeks to broaden the vaccine portfolio for Ebola virus disease in the DRC amid continued efforts to enhance protective options. The report does not provide trial specifics, current case counts, or a timeline for entry beyond regulatory clearance.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,不明,不明,No,0,No,Yes,No,インドは血清研究所（Serum Institute of India）がワクチン開発に関与しているのみで、発生国ではないため除外。英国もオックスフォード大学の関与のみで除外。記事は臨床試験への薬剤追加に関する行政的な内容であり、新規症例や流行状況の記載はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9vYWx0b2FjcmUuY29tL2FjcmUtbWFudGVtLXZpZ2lsYW5jaWEtY29udHJhLWEtZG9lbmNhLWRlLW5ld2Nhc3RsZS1hcG9zLWFsZXJ0YS1lbS1zYy8=,DISMISS,動物衛生（家禽）に関する事案であり、ヒトへの感染や公衆衛生上の深刻な影響を示す情報がない。アクレ州では確認症例もなく、通常の監視活動の範囲内。,Human Infection with Avian Influenza; Newcastle Disease; Avian Influenza,Santa Catarina; Federative Republic of Brazil,Acre remains vigilant against Newcastle disease after alert in Santa Catarina.,Acre mantém vigilância contra a doença de Newcastle após alerta em SC,2026-11-04T20:16:18+00:00,https://oaltoacre.com/acre-mantem-vigilancia-contra-a-doenca-de-newcastle-apos-alerta-em-sc/,PORTUGUESE,animals,"Idaf in Acre intensified surveillance for Newcastle disease and avian influenza after MAPA confirmed a new Newcastle focus in Santa Catarina on November 3, 2026. This is the fourth Newcastle record since the zoosanitary emergency was declared. Acre has no confirmed cases; the last sampling phase in October was negative. A new surveillance phase began in November and runs through June 2027, under the National Avian Health Program (PNSA). Tasks include technical visits and serological sampling; blood and cloacal/tracheal swabs detect the virus and prior exposures. Producers are urged to report dead birds or suspicious behavior to Idaf promptly. Newcastle is highly contagious, affecting over 200 avian species, with symptoms such as sneezing, labored breathing, loss of appetite, greenish diarrhea, wing droop, and motor difficulties; outbreaks require swift public-health responses.",No,No,No,不明,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,No,本件はニューカッスル病（家禽の鳥病）に関する動物衛生当局の監視活動の記事であり、ヒト感染事例の報告はない。アクレ州では確認症例なし、サンタカタリーナ州で発生が確認されているが家禽疾患であり公衆衛生上の緊急性は低い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9mci5hZnJpY2FuZXdzLmNvbS8yMDI2LzExLzA0L2Vib2xhLWxvbXMtdmFsaWRlLWRldXgtbm91dmVhdXgtY2FuZGlkYXRzLXZhY2NpbnMtY29udHJlLWxlLXZpcnVzLWJ1bmRpYnVneW8v,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で継続中のエボラ（ブンディブギョウ株）アウトブレイクは致死率50%超・死者5,300人超と深刻であり、国際的な対応（WHO主導のワクチン治験）が継続している重大な公衆衛生事案であるため。",Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,Ebola: WHO approves two new vaccine candidates against Bundibugyo virus.,Ebola : l'OMS valide deux nouveaux candidats vaccins contre le virus Bundibugyo,2026-11-04T20:17:41+00:00,https://fr.africanews.com/2026/11/04/ebola-loms-valide-deux-nouveaux-candidats-vaccins-contre-le-virus-bundibugyo/,FRENCH,humans,"Two new vaccine candidates against Bundibugyo ebolavirus receive WHO recommendation amid the ongoing Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC). The vaccines are ChAdOx1 BDBV, developed by University of Oxford with Serum Institute of India, and mRNA-1469 from Moderna. They are specifically designed against Bundibugyo and will be added to a clinical trial launched last month alongside the Ervebo vaccine, previously approved for Ebola but not for this strain. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus said the recommendation comes from expert groups. The trial is led by the DRC's Institut National de Recherche Biomédicale with international partners, including WHO. Early safety and immunogenicity data are encouraging, but efficacy must be confirmed through trials. Africa CDC reports 10,444 confirmed cases and over 5,300 deaths, CFR >50%, mostly in the DRC. Vaccination alone cannot stop spread; surveillance, treatment, contact tracing, safe burials, and community engagement remain essential.",Yes,No,不明,不明,1,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事は既存のDRCにおけるエボラ（ブンディブギョウ株）アウトブレイクに対する新規ワクチン候補の承認に関する続報。インドはワクチン製造元（Serum Institute of India）として言及されているのみで、発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外。英国も発生国としての言及はない。,
