aHR0cHM6Ly90aGVpbnNpZ2h0aW50ZXJuYXRpb25hbC5jb20vdWstaGVhbHRoY2FyZS13b3JrZXItZWJvbGEtZHItY29uZ28tZmxvd24tYmFjay1ub3ZlbWJlci00Lw==,PICKUP,DRC国内で死者5000人超・感染者1万人超・致死率48.6%の大規模エボラアウトブレイクが継続中であり、英国人感染者の国際移送やケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダへの波及も確認されているため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する重大シグナル。,Ebola,Republic of Angola; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,British man infected with Ebola in DR Congo to be flown back to UK,2026-11-04T20:10:23+00:00,https://theinsightinternational.com/uk-healthcare-worker-ebola-dr-congo-flown-back-november-4/,ENGLISH,humans,"British national diagnosed with Ebola virus disease in the Democratic Republic of Congo will be repatriated to the United Kingdom. This marks the first confirmed case of a UK citizen contracting Ebola in the Congo outbreak, which has killed over 5,000 and surpassed 10,000 confirmed cases since May, with a 48.6% fatality rate by end-October. The patient, a healthcare worker, tested positive and will be flown back when arrangements are in place; UK authorities say public risk remains low and procedures have been activated. Imported Ebola cases are rare in Britain; four confirmed cases in total, none fatal, including a 1976 lab incident and three health workers from West Africa’s 2014–2015 outbreak. Bundibugyo strain drives this outbreak, with no approved vaccine. WHO notes two candidate vaccines (Oxford/Serum Institute of India; Moderna) may enter trials pending Congolese approval. Spillovers linked to Kenya, Nigeria, and Uganda.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事の主題はDRCでのエボラアウトブレイクであり、英国人患者の帰国が報じられているが発生国はDRC。アンゴラ・ケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリア・英国は対象国リストに含まれないため除外。承認ワクチンなし、Bundibugyo株で致死率が高く、国際的な波及（スピルオーバー）も報告されている点で緊急性が高い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZGluYW1hbmkuY29tL2FsbC1lZGl0aW9ucy9lZGl0aW9uLWNoZW5uYWkvY2hlbm5haS8yMDI2L05vdi8wNC9kZW5ndWUtc2l0dWF0aW9uLXVuZGVyLWNvbnRyb2wtaW4tY2hlbm5haS1zYXktaGVhbHRoLW9mZmljaWFscw==,DISMISS,デング熱は季節的に流行している既知の疾患で、当局により制御下にあると報告されており、異常性・深刻性ともに認められない。,Dengue,State of Tamil Nādu; Chennai; Republic of India,Dengue infection under lockdown in Chennai: officials say.,சென்னையில் கட்டுக்குள் டெங்கு பாதிப்பு: அதிகாரிகள் தகவல்,2026-11-04T20:16:50+00:00,https://www.dinamani.com/all-editions/edition-chennai/chennai/2026/Nov/04/dengue-situation-under-control-in-chennai-say-health-officials,TAMIL,humans; vectors,"Dengue infection under control in Chennai despite ongoing monsoon rains, according to the city health department. From January to October, 4,592 dengue cases were reported in Chennai; August saw 605 cases, September 1,600. October cases were kept around 600. In the first five days of November, only 48 dengue cases were reported. To curb the rising mosquito population, a meeting of vector-control experts—led by Chief Pest Control Officer Selvakumar and attended by about 20 specialists—was held to tighten measures against mosquito breeding in rainwater drains. Concurrent medical camps were organized in Chennai’s Thiru Vi Ka Nagar zone and adjacent areas to prevent dengue-like febrile illnesses during the monsoon. Ongoing emphasis on larval source reduction and surveillance to sustain control.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,No,No,1,No,Yes,No,モンスーン期の蚊媒介感染症対策として現地保健当局が通常の監視・対策活動を実施している内容であり、特段のシグナルとしての緊急性は見られない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cub3RlbXBvLmNvbS5ici9zYXVkZS1lLWJlbS1lc3Rhci8yMDI2LzExLzQvZWwtbmluby1wb2RlLWVsZXZhci1jYXNvcy1kZS1kZW5ndWUtZW0tYXRlLTQwLWVtLTIwMjctcHJldmUtbWluaXN0ZXJpby1kYS1zYXVkZQ==,WATCH,2027年のデング熱症例増加予測やワクチン政策に関する統計・予測報道であり、現時点での異常な急性アウトブレイクを示すものではないが、2026年の死亡者数（368人）やワクチン安全性問題など注視すべき情報を含むため経過観察とする。,Dengue,Pará; Federative Republic of Brazil; Türkiye,"El Niño could boost dengue cases by as much as 40% in 2027, says the Ministry of Health.","El Niño pode elevar casos de dengue em até 40% em 2027, prevê Ministério da Saúde",2026-11-04T20:26:42+00:00,https://www.otempo.com.br/saude-e-bem-estar/2026/11/4/el-nino-pode-elevar-casos-de-dengue-em-ate-40-em-2027-preve-ministerio-da-saude,PORTUGUESE,humans; environment,"Brazil’s Ministry of Health warns dengue cases could rise 20-40% in 2027 due to El Niño, with regional variations in the semi-arid and Amazon zones. Fiocruz projects about 1.5 million probable dengue cases in 2027 without El Niño; under a strong El Niño, increases are projected across all regions (South +138.2%, Central-West +98.4%, Southeast +84.9%, North +68.9%, Northeast +49.1%). Since January 2026, Brazil has recorded 489,197 probable dengue cases; 368 deaths in 2026 with 116 under investigation. The government is evaluating the Butantan-DV vaccine (suspended June 8 after 42 adverse events including 2 deaths) for potential resumption in the SUS next year, after safety analyses. The public network’s only current dengue vaccine is Qdenga (Takeda), for ages 4-60, with vaccination of adolescents 10-14. Brazil will present climate-health actions at COP31 in Turkey (Nov 9–20).",不明,No,No,No,0,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,No,記事は2027年のデング熱予測（エルニーニョ影響）とButantan-DVワクチンの安全性評価・再開検討に関する内容。デング熱はブラジルで季節的・地方病的に流行しており、異常・予期せぬ事象とは言えないが、死亡者数やワクチン供給状況は継続監視の価値がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9pbmZvcm1hdGlvbi50djVtb25kZS5jb20vYWZyaXF1ZS9lcGlkZW1pZS1kZS1jaG9sZXJhLWVuLXJkYy0xODAwLW1vcnRzLWRlcHVpcy1sZS1kZWJ1dC1kZS1sYW5uZWUtc2Vsb24tbG9tcy0yODQ0NTA2,PICKUP,コレラとエボラの同時流行で死者数が極めて多く、紛争地域での対応困難とキンシャサへの拡大懸念があり、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルRRAへ進むべき。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"Cholera epidemic in the DRC: 1,800 deaths since the start of the year, according to the WHO.","Épidémie de choléra en RDC : 1.800 morts depuis le début de l'année, selon l'OMS",2026-11-04T20:11:09+00:00,https://information.tv5monde.com/afrique/epidemie-de-cholera-en-rdc-1800-morts-depuis-le-debut-de-lannee-selon-loms-2844506,FRENCH,humans; environment,"As of November 4, 2026, the Democratic Republic of Congo faces a severe cholera epidemic with more than 60,000 suspected or confirmed cases and 1,800 deaths this year, according to the WHO. The outbreak coincides with an Ebola epidemic that has killed over 5,300 people among more than 10,400 cases in five months. Most cholera cases are in the eastern provinces of North Kivu and South Kivu, but transmissions are now reported along the Congo River basin toward Kinshasa, raising concern of wider spread. The case fatality rate is around 3%, underscoring access-to-treatment challenges amid conflict-affected, hard-to-reach areas and ongoing rainy-season conditions that favor transmission including the capital. Emphasis on vaccination campaigns is highlighted; a global vaccine coordination group has approved 7.4 million doses for 2026, with support from UNICEF, MSF, IFRC, and Gavi, and further requests are under review.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,コレラとエボラの同時流行というダブルアウトブレイクで、特にコレラが河川沿いにキンシャサへ拡大する懸念が強調されている。エボラも同国で同時進行中だが、本記事の主題はコレラ流行。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9ib2hlbWlhLmN1L2VsLWVib2xhLWRlLW51ZXZvLWVuLXRpZXJyYXMtYWZyaWNhbmFzLw==,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ流行が同国史上最悪規模（1万人超の感染、死者約5千人）に達し、既にケニア・ナイジェリアへの国際的拡大が確認されており、渡航・貿易制限的対応（空港・港湾での管理強化）も取られているためIHR基準を複数満たす。,Ebola,Africa; Republic of Sierra Leone; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Liberia; Republic of Guinea; Federal Republic of Nigeria,"Ebola, once again on African soil.","El Ébola, de nuevo en tierras africanas",2026-11-04T20:10:31+00:00,https://bohemia.cu/el-ebola-de-nuevo-en-tierras-africanas/,SPANISH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) in 2026 has reached 10,172 confirmed cases and 4,932 deaths as of late October, making it the deadliest in DRC’s history and with potential to surpass the 2014–2016 West Africa epidemic (Guinea, Liberia, Sierra Leone) which reported 28,616 cases and 11,325 deaths. The virus spreads through direct contact with infected bodily fluids (urine, saliva, sweat, feces, vomit, breast milk, semen) and can enter via broken skin or mucous membranes (eyes, nose, mouth). Africa CDC convened an extraordinary ministerial meeting (virtual) on Oct 29 to coordinate cross-border surveillance. Kenya reported three cases on Oct 16 linked to a first contact; Nigeria intensified airport and seaport controls after its first case that week, stressing isolation and vigilant border monitoring to prevent community spread. Health workers and communities must maintain PPE use and rigorous hand hygiene to curb transmission.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ケニア・ナイジェリアへの感染拡大が報告されているが、両国は対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations には含めていない。シエラレオネ・リベリア・ギニアは2014-2016年の過去の流行事例として言及されているのみで、今回の発生国ではないため除外した。Africa CDCが緊急閣僚級会合を開催するなど国際的な危機対応が進行中。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2hvLmludC9mci9uZXdzL2l0ZW0vMDQtMTEtMjAyNi10d28tbmV3LWNhbmRpZGF0ZS12YWNjaW5lcy10by1qb2luLWVib2xhLXRyaWFsLWFzLXRyZWF0bWVudC1yZXNlYXJjaC1hZHZhbmNlcw==,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国でブンディブギョ・エボラウイルスによるアウトブレイクが継続しており、WHOが主導するワクチン・治療薬の臨床試験拡大が報じられていることから、重篤な公衆衛生イベントとして継続的な注視が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Kingdom of Belgium,Two new candidate vaccines join the Ebola virus disease trial amid advances in treatment research.,Deux nouveaux vaccins candidats rejoignent l'essai sur la maladie d'Ebola dans un contexte de progrès de la recherche en matière de traitement,2026-11-04T20:30:29+00:00,https://www.who.int/fr/news/item/04-11-2026-two-new-candidate-vaccines-to-join-ebola-trial-as-treatment-research-advances,FRENCH,humans,"WHO expert groups recommended adding two new Ebola vaccines to the Tumaini trial in the Democratic Republic of Congo, amid a Bundibugyo ebolavirus outbreak. The candidates are ChAdOx1 (Oxford/SII) and mRNA-1469 (Moderna). Trials will proceed after national approvals, based on preclinical and early clinical data. Tumaini, led by the DRC’s National Biomedical Research Institute with partners including University of Antwerp, WHO, Epicentre, MSF, ITM Antwerp, and Africa CDCs, uses a ring-vaccination approach around confirmed Bundibugyo cases and already has four rings. Ervebo (Ebolavirus Zaïre vaccine) is being assessed for Bundibugyo within Tumaini. The PARTNERS trial tests MBP134 and remdesivir, with maftivimab to be added and obeldesivir PEP studied. First vaccine results are expected in early 2027.",Yes,Yes,No,不明,2,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,ベルギーはアントワープ大学など研究パートナー機関の所在地として言及されているのみで、アウトブレイク発生国ではないため verified_locations から除外した。既に4つのワクチン接種リング（ring vaccination）が設定されている既存アウトブレイクであり、本記事は治療・ワクチン研究の進展に関する続報。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9zYW5hLnN5L2hlYWx0aC8yNjI2MzEyLw==,PICKUP,"DRCにおけるBundibugyoエボラウイルスのアウトブレイクで死者が5,300人を超えており、WHOが新規ワクチンの臨床試験追加を推奨するなど国際的な対応が進行中であるため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。",Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,World Health Organization recommends adding two new vaccines to trials of Ebola countermeasures.,الصحة العالمية توصي بإضافة لقاحين جديدين لتجارب مكافحة إيبولا,2026-11-04T20:29:11+00:00,https://sana.sy/health/2626312/,ARABIC,humans,"World Health Organization (WHO) recommends adding two candidate vaccines—ChAdOx1 BDBV and mRNA-1469 (Moderna)—to ongoing Ebola countermeasures trials in Africa, focusing on Bundibugyo ebolavirus circulating in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), where deaths exceed 5,300. Trials began last month using Ervebo (rVSV-ZEBOV) vaccine, approved for Ebola Zaire but not Bundibugyo. The new vaccines were developed by Oxford University with the Serum Institute of India and Moderna, targeting Bundibugyo virus. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus said expert groups endorsed adding these vaccines to the trials. The outbreak underscores the urgency to complete international pandemic accords and bolster cross-border health cooperation.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"インドは血清研究所がワクチン開発に関与しているのみで発生国ではないため除外。アフリカ大陸は対象国リストに該当なし。死者数5,300人超はBundibugyoエボラの累積数として異例の規模であり、既存のアウトブレイクの深刻化を示唆する。",
aHR0cDovL3RoZXBlbmluc3VsYXFhdGFyLmNvbS9hcnRpY2xlLzA0LzExLzIwMjYvd2hvLWFwcHJvdmVzLWNsaW5pY2FsLXRyaWFscy1vbi10d28tbmV3LWVib2xhLXZhY2NpbmVz,PICKUP,"コンゴ民主共和国で5,300人以上の死者を出しているエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクに対し、WHOが新規ワクチン候補の臨床試験を承認するなど国際的な対応が継続しており、深刻性・異常性ともに高い。",Ebola,Genève; Genève; Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Switzerland,,WHO approves clinical trials on two new Ebola vaccines,2026-11-04T19:36:06+00:00,http://thepeninsulaqatar.com/article/04/11/2026/who-approves-clinical-trials-on-two-new-ebola-vaccines,ENGLISH,humans,"As of 2026-11-04, the World Health Organization approved clinical trials for two new Ebola vaccine candidates amid an ongoing African outbreak that has killed more than 5,300 people. Geneva reports that WHO expert groups are recommending adding two vaccines to the trial originally developed in October for the Bundibugyo virus ravaging the Democratic Republic of Congo. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus told reporters the additions aim to accelerate protective options against this Ebola lineage. The Democratic Republic of Congo outbreak remains severe, with the two vaccines proceeding to clinical testing to assess safety and efficacy in this context. The development underscores international efforts to expand vaccination responses to the Bundibugyo virus outbreak in Africa.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,発生地域にGenevaやSwitzerlandが含まれるが、これらはWHO本部所在地であり実際の感染発生地ではないため除外。記事の主題はDRCでのエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクとそれに対するWHOのワクチン開発支援。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGEzLmNvbS96YWhyYW5pY2llL2NsYW5vay8xMDgwOTk3L3ZpYWMtYWtvLXBvbG92aWNhLW5ha2F6ZW55Y2gtem9taWVyYS13aG8tc2NodmFsaWxhLXNrdXNreS1ub3Z5Y2gtdmFrY2luLXByb3RpLWVib2xl,PICKUP,DRCにおけるエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクが継続・拡大しており、致死率50%超、1万人超の感染者という深刻な公衆衛生影響があるため。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,More than half of those infected die. WHO approved trials of new Ebola vaccines.,Viac ako polovica nakazených zomiera. WHO schválila skúšky nových vakcín proti ebole,2026-11-04T20:28:13+00:00,https://www.ta3.com/zahranicie/clanok/1080997/viac-ako-polovica-nakazenych-zomiera-who-schvalila-skusky-novych-vakcin-proti-ebole,SLOVAK,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) continues to surge, with 10,444 confirmed cases and more than 5,300 deaths, giving a case-fatality rate above 50% and most fatalities in the DRC. The World Health Organization (WHO) approved clinical trials for two new Bundibugyo-strain vaccines: ChAdOx1 BDBV (Oxford University) and mRNA-1469 (Moderna, developed with the Serum Institute of India). Ervebo, approved for Ebola virus, began testing in October 2026 but is not licensed for Bundibugyo. The trials are led by the DRC’s National Institute for Biomedical Research, with WHO and partners. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus stressed that vaccines complement, not replace, established outbreak measures such as timely care, contact tracing, isolation, safe and dignified burials.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドは本記事内でSerum Institute of Indiaがワクチン開発に関与しているとして言及されているのみで、発生地ではないためverified_locationsから除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucG9saXRpY2FkaXN0cml0YWwuY29tLmJyL21wb3gtc2VjcmV0YXJpYS1kZS1zYXVkZS1vcmllbnRhLXBvcHVsYWNhby1zb2JyZS1wcmV2ZW5jYW8tZS1zaW50b21hcy1kYS1kb2VuY2Ev,WATCH,ブラジル連邦直轄区でMpox23例が確認されているが、重症度は軽度〜中等度で管理可能とみられ、国際的拡大や渡航制限のリスクを示す情報はないため、続報を注視する段階と判断。,Mpox; Mpox Clade I; Mpox Clade II; HIV,Federative Republic of Brazil,"Mpox: Health Secretariat advises the public on Mpox prevention and symptoms -- Política Distrital is now PDNews, news about politics and health in the DF.","Mpox: Secretaria de Saúde orienta população sobre prevenção e sintomas da doença -- Política Distrital agora é PDNews, notícias sobre Política e Saúde do DF",2026-11-04T20:35:15+00:00,https://www.politicadistrital.com.br/mpox-secretaria-de-saude-orienta-populacao-sobre-prevencao-e-sintomas-da-doenca/,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Mpox (monkeypox) in the Distrito Federal totaled 23 confirmed cases by the first week of November 2026. Most patients have mild to moderate illness with skin lesions, lymphadenopathy, fever, headache, myalgia, chills, and asthenia. Transmission mainly occurs through direct contact with affected individuals, including intimate or sexual contact, or prolonged exposure to respiratory secretions. Recovery typically follows weeks of observation with supportive care. Seek care promptly for sudden mucosal lesions or acute eruptions. Prevention emphasizes avoiding close contact with cases, frequent hand hygiene, and not sharing utensils, clothing, or bedding; isolation per local guidance mitigates spread. Therapy is supportive; no antiviral directly targets the virus. Vaccination is limited to federally defined groups, notably HIV-diagnosed individuals with significant immunosuppression and laboratory personnel handling the pathogen.",No,No,不明,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,Yes,Yes,不明,地元保健当局が予防啓発を行っている段階の記事であり、既知のMpoxアウトブレイクの継続的な国内対応を示す内容。新規性や異常性は低い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9rdW1hbmljaGkuY29tL2FydGljbGVzLzIwNTQyNzk=,PICKUP,コンゴ東部でのBundibugyo株エボラ出血熱流行が継続中で感染者1万人超・死者5千人超と深刻であり、WHOが新規ワクチン治験追加を発表するなど国際的対応が進行しているため、フルリスク評価が必要と判断する。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,New Ebola vaccine trials: WHO to add two more vaccine types (Kyodo News) | Kumamoto Nichinichi Shimbun,エボラ出血熱巡り新ワクチン治験　世界保健機関、２種類追加へ（共同通信）｜熊本日日新聞社,2026-11-04T20:42:27+00:00,https://kumanichi.com/articles/2054279,JAPANESE,humans,"Ebola virus disease persists in eastern Congo (formerly Zaire), driven by the Bundibugyo strain. As of 2026-11-04, the World Health Organization announced two additional vaccine candidates will enter clinical trials to target the Bundibugyo outbreak. The new candidates include a vaccine jointly developed by the UK’s University of Oxford and an Indian research institute, and Moderna’s vaccine. In Congo, more than 10,000 infections and over 5,000 deaths have been reported. Since October, trials using existing vaccines against the Zaire strain have been conducted in Congo, with the two new vaccines to be added after local regulatory approval. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus noted that while some areas show slower transmission, new outbreak zones continue to emerge.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,発生地域にIndiaとUKが含まれているが、これらはワクチン共同開発機関の所在地であり、実際の感染発生国ではないため除外した。実際のアウトブレイクはコンゴ東部（旧ザイール）に限定されている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaGVzcHJlc3MuY29tLyVEOCVBQSVEOSU4MSVEOCVCNCVEOSU4QS0lRDglQTclRDklODQlRDklODMlRDklODglRDklODQlRDklOEElRDglQjElRDglQTctJUQ5JThBJUQ5JTg4JUQ4JUFGJUQ5JThBLSVEOCVBOCVEOCVBRCVEOSU4QSVEOCVBNyVEOCVBOS0xODAwLSVEOSU4MyVEOSU4OCVEOSU4NiVEOCVCQSU=,PICKUP,DRCで過去数十年で最悪規模のコレラ流行（死者1800人、感染約6万人）が発生し、同時にエボラも史上最悪級の流行となっており、武装勢力による医療アクセス制限や都市部（キンシャサ）への拡大リスクも指摘されているため。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"The cholera outbreak claims the lives of 1,800 Congolese.",تفشي الكوليرا يودي بحياة 1800 كونغولي,2026-11-04T20:16:11+00:00,https://www.hespress.com/%D8%AA%D9%81%D8%B4%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%83%D9%88%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%B1%D8%A7-%D9%8A%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A-%D8%A8%D8%AD%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%A9-1800-%D9%83%D9%88%D9%86%D8%BA%D9%88%D9%84%D9%8A-1834779.html,ARABIC,humans; environment,"World Health Organization figures released on 2026-11-04 show 1,800 people have died and about 60,000 cholera cases in the Democratic Republic of the Congo since the start of the year, the worst outbreak in decades. Most infections are in North Kivu and South Kivu in the eastern region, where armed groups like M23 control areas and hinder medical and humanitarian access. WHO cautions that new cases could spill into Kinshasa along the Congo River basin, elevating urban risk. The cholera outbreak compounds an Ebola surge described as the country's worst in history, with some areas affected by both diseases. The rainy season may speed transmission of waterborne cholera. The case fatality rate among reported cholera cases is about 3%. WHO urges integrated response and Ebola vaccination efforts in the east.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,コレラとエボラが同時流行し、武装勢力の活動によるアクセス制限が状況を悪化させている。WHOは統合対応とエボラワクチン接種の強化を呼びかけている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuNDduZXdzLmpwLzE1MTg0OTUzLmh0bWw=,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国でエボラ感染者1万人・死者5000人を超える大規模アウトブレイクが継続中で、新たな発生地域も出現しており、国際的関心・対応（WHOによるワクチン治験追加）も高いためフルRRA対象とする。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,WHO to add two more Ebola hemorrhagic fever vaccine trials.,エボラ出血熱巡り新ワクチン治験　世界保健機関、2種類追加へ,2026-11-04T20:33:27+00:00,https://www.47news.jp/15184953.html,JAPANESE,humans,"WHO to add two Ebola virus disease vaccine trials in the Democratic Republic of the Congo's eastern outbreaks, focusing on the Bundibugyo strain responsible for the current surge. The two candidates are: 1) a vaccine jointly developed by the University of Oxford and an Indian research institute; and 2) Moderna's vaccine. Trials will be added after local regulatory approval, with results expected in early 2027. Since October, Congo has been conducting clinical trials using vaccines based on the Zaire (Ebola) strain. The Bundibugyo-targeted candidates will join these efforts. WHO notes Congo has surpassed 10,000 Ebola infections and 5,000 deaths. Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus warned during a briefing that while transmission in some areas has slowed, new outbreak regions continue to appear, underscoring the ongoing threat and the need for vaccine evaluation.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,WHOテドロス事務局長が会見で伝播減速地域がある一方、新規発生地域の出現を警告しており、依然として拡大リスクが懸念される状況。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucHJhdmRhLnJ1L25ld3Mvd29ybGQvMjQzNzM5Ny1ib2xlem4tbnl1a2FzbGEtYnJhemlsaWEv,WATCH,動物疾病（家禽のニューカッスル病）のアウトブレイクで人への直接的な公衆衛生リスクは報告されていないが、WOAH通知対象であり感染拡大が継続している点から経過観察とする。,Newcastle Disease,Santa Catarina; Nova Itaberaba; Federative Republic of Brazil,"In Brazil, the fourth outbreak of Newcastle disease has been recorded in the state of Santa Catarina.",В Бразилии зафиксировали четвертый очаг болезни Ньюкасла в штате Санта-Катарина,2026-11-04T20:27:00+00:00,https://www.pravda.ru/news/world/2437397-bolezn-nyukasla-brazilia/,RUSSIAN,animals,"Brazil's Ministry of Agriculture confirmed the fourth Newcastle disease outbreak in Santa Catarina in a commercial poultry operation. A new outbreak was detected in Nova Erechim municipality within an established zoosanitary disaster zone, with virus confirmation on Tuesday, December 3, in a turkey farm; initial sampling began on November 31. Four active outbreaks are now reported in Santa Catarina—Nova Itaberaba, Coronel Freitas, and Nova Erechim—dating to October 18. Containment follows standard zoosanitary procedures; the veterinary authority is conducting epidemiological investigations and control measures. In farms where the first three cases occurred, a sanitary vacuum regime—full cleaning and disinfection before a new production cycle—has been implemented, effectively suspending production during quarantine. Newcastle disease is highly contagious to domestic and wild birds, causes respiratory then neurological signs, and is notifiable to WOAH. Meat from properly inspected poultry remains safe for consumption.",No,No,No,不明,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,不明,2,No,Yes,不明,動物疾病(家禽)であり人獣共通感染症としてのヒトへの感染報告はなし。家禽産業への経済的影響と貿易制限の可能性はあるが、公衆衛生上の直接的リスクは低い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9lbHBhaXMuY29tL3NvY2llZGFkLzIwMjYtMTEtMDQvdW5hLXBlcnNvbmEtY29uLWVib2xhLWV2YWN1YWRhLWEtcmVpbm8tdW5pZG8tZGVzZGUtcmVwdWJsaWNhLWRlbW9jcmF0aWNhLWRlbC1jb25nby5odG1s,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で発生中のエボラ出血熱アウトブレイクは史上2番目の規模(感染者1万人超、死者約5000人)であり、英国人患者の国際搬送という国際的拡大の実例も発生しているため、フルリスク評価に進むべき案件である。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,A person with Ebola evacuated to the United Kingdom from the Democratic Republic of the Congo.,"Una persona con ébola, evacuada a Reino Unido desde República Democrática del Congo",2026-11-04T20:28:42+00:00,https://elpais.com/sociedad/2026-11-04/una-persona-con-ebola-evacuada-a-reino-unido-desde-republica-democratica-del-congo.html,SPANISH,humans,"An Ebola patient, a British worker, is being evacuated from the Democratic Republic of the Congo to the United Kingdom for treatment. The patient is stable and is due to reach the UK on Wednesday or Thursday, after which an ambulance will transport him to a high-risk infectious diseases unit. British authorities say the risk to the general population remains low and no travel or trade disruptions are expected. This marks the first British citizen affected by the current outbreak, though several people from other European countries have been infected. The World Health Organization has supported evacuations on behalf of partners and governments. Imported cases remain rare in the UK—four confirmed since 1976. The Democratic Republic of the Congo outbreak is the second-largest on record, with over 10,000 confirmed cases and nearly 5,000 deaths by late October. Ebola is a viral disease spread by contact with bodily fluids.",Yes,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,英国への患者搬送はIHR基準上の国際的拡大の一例だが、感染源はDRCの既存アウトブレイクであり、記事の主題もDRCの流行状況にあるため、verified_locationsはDRCのみとした。英国は対象国リストに含まれない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZGF2YXIxLmNvLmlsLzcwNTc2Mi8=,DISMISS,コンゴ帰国者のエボラ疑い例はイスラエルで検査の結果陰性と確定しており、実際の感染事例は確認されていない。,Ebola,State of Israel,Suspected Ebola: Two hospitalized after returning from Congo tested negative,החשד לאבולה: תוצאה שלילית לשניים שאושפזו לאחר שחזרו מקונגו,2026-11-04T20:34:04+00:00,https://www.davar1.co.il/705762/,HEBREW,humans,"Two patients were hospitalized on 3 November 2026 in Israel after returning from the Democratic Republic of the Congo and developing fever, raising suspicion for Ebola virus disease. The Israeli Health Ministry said that Ebola tests for both patients returned negative, indicating no evidence of infection. To date, Israel has not identified any confirmed Ebola case. The ministry emphasized that the testing was carried out in accordance with professional medical standards and with international guidelines currently governing the management of highly contagious diseases. The update underscores adherence to established protocols in responding to potential cases linked to travel from the Congo.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事の主題はイスラエルでの疑い例が陰性と判明したことであり、DRCでのエボラ流行の実態については言及がないため対象国として検証できない。イスラエルは対象国リストに含まれない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hamVsLnNhL21pc2MvOG0yeHhyNmVv,WATCH,既知のDRCエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）アウトブレイクに対するワクチン試験拡大の報道であり、新規性のある公衆衛生上の緊急事態ではないが、進行中のアウトブレイク関連情報として経過観察が必要。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,WHO adds two new vaccines to Ebola vaccine trials in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.,الصحة العالمية تضيف لقاحين جديدين لتجارب إيبولا في الكونغو الديمقراطية,2026-11-04T20:52:00+00:00,https://ajel.sa/misc/8m2xxr6eo,ARABIC,humans,"WHO adds two vaccines to Ebola vaccine trials in the Democratic Republic of the Congo to address the current outbreak caused by Bundibugyo ebolavirus. The vaccines, developed by the University of Oxford in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India and Moderna, will join ongoing clinical trials in the DRC. These two candidates are described as the first vaccines specifically designed to target Bundibugyo virus in this outbreak. The update underscores international collaboration to expand countermeasures against Ebola and to evaluate safety, immunogenicity, and potential effectiveness against the Bundibugyo strain through ongoing testing. The article does not provide case or death counts, but the development represents a strategic step to broaden protection against Ebola and adapt to the circulating strain.",不明,No,不明,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,Yes,3,不明,Yes,Yes,記事はワクチン試験の拡大に関する内容で、症例数・死亡数の記載なし。米国・インド・英国はワクチン開発関係国として言及されているが、発生地ではないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9pYmkub25nLmJyL25vdGljaWEvMjY1NzMzL211dGlyYW8tY29udHJhLWRlbmd1ZS1wYXNzYS1wZWxvLW5vdmEtZXNwZXJhbmNhLWUtdmlsYS1lbHZpcmE=,DISMISS,通常の蚊媒介対策・予防活動の告知記事であり、異常な発生や公衆衛生上の深刻な影響を示す情報がないため。,Dengue,Federative Republic of Brazil,Dengue prevention drive passes through Nova Esperança and Vila Elvira.,Mutirão contra dengue passa pelo Nova Esperança e Vila Elvira,2026-11-04T20:46:34+00:00,https://ibi.ong.br/noticia/265733/mutirao-contra-dengue-passa-pelo-nova-esperanca-e-vila-elvira,PORTUGUESE,environment; humans; vectors,"Dengue prevention drive by health agents will occur in Nova Esperança and Vila Elvira on Saturday, November 7, from 08:00 to 14:00, focusing on identifying and eliminating Aedes aegypti breeding sites inside homes. Inspections include guidance for residents to maintain properties free of standing water, with weekly checks to remove containers that can hold water, such as buckets, plant saucers, and pet waterers. This year, agents conducted 48,218 Saturday residential visits, aiming to reach homes that are closed during the week. In addition to the mutirão, the Health Department continues Aedes control efforts, including Residual Intradomiciliary Spraying (BRI), nebulization, maintenance of Larvicidal Dissemination Stations (EDLs), and inspections of special properties, with plans to implement the Wolbachia method. The initiative supports UN SDGs 3, 16, and 17.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事はルーチンのデング熱予防・媒介蚊対策活動の告知であり、新規感染拡大や異常事態の報告はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hamVsLnNhL2ludGVybmF0aW9uYWwvcWpsaHN0cmt1,PICKUP,エボラ出血熱はIHR基準における重大な公衆衛生上の影響を有し、英国人感染者の確認は国際的拡大の可能性を示唆するため、フルリスク評価への移行が妥当と判断。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,Britain announces that one of its citizens has contracted the Ebola virus in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.,بريطانيا تعلن إصابة أحد مواطنيها بفيروس إيبولا في الكونجو الديمقراطية,2026-11-04T20:46:00+00:00,https://ajel.sa/international/qjlhstrku,ARABIC,humans,"On 4 November 2026, a British citizen in the Democratic Republic of the Congo has tested positive for Ebola virus disease, with the case lab-confirmed. The government spokesperson stated the individual is currently in the DRC and that the risk to people in Britain remains low. No details were provided on symptoms, exposure source, or travel history, and no additional British cases were indicated. The report confirms a single confirmed case among Britons abroad, with authorities monitoring potential contacts and advising standard precautions for travellers. No UK-wide public health measures were announced, and Britain's overall risk level is described as low despite Ebola activity in the DRC.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,不明,感染はDRC国内で発生しており、英国は感染者の国籍国にすぎないため、英国は対象国リストに含まれず除外。症状・曝露経路・渡航歴等の詳細情報が不足しており、続報の確認が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9leHRyYS5nbG9iby5jb20vYmxvZ3MvYWdpdG8vcG9zdC8yMDI2LzExL21pbmlzdGVyaW8tZGEtc2F1ZGUtcmVmb3JjYXJhLXZhY2luYWNhby1jb250cmEtbXBveC1uby1yaW8tZGUtamFuZWlyby1hcG9zLWF1bWVudG8tZGUtaW5mZWNjb2VzLmdodG1s,PICKUP,リオデジャネイロ州でMpox症例が前年比約126%増加し、2026年10月は2022年以来最多の月間症例数を記録。保健省がワクチン供給強化で対応しており、WPRO基準（異常な増加、継続的曝露、流行しやすさ）に複数該当し、行政・社会的関心も高いためPICKUPと判断。,Mpox; HIV,Rio de Janeiro; Rio de Janeiro; Federative Republic of Brazil,Ministry of Health will boost Mpox vaccination in Rio de Janeiro after an increase in infections.,Ministério da Saúde reforçará vacinação contra Mpox no Rio de Janeiro após aumento de infecções,2026-11-04T20:49:01+00:00,https://extra.globo.com/blogs/agito/post/2026/11/ministerio-da-saude-reforcara-vacinacao-contra-mpox-no-rio-de-janeiro-apos-aumento-de-infeccoes.ghtml,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Mpox vaccination in Rio de Janeiro state will be strengthened as infections rise, with increased vaccine stocks to boost year-end response, especially in the capital. In 2026, 953 doses have been administered in Rio de Janeiro. The vaccine is given in two doses, 28 days apart, prioritizing laboratory workers handling Orthopoxviruses, people living with HIV/AIDS with immunosuppression, and medium/high-risk direct contacts of suspected or confirmed Mpox cases after surveillance; surplus doses may cover PrEP users. Brazil has 665 mpox cases through October, with Rio de Janeiro accounting for 218 (about one‑third). Although below 2022’s peak (10,821 globally; RJ fell 84.2% since 2022), RJ reached 269 cases in 2026, up ~126% from 119 in 2025. In Rio de Janeiro city, October closed with 55 cases, the highest monthly total since October 2022; September had 47, August 13. Ongoing vigilance, diagnosis, and vaccination are needed.",No,Yes,不明,No,1,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,No,3,Yes,Yes,不明,2022年のピーク時と比べると症例数は依然低いが、2025年比で大幅増加しており、リオデジャネイロ市では2022年10月以来最多の月間症例数を記録。HIV陽性者など免疫抑制状態の高リスク群へのワクチン優先接種が実施されている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hYzI0aG9yYXMuY29tLzIwMjYvMTEvMDQvc2VtLXJlZ2lzdHJvLWRhLWRvZW5jYS1kZS1uZXdjYXN0bGUtbm8tYWNyZS1pZGFmLW1hbnRlbS12aWdpbGFuY2lhLWFwb3Mtbm92by1mb2NvLWVtLXNhbnRhLWNhdGFyaW5hLw==,DISMISS,家きんのニューカッスル病に関する動物衛生サーベイランスの報告であり、ヒトへの感染や公衆衛生上の深刻な影響は確認されていない。,Human Infection with Avian Influenza; Newcastle Disease; Avian Influenza,Santa Catarina; Federative Republic of Brazil,"No record of Newcastle disease in Acre, Idaf maintains surveillance after a new outbreak in Santa Catarina.","Sem registro da doença de Newcastle no Acre, Idaf mantém vigilância após novo foco em Santa Catarina",2026-11-04T20:48:51+00:00,https://ac24horas.com/2026/11/04/sem-registro-da-doenca-de-newcastle-no-acre-idaf-mantem-vigilancia-apos-novo-foco-em-santa-catarina/,PORTUGUESE,animals,"Newcastle disease is not recorded in Acre, Brazil, as Idaf maintains surveillance after a new outbreak in Santa Catarina. MAPA reported the Santa Catarina case on November 3 at Nova Erechim—the fourth outbreak since a zoosanitary emergency was declared. Idaf, through the Avian Health Program led by Everton Arruda, monitors farms to prevent entry into Acre by integrating with the national program. A new monitoring phase runs through June 2027; October’s phase yielded negative results for Newcastle disease and avian influenza. In Acre, blood serum and cloacal and tracheal swabs detect active infection and past exposure. Newcastle disease is highly contagious, affecting over 200 bird species, with signs such as sneezing, labored breathing, loss of appetite, greenish diarrhea, drooped wings, ataxia, and twisted head/neck. Producers should report suspicious mortality to Idaf.",No,No,No,不明,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,本記事はブラジル国内の家きん（鳥類）疾病であるニューカッスル病に関する動物衛生当局（Idaf/MAPA）のルーティン監視報告であり、ヒト感染例の報告はない。鳥インフルエンザも検査対象だが陰性。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9jbmEub3JnLmN5L2FydGljbGUvMTExNDMxNzQ=,PICKUP,WHOが報告する大規模なコレラ流行（死者1800人、症例6万人超）がエボラ流行と同時進行しており、公衆衛生への深刻な影響と国際的拡大リスクが認められるためフルRRAへ進むべきと判断した。,Cholera; Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,"1,800 dead from a cholera outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo in 2026, says the WHO.","Στους 1.800 οι νεκροί από επιδημία χολέρας στη Λ.Δ. Κονγκό το 2026, λέει ο ΠΟΥ",2026-11-04T21:01:13+00:00,https://cna.org.cy/article/11143174,GREEK,humans; environment,"Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), already grappling with an Ebola outbreak, is also experiencing a severe cholera surge in 2026, with the World Health Organization reporting about 1,800 cholera deaths and more than 60,000 confirmed cases. The simultaneous outbreaks highlight the country’s ongoing public health challenges and strain on healthcare infrastructure. The cholera figures reflect transmission across the year, though the report does not provide regional breakdowns or transmission sources. The figures underscore the urgency of strengthened surveillance, case management, and public health interventions to curb transmission while the Ebola situation persists.",Yes,No,Yes,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,エボラとコレラの同時流行により医療インフラへの負荷が高まっている。地域別内訳や感染源は不明。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucHVsem8uY29tL211bmRvL251ZXZvLXJlcXVpc2l0by1zYW5pdGFyaW8tcGFyYS12aWFqYXItYS1lc3RhZG9zLXVuaWRvcy1kZWNsYXJhY2lvbi1qdXJhZGEtcG9yLWVib2xhLVBQNTM0ODU0MEE=,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ出血熱流行を受け、米国が渡航者に健康宣誓書提出を義務付けるという具体的な渡航制限措置が実施されており、IHR基準の複数（深刻性・異常性・国際的拡大・渡航制限）に該当する。,Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States,Passengers bound for or with a layover in the United States must present a new health declaration in response to the Ebola outbreak in Africa.,Pasajeros con destino o escala en EE.UU. deben presentar nueva declaración jurada sanitaria ante brote de ébola en África,2026-11-04T21:16:41+00:00,https://www.pulzo.com/mundo/nuevo-requisito-sanitario-para-viajar-a-estados-unidos-declaracion-jurada-por-ebola-PP5348540A,SPANISH,humans,"Passenger travel to the United States or through US airports requires a free online health declaration starting November 3 due to an Ebola outbreak in Africa. Travelers must declare under oath that they have not been in the Democratic Republic of the Congo within the past 21 days. Submissions are via official airline portals, yielding a digital certificate for mobile or printed presentation at the airport. For minors, guardians complete the form. The declaration supplements, not replaces, standard immigration requirements (passport, visa, travel authorization). Travelers should complete it well before departure to avoid delays and avoid unofficial intermediaries charging fees. Applies to those headed to the United States and those merely transiting through US airports. Source cited: Noticiero 90 Minutos.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,不明,記事はDRCでのエボラ発生そのものではなく、米国が導入した渡航関連の健康宣誓書義務化措置について報じている。発生地域にUnited Statesが含まれるが対象国リストには該当せず、また記事の主題は渡航制限措置でありDRCでの流行状況の詳細（症例数等）は本文に記載がない。フルRRAでDRCでの流行状況の最新情報を確認する必要がある。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9kZXN0YWtqb3JuYWwuY29tLmJyL3BhbGVzdHJhLW9yaWVudGF0aXZhLXNvYnJlLXByZXZlbmNhby1kby1jYXJidW5jdWxvLXNpbnRvbWF0aWNvLXBhcmEtcHJvZHV0b3Jlcy1ydXJhaXMv,DISMISS,これは牛の気腫疽（Clostridium chauvoei）に関する予防啓発講演の記事であり、疾患名がAnthraxとタグ付けされているが実際はヒトの炭疽ではなく家畜の気腫疽であり、ヒトへの公衆衛生リスクや感染拡大の兆候はない。,Anthrax,,Informative lecture on preventing symptomatic anthrax for rural producers.,Palestra orientativa sobre prevenção do carbúnculo sintomático para produtores rurais,2026-11-04T21:17:33+00:00,https://destakjornal.com.br/palestra-orientativa-sobre-prevencao-do-carbunculo-sintomatico-para-produtores-rurais/,PORTUGUESE,environment; animals,"Symptomatic blackleg (Clostridium chauvoei) in cattle was the focus of a 20 October preventive briefing in Mogi das Cruzes, Brazil, organized by the Municipal Secretariat of Agriculture and Food Security with students from Centro Universitário Braz Cubas. The session highlighted rapid disease progression and high mortality, listing signs such as muscular swelling (especially in the thighs and neck), high fever, depression, lethargy, and crepitation from gas in tissues, with death typically within 12–48 hours of onset. Producers were warned not to confuse symptomatic blackleg with anthrax (carbúnculo hemático) and to avoid carcass necropsy to prevent environmental and human contamination by spores. Preventive measures emphasized include strict vaccination schedules, proper carcass disposal per sanitary and environmental norms, and ongoing herd biosafety and surveillance. If signs appear, immediate veterinary evaluation is essential.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,No,No,0,No,No,No,記事は家畜の気腫疽（symptomatic blackleg）に関する予防啓発講演であり、炭疽（anthrax）とは明確に区別されている。ヒトへの健康被害の記載なし。Bluedotの疾患タグ付けが誤っている可能性が高い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudnZhbGUuY29tLmJyL3NhdWRlL3ZpZ2lsYW5jaWEtc2FuaXRhcmlhLW9yaWVudGEtcG9wdWxhY2FvLXNvYnJlLW1hY2Fjb3MtbW9ydG9zLWVtLXNhby1tYXRldXMtZG8tc3VsLw==,WATCH,黄熱ウイルス circulation の指標となる死亡サルの報告があり、ヒト感染の可能性を監視する段階だが、現時点でヒト感染例は確認されていないため経過観察とする。,Yellow Fever,Paraná; Federative Republic of Brazil,Sanitary Surveillance advises the public about dead monkeys in São Mateus do Sul | Portal Vvale,Vigilância Sanitária orienta população sobre macacos mortos em São Mateus do Sul | Portal Vvale,2026-11-04T12:35:51+00:00,https://www.vvale.com.br/saude/vigilancia-sanitaria-orienta-populacao-sobre-macacos-mortos-em-sao-mateus-do-sul/,PORTUGUESE,humans; vectors; animals,"On 2026-11-04, Sanitary Surveillance in São Mateus do Sul, southern Paraná, Brazil, issued an alert after reports of dead monkeys. Residents should not touch or remove the carcasses and must immediately report the exact location to the Sanitary Surveillance, which provides two phone numbers for reporting. Prompt notification enables epidemiological investigation and monitoring. The appearance of dead monkeys can signal possible circulation of the yellow fever virus, as non-human primates are affected and serve as surveillance indicators; human transmission occurs via mosquito bites, not direct contact. Do not handle, bury, or relocate the animals and await guidance from health professionals. As of this notice, there are no confirmed yellow fever cases linked to the alert.",No,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,不明,2,Yes,Yes,No,ヒト感染例は未確認。動物（サル）における黄熱ウイルス循環の兆候として地元衛生当局が監視を強化している段階。続報でヒト症例の有無を確認する必要あり。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hdGFyZGUuY29tLmJyL3NhdWRlL2JyYXNpbC1wb2RlLWVuZnJlbnRhci1ub3ZhLWFsdGEtZGEtZGVuZ3VlLWVtLTIwMjctdmVqYS1wcmV2aXNhby0xNDA4MzQz,WATCH,2027年の将来予測に関する記事であり、現時点での急性のアウトブレイクではないが、デング熱・チクングニア熱の流行拡大リスクが指摘されているため経過観察とする。,Chikungunya; Dengue,Pará; Federative Republic of Brazil,Brazil may face a new dengue surge in 2027; see forecast.,Brasil pode enfrentar nova alta da dengue em 2027; veja previsão,2026-11-04T21:19:49+00:00,https://atarde.com.br/saude/brasil-pode-enfrentar-nova-alta-da-dengue-em-2027-veja-previsao-1408343,PORTUGUESE,humans; vectors; environment,"Brazil may see a 20-40% rise in dengue cases in 2027 due to El Niño impacts and ongoing dengue transmission, with chikungunya risk rising as well. Health Minister Alexandre Padilha said intensity will vary by region, likely higher in drier areas such as the semiarid interior and the Amazon. The forecast incorporates El Niño effects and the dengue serotype dynamics after a two-year decline left more people susceptible. Fiocruz projects about 1.5 million probable dengue cases in 2027, near 2025's 1.66 million, though the initial estimate did not include El Niño. Since January, Brazil has logged 489,197 probable dengue cases, per the Ministry of Health dashboard. The outlook signals broader arboviral risk across the country.",不明,No,No,No,0,No,不明,Yes,Yes,不明,2,不明,Yes,不明,本記事は将来予測（2027年）に関する内容であり、現在進行中の緊急事態ではない。デング熱は毎年流行する風土病的性格が強く、IHR基準の「異常性」は低いと判断した。保健省やFiocruzによる公式予測であり、政府の関心は高いと考えられる。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubGVtb25kZS5mci9hZnJpcXVlL2FydGljbGUvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC9lbi1yZGMtbC1vbXMtYWxlcnRlLXN1ci1sYS1waXJlLWVwaWRlbWllLWRlLWNob2xlcmEtZGVwdWlzLWRlcy1kZWNlbm5pZXMtYXZlYy0xLTgwMC1tb3J0cy1zdXItZm9uZC1kZS1jcmlzZS1saWVlLWEtZWJvbGFfNjgwNjQzMl8zMjEyLmg=,PICKUP,"コレラとエボラの同時流行で死者数が極めて多く（コレラ1,800人、エボラ5,300人超）、IHR基準の複数（深刻な公衆衛生影響、異常性、国際拡大リスク）に該当するため、フルRRAへ進むべきシグナルと判断。",Cholera; Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,"In the DRC, the WHO warns of the ""worst cholera outbreak in decades,"" with 1,800 deaths, amid an Ebola-related crisis.","En RDC, l'OMS alerte sur la "" pire épidémie de choléra depuis des décennies "", avec 1 800 morts, sur fond de crise liée à Ebola",2026-11-04T21:17:39+00:00,https://www.lemonde.fr/afrique/article/2026/11/04/en-rdc-l-oms-alerte-sur-la-pire-epidemie-de-cholera-depuis-des-decennies-avec-1-800-morts-sur-fond-de-crise-liee-a-ebola_6806432_3212.html,FRENCH,humans; environment,"As of November 4, 2026, the World Health Organization warns that the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) is experiencing its worst cholera outbreak in decades, with more than 60,000 cases and 1,800 related deaths reported since the start of the year. The cholera surge unfolds amid an Ebola-related crisis in the DRC, where Ebola has claimed over 5,300 lives in about five months. The convergence of these outbreaks highlights a severe public health emergency in the country. The figures cited reflect ongoing transmission for both diseases, underscoring the challenge of outbreak control in a setting already affected by multiple concurrent health threats.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,コレラとエボラの複合アウトブレイクであり、WHOが公式に警告を発している点から社会的・国際的関心が極めて高い。二つの感染症が同時に拡大している点で医療システムへの負荷が懸念される。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hY3AuY2QvcHJvdmluY2UvaXR1cmktYXJyaXZlZS1kdW4tbGFib3JhdG9pcmUtbW9iaWxlLXBvdXItcmVuZm9yY2VyLWxhLXJpcG9zdGUtY29udHJlLWVib2xhLWEtYnVuaWEv,PICKUP,"DRCで継続中のエボラ出血熱アウトブレイクが大規模（累計7,412例、死亡3,483例）であり、国際支援（ベルギー・EU）を伴う対応強化が行われている重大な公衆衛生事案であるため。",Ebola,Ituri; Bunia; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Kingdom of Belgium,Ituri: Arrival of a mobile laboratory to bolster the Ebola response in Bunia - ACP,Ituri : arrivée d'un laboratoire mobile pour renforcer la riposte contre Ebola à Bunia - ACP,2026-11-04T21:26:09+00:00,https://acp.cd/province/ituri-arrivee-dun-laboratoire-mobile-pour-renforcer-la-riposte-contre-ebola-a-bunia/,FRENCH,humans,"A mobile Ebola laboratory, deployed with support from Belgium and the European Union, arrived in Bunia, Ituri province, in northeastern Democratic Republic of Congo, to bolster the Ebola virus disease (EVD) response. The unit will strengthen diagnostic and laboratory operations, with the Institut National de Recherche Biomédicale (INRB) prepared to deploy the equipment in field activities. Ituri remains the outbreak’s most affected province. An INSP situation report dated 2 November (data through 31 October 2026) records 7,412 confirmed EVD cases and 3,483 deaths since the start of the epidemic, with 32 new cases in the last 24 hours. In Bunia Health Zone, the 20 October epidemiological bulletin lists 1,914 confirmed cases and 643 deaths. The development underscores the ongoing transmission and the need for enhanced diagnostics and surveillance.",Yes,No,Yes,不明,2,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,既知の継続的アウトブレイクであり新規発生ではないが、感染者・死亡者数が多く、国際的な診断・サーベイランス支援が行われている点でリスク評価継続が妥当。ベルギーは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9tYWxldml6aW90aXMuZ3IvMjAyNi8xMS8wNC8xLTgwMC1uZWtyb2ktYXBvLWNob2xlcmEta2FpLXBhbm8tYXBvLTYwLTAwMC1rcm91c21hdGEv,PICKUP,コレラとエボラの二重アウトブレイクがDRCで大規模な公衆衛生危機を引き起こしており、死亡者数・症例数が極めて多く、国際的拡大や渡航制限のリスクも懸念されるためフルRRAへ進めるべきと判断。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"1,800 deaths from cholera and more than 60,000 cases.",1.800 νεκροί από χολέρα και πάνω από 60.000 κρούσματα,2026-11-04T21:39:02+00:00,https://maleviziotis.gr/2026/11/04/1-800-nekroi-apo-cholera-kai-pano-apo-60-000-krousmata/,GREEK,humans; environment,"Cholera outbreak drives a severe health crisis in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) alongside an Ebola surge. Since the start of 2026, cholera has surpassed 60,000 cases with at least 1,800 deaths, described by WHO as the worst cholera year in decades. In the same period, the Ebola outbreak has produced more than 10,400 cases and over 5,300 deaths in five months. The Eastern provinces of North Kivu and South Kivu bear the highest cholera burden, with cases also emerging along the Congo River basin, raising concerns of westward spread toward Kinshasa. Difficulties include remote geography, limited health worker access, and ongoing armed conflict that hamper response, with the rainy season potentially accelerating transmission. WHO urges intensified health interventions and vaccination campaigns, particularly in the eastern provinces, as the country confronts two major outbreaks simultaneously.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,WHOが数十年で最悪のコレラ流行年と表現し、同時にエボラも大規模発生中。武力紛争・雨季・医療アクセス制限が対応を困難にしており、国際的支援ニーズが高い。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9lbmdsaXNoLmFqZWwuc2EvbGlmZXN0eWxlL21hbGdqZGw3dQ==,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で継続中のブンディブギョ・エボラウイルス流行に対し、WHOが新たなワクチンを臨床試験に追加しており、Ebolaは常に重篤な公衆衛生上の脅威であるためフルリスク評価が妥当。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,WHO adds two new vaccines to Ebola trials in DR Congo,2026-11-04T20:52:11+00:00,https://english.ajel.sa/lifestyle/malgjdl7u,ENGLISH,humans,"Two vaccines developed by the University of Oxford, in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India and Moderna, were added by the World Health Organization to ongoing clinical trials in the Democratic Republic of Congo to combat the Bundibugyo Ebola outbreak. These are the first vaccines specifically designed to target Bundibugyo ebolavirus. The addition expands trial options in DR Congo as part of outbreak containment efforts, with no case or death counts provided in the article. The multi-institution collaboration highlights an international effort to advance targeted immunization against the Bundibugyo virus during the DR Congo outbreak as of 2026-11-04.",Yes,No,不明,不明,1,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドと英国はワクチン開発機関（Serum Institute of India、University of Oxford）の所在地として言及されているが、実際のエボラ流行発生地ではないためverified_locationsから除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9lbmdsaXNoLmFqZWwuc2Evd29ybGQvd3QxdG1hMGF4,PICKUP,エボラ出血熱は致死率が高く国際的拡大リスクのある疾患であり、英国人感染者の発生はIHR基準上複数該当し得るためフルRRAへの移行が妥当。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,UK citizen in DR Congo tests positive for Ebola,2026-11-04T20:46:11+00:00,https://english.ajel.sa/world/wt1tma0ax,ENGLISH,humans,"Laboratory-confirmed Ebola infection detected in a British national currently in the Democratic Republic of Congo. The individual tested positive for Ebola while in DR Congo, and officials stressed that the risk to people in the United Kingdom remains low. A British government spokesperson said on Wednesday that a British national in the Democratic Republic of Congo has tested positive for Ebola, reiterating that the UK-facing risk is low. No additional information on symptoms, exposure history, or patient condition was disclosed in the briefing. The report highlights that the confirmed case is located in DR Congo, with no indication of further cases or transmission in the UK at this time.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,不明,不明,Yes,不明,2,Yes,Yes,不明,英国は対象国リストに含まれないため除外。症状・曝露歴・患者状態等の詳細情報は不明であり、続報の確認が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY2ljN25vdGljaWFzLmNvbS9icmFzaWwvcmlvLWNvbmZpcm1hLTI2OS1jYXNvcy1tcG94LTIwMjYv,WATCH,mpox症例が前年比で大幅増加しているが死亡例はなく、ブラジル国内での既知流行の継続報告であり国際的な異常事態とは言えないため、経過観察とする。,Mpox; HIV,Rio de Janeiro; Rio de Janeiro,State of Rio de Janeiro confirms 269 mpox cases in 2026; in the same period in 2025 there were 92 - CIC7 News.,Estado do Rio confirma 269 casos de mpox em 2026; no mesmo período de 2025 foram 92 - CIC7 Notícias,2026-11-04T21:53:48+00:00,https://www.cic7noticias.com/brasil/rio-confirma-269-casos-mpox-2026/,PORTUGUESE,humans,"As of November 3, 2026, the state of Rio de Janeiro confirmed 269 mpox cases, with no deaths, per SES-RJ. For the same period in 2025 there were 92 cases; nationwide Brazil totals 665 mpox cases in 2026. Vaccines: SES-RJ expects stock reinforcement, especially toward year-end when activity increases. Panel data from Rede Nacional de Dados em Saúde shows the state administered 953 doses through November 2. The vaccination regimen is two doses, spaced 28 days apart. Priority groups include laboratory workers handling orthopoxviruses, people living with HIV/AIDS with immunosuppression, and direct medium- or high-risk contacts of a suspected or confirmed case after health surveillance assessment. Mpox is a viral illness causing skin eruptions and lesions. Prevention emphasizes avoiding close contact with symptomatic individuals, avoiding intimate contact during symptoms, and not sharing personal items; individuals with suspicious lesions should seek health care. The page remains open for clarifications and updates.",No,No,No,No,0,Yes,No,Yes,Yes,No,3,不明,Yes,No,ブラジルは対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations は空配列。症例数が前年比約3倍に増加しており、ワクチン供給体制強化の動きがあるため継続的な注視が望ましい。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9mci5xei5jb20vb21zLXNpZ25hbGUtY2hvbGVyYS1yZGMtNjAwMDAtY2FzLTE4MDAtZGVjZXMtMTEwNDI2,PICKUP,IHR基準4項目中3項目に該当し、WHO事務局長が『数十年で最悪』と表明するなど社会的関心も高く、エボラ流行と重なる複合的公衆衛生危機であるためフルRRAへ進むべき。,Cholera; Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,"WHO reports 1,800 cholera deaths in the DRC this year.",L'OMS signale 1 800 décès dus au choléra en RDC cette année,2026-11-04T21:46:11+00:00,https://fr.qz.com/oms-signale-cholera-rdc-60000-cas-1800-deces-110426,FRENCH,humans; environment,"On November 4, 2026, the World Health Organization reported over 60,000 cholera cases and 1,800 deaths in the Democratic Republic of Congo since January, with a case fatality rate around 3%, and cases spreading along the Congo River in conflict-affected, hard-to-reach areas. Tedros Ghebreyesus called it the worst cholera outbreak in decades, amid a concurrent Ebola epidemic that has caused more than 5,300 deaths in five months. Although 2025 recorded the highest case counts in over 25 years, 2026 is expected to be even worse. Emphasis on vaccination campaigns, especially in eastern DRC, is highlighted. The International Vaccine Coordination Group, including WHO and UNICEF, approved 7.4 million doses for 2026 with funding from GAVI; a new request is under review.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"同国内で同時進行中のエボラ流行（5カ月で5,300人以上死亡）も報告されており、複合的な公衆衛生危機として注視が必要。コレラはコンゴ川沿いの紛争影響地域・アクセス困難地域で拡大中。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZGlhcmlvZGFhbWF6b25pYS5jb20uYnIvbm90aWNpYS8yLzQ1NDA1NS8=,WATCH,コンゴ民主共和国のヴィルンガ国立公園でカバの炭疽死が確認されているが、現時点でヒト感染例はなく、情報が限定的なため続報を注視する必要がある。,Cholera; Anthrax; Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Uganda,Anthrax kills 30 hippos and raises alarm in an African country.,Antraz provoca morte de 30 hipopótamos e acende alerta em país africano,2026-11-04T17:49:00+00:00,https://www.diariodaamazonia.com.br/noticia/2/454055/,PORTUGUESE,animals; humans; environment,"Anthrax outbreak kills at least 30 hippos in Virunga National Park, eastern Democratic Republic of Congo, over the past month; first carcasses were found in September and labs confirmed Bacillus anthracis. No human infections are confirmed to date, but transmission risk exists via contact with infected animals or consumption of contaminated meat. Park authorities are intensifying surveillance and ensuring safe handling and disposal of carcasses; no new wildlife deaths reported in the past two weeks. The DRC continues to face other health crises, including Ebola and cholera, amid a humanitarian emergency from armed conflict. Anthrax spores persist in soil, posing ongoing risk to wildlife and people who handle carcasses. In March 2025, a separate outbreak killed about 65 hippos in the country; Uganda reported 15 human cases and two deaths. Emphasize continued monitoring and prompt antibiotic treatment if suspected.",No,不明,不明,No,0,不明,No,Yes,Yes,Yes,3,不明,不明,不明,記事はウガンダでの2025年3月の過去事例（ヒト感染15例、死亡2例）にも言及しているが、現在進行中の発生はDRCのヴィルンガ国立公園に限定されており、ヒトへの感染は未確認。DRCは既にエボラ・コレラ等の公衆衛生危機を抱えており、炭疽菌の土壌残存による長期的リスクが懸念される。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYnRhLmJnL2JnL25ld3Mvd29ybGQvMTI0MDI4MC1icml0YW5za2ktZ3JhemhkYW5pbi1kYWwtcG9sb3poaXRlbG5hLXByb2JhLXphLWVib2xhLXNodGUtYmFkZS12YXJuYXQtb3QtZHIta28=,PICKUP,"DRコンゴでのエボラ大規模流行（死者5,000人超）に加え、国際的な患者移送（英国への帰還）が発生しており、国際的拡大リスクと渡航制限の可能性がある重大事案。",Ebola,Republic of Sierra Leone; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Liberia; Republic of Guinea; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,"A British citizen who tested positive for Ebola will be repatriated from DR Congo to the United Kingdom, where he will be treated.","Британски гражданин, дал положителна проба за ебола, ще бъде върнат от ДР Конго във Великобритания, където ще бъде лекуван",2026-11-04T21:46:40+00:00,https://www.bta.bg/bg/news/world/1240280-britanski-grazhdanin-dal-polozhitelna-proba-za-ebola-shte-bade-varnat-ot-dr-ko,BULGARIAN,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo: a British citizen in DR Congo has tested positive for Ebola and will be repatriated to the United Kingdom for treatment. Government data indicate the DR Congo outbreak has killed more than 5,000 people. The patient will be evacuated for medical reasons and transported back to the UK; flight timing is not yet clear. UK officials say established procedures for handling such cases are in place, and the risk to the UK population remains low. To date, the UK has four confirmed Ebola cases, including three healthcare workers who treated patients during the 2014-2015 West Africa outbreak. The current outbreak in DR Congo is the second-largest in global history, surpassed only by the 2014-2016 West Africa epidemic that infected over 28,600 people and caused more than 11,000 deaths, with affected countries Guinea, Liberia, and Sierra Leone.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,シエラレオネ・リベリア・ギニア・英国は2014-2016年流行の歴史的言及であり、現行の発生国はDRCのみ。英国は患者移送先であり発生国ではないため対象国リストに含めない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9zcHJhdnkucG96cmkuc2svY2xhbm9rL2RvLWJvamEtcy1lYm9sb3UtcHJpYnVkbnUtZHZlLW5vdmUtdmFrY2lueS1lcGlkZW1pYS1tYS11ei12eXNlLTUtMzAwLW9iZXRpLW96bmFtaWxhLXdoby8xNjE1OTAw,PICKUP,"DRCでのエボラ（ブンディブギョ株）流行が致死率50%超・死者5,300人超と深刻化しており、IHR基準の複数項目に該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Africa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"Two new vaccines join the fight against Ebola; the Ebola epidemic has more than 5,300 victims, announced by WHO.","Do boja s ebolou pribudnú dve nové vakcíny, epidémia má už vyše 5 300 obetí, oznámila WHO",2026-11-04T21:47:11+00:00,https://spravy.pozri.sk/clanok/do-boja-s-ebolou-pribudnu-dve-nove-vakciny-epidemia-ma-uz-vyse-5-300-obeti-oznamila-who/1615900,SLOVAK,humans,"Two new Ebola vaccines targeting the Bundibugyo strain join the fight as the outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo continues. The World Health Organization expanded clinical trials on two experimental vaccines, ChAdOx1 BDBV (Oxford University and Serum Institute of India) and Moderna’s mRNA-1469, aimed specifically at Bundibugyo, as Ervebo’s vaccine—already approved for Ebola generally—has not yet proven efficacy against this strain. Trials are led by the Democratic Republic of the Congo National Institute for Biomedical Research with WHO backing. Africa CDC counts 10,444 confirmed cases across Africa, with more than 5,300 deaths, a case-fatality rate above 50%, concentrated mainly in the DRC. There is no approved vaccine or specific treatment for Bundibugyo yet. Authorities emphasize vaccines alongside essential public health measures: prompt healthcare, contact tracing, isolation, safe burials, and community engagement, to curb further spread.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"インドはSerum Institute of Indiaがワクチン開発に関与している文脈で言及されているのみで、インド国内での発生ではないためverified_locationsから除外した。致死率50%超のブンディブギョ株という通常と異なる株での大規模流行であり、Africa CDC全体で10,444症例・5,300人超の死亡が報告されている点で極めて深刻。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93eWRhcnplbmlhLmludGVyaWEucGwvemFncmFuaWNhL25ld3MtZHJrLXptYWdhLXNpZS16LWVwaWRlbWlhLXdoby1hbGFybXVqZS1uYWpnb3JzemEtb2QtZHppZXNpZWNpLG5JZCwyMzU2OTExNg==,PICKUP,WHOが「数十年で最悪」と警告する大規模コレラ流行（患者約6万人、死者約1800人、致死率約3%）であり、紛争地域での対応困難さや首都キンシャサへの拡大懸念があるため、フルリスク評価が必要と判断した。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,DRK grapples with a cholera epidemic. WHO warns: The worst in decades.,DRK zmaga się z epidemią cholery. WHO alarmuje: Najgorsza od dziesięcioleci,2026-11-04T22:08:54+00:00,"https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/zagranica/news-drk-zmaga-sie-z-epidemia-who-alarmuje-najgorsza-od-dziesieci,nId,23569116",POLISH,humans; environment,"DR Congo is experiencing about 60,000 cholera cases this year with roughly 1,800 deaths, marking the worst cholera outbreak in decades per the World Health Organization. Most infections are in the eastern provinces of North Kivu and South Kivu, areas affected by conflict and partially under influence of the M23 militia. There is concern that cholera could spread along the Congo River basin to Kinshasa, the capital. Cholera is waterborne, and the ongoing rainy season may worsen transmission, while hard-to-reach, conflict-affected regions hinder response. The case fatality rate is around 3%. WHO notes that alongside the ongoing Ebola epidemic, the campaign to vaccinate against Ebola will be very important for addressing cholera as well.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はコレラ流行に焦点を当てているが、同時進行中のエボラ流行とのワクチン接種キャンペーンの連携についても言及されている。国際的な越境拡大の明示的記述はないため international_spread は不明と評価した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9uZXdzLmNoaW5hLmNvbS5hdS81Njc3NDkuaHRtbA==,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国で1万人超の感染者・5000人超の死者を出す過去最大規模かつ最も致死的なエボラ流行が発生しており、英国人患者の国際搬送や複数国での症例報告など国際的拡大のリスクが明白であるため。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,A British man infected with the Ebola virus will be airlifted from the Democratic Republic of the Congo back to the United Kingdom,一名感染埃博拉病毒的英国男子将从刚果民主共和国被空运回英国Australia ChinaTown News 中文华人新闻 - NEWS.CHINA.COM.AU 这里是生活在墨尔本咱自家人的地盘！把客场当主场，视异乡为故园。澳洲唐人街 - 中华澳网 China Town News澳洲唐人街;澳大利亚华人社区和主流新闻媒体,2026-11-04T22:01:47+00:00,https://news.china.com.au/567749.html,CHINESE,humans,"A British man infected with Ebola is being airlifted from the Democratic Republic of the Congo to the United Kingdom, the first diagnosed case in the current outbreak in Britain. The patient, a healthcare worker, highlights a DRC crisis centered on Bundibugyo virus, with over 10,000 confirmed cases and more than 5,000 deaths since May, making it the second-largest Ebola outbreak and the deadliest in DRC history, with a 48.6% fatality rate last month. Ebola spreads via infected body fluids and can progress from vomiting and diarrhea to organ failure and internal bleeding. No approved vaccine exists; two candidates are in trials—Oxford University/Serum Institute of India and Moderna—pending approval by DRC authorities to test against Bundibugyo virus. Kenya, Nigeria, and Uganda have also reported cases. The UK says public risk remains low; flight timing is unclear, but procedures are in place.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドはワクチン開発パートナー（Serum Institute of India）として言及されているのみで、実際の発生国ではないためverified_locationsから除外。ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダ・英国は対象国リストに含まれないため除外。,
