aHR0cHM6Ly9zYW5hLnN5L2hlYWx0aC8yNjI2NDQ0Lw==,PICKUP,"DRCでコレラによる死者1,800人・症例6万人に加え、同時進行するエボラ流行、武力紛争による対応阻害、WHOによる国際協調の呼びかけがあり、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルRRAへ進むべき。",Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"WHO: Cholera claims 1,800 lives in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.",الصحة العالمية: الكوليرا تودي بحياة 1800 شخص في الكونغو الديمقراطية‏,2026-11-04T22:50:14+00:00,https://sana.sy/health/2626444/,ARABIC,humans; environment,"As of 2026-11-05, the World Health Organization reports about 1,800 cholera deaths and 60,000 cases in the Democratic Republic of the Congo this year, amid a concurrent Ebola outbreak. Most cholera cases are centered in the eastern provinces of North Kivu and South Kivu along the Congo River basin, raising concerns that transmission could reach Kinshasa. Ongoing violence and armed groups hinder access and response efforts to both diseases. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus urged rapid deployment of vaccination campaigns, especially Ebola vaccines, in the war-affected eastern regions to curb spread and ease pressure on the health system. He also reiterated calls to finalize the international pandemic accord and strengthen cross-border cooperation to confront health threats that cross borders.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,コレラとエボラの同時流行、紛争地域での対応困難、キンシャサへの拡大懸念、WHO事務局長によるパンデミック条約早期妥結の呼びかけなど、国際的関心が高い事案。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9zYWJxLm9yZy9hcnRpY2xlLzIydm4yMjk=,PICKUP,DRCでコレラが過去数十年で最大規模の流行となり1800人死亡、致死率約3%と高く、同時にエボラ最悪流行も進行中で首都キンシャサへの拡大リスクがあるため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当し国際的関心も高い。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"Cholera claims 1,800 lives in Congo, and 60,000 cases warn of the epidemic spreading to the capital.",الكوليرا تفتك بـ1800 شخص في الكونغو.. و60 ألف إصابة تنذر بانتشار الوباء للعاصمة,2026-11-04T22:46:00+00:00,https://sabq.org/article/22vn229,ARABIC,humans; environment,"On 4 November 2026, the World Health Organization warned that cholera in the Democratic Republic of the Congo is worsening amid the worst Ebola outbreak in its history. Since the start of the year, cholera has claimed 1,800 lives and caused about 60,000 infections, the largest outbreak in decades. Most cases are in North Kivu and South Kivu in the eastern region, including areas within the Congo River Basin, raising the risk of spread toward Kinshasa, the capital. Regions already burdened by Ebola are also vulnerable to widespread cholera; the upcoming rainy season could accelerate transmission through contaminated water. The case fatality rate is around 3%, notably high for cholera. The report underscores concurrent public health crises in the DRC and the potential for rapid spread if the outbreak is not contained.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,WHOがコレラとエボラの同時流行を警告。雨季による感染拡大懸念あり。首都キンシャサへの拡大リスクが指摘されている。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZGdhYmMuY29tLmJyL05vdGljaWEvNDM2NjkwNy9tdW5pY2lwaW9zLWRhLXJlZ2lhby1zZS1tb2JpbGl6YW0tZW0tY2FtcGFuaGEtY29udHJhLW8tc2FyYW1wbw==,PICKUP,ブラジル・サンパウロ州ABC地域で麻疹の確定例・疑い例が複数報告されており、ワクチン接種キャンペーンなど行政の対応が進んでいるため、エピデミック傾向と行政の関心が高いと判断しPICKUPとする。,Measles,São Paulo; Diadema; São Paulo; Federative Republic of Brazil,Regional municipalities mobilize in a campaign against measles.,Municípios da região se mobilizam em campanha contra o sarampo,2026-11-04T19:38:00+00:00,https://www.dgabc.com.br/Noticia/4366907/municipios-da-regiao-se-mobilizam-em-campanha-contra-o-sarampo,PORTUGUESE,humans,"Measles outbreak response unfolds in the ABC region of São Paulo as cities join the Day S campaign on November 4, 2026. The region reports three confirmed cases this year—one in Santo André and two in São Bernardo do Campo—and statewide there are 41 cases; since 2026 began, 61 have been registered, with 60 discarded. In São Caetano do Sul two cases are under evaluation, and Diadema has one suspected case; notifications reach 60. São Bernardo held a training for 170 community health agents to reinforce vaccination, while Santo André’s health department conducts searches for symptomatic patients in communities and urgent care units. São Caetano broadened vaccine access in parks and extended Saturday hours at health units. Infectious disease expert Tânia Petraglia emphasizes measles’ high transmissibility, potentially infecting 90% of unvaccinated close contacts. Day S aims for early detection, training, and review of fever and rash records to interrupt transmission.",No,Yes,不明,No,1,Yes,No,不明,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,ブラジルは過去に麻疹排除認定を受けており、再流行は公衆衛生上の懸念材料となる可能性があるが、現時点では確定例・疑い例ともに少数で、重症例・死亡例の報告はない。続報でケース数の推移や感染拡大の有無を確認する必要がある。,
