aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudHZzbWFpcy5jb20uYnIvc3VwZXItZWwtbmluby1hdW1lbnRhLWFsZXJ0YS1wYXJhLWRlbmd1ZS1lbS1zb3JvY2FiYS8=,WATCH,デング熱はブラジルで季節的・地域的流行が継続しており驚異性は低いが、今後の気候要因による拡大予測があるため経過観察とする。,Zika; Chikungunya; Dengue,São Paulo; Jundiaí; Sorocaba; Itapetininga; São Paulo; Federative Republic of Brazil,Super El Niño Raises Dengue Fever Alert in Sorocaba | TVS+.,Super El Niño aumenta alerta para dengue em Sorocaba | TVS+,2026-11-04T22:47:24+00:00,https://www.tvsmais.com.br/super-el-nino-aumenta-alerta-para-dengue-em-sorocaba/,PORTUGUESE,environment; humans; vectors,"Super El Niño may intensify rainfall and heat, boosting Aedes aegypti, the dengue, Zika, and chikungunya vector, prompting a dengue alert in Sorocaba, Brazil. Zoonoses teams intensify home visits to remove breeding sites and educate residents. In Sorocaba, dengue cases fell from 14,130 (Jan–Oct 2025) to 81 (Jan–Oct 2026). No dengue deaths were recorded in 2026 in the city; teams conducted over 459,000 home visits in 2026. In the state of São Paulo, 60,965 cases and 43 deaths in 2026. InfoDengue/Fiocruz projects about 1.7 million dengue cases in Brazil in 2027. Vaccination with Qdenga is part of prevention strategies. Regionally, Jundiaí reported 505 cases (Jan–Sep 2026) vs 7,960 in 2025; Itapetininga had 10 cases in 2026 vs 406 in 2025. Authorities urge eliminating standing water and maintaining vigilance year-round; fever, headache, or body pains warrant medical care and avoiding self-medication.",No,No,No,No,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,No,Yes,No,記事は2026年の実績データとして、ソロカバ市および近隣地域でデング熱症例数が2025年比で大幅に減少していることを示している。ただしスーパーエルニーニョによる気候変動がAedes aegyptiの増殖を助長する可能性があり、2027年には全国で約170万症例が予測されている点は注視が必要。現時点で異常な重症化や国際的拡大の兆候はない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubXlqb3lvbmxpbmUuY29tL2JyaXRpc2gtbWFuLWluZmVjdGVkLXdpdGgtZWJvbGEtaW4tZHItY29uZ28tdG8tYmUtZmxvd24tYmFjay10by11ay8=,PICKUP,DRCでのエボラ流行は1万人超の症例と48.6%の致死率、周辺国（ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダ）への拡大、さらに英国人感染者の本国搬送という国際的拡大事例であり、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する重大シグナル。,Ebola,Republic of Angola; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,British man infected with Ebola in DR Congo to be flown back to UK,2026-11-04T21:44:00+00:00,https://www.myjoyonline.com/british-man-infected-with-ebola-in-dr-congo-to-be-flown-back-to-uk/,ENGLISH,humans,"British man infected with Ebola in DR Congo will be flown back to the UK; first UK national case in DR Congo outbreak, which has caused more than 5,000 deaths. Flight date is not disclosed. UK officials say there are established procedures and the public risk remains low; Reuters cites the patient as a healthcare worker. Imported UK Ebola cases are rare; four have occurred—one in 1976 from a lab incident and three in West Africa during 2014–2015. The DR Congo outbreak began in May, with more than 10,000 cases and a 48.6% fatality rate by month’s end, driven by Bundibugyo variant. Early symptoms include vomiting and diarrhoea and can progress to organ failure; transmission is via infected bodily fluids. No approved vaccine; two candidate drugs will join an ongoing trial, including Oxford/Serum Institute and Moderna vaccines, once Congolese approval is granted. Cases have appeared in Kenya, Nigeria and Uganda.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,発生地域にはAngola、Kenya、Nigeria、Uganda、UKも含まれるが、記事主題はDRCでの流行とその英国人患者の帰国であり、対象国リストに該当するのはDRCのみ。ケニア・ナイジェリア・ウガンダは二次的な症例発生地として言及されているが対象国リストには含まれない。,
