aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZnJlZW1hbGF5c2lhdG9kYXkuY29tL2NhdGVnb3J5L3dvcmxkLzIwMjYvMTEvMDUvc29tZS0xLTgwMC1kZWFkLWZyb20tY2hvbGVyYS1pbi1lYm9sYS1oaXQtZHItY29uZ28=,PICKUP,コレラとエボラの同時流行により大規模な死者・患者数が発生し、紛争地域での対応困難と首都圏への拡大リスクがあるため、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,,"Some 1,800 dead from cholera in Ebola-hit DR Congo",2026-11-04T22:58:25+00:00,https://www.freemalaysiatoday.com/category/world/2026/11/05/some-1-800-dead-from-cholera-in-ebola-hit-dr-congo,ENGLISH,humans; environment,"Cholera has killed about 1,800 people and caused around 60,000 cases in the Democratic Republic of Congo this year, as the country confronts its deadliest Ebola outbreak to date. Most infections have occurred in the eastern provinces of North Kivu and South Kivu, which are long plagued by armed conflict and instability. Health officials warn that cases could spill toward Kinshasa, the capital, as cholera spreads along the Congo river basin. Hard-to-reach, conflict-affected regions hinder response efforts, risking a dual crisis of rampant cholera on top of Ebola. The rainy season is expected to facilitate transmission. The current cholera mortality rate is about 3%. WHO emphasizes that Ebola vaccination campaigns, especially in the conflict-hit east, are very important to curb the concurrent outbreaks.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,コレラとエボラの同時流行、紛争地域での対応困難、首都キンシャサへの拡大懸念、雨季による感染拡大リスクが報告されている。WHOはエボラワクチン接種キャンペーンの重要性を強調。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9hY3AuY2QvYW5nbGFpcy9lYm9sYS1pbi1pdHVyaS1tb251c2NvLXN0cmVuZ3RoZW5zLXByb3RlY3Rpb24tZm9yLXBvbGljZS1vZmZpY2Vycy8=,PICKUP,コンゴ民主共和国イツリ州でエボラ出血熱への対応としてMONUSCOが警察官への防護資材を提供しており、エボラは重症度・伝播性ともに高く国際的関心も高い疾患であるため、フルリスク評価に進むべきシグナルと判断する。,Ebola,Ituri; Bunia; Democratic Republic of the Congo,,Ebola in Ituri: MONUSCO strengthens protection for police officers - ACP,2026-11-04T23:35:35+00:00,https://acp.cd/anglais/ebola-in-ituri-monusco-strengthens-protection-for-police-officers/,ENGLISH,humans,"Ebola in Ituri: MONUSCO provided protective equipment against Ebola to the Congolese National Police in Bunia, Ituri Province, Democratic Republic of Congo, to reduce officers’ exposure and protect communities. The donation, via UNPOL, includes 500 FFP2/N95 masks, 20 infrared thermometers, 100 bottles of hand sanitizer, 125 bottles of disinfectant liquid soap, ten 100-liter hand-washing stations, medical gloves, powdered chlorine, bin bags, and awareness materials (700 leaflets, 100 posters). Five police units in Ituri — provincial police station, Bunia Police Academy, urban police station, Mobile Intervention Group, and Anti-Crime and Anti-Narcotics Squadron — will receive the gear to improve checkpoint management and response operations in coordination with health authorities. No case/death counts are provided in this report; the effort aims to minimize transmission risk during Ebola response. The initiative reinforces ongoing protective measures in Ituri as of 2026-11-04.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事は症例数・死亡数などの詳細を含まず、PPE配布など予防的対応に関する内容。エボラの発生規模や感染拡大状況については続報の確認が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudXJkdXBvaW50LmNvbS9hcmFiaWMvc3RvcnkvMjI4NDIwNC5odG1s,PICKUP,致死率48.7%のエボラ出血熱が大規模に拡大しており、Africa CDCが近隣国への波及を警告していることからIHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。,Ebola,Africa; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,"Ebola death toll in the Democratic Republic of the Congo rises to 5,163.",ارتفاع حصيلة وفيات إيبولا بالكونغو الديمقراطية إلى 5163,2026-11-04T23:40:05+00:00,https://www.urdupoint.com/arabic/story/2284204.html,ARABIC,humans,"Ebola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo has reached 5,163 deaths and 10,603 confirmed infections as of 2 November 2026, a case fatality rate of 48.7%. The Ministry of Health reported the totals via its website, with Kinshasa cited in the update. The outbreak continues to spread across the country, and Africa CDC Director Jean Kasia warned that the virus threatens neighboring countries as transmission persists throughout the Congo. The report provides official counts but does not include further details on infection sources or laboratory confirmation beyond the numbers. Published 4 November 2026, the article underscores the rising fatalities and ongoing regional public health risk from the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"致死率約48.7%と非常に高く、感染者10,603人・死者5,163人という大規模流行。Africa CDCが周辺国への拡大リスクを公式に警告しており、国際的な注視が必要な事案。",
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudXJkdXBvaW50LmNvbS9lbi9taWRkbGUtZWFzdC9jaG9sZXJhLWtpbGxzLTE4MDAtaW4tZHItY29uZ28tc2luY2Utc3RhcnQtby0yMjg0MjAyLmh0bWw=,PICKUP,"WHOが「数十年で最悪」と評する大規模コレラ流行（死者1,800人、症例6万件）で、紛争地域でのアクセス困難と雨季による拡大、キンシャサ波及懸念があり、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。",Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo,,"Cholera Kills 1,800 In DR Congo Since Start Of 2026",2026-11-04T23:30:05+00:00,https://www.urdupoint.com/en/middle-east/cholera-kills-1800-in-dr-congo-since-start-o-2284202.html,ENGLISH,humans; environment,"Cholera has killed 1,800 people in the Democratic Republic of the Congo since January 2026, with about 60,000 cases reported. WHO says this is the country’s worst cholera outbreak in decades, with the majority of cases in North Kivu and South Kivu in the eastern provinces. The Congo River basin corridor and expanding transmission along waterways raise concern that urban centers, including Kinshasa, could be affected as the rainy season accelerates spread. Difficulties accessing remote and conflict-affected areas hinder containment. The case fatality rate is about 3%. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus called for intensified response, including Ebola vaccination campaigns in conflict-affected eastern regions, as the country simultaneously battles multiple outbreaks. Efforts focus on safe water, sanitation, and rapid case management to curb transmission and prevent escalation toward Kinshasa.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はコレラが主題だが、同時にエボラワクチン接種キャンペーンにも言及されており、DRCが複数の感染症流行に同時対応している点に留意。国境を越えた国際的拡大の明示的記述はないため不明と評価。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubWVkaWNhbGJyaWVmLmNvLnphL2Vib2xhLWtpbGxzLXR3by1kb2N0b3JzLXdpdGhpbi00OC1ob3Vycy8=,PICKUP,DRCで史上最大・最悪のエボラ流行が継続し、致死率約49%、ケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリア・フランスへの国際的拡大も確認されており、IHR基準・WPRO基準を複数満たすためフルRRAへ進むべき。,Ebola,Ituri; Republic of France; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Kenya; Republic of Uganda; Federal Republic of Nigeria,,Ebola kills two doctors within 48 hours - Juta MedicalBrief,2026-11-04T15:06:10+00:00,https://www.medicalbrief.co.za/ebola-kills-two-doctors-within-48-hours/,ENGLISH,humans,"Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) persists as two doctors die within 48 hours: Dr Marie-France Shogogo on Oct 27 at the Beni Ebola Treatment Centre (North Kivu) and Dr Samuel Safari on Oct 29 in Ituri; a third, Dr Charles Mbusa Munyumu, died Aug 10 at Katwa ETC. By 2026-11-04, the DRC had about 10,193 confirmed cases and 4,960 deaths (CFR 48.7%), up from 9,704 cases and 4,687 deaths the prior week; 489 new cases and 273 new deaths in the week, with 52 cases in the last 24 hours. Ituri remains the epicentre; eight provinces affected. The outbreak, caused by Bundibugyo virus, is the 17th in the DRC and the largest/deadliest in its history, spreading to Kenya and Uganda, and Nigeria in West Africa; France reported a non-African case linked to Congo in June. Vaccine trials are underway; no approved therapy. Calls for cross-border screening, faster funding, and a global preparedness corridor.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,ケニア・ウガンダ・ナイジェリア・フランスへの波及が報告されているが、いずれも対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations には含めていない。DRCにおける史上最大規模のアウトブレイクであり、継続的な監視と国際支援の必要性が高い。,
