aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubWlyYWdlbmV3cy5jb20vYnJpdGlzaC1oZWFsdGhjYXJlLXdvcmtlci13aXRoLWVib2xhLXRvLWJlLTE3NzIyMTQv,PICKUP,"DRCでのエボラ（ブンディブギョウイルス）アウトブレイクで死者5,000人超と報告されており、公衆衛生上深刻かつ異常な規模。国際的な医療搬送も発生しておりIHR基準を複数満たす。",Ebola,London; Newcastle upon Tyne; England; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Angola; Republic of Sierra Leone; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,,British Healthcare Worker With Ebola To Be Flown To UK,2026-11-05T00:07:53+00:00,https://www.miragenews.com/british-healthcare-worker-with-ebola-to-be-1772214/,ENGLISH,humans,"British man infected with Ebola in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) linked to Bundibugyo virus will be flown to the UK in a planned medical evacuation confirmed 4 November 2026. The outbreak has caused over 5,000 deaths. The patient, working for a humanitarian organization, represents frontline exposure risk. Dr Damien Tully of MRC/UVRI and LSHTM says the UK risk from the evacuation is extremely low; Ebola transmission is primarily via direct contact with infected fluids, and persons are not infectious until symptoms appear. The UK maintains two high‑level isolation units at Royal Free Hospital (London) and Royal Victoria Infirmary (Newcastle) with controlled transport and PPE. Historical context: during 2014–2016 West Africa Ebola, three infected healthcare workers were treated in the UK with no onward transmission, including two evacuated from Sierra Leone. Emphasis remains on protecting frontline workers and rapid isolation in the DRC outbreak.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,"記事の主眼は英国人医療従事者の本国搬送だが、背景にあるDRCでのエボラアウトブレイクが死者5,000人超と甚大であり、これが主要な懸念事項。英国・アンゴラ・シエラレオネは対象国リスト外のためverified_locationsから除外。",
