aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuem9jYWxvLmNvbS5teC9hZXJvbGluZWFzLW1leGljYW5hcy1waWRlbi1kZWNsYXJhY2lvbi1zYW5pdGFyaWEtYS12aWFqZXJvcy1hLWV1LXBvci1icm90ZS1kZS1lYm9sYS1lbi1lbC1jb25nby8=,PICKUP,エボラ出血熱の流行を受けて米CDCが渡航者への健康申告義務化という渡航制限措置を課しており、IHR基準の複数該当とフルRRAの必要性が認められる。,Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United States; Mexico,Mexican airlines request a health declaration from travelers to the EU due to Ebola outbreak in the Congo.,Aerolíneas mexicanas piden declaración sanitaria a viajeros a EU por brote de ébola en el Congo,2026-11-05T00:33:40+00:00,https://www.zocalo.com.mx/aerolineas-mexicanas-piden-declaracion-sanitaria-a-viajeros-a-eu-por-brote-de-ebola-en-el-congo/,SPANISH,humans; environment,"November 4, 2026: Mexican airlines Aeroméxico, Volaris, and Viva require international passengers traveling to the United States to present a sworn declaration that they have notbeen in the Democratic Republic of the Congo in the last 21 days. The measure, mandated by the U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), follows an Ebola outbreak in the DRC and applies to flights bound for the United States. The declaration is a health-documentation step for inbound travelers and is effective immediately. No case counts or fatality details are provided in the report. The policy targets US-bound passengers and represents an added border-control measure in response to the outbreak in Central Africa.",Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,Yes,不明,不明,Yes,Yes,3,Yes,Yes,不明,記事はメキシコ・米国の渡航対応措置についてであり、エボラ流行自体はDRCで発生。米国・メキシコは対象国リストに含まれないため、verified_locationsはDRCのみとした。症例数・死亡者数等の詳細情報は本記事に記載なし。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cub2thei5jb20uc2EvdmFyaWV0eS9uYS8yMjc0MDU2,PICKUP,"致死率48.7%、死者5,163人・確定症例10,603人に及ぶ大規模なエボラ流行が継続しており、近隣諸国への越境リスクも指摘されているため、フルリスク評価が必要と判断される。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo,"Ebola virus deaths in the Democratic Republic of the Congo rise to 5,163.","ارتفاع وفيات فايروس ""إيبولا"" في الكونغو الديمقراطية إلى 5163 حالة",2026-11-05T00:30:14+00:00,https://www.okaz.com.sa/variety/na/2274056,ARABIC,humans,"Ebola deaths rise to 5,163 in the Democratic Republic of the Congo as of 2 November, according to the DRC Ministry of Health. The outbreak continues across multiple regions of the country, with confirmed Ebola cases totaling 10,603 and a case fatality ratio of 48.7%. The report notes ongoing transmission within the DRC and warns that the outbreak threatens neighboring nations. No laboratory confirmation details beyond confirmed cases are provided in the article, and there are no specifics on transmission sources or imported/exported cases. The figures underscore a persistent, countrywide crisis despite public health efforts, highlighting regional vigilance and cross-border risk. The date of publication is 2026-11-05.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,死者数・症例数・致死率ともに高水準で、国全体にわたる持続的流行となっている。近隣国への拡大懸念が明記されているが、具体的な越境症例の報告はまだない。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2FtLmFlL2FyL2FydGljbGUvMTdpZGM4ay0lRDglQTclRDklODQlRDglQjUlRDglQUQlRDglQTktJUQ4JUE3JUQ5JTg0JUQ4JUI5JUQ4JUE3JUQ5JTg0JUQ5JTg1JUQ5JThBJUQ4JUE5LSVEOCVBQSVEOCVCNiVEOSU4QSVEOSU4MS0lRDklODQlRDklODIlRDglQTclRDglQUQlRDklOEElRDklODYtJUQ4JUE=,PICKUP,"DRCでのBundibugyoエボラウイルス流行による死亡者5,163人・致死率48.7%という深刻な公衆衛生上の影響があり、WHOが国際的なワクチン開発支援を行っていることからIHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。",Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,World Health Organization adds two new vaccines to Ebola clinical trials.,"""الصحة العالمية"" تضيف لقاحين جديدين إلى التجارب السريرية لـ""إيبولا""",2026-11-05T00:29:56+00:00,https://www.wam.ae/ar/article/17idc8k-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B5%D8%AD%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D8%AA%D8%B6%D9%8A%D9%81-%D9%84%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%AD%D9%8A%D9%86-%D8%AC%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86-%D8%A5%D9%84%D9%89-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AA%D8%AC%D8%A7%D8%B1%D8%A8,ARABIC,humans,"On November 5, 2026, the World Health Organization added two new vaccines to ongoing clinical trials in the Democratic Republic of Congo to address Bundibugyo ebolavirus outbreaks. The vaccines, developed by Oxford University in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India and Moderna, are the first designed specifically to combat this Ebola virus type. The DRC Ministry of Health reported 5,163 deaths and 10,603 confirmed cases as of November 2, with a case fatality rate of 48.7%. Trials continue in the DRC to evaluate safety and efficacy, informing outbreak response against this Ebola species. These vaccines were designed to address Bundibugyo ebolavirus and form part of WHO's broader vaccination strategy.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,インドおよび英国は記事中でワクチン開発機関（Serum Institute of India、Oxford大学）の所在地として言及されているのみで、実際の感染発生地ではないためverified_locationsから除外した。,
aHR0cHM6Ly9nbG9ib3J1cmFsLmdsb2JvLmNvbS9wZWN1YXJpYS9hdmVzL25vdGljaWEvMjAyNi8xMS9taW5pc3RlcmlvLWRhLWFncmljdWx0dXJhLWludmVzdGlnYS10cmVzLXN1c3BlaXRhcy1kZS1zaW5kcm9tZXMtcmVzcGlyYXRvcmlhcy1lbS1hdmVzLW5vLXN1bC1lLXN1ZGVzdGUuZ2h0bWw=,WATCH,鳥インフルエンザは検査未確定で疑い例の段階であり、確定しているのはニューカッスル病（家禽）のみ。ヒトへの感染報告はなく、現時点では情報不足のため続報を注視する。,Human Infection with Avian Influenza; Newcastle Disease; Avian Influenza,Nova Itaberaba; São Paulo; Santa Catarina; São Paulo; Chapecó; Guarujá; Federative Republic of Brazil,Ministry of Agriculture investigates three suspected cases of respiratory syndromes in birds in the South and Southeast.,Ministério da Agricultura investiga três suspeitas de síndromes respiratórias em aves no Sul e Sudeste,2026-11-05T00:37:10+00:00,https://globorural.globo.com/pecuaria/aves/noticia/2026/11/ministerio-da-agricultura-investiga-tres-suspeitas-de-sindromes-respiratorias-em-aves-no-sul-e-sudeste.ghtml,PORTUGUESE,animals,"As of November 4, 2026, Brazil's Ministry of Agriculture reports three suspected cases of respiratory syndromes in birds: in Chapecó, Santa Catarina, a turkey and a backyard chicken; and in Guarujá, São Paulo, a wild duck (pato-do-mato). Samples are being collected and await laboratory confirmation. The ministry has also confirmed the fourth Newcastle Disease outbreak on a farm in Nova Erechim, Santa Catarina, about 45 km from Chapecó, with additional Newcastle foci in Nova Erechim, Nova Itaberaba, and Coronel Freitas—all in Santa Catarina. The ministry's tool monitors avian influenza and Newcastle Disease. There is no reported lab-confirmed avian influenza in these cases; investigations center on respiratory syndromes and Newcastle Disease status.",No,No,不明,不明,0,No,No,Yes,Yes,No,2,不明,Yes,No,鳥インフルエンザは検査中で未確定。確定しているのはニューカッスル病（サンタカタリーナ州の複数農場）であり、ヒト感染例の報告はない。家禽産業・貿易への影響可能性があるため、検査結果が出次第再評価が必要。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudXJkdXBvaW50LmNvbS9hcmFiaWMvc3RvcnkvMjI4NDIwNy5odG1s,PICKUP,"DRCでのブンディブギョ・エボラウイルスによるアウトブレイクは10,603症例・致死率48.7%と極めて深刻であり、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当するためフルリスク評価が必要。",Ebola,Genève; Genève; Oxford; England; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Switzerland; United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland,World Health Organization adds two new vaccines to the clinical trials for Ebola.,الصحة العالمية تضيف لقاحين جديدين إلى التجارب السريرية لـإيبولا,2026-11-05T00:30:07+00:00,https://www.urdupoint.com/arabic/story/2284207.html,ARABIC,humans,"Geneva-based World Health Organization announced the addition of two vaccines to ongoing clinical trials in the Democratic Republic of Congo to combat Ebola caused by Bundibugyo ebolavirus. The vaccines, developed by the University of Oxford in collaboration with the Serum Institute of India and Moderna, are the first designed specifically to target this Ebola species. In the Democratic Republic of Congo, the Ministry of Health reported 10,603 confirmed cases and 5,163 deaths as of 2 November 2026, yielding a case fatality rate of 48.7%. The development of these vaccines aligns with efforts to expand preventive tools amid sustained transmission from this outbreak. The WHO’s update highlights international partnerships in vaccine development and ongoing evaluation of candidate vaccines within Congo’s outbreak response.",Yes,Yes,不明,不明,2,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はWHOによるワクチン臨床試験追加の発表が主題だが、DRCにおける進行中のエボラ（ブンディブギョ種）アウトブレイクの規模と致死率が極めて高いため、感染症危機管理上重要なシグナルと判断。スイス・英国・インドはワクチン開発関連機関の所在地であり、発生地域ではないため除外。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudmlldG5hbXBsdXMudm4vd2hvLWNhbmgtYmFvLWRpY2gtdGEtbmdoaWVtLXRyb25nLXRhaS1jb25nLWhvYS1kYW4tY2h1LWNvbmdvLXBvc3QxMTQ2MjUyLnZucA==,PICKUP,コレラとエボラの同時流行により死者数・症例数が極めて多く、紛争地域での対応困難と国際河川流域への拡大懸念があり、IHR基準・WPRO基準ともに複数該当する。,Cholera; Ebola,South Kivu Province; Kinshasa City; Kinshasa; Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of the Sudan,WHO warns of a severe cholera outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.,WHO cảnh báo dịch tả nghiêm trọng tại Cộng hòa Dân chủ Congo,2026-11-05T00:47:47+00:00,https://www.vietnamplus.vn/who-canh-bao-dich-ta-nghiem-trong-tai-cong-hoa-dan-chu-congo-post1146252.vnp,VIETNAMESE,humans; environment,"Cholera outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) has reached severe levels, with WHO reporting about 1,800 deaths and nearly 60,000 cases since the start of the year (as of Nov 4). The DRC is concurrently contending the largest Ebola outbreak to date, creating a critical health emergency. Most cholera cases are in the eastern provinces of North Kivu and South Kivu, regions contested by armed groups including the M23, with concerns about spread along the Congo River basin toward Kinshasa. Ongoing insecurity and remote outbreaks hinder surveillance, patient access, and delivery of supplies. The rainy season could worsen transmission, given sanitation and water challenges. WHO urges intensified Ebola vaccination campaigns, especially in eastern areas hit by conflict, to reduce community spread. Separately, Sudan reports a severe cholera outbreak with at least 120 deaths; prior outbreak (July 2024–March 2026) recorded around 124,400 cases and 3,500 deaths.",Yes,Yes,Yes,不明,3,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,Yes,5,Yes,Yes,Yes,記事はスーダンのコレラ流行にも言及しているが、スーダンは対象国リストに含まれないため除外。DRCにおけるコレラとエボラの同時流行、治安悪化による対応困難、コンゴ川流域からキンシャサへの拡大懸念が主題。,
aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGhhaWxhbmRtZWRpY2FsLm5ld3MvbmV3cy9kcmMtcy1hbnRocmF4LW91dGJyZWFrLWFtb25nLXdpbGRsaWZlLXRocmVhdGVucy1odW1hbnM=,WATCH,現時点で人への感染例は報告されていないが、過去にウガンダへのスピルオーバーで人的被害が出ており、干ばつによる接触機会増加で今後の人獣共通感染リスクが懸念されるため、続報を注視する。,Cholera; Anthrax; Ebola,Democratic Republic of the Congo; Republic of Uganda,,DRC's Anthrax Outbreak Among Wildlife Threatens Humans,2026-11-05T00:54:18+00:00,https://www.thailandmedical.news/news/drc-s-anthrax-outbreak-among-wildlife-threatens-humans,ENGLISH,humans; environment; animals,"Anthrax (Bacillus anthracis) outbreaks are killing hippos in Democratic Republic of the Congo's Virunga National Park, with lab confirmation of approximately 30 hippo deaths within a month. No human infections reported in the current outbreak as of 2026-11-05, but authorities warn that handling infected carcasses, skinning, or consuming contaminated meat could transmit the disease. March 2025 saw a more severe spillover, with about 65 hippos killed in Virunga and 15 human infections in neighboring Uganda, including two deaths. Anthrax spores can persist in soil for decades; drought drives wildlife to scarce water sources, heightening exposure. The DR Congo faces Ebola, cholera, poor sanitation, and conflict, complicating response. Park authorities are disposing of carcasses and advising residents against handling them. Authorities stress strengthened surveillance, rapid antibiotic access, and integrated veterinary-public health action to prevent a human outbreak.",No,Yes,Yes,No,2,Yes,不明,Yes,Yes,Yes,4,不明,Yes,Yes,現行アウトブレイクでは人への感染は未確認だが、2025年3月の同地域でのスピルオーバーではウガンダで15例・死亡2例が発生しており、再燃リスクがある。DRCはエボラ・コレラ・紛争等複合的な公衆衛生課題を抱えており、監視体制強化が求められている。ウガンダは対象国リストに含まれないため verified_locations からは除外した。,
